x_comment(x_ScenarioContext,"A specialization of #$ConjecturalContext. Each instance of #$ScenarioContext denotes a \"possible world\" -- each instance is a context in which possibly true assertions are made to describe a state of affairs that might or might not obtain. With the exception of \"seed contexts\" (about which more later), instances of #$ScenarioContext are constructed automatically by the scenario generation abduction harness via the application of #$abductiveExpansion rules (see #$abductiveExpansion). Assertions directly made in a non-seed scenario context are possibly true. They are assertions which, if actually true, would serve to explain assertions in more general scenario contexts. Scenario contexts that are not automatically generated are seed contexts that contain assertions for which one desires explanatory scenarios to be generated.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9763).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9763,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
