x_comment(x_ScientificNumberFn,"(#$ScientificNumberFn SIGNIFICAND EXPONENT) denotes a number in scientific notation which has SIGNIFICAND with an implicit decimal point after its first digit as its significand and EXPONENT as its exponent.  So, e.g., (#$ScientificNumberFn 314159 0) denotes 3.14159.  Likewise, (#$ScientificNumberFn 23648762469238472354 32) denotes 2.3648762469238472354e32 or 2.3648762469238472354 * 10^32.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9774).
