x_comment(x_relationOnlyAll,"A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can be used to state that a #$BinaryPredicate stands in a certain relation to two collections.  <code>(#$relationOnlyAll BINPRED COL1 COL2)</code> means for any instance <code>Y</code> of <code>COL2</code>, <code>(BINPRED X Y)</code> holds only if <code>X</code> is an instance of <code>COL1</code>.  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used as shorthand for) the more complex form\n<pre>\n(#$implies\n  (#$and\n    (BINPRED ?X ?Y)\n    (#$isa ?Y COL2))\n  (#$isa ?X COL1)).\n</pre>\nFor example, <code>(#$relationOnlyAll #$wearsClothing #$HumanChild #$ChildrensClothing)</code> means that only children wear children's clothing.  This assertion is shorthand for the following rule:\n<pre>\n(#$implies\n  (#$and\n    (#$wearsClothing ?PERSON ?CLOTHING)\n    (#$isa ?CLOTHING #$ChildrensClothing))\n  (#$isa ?PERSON #$HumanChild)).\n</pre>\nSee also #$relationAllOnly and #$NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a977b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a977b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a977b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a977b,90).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517a977b,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a977b,[]).
x_comment(x_relationInstanceOnly,"A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate (q.v.) that can be used to state that a given binary predicate holds between a specified thing and some instance of a given collection.  (#$relationInstanceOnly PRED THING COL) means that only instances of COL, say INST, are such that (PRED THING INST) holds.  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:\n<p>\n(#$implies\n(PRED THING ?INST)\n(#$isa ?INST COL)).\n<p>\nFor example, `(#$relationInstanceOnly #$presidentOfCountry #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica #$UnitedStatesPresident)' means that only U.S. presidents are president of the U.S.A..  Cf. #$relationOnlyInstance, and see the shared #$NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a977c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a977c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a977c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
