x_comment(x_GreatestCommonDivisorFn,"A variable-arity #$MathematicalFunctionOnScalars that returns the greatest common (integer) divisor of its (\"co-integral\" scalar) arguments.\n<p>\nWhere <code>INT1</code>, ..., <code>INTn</code> are #$ScalarIntegralValues (q.v.) such that for any <code>i</code> and <code>j</code> (1 <code><= i,j <= n) (#$coIntegralScalars INTi INTj)</code> holds, <code>(#$GreatestCommonDivisorFn INT1 ... INTn)</code> is the #$Integer that is the greatest common divisor of <code>INT1</code>, ..., <code>INTn</code>.\n<p>\nFor example, (#$GreatestCommonDivisorFn  (#$Mile 6) (#$Mile 12) (#$Mile 15)) is equal to 3.\n<p>\nSee the comment on #$coIntegralScalars for more detail about the inter-argument constraints on this function.  Also see #$LeastCommonMultipleFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a97ba).
