x_comment(x_CyclicalIntervalGroupType,"A collection of collections of collections of #$TimeIntervals. Each instance CIGTYPE of #$CyclicalIntervalGroupType is a specialization #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries, and is a collection of interval-types whose instances recur throughout all of calendar history.  Unlike instances of #$CyclicalSuccessiveIntervalGroupType, CIGTYPE may or may not partition all of time.  For example, CIGTYPE could be the collection of the seven calendar days of the week (see #$DayOfWeekType) or the collection of the twelve calendar months (see #$MonthOfYearType) or simply the collection of various times of the year (see #$TimeOfYearType).") :- x_cid(a65b16517a97e3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a97e3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a97e3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
