xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a97f0,[]).
x_comment(x_localTo,"(#$localTo OBJECT SPATIAL-THING) means that in the current context OBJECT is considered to be local to SPATIAL-THING, which may be a place, a person, or even an event.  Something is ``local'' if it can affect an agent (of the appropriate type) located in/at SPATIAL-THING whereas more distant things of the same type could not affect the agent in the same way, or that if an agent located in/at SPATIAL-THING wants to go to a place similar to OBJECT, OBJECT itself would be close enough to be considered as the destination.  Whether something is considered local is dependent upon the object type, the agent type, and the distance between them.  Even political considerations may ensue.  A local airport is likely to be further away than a local restaurant or post office.  If the closest library or elementary is in another country, it is unlikely to be considered as local.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a97f1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a97f1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a97f1,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a97f1,313).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517a97f1,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a97f1,[]).
x_comment(x_animalInjuredIn,"(#$animalInjuredIn EVENT ANIMAL) means that, during the course of EVENT, ANIMAL suffers damage to some part(s) of its body sufficient to qualify as an 'injury'.  The injury may be due to the actions of an outside actor on ANIMAL, such as when a person is struck by a falling rock, or not, as when a person strains a calf muscle while jogging.  For the special case of injuries suffered during hostile actions, see #$animalWoundedIn") :- x_cid(a65b16517a97f2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a97f2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a97f2,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
