x_comment(x_TimeOfTypeFn,"(#$TimeOfTypeFn X Y) is the subset of Y containing all and only those members of Y which intersect, in fact are subsumed by, some member of X, i.e., (#$TimeOfMonthFn X Y) = {y: y is a member of Y, and (#$temporallySubsumes x y) for some member x of X}.  Here are some examples: (1) (#$TimeOfTypeFn #$May (#$DayOfMonthFn 7)) is the collection of all `May 7th' time intervals, (2) (#$TimeOfTypeFn (#$DayOfMonthFn 7) #$TimeOfDay-10AM) is the collection of all `the 7th day of the month 10:00am-11:00am' time intervals, and (3) (#$TimeOfTypeFn (#$DayOfMonthFn 7) (#$TimeOfTypeFn #$TimeOfDay-10AM (#$TimeOfTypeFn (#$MinuteOfHourFn 0) (#$SecondOfMinuteFn 0)))) is the collection of all `the 7th day of the month 10:00:00am-10:00:01am' time intervals.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a980f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a980f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
