x_comment(x_interArgInsIsa,"A quintary instance of #$InterArgConstraintPredicate (q.v.).  (#$interArgInsIsa RELN k INDEP-INS n DEP-COL) means that, in order for any atomic sentence formed by RELN to be true, if INDEP-INS appears as the k-th argument to RELN, the n-th argument must be a member of DEP-COL. For example, (#$interArgInsIsa #$willBe-Metric-CalendarTime 1 #$CalendarYear 3 #$TimeOfYearType) means that in order for (#$willBe-Metric-CalendarTime X k Y PROP) to be true, X is (identical to) #$CalendarYear only if Y is a member of the collection #$TimeOfYearType.  For a more general explanation of independent and dependent arguments in the present sense, see #$InterArgConstraintPredicate.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a981b).
