x_comment(x_ConventionallyClassifiedTemporalObjectSeries,"A specialization of #$ConventionalClassificationType (q.v.) and #$TemporalObjectType.  Each instance of #$ConventionallyClassifiedTemporalObjectSeries is a series of temporal objects (of the same kind) such that for each E in the series one can meaningfully speak of `the one before E' or `the one after E' in the series (or speak of `the last one' or `the next one' etc. in the series if we are to temporally locate ourselves in E). Examples of instances of this collection include #$CalendarYear, #$Friday and #$ChristmasHoliday etc.  Two important specializations of this collection are #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries and #$AnnualHolidayType (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16517a98ca).
