x_comment(x_resultGenlArgArgIsa,"(#$resultGenlArgArgIsa FUNCTION ARG-NUM ARGISA-NUM) says that any #$CycLNonAtomicTerm NAT built from the #$CollectionDenotingFunction FUNCTION will be a specialization of TYPE, where (#$argIsa RELN ARGISA-NUM TYPE) and (#$argN RELN ARG-NUM NAT).  So, for example, (#$resultGenlArgArgIsa #$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn 2 1) entails that (#$genls (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn #$Thing #$likesAsFriend FRED) #$PerceptualAgent), since (#$argIsa #$likesAsFriend 1 #$PerceptualAgent) and #$likesAsFriend appears as the 2nd argument to the NART.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a98ce).
