x_comment(x_RatioQuantity,"A specialization of #$MultiDimensionalQuantity (q.v.).  Each instance of #$RatioQuantity is a quantity that is derivable (via #$QuotientFn) as a ratio of other quantities.  For example, (#$MilesPerHour 65) is a ratio quantity obtainable by dividing (#$Mile 65) by (#$HoursDuration 1); and  (#$PoundsPerSquareInch 50) is equal to\n<p>\n<pre>\n  (#$QuotientFn\n    (#$Pound-UnitOfForce 50)\n    (#$SquaredFn (#$Inch 1))) .\n</pre>\n<p>\nRatio quantities are used for measuring a difference or change in one quantity against a (usually incremental) difference or change in another quantity.  When the later quantity is a #$Time-Quantity (as in the first example above), the ratio quantity is an instance of the specialization #$Rate.\n<p>\nSee also #$PerFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9941).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9941,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9941,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a9941,704).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517a9941,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a9941,[]).
x_comment(x_conditionalMeaningSentenceOfSchema,"This predicate is used to state sksi 'conditional meaning\nsentences', i.e. meaning sentences which include an additional query\n(either a boolean check or with unbound variables) that is asked to\ncheck the applicability of a meaning sentence, or to limit its scope.\n(#$conditionalMeaningSentenceOfSchema LS1 SENTENCE1 LS2 SENTENCE2)\nmeans that SENTENCE2 is a meaning sentence for LS2 only if SENTENCE1\nis true in the context of LS1. For example, if we have asserted\n(#$conditionalMeaningSentenceOfSchema #$OFAC-main-LS (#$isa (#$TheFn\n#$PartiallyTangible) #$Watercraft) #$OFAC-main-LS (#$massOfObject\n(#$TheFn #$PartiallyTangible) (#$TheFn #$Mass))) in the (#$MappingMtFn\n#$OFAC-KS), then any query in (#$ContentMtFn #$OFAC-main-KS) that\nincludes a #$massOfObject clause will result in bindings from the\ndatabase that also satisfy the condition (#$isa ?FOO #$Watercraft).\nHowever note that this additional restriction only applies to the database\nquery. It does not affect the answers which may return from other tactics.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9942).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9942,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9942,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a9942,715).
