x_comment(x_Detonation,"A specialization of #$Explosion, #$CombustionReaction, and #$WavePropagation.  Each instance of #$Detonation is  fast high-pressure combustion reaction. A detonation event is a reaction which happens so quickly that the reaction speed exceeds the speed of sound in the reacting material.  A detonation reaction is propagated by a supersonic shock wave travelling through the reacting medium.  After initiation, the shock wave accelerates quickly until it reaches a maximum speed -- the \"detonation velocity\" (see #$explosiveVelocityOfType) of the explosive.  Cf. #$Deflagration.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9948).
