x_comment(x_Commitment,"The collection of commitments.  Each instance of this collection is an agent's commitment to some instance of #$Situation.  For example, if I am commited to \"world peace\" then I am in a particular mental state -- a state that, in some sense, guides my future actions.  If so committed, then I will try to avoid actions that are inconsistent with there being world peace.  It is likely, as well, that I will attempt to perform some  actions which are directed at helping to bring about that state of affairs.  There is,  perhaps, a fine line between genuine commitments and mere \"lip service\" and in some cases, the agent may not even be able to tell whether their commitment is genuine.  Where we draw the line likely depends on the type of commitment it is.  A minimal commitment to world peace presumably requires less (that is, your having the commitment has less of an effect on your day to day behavior) than a minimal commitment towards a marriage.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9982).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9982,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
