x_comment(x_exceptionalSpecWRTSlot,"A predicate used to identify subcollections that are important exception-classes to default truths about a more general collection.  (#$exceptionalSpecWRTSlot SPEC GENL SLOT) says that SPEC is an exception to (#$relationAllInstance SLOT GENL VALUE), whatever the value is of VALUE.  So for example, as a default, we might assert (#$relationAllInstance numberOfInningsPlayed BaseballGame 9).  But we might also wish to assert (#$relationAllInstance numberOfInningsPlayed LittleLeagueBaseballGame 6), where (genls LittleLeagueBaseballGame BaseballGame).  Cyc's behavior will be to use the assertion on LittleLeagueBaseballGame to override the assertion on BaseballGame, treating LittleLeagueBaseballGame as an exception-sub-class of BaseballGame with respect to numberOfInningsPlayed: (#$exceptionalSpecWRTSlot LittleLeagueBaseballGame BaseballGame numberOfInningsPlayed).") :- x_cid(a65b16517a99c5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a99c5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
