x_comment(x_objectHasColorTinge,"(objectHasColorTinge OBJ COLOR-TINGE) holds just in case some visible part\nof object is colored COLOR-TINGE.  This is the most general of the color tinge predicates.\nSee #$mainColorTingeOfObject, and #$uniformColorTingeOfObject.  Unlike the other two \ncolor tinge predicates, this predicate is not a specialization of #$isa.  This is because\nit doesn't follow from the fact that an object's part is color COLOR-TINGE that that object\nis an instance of the collection COLOR-TINGE that characterizes that color tinge.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9aab).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9aab,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
