x_comment(x_uniformColorTingeOfObject,"(#$uniformColorTingeOfObject OBJ COLOR-TINGE) holds just in case OBJ \nis uniformly the color COLOR-TINGE.  This is the strongest of of the color tinge predicates \nand should be used only when OBJ is entirely one color.  To assert that an object is uniformly\nsome particular color instead of a color tinge use #$uniformColorOfObject.  If weaker relations \nto color tinges are needed use #$mainColorTingeOfObject, or #$objectHasColorTinge.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9aad).
