x_comment('x_preservesDisjointness-Unary',"#$preservesDisjointness-Unary is a unary instance of #$MetaRelation.  <code>(#$preservesDisjointness-Unary FUNCTION)</code> means that <code>FUNCTION</code> (an instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction and #$UnaryRelation) has the following property: if <code>COL1</code> and <code>COL2</code> are specializations of #$Collection that can both serve as the 1st argument of <code>FUNCTION</code>, and <code>COL2</code> is disjoint with <code>COL1</code> (so that <code>(#$disjointWith COL2 COL1)</code> holds), then the result of <code>FUNCTION</code> taking <code>COL2</code> as its argument will be disjoint with the result of <code>FUNCTION</code> taking <code>COL1</code> as its argument. For example, (#$preservesDisjointness-Unary #$GroupFn) holds because <code>(#$disjointWith COL-2 COL-1)</code> implies <code>(#$disjointWith (#$GroupFn COL-2) (#$GroupFn COL-1))</code>, for all collections <code>COL-1</code> and <code>COL-2</code> that satisfy the argument constraints for #$GroupFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9af0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9af0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
