x_comment(x_argumentCountType,"(#$argumentCountType PRED ARG-NUM TYPE) means that the type of the\nentities being counted in the ARG-NUM position of a CycL sentence headed\nby PRED is TYPE. For example, (#$argumentCountType #$numberOfInhabitants 2 #$Person)\nmeans that the number 2800000 in (#$numberOfInhabitants #$CityOfRomeItaly\n2800000) is used as a count of 2800000 instances of #$Person and not, say, of 2800000 instances of #$Dog. This intention that could not be directly expressed as an argument constraint on the second argument of #$numberOfInhabitants, which is bound to be a #$NonNegativeInteger, i.e #$disjointWith #$Person.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9af7).
