x_comment(x_BurntFn,"A #$UnaryIntersectionFunction (q.v.) that maps a given type of tangible thing to the collection all burnt things of that type.  (#$BurntFn TYPE) is the specialization of TYPE consisting of all burnt instances of TYPE.  For example, (#$BurntFn #$Toast) is the collection of slices of burnt toast and (#$BurntFn #$Skin) is the collection of regions burnt skin.  Note that if a given instance of TYPE becomes so completely burned that it is no longer an instance of TYPE (but is, say, a portion of ash), then it will _not_ be an instance of (#$BurntFn TYPE).") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9b22).
