x_comment(x_vaporDensityOfTypeAtTemperatureToType,"(#$vaporDensityOfTypeAtTemperatureToType SUBSTANCE1 RATIO\nTEMPERATURE SUBSTANCE2) is a relation that expresses the ratio of\nvapor density RATIO for the substance SUBSTANCE1 when compared to an\nequal volume of SUBSTANCE2 (typically either #$Air or\n(#$ChemicalSubstanceFn #$H2Molecule)), where SUBSTANCE2 = 1.  Thus, if\nthe RATIO is greater than 1, SUBSTANCE1 is heavier than SUBSTANCE2,\nand if RATIO is less than 1, then SUBSTANCE1 is lighter than\nSUBSTANCE2.  This predicate assumes standard pressure.  WHen the\ntemperature is not explicitly stated in the source, it is assumed to\nbe standard temperature, which is (#$DegreeCelsius 0).") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9b4f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9b4f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
