x_comment(x_SubLQuoteFn,"<code>(#$SubLQuoteFn SUBL-EXPRESSION)</code> is one of exactly two escapes to SubL from CycL, the other being #$ExpandSubLFn.  These are the only two ways to represent arbitrary SubL in CycL.  #$SubLQuoteFn encapsulates <code>SUBL-EXPRESSION</code> such that it will not be rejected by the CycL wff-checker as ill-formed CycL.  For example, <code>(#$SubLQuoteFn (+ 1 2))</code>, which <i>is</i> a #$CycLExpression, denotes the #$SubLSExpression (+ 1 2), which itself is <i>not</i> a #$CycLExpression.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9b63).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9b63,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9b63,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
