x_comment(x_FunctionTypeByRangeType,"A collection of collections that is a specialization of #$FunctionType.  Each instance of #$FunctionTypeByRangeType is a collection of #$Function-Denotationals such that each of its instances always returns as value (see #$resultIsa) something of the same (typically very general) type.  For example, #$IndividualDenotingFunction is an instance of #$FunctionTypeByRangeType; each instance of the former is a function that maps any (sequence of) argument(s) for which it is defined to some #$Individual.  Other instances of #$FunctionTypeByRangeType are #$CollectionDenotingFunction, #$FunctionDenotingFunction, and #$PredicateDenotingFunction.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9b6d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9b6d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
