x_comment(x_userRightsRelation,"This predicate relates an agent to the use rights which that agent has over an object. (#$userRightsRelation AGENT OBJECT URA) means that AGENT enjoys the #$SituationTypeByUserRights URA over OBJECT. URA is a collection of situations in which someone has a particular user right over an object.  If the #$userRightsRelation holds, there is a user rights situation whose constituents include AGENT and OBJECT and in which OBJECT is the object of the user rights.  Furthermore, this situation must be an instance of URA.  For example, if AGENT owns OBJECT, then there exists a situation which consists of AGENT possessing certain \"full use\" rights to use OBJECT and this situation is an instance of #$FullUseRights.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9be0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9be0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9be0,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
