x_comment(x_GeologicalTimePeriod,"The collection of significant continuous periods of geological time on earth.  The largest divisions are #$GeologicalEras (the #$Precambrian-GeologicalEra, #$Palaeozoic-GeologicalEra, #$Mesozoic-GeologicalEra, and #$Cenozoic-GeologicalEra); these are subdivided into #$GeologicalPeriods and the #$Tertiary-GeologicalPeriod and #$Quaternary-GeologicalPeriod (the two periods of the #$Cenozoic-GeologicalEra) are further subdivided into #$GeologicalEpochs, which consist of several #$GeologicalAges.  The divisions are not uniform time intervals but are based mainly on major evolutionary changes. For example, at the beginning of the #$Cambrian-GeologicalPeriod, about 590 million years ago, marine organisms suddenly became abundant and varied.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9c3d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9c3d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
