x_comment(x_GenlsPreservingFunction,"A specialization of #$CollectionRelatingFunction (q.v.).  Each instance <code>FUNC</code> of #$GenlsPreservingFunction is a collection-relating function such that whenever #$genls holds between successive arguments (in some particular argument-place) to <code>FUNC</code>, it holds between the corresponding successive values as well.  That is, <code>(#$preservesGenlsInArg FUNC N)</code> holds for some <code>N</code>.\n<p>\nMore precisely, a function <code>FUNC</code> is a #$GenlsPreservingFunction if and only if it has an argument-place (say the <code>N</code>th) such that the following hold:\n<p>\n(i) <code>(#$resultIsa FUNC #$Collection)</code>\n<p>\n(ii) <code>(#$argIsa FUNC N #$Collection)</code>\n<p>\n(iii) if <code>(#$genls SPEC GENL)</code> holds and <code>FUNC</code> is defined for both <code><... SPEC ...> </code>and<code> <... GENL ...></code> (where <code>SPEC</code> and <code>GENL</code> are the respective <code>N</code>th items in these otherwise identical sequences), then <code>(#$genls (FUNC ... SPEC ...) (FUNC ... GENL ...))</code> holds.\n<p>\nFor example, #$AdultFn is a genls-preserving function.  Just as a dog is a type of mammal (e.g.), so is an adult dog a type of adult mammal.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9c4f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9c4f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9c4f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a9c4f,2181).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517a9c4f,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a9c4f,[]).
