x_comment(x_BioregulatorType,"Bioregulators are '[b]iochemicals normally present in humans in small amounts that regulate the release of hormones that control normal body functions. Bioengineered bioregulators could be weaponized and function similar to toxins. They would cause disruption in normal body function and homeostasis. These agents would have the advantage that their effects would be immediate, they could escape detection and they could be more potent than traditional chemical agents and toxins.' (definition courtesy of the Vermont Health Alert Network, http://www.vdh.state.vt.us/common/define.htm)") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9c60).
