x_comment(x_properSubSituations,"An #$AsymmetricBinaryPredicate and a specialization of #$subSituations. This predicate relates situations to further situations which are their proper parts.\n<p>  \n<code>(#$properSubSituations SIT SUBSIT)</code> means that:<br>\n(1) the #$Situation <code>SUBSIT</code> is a part of the #$Situation <code>SIT</code> such that a complete description of <code>SIT</code> would have to involve a description of <code>SUBSIT</code>, and<br> \n(2)<code>SUBSIT</code> is not identical to <code>SIT</code> itself.  \n<p>\nFor example, a situation in which a car engine is non-functioning might have as a proper subsituation the situation of a carburetor being misconfigured.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9c73).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9c73,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9c73,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a9c73,2269).
