x_comment(x_ArtifactTypeByFunction,"A collection of collections; a subcollection of #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory. Instances of #$ArtifactTypeByFunction are mutually unique with respect to the full set of the primary intended uses of their instances. Examples include #$DessertFood and #$Sofa-PieceOfFurniture. Counter-examples include #$FountainPen (which has the same primary function as its genls, #$WritingPen) and #$FurniturePiece (specs of which have different primary uses). There may be cases where two instances of #$ArtifactTypeByFunction (PROD1 and PROD2) are related by (#$genls PROD1 PROD2); but this will only happen in cases where instances of PROD1 have some additional primary function(s) to those of PROD2. For example, the collections #$Sofa-PieceOfFurniture and #$SofaBed are both instances of #$ArtifactTypeByFunction, and (#$genls #$SofaBed #$Sofa-PieceOfFurniture) is true.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9c86).
