x_comment(x_facetBasedOnPredicateArg,"A #$TernaryPredicate that is used to assert that a special relation holds between a #$FacetingCollectionType and a #$Predicate -- that the former is \"based on\" the latter in a specific sense.\n<p>\nWhere <code>(#$facets-Generic COL FACET-COL)</code> and <code>PRED</code> is an n-place predicate, <code>(#$facetBasedOnPredicateArg FACET-COL PRED ARG)</code> means that for all <code>X</code> in <code>FACET-COL</code>, there is an ordered n-tuple <<code>Y<sub>1</sub>,...,Y<sub>n</sub></code>> such that, by the definition of <code>X</code>, for any <code>Z</code> in <code>COL</code>, <code>Z</code> is in <code>X</code> iff the result of replacing <code>Y<sub>ARG</sub></code> with <code>Z</code> in <code>(PRED Y<sub>1</sub>...Y<sub>n</sub>))</code> holds.\n<p>\nFor example, <code>(#$facetBasedOnPredicateArg #$WineTypeByColor #$uniformColorOfObject 1)</code> means that for all <code>WINE-TYPE</code> in #$WineTypeByColor, there is an ordered pair <<code>DUMMY, COLOR</code>> such that, by the definition of <code>WINE-TYPE</code>, for any <code>WINE</code> in #$Wine, <code>WINE</code> is in <code>WINE-TYPE</code> iff the result of replacing <code>DUMMY</code> with <code>WINE</code> in <code>(#$uniformColorOfObject DUMMY COLOR)</code>, i.e. <code>(#$uniformColorOfObject WINE COLOR)</code>, holds.\n<p>\nNote that it is also true that <code>(#$facetBasedOnPredicateArg #$PersonTypeByOccupation #$isa 1)</code>.  Indeed, <code>(#$facetBasedOnPredicateArg FACET-COL #$isa 1)</code> is trivially true for any <code>FACET-COL</code>, since the following is a logical truth:\n<pre>\n(#$forAll ?X \n  (#$thereExists ?Y \n    (#$forAll ?Z \n      (#$equiv (#$isa ?Z ?X) (#$isa ?Z ?Y)))))\n</pre>\nFor precisely this reason, there is no point in asserting that a facet is based on #$isa.\n<p>\nFor the very common special case in which <code>PRED</code> is a #$BinaryPredicate, see #$facetBasedOnBinaryPred and #$facetBasedOnBinaryPredInverse.  (Note that the meanings of these latter two predicates are much easier to understand.)  See also #$facetBasedOnTypePredicateArg.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9c91).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9c91,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9c91,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a9c91,2309).
