x_comment(x_properParts,"An #$AsymmetricBinaryPredicate and a specialization of #$parts. This predicate relates individuals to other individuals which are their proper parts (i.e., parts that are different from the whole). \n<p>\n<code>(#$properParts WHOLE PART)</code> means that:<br>\n(1) <code>PART</code> is a part of <code>WHOLE</code> (in the very broad sense in which #$parts is defined, meaning basically that a complete description of <code>WHOLE</code> would have to involve a description of <code>PART</code>), and<br> \n(2)<code>PART</code> is not identical to <code>WHOLE</code> itself.\n<p>\nThere is a range of useful specializations of this predicate.  For example, for individuals that are instances of #$Situation, see the more specific #$properSubSituations.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9c94).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9c94,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9c94,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
