x_comment(x_interArgEqualsIsa,"A quintary instance of #$InterArgEqualsIsaPredicate (q.v.). (#$interArgEqualsIsa RELN INDEP-ARGNUM INDEPENDENT-ARG DEP-ARGNUM DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when INDEPENDENT-ARG appears as the INDEP-ARGNUMth argument to RELN, a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the DEP-ARGNUMth argument must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL. That is, (RELN ... INDEPENDENT-ARG ...), where INDEPENDENT-ARG is the INDEP-ARGNUMth argument to RELN, is semantically well-formed only if the DEP-ARGNUMth argument is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.\n<p>\nFor example, (#$interArgIsa #$softwareParameterValueInSpecification 1 #$InferenceSentenceParameter 2 #$ELSentence-Assertible) means that (#$softwareParameterValueInSpecification #$InferenceSentenceParameter VALUE SPEC) is semantically well-formed only if VALUE is an instance of #$ELSentence-Assertible.\n<p>\nFor an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations. For similar to but less flexible predicates than #$interArgEqualsIsa, which have already-fixed positions for the independent and dependent arguments, see the ternary #$interArgEqualsIsa1-2 et al.  Cf. #$interArgIsa.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9ccc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9ccc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9ccc,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a9ccc,2506).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517a9ccc,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a9ccc,[]).
x_comment('x_interArgEqualsIsa1-3',"A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.). (#$interArgEqualsIsa1-3 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when INDEPENDENT-ARG appears as the first argument to RELN, a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the third argument must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, (RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG ARG2 ARG3 ...) is semantically well-formed only if ARG3 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.\n<p>\nFor an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations. See #$interArgEqualsIsa for a similar but more general predicate that is quintary, allowing the user to specify the positions of the independent and dependent arguments.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9ccd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9ccd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
