x_comment(x_penetrativeToxicityFor,"A predicate for indicating the level of toxicity a substance\nhas (under normal circumstances) when it penetrates (e.g. by an\narrow or insect stinger) the external surface of some instance\nof some type of #$BiologicalLivingObject.\n(#$penetrativeToxicityFor SUBSTANCE BLO-TYPE TOX) means that\nunder normal circumstances SUBSTANCE will have a toxicity\nlevel of TOX when it penetrates the surface layer\nof a #$BiologicalLivingObject BLO via,\ne.g., a sharp object or body part,\nwhere BLO is a typical instance of BLO-TYPE.\nSee also #$PenetrativeToxinType.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9cf2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9cf2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9cf2,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a9cf2,2609).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517a9cf2,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a9cf2,[]).
x_comment(x_PenetrativeToxinType,"A specialization of #$HazardousChemicalSubstanceType (q.v.).\nEach instance of #$PenetrativeToxinType is a collection\neach of whose instances is by default toxic when it\npenetrates the skin of some instance of #$HomoSapiens (say via an arrow, knife\nor insect stinger).  See #$penetrativeToxicityFor.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9cf3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9cf3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9cf3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a9cf3,2620).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517a9cf3,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a9cf3,[]).
x_comment(x_PenetratingOuterLayerOfBLO,"A specialization of #$PhysicalContactMakingEvent (q.v.).\nThis collection includes all #$PhysicalEvents in which\na \"sharp\" object (say a bullet, stinger, tooth or knife)\npenetrates the _outer_layer_ of a #$BiologicalLivingObject\n(in the case of an organism, this will often be its skin).\nSince this collection includes only the _penetration_\nof the outer layer, instances will usually be #$subEvents\nof, for example, stabbing or puncturing events.\nCommon examples include an animal being scraped by a\nknife or thorn, a woodpecker penetrating the bark of a tree or\na cell wall being penetrated.  See #$PenetratingOuterLayerOfBLOWithFn\n          and #$PenetratingOuterLayerOfBLOFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9cf4).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9cf4,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9cf4,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a9cf4,2625).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517a9cf4,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a9cf4,[]).
x_comment(x_PenetratingOuterLayerOfBLOWithFn,"An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction (q.v.).\n(#$PenetratingOuterLayerOfBLOWithFn SUB-TYPE)\ndenotes the collection of #$PhysicalEvents in which\nan instance of SUB-TYPE penetrates the outer layer\nof some #$BiologicalLivingObject.  Something\ncan penetrate a #$BiologicalLivingObject BLO\nby (at least) two means: (1) an object itself penetrates the\nBLO, as when a knife penetrates the skin of an\nanimal, or (2) an \"instrument\", such as a knife\nor insect stinger, is used to push or inject a\nsubstance through the outer layer of the BLO, as\nwhen a knife edge or point is coated with some\nsubstance.  In the latter case, both the\n\"instrument\" and the substance penetrate \nthe outer layer of the BLO.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9cf5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9cf5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9cf5,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a9cf5,2637).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517a9cf5,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a9cf5,[]).
x_comment(x_penetratingOuterLayerOfBLOWithType,"The corresponding predicate to #$PenetratingOuterLayerOfBLOWithFn.\n(#$penetratingOuterLayerOfBLOWithType PENE-EVT SUB-TYPE) means that\nPENE-EVT is the collection of events in which an instance of\nSUB-TYPE penetrates the surface layer of some #$BiologicalLivingObject\nvia a \"sharp\" object, like a bullet, knife, thorn or tooth.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9cf6).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9cf6,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
