x_comment(x_surfaceTensionAtTemperature,"(#$surfaceTensionAtTemperature SUBSTANCE TENSION\nTEMPERATURE) means that the specialization of LiquidTangibleThing,\nSUBSTANCE, has a surface tension of TENSION, usually measured in (PerFn Dyne (Centi Meter)), at the temperature specified by\nTEMPERATURE.  Surface tension is a force found in\n#$LiquidTangibleThings, exherted by the high concentration of molecules\nof the liquid upon the lower concentration of molecules at the\nsurface/air interface.  These conditions create an internal pressure\nthat restrains the liquid.  The higher the surface tension, the less\nthe liquid will flow.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9d68).
