x_comment(x_DietProgram,"A specialization of #$DevisedStructuredActivity.  The  collection of all \"programs\" that constrain the types or amounts of things one eats or drinks.  A given diet program might be designed for losing weight (see #$WeightLossProgram), gaining weight, lowering cholesteral, lowering blood pressure, increasing strength, or some other purpose.  Some diet programs are commonly followed for at least partly ethical or religious reasons (e.g. a vegan diet or a kosher diet).  When following a diet program, one is #$Dieting (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9d97).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9d97,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9d97,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
