xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a9dc6,[]).
x_comment(x_IntermittentlyFlawed,"The collection of all things that have a flaw  that does not always make itself apparent.  Instances of this collection are often functionally denoted using #$IntermittentlyFlawedFn.  In software, an intermittent bug is a bug that does not affect every execution of the software program, but which seems to occur 'every now and then'. Such bugs make related instances of #$DebuggingAComputerProgram harder rather than easier. Sometimes programmers just live with such bugs, rather than fixing them, if they strike infrequently.  See also the situation type, #$Flaw-Intermittent.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9dc7).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9dc7,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
