xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a9dd8,[]).
x_comment(x_colorPerceptionCategoryRangeOfType,"(#$colorPerceptionCategoryRangeOfType TYPE CATEGORY-1 CATEGORY-2) means that all\ninstances of TYPE, a specialization of #$SpatialThing-Localized, are instances of some collection COL, where COL is such that: 1) it is an instance of #$ColorPerceptionCategoryType, and 2) COL falls along a spectrum of color-relevant perceptual properties between CATEGORY-1 and CATEGORY-2.  For\nexample, (#$colorPerceptionCategoryRangeOfType #$Adamsite #$LightGreen-Color \n#$YellowColor) says that individual samples of adamsite be a\ncolor somewhere on the spectrum between light green and yellow.  Similarly,  (#$colorPerceptionCategoryRangeOfType #$NitrogenMustard-1 #$ColorlessThing #$PaleYellow-Color) says that samples of HN-1 will be somewhere along the spectrum of having no color to being pale yellow.  \"The spectrum\" here refers to an intuitive range directly between and including the two types; one can think of mixing two substances with those color-perception properties in various proportions to imagine what sorts of types would belong in the spectrum.  See also #$colorRangeOfType, which is restricted to #$Colors, and is tied to a particular direction around the color wheel, and thus for which argument order matters significantly.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9dd9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9dd9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9dd9,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
