x_comment(x_LevelOfStandardSubstanceFoundInSystem,"A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity, each instance of #$LevelOfSubstanceInSystem is a qualitative or quantitative \"measure\" of the level of some substance in a system where the substance is of a type _standardly_ found in the relevant system type.  For example, water is standardly found in mammals but caffeine is not.  So instances of this collection could be used to indicate the level of water in a mammal, but not the level of caffeine. To indicate the level of caffeine use #$LevelOfSubstanceInSystem together with a #$GenericValueFunction (and #$LevelOfSubstanceTypeInSysTypeFn).") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9de3).
