x_comment('x_Goodness-Generic',"A linear-ordered specialization of #$EvaluativeQuantity whose instances reflect assessments of the relative worth of a particular thing.  Such assessments are usually made in relation to some (often implicit) standard held by the assessor; this standard might purport to measure a thing's usefulness, or its value, or its moral worth, or its beauty, or something else.  #$Goodness-Generic is thus \"generic\" with respect to these various categories of worth.  Particular instances of this collection can be obtained via the various #$GenericValueFunctions.  Note: If a particular dimension of goodness is sought you should use one of the specializations of this collection; e.g. #$Goodness-Moral, #$Goodness-Functional. ") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9df0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9df0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
