x_comment('x_detectsType-Genl',"(#$detectsType-Genl DEVICE-TYPE THING-TYPE) means that an\ninstance of DEVICE-TYPE can be used to detect instances of\nTHING-TYPE. More precisely, it means that an instance of DEVICE-TYPE\ncan be used to decide whether or not something is an instance of some\ncollection that is (i) a generalization of THING-TYPE and (ii) a\nspecialization of some type that is interesting in the current context\nwith respect to detection. In other words, it means that there are\nsome types GEN-TYPE and INTERMEDIATE-TYPE such that\n(#$interestingForRoleInType GEN-TYPE #$typeDetected #$DetectingSomething)\nand (#$genls THING-TYPE INTERMEDIATE-TYPE) and (#$genls INTERMEDIATE-TYPE\nGEN-TYPE) and (#$detectsType-Exact DEVICE-TYPE INTERMEDIATE-TYPE).") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9e0d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9e0d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
