x_comment('x_SituationTypeRelation-Conditional',"#$SituationTypeRelation-Conditional is a sub-collection of #$SituationTypeRelation.  Assertions using these relations entail conditional relations among a specializations of #$Situation and their sub-situation types, actor types, and roles. For example, (#$inheritRolePlayers-SubSitTypeToSubSitType SITTYPE ROLE1 SUBSITTYPE1 ROLE2 SUBSITTYPE2) states that in any instance of SITTYPE, any actor playing ROLE1 in an instance of SUBSITTYPE1 will also play role ROLE2 in the instance of SUBSITTYPE2. Such a statement makes no assertion regarding the existence of such an actor. Contrast this collection with #$SituationTypeRelation-Existential and #$SituationTypeRelation-NonEssential.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9e7a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9e7a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9e7a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a9e7a,3339).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517a9e7a,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a9e7a,[]).
x_comment('x_SituationTypeRelation-NonEssential',"#$SituationTypeRelation-NonEssential is a sub-collection of #$SituationTypeRelation.  Assertions using these relations represent features of a specialization of #$Situation that are not entailed by a situation properly instantiating it, but which are sufficiently common or important to be worth representing.  For instance, an assertion of the form (#$candidateProperSubSituationTypes SITTYPE SUBSITTYPE) states that instances of SITTYPE typically have a sub-situation of type SUBSITTYPE, though possession of this property is not essential to their membership in the collection SITTYPE. Contrast this collection with #$SituationTypeRelation-Existential.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9e7b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9e7b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9e7b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a9e7b,3340).
