x_comment(x_followingIntervalTypes,"A binary #$TemporalPredicate that relates types of #$TimeIntervals.  (#$followingIntervalTypes EARLIER-TYPE LATER-TYPE) means that every instance of EARLIER-TYPE is followed by (see #$startsAfterEndingOf) some instance of LATER-TYPE, and every instance of LATER-TYPE is preceded by some instance of EARLIER-TYPE.\n<p>\nNote that instances of EARLIER-TYPE need _not_ immediately precede (see #$contiguousAfter) instances of LATER-TYPE.  For example,  (#$followingIntervalTypes #$Saturday #$Sunday) holds, and so does (#$followingIntervalTypes #$Saturday #$Tuesday).   For a similar predicate that does entail immediate temporal succession, see the specialization #$succeedingIntervalType.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9e9a).
