x_comment('x_locatedAtPoint-SurfGeog-FromGIS',"(#$locatedAtPoint-SurfGeog-FromGIS OBJECT GEO-POINT) means\nthat according to some #$GeographicInformationSystem from which #$Cyc\nis gathering information: OBJECT, an instance of\nSpatialThing-Localized, is geographically located at GEO-POINT on the\ngeographical surface of reference. This relation is used to indicate\nthat extended spatial things located in a geography have their\ngeographical location including some precise point. This relation is\nused only for location information gathered from a GIS. For non-GIS use, see the more general #$locatedAtPoint-SurfaceGeographical.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9ea4).
