x_comment(x_InternationalUnitOfMeasure,"An instance of #$UnitOfMeasureTypeBySystem and a specialization of #$UnitOfMeasure.  Each instance of #$InternationalUnitOfMeasure is a #$UnitOfMeasure that is or was standardly (though not necessarily commonly--see #$InternationalUnitOfMeasure-Common) used in \"metric\" countries (i.e. countries that use the metric system, i.e. most countries in the world).  Note that some units of measure, e.g. #$SecondsDuration, #$Barrel-UnitOfVolume, #$Watt, and #$Byte, are instances of both #$InternationalUnitOfMeasure and #$USUnitOfMeasure.  (See #$UniversalUnitOfMeasure.)  Two important specializations of #$InternationalUnitOfMeasure are #$MetricUnitOfMeasure and #$SIUnitOfMeasure (qq.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9eaf).
