x_comment(x_DeReVersionFn,"A #$PredicateDenotingFunction used to convert \"de dicto\" cognitive attitude predicates (see #$PropositionalAttitudeSlot) into their \"de re\" counterparts (see #$DeReAttitudePredicate).  (#$DeReVersionFn PROP-ATT-SLOT) is the cognitive attitude predicate DE-RE-PRED that is the ternary \"de re version\" of the binary PROP-ATT-SLOT.  The extensions (see #$relationExtension) of PROP-ATT-SLOT and DE-RE-PRED are correlated roughly as follows.  (i) If (PROP-ATT-SLOT AGENT SENT) holds, and the Nth-place term within SENT denotes something, then (DE-RE-PRED AGENT SENT N) holds.  (ii) If (DE-RE-PRED AGENT SENT N) holds, then there must be some term NEWTERM that is codenoting (and possibly identical) with the Nth-place term OLDTERM within SENT such that (PROP-ATT-SLOT AGENT SENT-PRIME) holds, where SENT-PRIME is the result of replacing OLDTERM with NEWTERM in the Nth-place of SENT.  For example, (#$DeReVersionFn #$beliefs) is #$believesOfArg.  An agent's having a de dicto belief with respect to a given sentence entails her having analogous de re beliefs regarding each thing denoted by some constituent of that sentence; and an agent's having a de re belief regarding a given thing entails her having some analogous de dicto belief with respect to a sentence having an immediate constituent that denotes that thing.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9ec3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9ec3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
