x_comment(x_ScalarDenotingFunction,"A specialization of #$IndividualDenotingFunction.  Each instance of #$ScalarDenotingFunction is a function that returns some instance of #$ScalarInterval as its value, for any (sequence of) thing(s) in its domain (see #$relationDomain) taken as argument(s). Thus (e.g.) any function that always returns a real number is a scalar-denoting function.  There are no restrictions on what types of things a scalar-returning function can have in its domain. Notable specializations of this function-type are #$MathematicalFunctionOnScalars and #$UnitOfMeasure.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9edc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9edc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9edc,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
