x_comment(x_hasDiplomaticImmunityIn,"(#$hasDiplomaticImmunityIn PERSON COUNTRY) means that PERSON has diplomatic immunity in COUNTRY. Persons who have diplomatic immunity are, by virtue of their positions in the diplomatic corps of a country, not subject to arrest by authorities of the country to which they are posted. Moreover, they are not subject to search or seizure of their possessions, nor are they obliged to pay taxes in the host state nor to fulfil military obligations. Persons with diplomatic immunity in a host state also enjoy that status in intermediate states through which they travel. diplomatic immunity is extended to diplomatic couriers and those who carry a diplomatic bag. diplomats thereby have diplomatic immunity. Generally, members of diplomats' immediate families have diplomatic immunity, even though they themselves are not diplomats.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9ef5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9ef5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
