x_comment(x_associatedActorSlotList,"An instance of #$BinaryPredicate. (#$associatedActorSlotList EVENT-PRED SLOT-LIST) means that SLOT-LIST is a list of #$ActorSlots conceptually associated with the argument places of EVENT-PRED, in the following sense: Suppose (EVENT-PRED ARG-1 ARG-2 ... ARG-N) is true. Then, were one to represent the same fact within the Davidsonian framework, i.e., by asserting the existence of a particular event of type COLL (where COLL is the #$correspondingCycCollection for EVENT-PRED), ARG-K would play in the event the role expressed by SLOT-K (where SLOT-K is the Kth member of SLOT-LIST), for 1 <= K <= N.  See also the related predicate #$associateSlotInArg.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9f18).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9f18,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9f18,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
