xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a9f19,[]).
x_comment(x_regionTypeHasSurfaceLevelInNumberOfDirections,"An instance of #$TernaryPredicate, used to describe the surface level of the ground on each of the four 'sides' of a  #$GeographicalRegion. (The number 4 is a simplifying assumption used to make knowledge aquisition and representation easier.) (#$regionTypeHasSurfaceLevelInNumberOfDirections REGION-TYPE LEVEL NUM-SIDES) means that NUM-SIDES of REGION-TYPE have are LEVEL. For example, (#$regionTypeHasSurfaceLevelInNumberOfDirections Hill TerrainLowGround 4) means that hills have low ground in (all) four directions. To specify how many sides that share this ground level are adjacent, use #$regionTypeHasSurfaceLevelInNumberOfAdjacentDirections. Note that this predicate not only oversimplifies the number of sides of a type of terrain, but also ignores the point of view and the slope. For example, a hill has low ground on all sides from the point of view of the hilltop, but not from the point of view of the bottom of the hill. This predicate expects that one is refering to the 'most interesting' part of the terrain feature (eg the hilltop of a hill, the low middle part of a valley, the seat part of a saddle, etc.). To also specify the point of view and to be more specific about slopes, see #$regionTypeSlopeOfSidesFromPoint and #$regionTypeSlopeOfAdjacentSidesFromPoint. To specify slopes at an instance level, see #$regionSlopeOfSidesFromPoint and #$regionSlopeOfAdjacentSidesFromPoint.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9f1a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9f1a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9f1a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517a9f1a,3607).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517a9f1a,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517a9f1a,[]).
x_comment(x_regionTypeHasSurfaceLevelInNumberOfAdjacentDirections,"(#$regionTypeHasSurfaceLevelInNumberOfAdjacentDirections REGION-TYPE LEVEL NUM-SIDES) means that NUM-SIDES of REGION-TYPE that have a LEVEL kind of slope are adjacent to one another. For example, (#$regionTypeHasSurfaceLevelInNumberOfAdjacentDirections Saddle #$TerrainLowGround 0) means that, of the total number of low ground sides of a saddle, none of them are adjacent. Similarly, (#$regionTypeHasSurfaceLevelInNumberOfAdjacentDirections Saddle #$TerrainHighGround 0) means that, of the total number of high ground sides of a saddle, none of them are adjacent. Thus, if there are a total of two high ground and two low ground sides of a saddle, then the two similarly sloping sides are across from one another. To specify the total number of sides that are LEVEL, see #$regionTypeHasSurfaceLevelInNumberOfDirections. To specify slopes at an instance level, see #$regionSlopeOfSidesFromPoint and #$regionSlopeOfAdjacentSidesFromPoint.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9f1b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9f1b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9f1b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
