x_comment(x_MediumToHighAmountFn,"A #$GenericValueFunction (q.v.) that takes a given #$TotallyOrderedQuantityType to a #$GenericQuantity of that type. In a given context, <code>(#$MediumToHighAmountFn QUANTTYPE)</code> is the properly interval-like quantity (and instance) of <code>QUANTTYPE</code> that is considered a <i>medium-to-high amount</i> of <code>QUANTTYPE</code> with respect to that context.\n<p>\nFor example, (#$MediumToHighAmountFn #$Happiness) is the range from medium to high happiness.  It is more (see #$followingValue) than (#$LowAmountFn #$Happiness) and less than (#$VeryHighAmountFn #$Happiness).\n<p>\nSee also the corresponding predicate #$mediumToHighAmountOf.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9f35).
