x_comment(x_LowToMediumAmountFn,"A #$GenericValueFunction (q.v.) that takes a given #$TotallyOrderedQuantityType to a #$GenericQuantity of that type.  In a given context, <code>(#$LowToMediumAmountFn QUANTTYPE)</code> is the properly interval-like quantity (and instance) of <code>QUANTTYPE</code> that is considered a <i>low-to-medium amount</i> of <code>QUANTTYPE</code> with respect to that context.\n<p>\nFor example, (#$LowToMediumAmountFn #$Happiness) is the range from low to medium happiness.  It is more (see #$followingValue) than (#$VeryLowAmountFn #$Happiness) and less than (#$HighAmountFn #$Happiness) .\n<p>\nSee also the corresponding predicate #$lowToMediumAmountOf.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9f36).
