x_comment(x_tacticalTerrainTypeFromPosition,"(#$tacticalTerrainTypeFromPosition TERRAIN-TYPE TACTIC-TYPE LOCATIONAL-PRED) means that instances of TERRAIN-TYPE can often act as a type of TACTIC-TYPE for objects holding a LOCATIONAL-PRED relation to them. For example, (#$tacticalTerrainTypeFromPosition #$Hill #$ObservationFacilitatingTerrain #$on-Physical) means that observation (in general) done by objects that are #$on-Physical instances of #$Hill will often be facilitated because they are on the hill. Similarly one might say (#$tacticalTerrainTypeFromPosition #$Hill #$ObservationLimitingTerrain #$near), meaning that observation (in general) done by objects that are #$near instances of #$Hill will often be limited because they are near the hill. Also see #$tacticalTerrainTypeFromPositionForUnitType and #$tacticalTerrainFromPositionForUnitType.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9f46).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9f46,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
