x_comment(x_tacticalTerrainTypeFromPositionForUnitType,"(#$tacticalTerrainTypeFromPositionForUnitType TERRAIN-TYPE TACTIC-TYPE LOCATIONAL-PRED UNIT-TYPE) means that TERRAIN-TYPE is a type of TACTIC-TYPE for instances of UNIT-TYPE when they are located LOCATIONAL-PRED in relation to an instance of TERRAIN-TYPE. For example, (#$tacticalTerrainFromPositionForUnitType #$Hill #$ObservationFacilitatingTerrain #$on-Physical #$InfantryUnit-MilitarySpecialty) says that instances of #$Hill facilitate observation for instances of #$InfantryUnit-MilitarySpecialty when they are on them. Also see #$tacticalTerrainFromPositionForUnitType and #$tacticalTerrainTypeFromPosition.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9f47).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9f47,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
