x_comment(x_ScalarProperInterval,"A specialization of #$ScalarInterval.  Each instance of #$ScalarProperInterval is a proper interval or range of numbers or quantities, as opposed to a single number or quantity (cf. #$ScalarPointValue).\n<p>\nWhen a #$UnitOfMeasure is applied to a <i>pair</i> of distinct #$Number-Generals, the result is a #$Quantity that is an instance of #$ScalarProperInterval.  For example, (#$Meter 3 5) is the distance \"between 3 and 5 meters (inclusive)\" and (#$SecondsDuration  10 100) is  the duration \"between 10 and 100 seconds (inclusive)\".\n<p>\nAnother sort of scalar proper interval is any instance of the specialization #$OrderOfMagnitudeInterval.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9f58).
