x_comment(x_atLeastPartiallyResponsibleFor,"(#$atLeastPartiallyResponsibleFor AGT SIT) holds just in case AGT performed some deliberate actions prior to SIT that in some way contributed to SIT's occurrence.  This notion is somewhat weaker than with #$responsibleFor.  The latter's holding requires that SIT would not have occurred had AGT done something other than the action which was instrumental in bringing about SIT (see the #$comment on #$responsibleFor).  On the other hand, if an agent is #$atLeastPartiallyResponsibleFor SIT, it doesn't entail that their action was necessary for the occurrence of SIT.  Rather, it means that SIT's occurence was made easier/more probable.  One class of paradigm cases of partial responsibility in the sense defined are found in one agent's generic financial support of another agent's activities.  For example, an organization that financially supports a terrorist can be said to be #$atLeastPartiallyResponsibleFor that terrorist's actions in that the support made it more probable that the terrorist's actions would be successful.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9f8f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517a9f8f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517a9f8f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
