x_comment(x_termMentionedInProgram,"(#$termMentionedInProgram TERM PROGRAM) means that the #$CycLIndexedTerm TERM is mentioned in the code of the  #$ComputerProgram-CW PROGRAM.  For example, (#$termMentionedInProgram  #$isa (#$CycVersionWithFeatureSetSystemAndKBFn (#$TheSet #$Cyc-Time-CycProgramFeature #$Cyc-Date-CycProgramFeature) \"1.3345\" (#$CycKB 694))) means that \"#$isa\" is mentioned in the Cyc program built with just #$Cyc-Time-CycProgramFeature and #$Cyc-Date-CycProgramFeature from Cyc systemn number 1.3345 and Cyc KB 694.  Note that the first argument of this predicate is \"quoted\"; thus it is the term itself in the first argument position that is mentioned in the code -- it is not the denotation of the term that is mentioned in the code.") :- x_cid(a65b16517a9fe7).
