x_comment(x_assertedTermSetSentences,"(#$assertedTermSetSentences SET-OF-TERMS SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE has been asserted to the Cyc Knowledge Base (and is thus a  #$CycLAssertion) and that each of the #$CycLTerms in SET-OF-TERMS is mentioned in SENTENCE.  More precisely, and assuming the #$assertedTermSetSentences formula contains no free variables (and \nis thus a \"ground atomic formula\" or \"GAF\"): each of the CycL terms in the set which immediately follows the constant `#$assertedTermSentences' in the formula occurs in SENTENCE.  For example, (#$assertedTermSetSentences (#$TheSet #$France #$Germany) (#$bordersOn #$France #$Germany)) holds.  See also #$assertedTermSentences, #$assertedSentence and #$assertedPredicateArg for related predicates about assertions.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa03b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa03b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
