x_comment(x_rolesMapToProgramFunctionArgs,"(#$rolesMapToProgramFunctionArgs EVENT-TYPE SLOT PROG-FUNCTION NUM) means that in order to bring about an instance of EVENT-TYPE via the #$ProgramFunction PROG-FUNCTION, the arg2 value of the appropriate assertion using SLOT must occur as the NUM argument to PROG-FUNCTION.  For example, (#$rolesMapToProgramFunctionArgs  #$SingleEMailSending #$eMailSendingTextSlot (#$ProgramFunctionFn \"mail-message\" (#$CycorpSysdclFileFn \"mail-utilities.lisp\")) 3) means that to bring about an instance INST of #$SingleEMailSending, if (#$eMailSendingTextSlot INST TEXT) holds, then TEXT must be passed to argument 3 of the function mail-message defined in the mail-utilities.lisp file of the Cycorp sysdcl.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa05a).
