x_comment('x_BarrierSituation-PhysicalForce',"A collection of individual\nsituations. Each #$BarrierSituation-PhysicalForce consists of an\narrangement of some #$Path-Customary PATH, some #$PartiallyTangible\nthing(s) BLOCKER1, BLOCKER2, . . . and some #$PartiallyTangible\nthings(s) BLOCKED1, BLOCKED2, . . .. such that BLOCKED1, BLOCKED2,\n. . . could potentially move along PATH, were BLOCKER1, BLOCKER2,\n. . . not physically in contact with the blocked thing(s) in a way\nthat prevents such movement. Examples include a #$Dam blocking the\nflow of water and a person #$RestrainingSomeone in a\n#$WrestlingHold. To represent cases in which a path is effectively\nblocked by the mere likelihood of such physical contact -- that is,\nthe blocking object acts as a deterrent (such as a Fence keeping Cows\nin a pasture), see BarrierSituation-Deterrent. Note that\n#$BarrierSituation-PhysicalForce is #$not #$disjointWith\n#$BarrierSituation-Deterrent.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa080).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa080,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa080,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa080,4309).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa080,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa080,[]).
x_comment('x_BarrierSituation-Deterrent',"A collection of individual\nsituations. Each #$BarrierSituation-Deterrent consists of an\narrangement of some #$Path-Customary PATH, some #$PartiallyTangible\nthing(s) BLOCKER1, BLOCKER2, . . . and some #$PartiallyTangible\nthings(s) BLOCKED1, BLOCKED2, . . .. such that BLOCKED1, BLOCKED2,\n. . . could potentially move along PATH, were BLOCKER1, BLOCKER2,\n. . . not in the way. It is important that actual movement along PATH\nbe prevented, at least in part, by the deterrent effect of the\nblocking object(s).  That is, at least some of the blocked objects\nshould be blocked by the likelihood of being physically prevented from\nmoving, without having to come in contact with the blocking object(s)\nthemselves.  Examples include a #$Fence keeping #$Cows in a pasture,\nand an #$Obstacle blocking a #$Roadway. Objects whose movement is\nbeing blocked in this way may occassionally come into physical contact\nwith the blocking object (as a #$Cow bumping into, or pushing against,\na #$Fence), but the situation will be an instance of\n#$BarrierSituation-Deterrent just in case the blocking is at least\npartially accomplished by deterrence. To represent cases in which a\npath is blocked by physical force (such as a #$Dam blocking the flow\nof water), see #$BarrierSituation-PhysicalForce. Note that\n#$BarrierSituation-Deterrent is #$not #$disjointWith\n#$BarrierSituation-PhysicalForce.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa081).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa081,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
