x_comment(x_termForTemplatePositions,"(#$termForTemplatePositions TERM TEMPLATE-TYPE LIST) means that in the context of using TEMPLATE-TYPE, TERM is passed to positions in templates in a manner described by LIST, according to the following convention.  LIST is a list of sub-lists, each of which has a template TEMPLATE as a first argument and some non-zero number of #$FormulaArgPositions as subsequent elements.  In each sub-list, the #$FormulaArgPositions indicate where to pass TERM as a value to arguments to TEMPLATE.  For example, the following formula would hold in the context in which one was adding a scene to a #$BrushingTeeth script with #$SceneInScriptedEventType-TopicType:\n<p>\n(#$termForTemplatePositions #$BrushingTeeth\n#$SceneInScriptedEventType-TopicType\n(#$TheList\n(#$TheList\n#$SceneActorTypesTemplate\n(#$FormulaArgPositionFn 1))\n(#$TheList\n#$SceneRelatedToScriptTemplate\n(#$FormulaArgPositionFn 1))\n(#$TheList\n#$ScriptQuasiTemporalOrderingToOtherSceneTemplate\n(#$FormulaArgPositionFn 1))\n(#$TheList\n#$ScriptQuasiTemporalOrderingFromOtherSceneTemplate\n(#$FormulaArgPositionFn 1)))).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa08a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa08a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa08a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa08a,4373).
