x_comment(x_orthogonalInMt,"An instance of #$TernaryPredicate.  (#$orthogonalInMt MT COL1 COL2) means that it is true in the #$Microtheory MT that the #$Collection COL1 is orthogonal with (i.e. logically independent of) the #$Collection COL2.  More precisely, (#$orthogonalInMt MT COL1 COL2) means that (1) (#$orthogonalityCandidates COL1 COL2) is true in MT; and (2) each of the following sentences is such that it is true in some (not necessarily reified) specMt of MT: (a) (#$thereExists ?THING (#$isa ?THING (#$CollectionIntersection2Fn COL1 COL2))); (b) (#$thereExists ?THING (#$isa ?THING (#$CollectionDifferenceFn COL1 COL2))); (c) (#$thereExists ?THING (#$isa ?THING (#$CollectionDifferenceFn COL2 COL1))).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa08c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa08c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
