x_comment(x_orthogonalSetsOrCollections,"<code>(#$orthogonalSetsOrCollections SETORCOL1 SETORCOL2)</code> means that each of <code>SETORCOL1</code> and <code>SETORCOL2</code> has at least one element that the other lacks, and that at least one thing is an element of both collections.  It thus entails that all of the following are true: \n<p>\n(1) <code>(#$some SETORCOLL1 SETORCOLL2)</code>; \n<br>\n(2) <code>(#$not (#$subsetOf SETORCOLL1 SETORCOLL2))</code>; \n<br>\n(3) <code>(#$not (#$subsetOf SETORCOLL2 SETORCOLL1))</code>.  \n<p>\nUnlike #$orthogonalityCandidates (q.v.), #$orthogonalSetsOrCollections is assertible, and can hold of sets as well as collections.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa0a6).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa0a6,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
