x_comment(x_Moratorium,"A specialization of #$Inaction (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Moratorium is a #$Situation of there being in effect a legally authorized period of delay (see #$moratoriumPeriod) in the performance of a certain legal obligation or the payment of a certain debt (see #$moratoriumOn).\n<p>\nWhere <code>(#$moratoriumOn MORATORIUM OBLIGATION)</code> and <code>(#$moratoriumPeriod MORATORIUM PERIOD)</code>, <code>MORATORIUM</code> is <i>precisely</i> the situation such that those two statements (and anything logically or legally entailed by them) hold -- no more and no less.  It follows from this that <code>OBLIGATION</code>'s #$obligatedAgents (q.v.) are not legally required to fulfill <code>OBLIGATION</code> during <code>PERIOD</code>.  (It does <i>not</i> follow that the agents are <i>prohibited</i> from fulfilling <code>OBLIGATION</code> during <code>PERIOD</code>, although that might sometimes be the case.)  The #$temporalExtent of <code>MORATORIUM</code> is the #$TimeInterval <code>PERIOD</code> itself.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa0ac).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa0ac,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
