x_comment(x_levelOfExposureToSubstanceTypeViaRoute,"(#$levelOfExposureToSubstanceTypeViaRoute OBJECT STUFF-TYPE ROUTE-TYPE LEVEL) says that OBJECT is exposed to instances of STUFF-TYPE via the exposure route ROUTE-TYPE to the degree expressed by LEVEL.  For example, (#$levelOfExposureToSubstanceTypeViaRoute #$BobTheAdult CigaretteSmoke #$Inhaling #$veryHighAmountOf) says that Bob is exposed to cigarette smoke via inhalation to a high degree.  Despite the occurrence of a spec of #$Event in the arg3, this predicate is an instance of #$NonDavidsonianPredicate, intended to be used with temporal qualification, to talk about exposure without explicitly having to reify an exposure event.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa0f8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa0f8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
