x_comment(x_TemporallyQualifiableRolePredicate,"The intersection of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation and #$Role.  Each instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRolePredicate is a predicate that relates an instance of #$Situation to some individual that plays some role in that situation.  Since some roles are played by multiple individuals during the course of some situation, these predicates let you specify the times at which certain individuals play certain roles via our temporal qualification framework.  Often the instances of this collection will be \"present tense\" versions of non-temporally qualifiable role predicates.  For instance, #$actingInDramaticPerformance is an instance of this collection and (#$actingInDramaticPerformance PERF ACTOR)<MT T P> holds just in case during the time interval T ACTOR is playing the #$castMembers role in PERF.  In general, (TQ-ROLE-PRED SITUATION ROLE-PLAYER)<MT TIME P> entails that SITUATION and TIME, at the very least, intersect. ") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa0fa).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa0fa,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
