x_comment(x_cycLQueryInputBindings,"(#$cycLQueryInputBindings QUERY-EVENT BINDING) means that the\nvariable-value pair specified by BINDING is used to bind one of the\nvariables in the query run during QUERY-EVENT.  For example, the\nassertion (#$cycLQueryInputBindings TouristQueryEvent001\n(#$ELInferenceBindingFn ?THING1 #$WestminsterAbbeyCathedral-London))\nstates that for a particular #$CycQueryRunning event called\nTouristQueryEvent001, the variable ?THING1 in the query formula should\nbe bound to the term #$WestminsterAbbeyCathedral-London. So, for\nexample, if the relevant formula for this event is\n(#$lineOfSight-ObjectToObject ?THING1 ?THING2), the resulting query to\nbe run is (#$lineOfSight-ObjectToObject\n#$WestminsterAbbeyCathedral-London ?THING2) -- a query perhaps to\ndiscover what things can be seen from Westminster Abbey.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa108).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa108,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
