x_comment(x_taskCorrespondsToBugReport,"An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalPredicate. (#$taskCorrespondsToBugReport TASK BUG-REPORT) says that TASK is the task derivable from the contents of the #$BugReport BUG-REPORT. In particular, TASK is the task of correcting whatever shortcoming or problem that BUG-REPORT describes.  For example, if BUG-REPORT describes the sudden failure of a particular KBContent test, TASK would therefore be the task of getting this test working again.  Many sub-tasks might be derivable from this (e.g., test the KBContent test code, improve the ontology in the relevant area, etc.), but these can't be functionally derived from BUG-REPORT, and so don't stand in the #$taskCorrespondsToBugReport relationship to BUG-REPORT.  See aslo #$TaskFromBugReportFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa132).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa132,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
