x_comment(x_GenlPredsPreservingFunction,"A specialization of #$PredicateDenotingFunction (q.v.).  Each instance FUNC of #$GenlPredsPreservingFunction is a predicate-denoting function such that whenever #$genlPreds holds between successive arguments (in some particular argument-place) to FUNC, it holds between the corresponding successive values as well.  That is, (#$preservesGenlPredsInArg FUNC N) holds for some N.\n<p>\nMore precisely, a function FUNC is a #$GenlPredsPreservingFunction if and only if it has an argument-place (say the Nth) such that the following hold:\n<p>\n(i) (#$resultIsa FUNC #$Predicate)\n<p>\n(ii) (#$argIsa FUNC N #$Predicate)\n<p>\n(iii) if (#$genlPreds SPEC-PRED GENL-PRED) holds and FUNC is defined for both <... SPEC-PRED ...> and <... GENL-PRED ...> (where SPEC-PRED and GENL-PRED are the respective Nth items in these otherwise identical sequences), then (#$genlPreds (FUNC ... SPEC-PRED ...) (FUNC ... GENL-PRED ...)) holds.\n<p>\nFor example, #$BinaryRoleTypePredFn is an instance of #$GenlPredsPreservingFunction.  Just as #$primaryObjectMoving (the relation that holds between an event and the primary object moving in it) is a specialization of #$objectMoving (the relation that holds between an event and objects moving in it), (#$BinaryRoleTypePredFn #$primaryObjectMoving) (the relation that holds between an event and the type of primary object moving in it) is a specialization of (#$BinaryRoleTypePredFn #$objectMoving) (the relation that holds between an event and the type of any object moving in it).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa147).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa147,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa147,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa147,4747).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa147,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa147,[]).
