xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa1a0,[]).
x_comment(x_educationInFieldSufficientForActType,"(#$educationInFieldSufficientForActType EDU-LEVEL FIELD ACT-TYPE) holds just in case someone with an education level of EDU-LEVEL who is competent in FIELD would be capable of learning to (#$capableOfLearningTo) perform acts of ACT-TYPE.  This predicate states that anyone with the EDU-LEVEL and competence FIELD, as a default, would likely have the knowledge to perform acts of ACT-TYPE or could easily obtain that knowledge.  This entails that the basic procedures for performing acts of ACT-TYPE are known to that person or could easily be grasped with a minimal to moderate amount of study.  This predicate captures a sufficient condition on the educational requirements for performing act types, it doesn't state anything about further skills or materials that may be necessary to perform act of type ACT-TYPE. So, this does not entail that anyone with that education level and competence in the field would be able in some stronger sense to perform acts of that type.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa1a1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa1a1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa1a1,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa1a1,4860).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa1a1,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa1a1,[]).
