x_comment(x_NonAbducibleThing,"The collection #$NonAbducibleThing is a sub-collection of \n#$Thing.  Abductive inferences sometimes involve hypothesizing the \nexistence of entities as part of the explanation of some assertion or set \nof assertions. Cyc will not hypothesize the existence of instances of \n#$NonAbducibleThing.  Roughly, abductive inferences consume conceptual / \ntheoretical knowledge rather than produce it.  So, #$SecondOrderCollection \nis a sub-collection of #$NonAbducibleThing because Cyc should be employing \nexisting knowledge of instances of #$SecondOrderCollection rather than \nhypothesizing new instances.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa1cd).
