x_comment(x_notAbducibleWRTTypeInArg,"An assertion of the form (#$notAbducibleWRTTypeInArg PRED TYPE \nN) states that abductive inferences should not seek to posit hypothetical \nvalues for the other arguments of PRED when an instance of TYPE fills the \nPRED's Nth argument position.  Abductive inferences sometimes involving \nhypothesizing the existence of states of affairs.  Abductive inferences \noften seek to explain an assertion or set of assertions by hypothesizing \nthe truth of other assertions.  However, we wish to restrict the kinds of \nassertions which Cyc will hypothesize such that Cyc does not hypothesize \nnew theoretical or conceptual knowledge, or even contingent states of \naffairs that are quite rigidly constructed in the actual world.  Thus, the \nassertion (#$notAbducibleWRTValueInArg #$cityInState #$State-UnitedStates \n1) would prevent the Cyc inference engine from hypothesizing the existence \nof unknown cities within any of the states of the \n#$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa1d1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa1d1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
