xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa1d1,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa1d1,[]).
x_comment(x_notAbducibleWRTValueInArg,"An assertion of the form (#$notAbducibleWRTValueInArg PRED THING \nN) states that abductive inferences should not seek to posit hypothetical \nvalues for the other arguments of PRED when THING fills the PRED's Nth \nargument position.  Abductive inferences sometimes involving hypothesizing \nthe existence of states of affairs.  Abductive inferences often seek to \nexplain an assertion or set of assertions by hypothesizing the truth of \nother assertions.  However, we wish to restrict the kinds of assertions \nwhich Cyc will hypothesize such that Cyc does not hypothesize new \ntheoretical or conceptual knowledge, or even contingent states of affairs \nthat are quite rigidly constructed in the actual world.  Thus, the \nassertion (#$notAbducibleWRTValueInArg #$cityInState #$NewYork-State 1) \nwould prevent the Cyc inference engine from hypothesizing the existence of \nunknown cities within the state of New York.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa1d2).
