x_comment('x_facets-NearCovering',"A #$TaxonomicSlotForCollections and a specialization of #$facets-Generic (q.v.).  (#$facets-NearCovering COL COLTYPE) means that COLTYPE corresponds to one (non-arbitrary) way of dividing  most or all of COL into (not necessarily disjoint) subcollections.  The instances of COLTYPE are all \"the same sort\" of subcollection of COL.  For example, #$PersonTypeByOccupation is a near-covering (but not covering) faceting of #$Person: not every instance of #$Person will be an instance of an instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation, but it is expected that *most* will be.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa1e4).
