x_comment(x_scopedFormulaArg,"A binary #$MetaRelation that relates a #$ScopingRelation (q.v.) to an integer indicating the argument-place of the former that takes a CycL formula.  (#$scopedFormulaArg RELN N) means that RELN's Nth argument is a CycL formula FORM such that any free occurrences in FORM of the CycL variable(s) VAR (VAR1...VARm) serving as the corresponding \"scoping\" argument to RELN is (are) bound with respect to the entire RELN-based formula.  For example, given that (#$scopingArg #$thereExists 1) holds, (#$scopedFormulaArg #$thereExists 2) entails that in the sentence\n<p>\n<pre>\n  (#$thereExists ?KIT\n    (#$and\n      (#$isa ?KIT #$Cat)\n      (#$isa ?KIT #$BlackColor)))\n</pre>\n<p>\nthe occurrences of the variable '?KIT' free in the conjunction are bound by the quantifier #$thereExists.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa1f2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa1f2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa1f2,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
