x_comment(x_Topic,"An instance of #$FacetingCollectionType and a specialization of #$ConventionalClassificationType.  Each instance of #$Topic is a collection of #$Things falling under a common topic.  #$Topic is neither a strict [#$facets-Strict] nor a covering [#$facets-Covering] faceting of #$Thing: many #$Things may be instances of no #$Topic, or of multiple #$Topics.  IMPORTANT: Something's falling under a particular topic is purely a matter of convention: we simply *stipulate* that certain things fall under certain topics when we find it useful to do so, e.g. for browsing or inferential purposes.  There is no use in pondering what it \"really means\" for a thing to fall under a topic; #$Topics are just shallow (but useful) ways of \"clumping\" things together.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa1f8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa1f8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
