x_comment(x_EvaluativeCriterion,"A sub-collection of #$Criterion, the instances of #$EvaluativeCriterion are standards that dictate how the value, worth, or quality of entities should be judged based on some properties of that entity.  As an example, there may be several aspects to describing the offensive capabilities of a #$FootballTeam (say total yards gained during a game and the number of sacks allowed).  However, it is another matter to use such properties to judge the quality of a #$FootballTeam (i.e., using greater total yards to raise an evaluation, while using more sacks to lower it.).  The standard which transforms the descriptions into a judgment of the value of the team is an instance of #$EvaluativeCriterion.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa228).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa228,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa228,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa228,5191).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa228,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa228,[]).
x_comment('x_EvaluativeCriterion-Numerical',"A sub-collection of #$EvaluativeCriterion, the instances of\n#$EvaluativeCriterion-Numerical are those standards which when applied\nfor the evaluation of a set of entities result in the assignment of\nsome instance of #$PositiveInteger to the elements of the set.  For\nexample, charts which state the best-selling album for a particular\nweek rely on a relatively simple instance of\n#$EvaluativeCriterion-Numerical to compose such charts from a\ndescription of their sales.  A more complex example would be a\ncriterion which supports judgments of the livability of a city based\non a variety of distinct properties.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa229).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa229,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa229,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa229,5192).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa229,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa229,[]).
x_comment('x_EvaluativeCriterion-1IsBest',"The sub-collection of #$EvaluativeCriterion-Numerical where (1) ratings are assigned using integers (2) the lower the assigned integer the better the ranking and (3) the integer one is the highest possible ranking.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa22a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa22a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa22a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa22a,5202).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa22a,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa22a,[]).
x_comment(x_EvaluatedNumericalRating,"#$EvaluatedNumericalRating, a sub-collection of #$EvaluativeQuantity, is a collection of collections. The instances of #$EvaluatedNumericalRating are instances of #$FirstOrderCollection whose instances all share a common evaluation relative to some instance of #$EvaluativeCriterion-Numerical.  What distinguishes this collection from #$EvaluativeQuantity is that the evaluations include assigning a number to the collection such that individuals can be compared based on the number assigned to the collection of which they are a member.  For example, a sub-collection of #$EvaluatedNumericalRating could be the set of weekly rankings for instances of #$Song-CW by the organization responsible for #$RollingStone-TheMagazine.  'This is Rolling Stone's number one song this week.' assigns that individual song to a collection that is an instance of #$EvaluatedNumericalRating.  The collection 'Rolling Stone's Number One Song' is such that at any given time there is exactly one instance of it.  However, this is not a necessary feature of the instances of #$EvaluatedNumericalRating.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa22b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa22b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa22b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa22b,5203).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa22b,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa22b,[]).
x_comment(x_numericalRatingWRTCriterion,"An assertion of the form (#$numericalRatingWRTCriterion RANK NUM CRITERION) states that RANK, an instance of #$EvaluatedNumericalRating is associated with NUM, some #$Number-General, with regard to the instance of #$EvaluativeCriterion-Numerical.  For instance, (#$numericalRatingWRTCriterion HighestRatedHooHa 1 Foo) would assert that the collection HighestRatedHooHa receives the numerical rank of 1 relative to the Foo standard.  It is important to note that #$numericalRatingWRTCriterion is a #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa22c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa22c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa22c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa22c,5204).
