x_comment(x_facetBasedOnBinaryPred,"A #$BinaryPredicate that is used to state that a special relation holds between a #$FacetingCollectionType and a #$BinaryPredicate -- that the former is \"based on\" the latter in a specific sense.\n<p>\nWhere <code>(#$facets-Generic COL FACET-COL)</code>, <code>(#$facetBasedOnBinaryPred FACET-COL BINPRED)</code> means that for all <code>X</code> in <code>FACET-COL</code> there is a <code>Y</code> such that, by the definition of <code>X</code>, for all <code>Z</code> in <code>COL</code>, <code>Z</code> is in <code>X</code> iff <code>(PRED Z Y)</code> holds.\n<p>\nFor example, <code>(#$facetBasedOnBinaryPred #$WineTypeByColor #$uniformColorOfObject)</code> means that for all <code>WINE-TYPE</code> in #$WineTypeByColor there is a <code>COLOR</code> such that, by the definition of <code>WINE-TYPE</code>, for all <code>WINE</code> in #$Wine, <code>WINE</code> is in <code>WINE-TYPE</code> iff <code>(#$uniformColorOfObject WINE COLOR)</code> holds.\n<p>\nNote that it is also true that <code>(#$facetBasedOnBinaryPred #$WineTypeByColor #$isa)</code>. Indeed, <code>(#$facetBasedOnBinaryPred FACET-COL #$isa)</code> is trivially true for any <code>FACET-COL</code>, since the following is a logical truth:\n<pre>\n(#$forAll ?X \n  (#$thereExists ?Y \n    (#$forAll ?Z \n      (#$equiv\n        (#$isa ?Z ?X)\n        (#$isa ?Z ?Y)))))\n</pre>\nFor cases in which the arguments of <code>BINPRED</code> are reversed, see #$facetBasedOnBinaryPredInverse.  See also #$facetBasedOnTypeBinaryPred, #$facetBasedOnTypeBinaryPredInverse, and #$SharedNoteOnFacetBasisPredicates.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa23f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa23f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa23f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa23f,5224).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa23f,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa23f,[]).
