x_comment(x_facetBasedOnBinaryPredInverse,"A #$BinaryPredicate that is used to state that a special relation holds between a #$FacetingCollectionType and a #$BinaryPredicate -- that the former is \"based on\" the latter in a specific sense.\n<p>\nWhere <code>(#$facets-Generic COL FACET-COL)</code>, <code>(#$facetBasedOnBinaryPredInverse FACET-COL BINPRED)</code> means that for all <code>X</code> in <code>FACET-COL</code> there is a <code>Y</code> such that, by the definition of <code>X</code>, for all <code>Z</code> in <code>COL</code>, <code>Z</code> is in <code>X</code> iff <code>(PRED Y Z)</code> holds.\n<p>\nFor example, <code>(#$facetBasedOnBinaryPredInverse #$PersonTypeByCulture #$cultureParticipants)</code> means that for all <code>PERSON-TYPE</code> in #$PersonTypeByCulture there is a <code>CULTURE</code> such that, by the definition of <code>PERSON-TYPE</code>, for all <code>PERSON</code> in #$Person, <code>PERSON</code> is in <code>PERSON-TYPE</code> iff <code>(#$cultureParticipants CULTURE PERSON)</code> holds.\n<p>\nFor cases in which the arguments of <code>BINPRED</code> are reversed, see #$facetBasedOnBinaryPred.  See also #$facetBasedOnTypeBinaryPred, #$facetBasedOnTypeBinaryPredInverse, and #$SharedNoteOnFacetBasisPredicates.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa242).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa242,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
