x_comment(x_facetBasedOnTypeBinaryPred,"A #$BinaryPredicate that is used to state that a special relation holds between a #$FacetingCollectionType and a #$BinaryPredicate -- that the former is \"based on\" the latter in a specific way.\n<p>\nWhere <code>(#$facets-Generic COL FACET-COL)</code>, <code>(#$facetBasedOnTypeBinaryPred FACET-COL BINPRED)</code> means that for each <code>X</code> in <code>FACET-COL</code>, there is a <code>Y</code> such that, by the definition of <code>X</code>, <code>X</code> is the one and only specialization of <code>COL</code> that bears <code>BINPRED</code> to <code>Y</code>.\n<p>\nFor example, <code>(#$facetBasedOnTypeBinaryPred #$OrganizationTypeByActivityType #$characteristicActivityTypeOfOrganizationType)</code> means that for all <code>ORG-TYPE</code> in #$OrganizationTypeByActivityType there is an <code>ACT-TYPE</code> such that only the specializations of  <code>ORG-TYPE</code> (including <code>ORG-TYPE</code> itself) are the  specializations of #$Organization that bear the #$characteristicActivityTypeOfOrganizationType relation to <code>ACT-TYPE</code>.\n<p>\nE.g., #$SugarManufacturingOrganization, an instance of #$OrganizationTypeByActivityType, is by definition the one and only specialization of #$Organization that bears #$characteristicActivityTypeOfOrganizationType to #$SugarManufacturing. \n<p>\nFor cases in which the arguments of <code>BINPRED</code> are reversed, see #$facetBasedOnTypeBinaryPredInverse.  See also #$facetBasedOnBinaryPred and #$SharedNoteOnFacetBasisPredicates.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa248).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa248,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
