x_comment(x_facetBasedOnTypeBinaryPredInverse,"A #$BinaryPredicate that is used to state that a special relation holds between a #$FacetingCollectionType and a #$BinaryPredicate -- that the former is \"based on\" the latter in a specific way.\n<p>\nWhere <code>(#$facets-Generic COL FACET-COL)</code>, <code>(#$facetBasedOnTypeBinaryPredInverse FACET-COL BINPRED)</code> means that for all <code>X</code> in <code>FACET-COL</code>, there is a <code>Y</code> such that, by the definition of <code>X</code>, <code>X</code> is the one and only specialization of <code>COL</code> to which <code>Y</code> bears <code>BINPRED</code>.\n<p>\nFor example, <code>(#$facetBasedOnTypeBinaryPredInverse #$PersonTypeByNationality #$countryOfNationality)</code> means that for all <code>NATIONALITY</code> in #$PersonTypeByNationality, there is a <code>COUNTRY</code> such that, by the definition of <code>NATIONALITY</code>, <code>NATIONALITY</code> is the one and only specialization of #$Person to which <code>COUNTRY</code> bears the #$countryOfNationality relation.\n<p>\nE.g. #$ItalianPerson, an instance of #$PersonTypeByNationality, is the one and only specialization of #$Person to which #$Italy bears the #$countryOfNationality relation.\n<p>\nFor cases in which the arguments of <code>BINPRED</code> are reversed, see #$facetBasedOnTypeBinaryPred.  See also #$facetBasedOnBinaryPredInverse and #$SharedNoteOnFacetBasisPredicates.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa249).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa249,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
