x_comment(x_GenlsPreservingSubcollectionDenotingFunction,"A specialization of both #$GenlsPreservingFunction and #$SubcollectionDenotingFunction (qq.v.).  This is the type of function that always returns a subcollection of one of its arguments, and does so in a way that is #$genls preserving with respect to that argument-place.  More precisely, a function FUNC is an instance of #$GenlsPreservingSubcollectionDenotingFunction if and only if it has an argument-place (say the Nth) such that both of the following hold:\n<p>\n(i) (#$resultGenlArg FUNC N)\n<p>\n(ii) (#$preservesGenlsInArg FUNC N) .\n<p>\nFor example, #$PartTypeFn always returns a subcollection of its second argument, and is generalization-preserving in that argument-place.  Thus (#$PartTypeFn #$Cat #$Paw), the collection of cat paws, is a subcollection of #$Paw; and (#$PartTypeFn #$Cat FrontPaw), the collection of cat front paws, is a specialization of the former collection.\n<p>\nSpecializations of #$SubcollectionDenotingFunction include #$UnaryIntersectionFunction and #$SubcollectionFunction.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa264).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa264,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa264,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa264,5323).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa264,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa264,[]).
x_comment(x_SingletonCollectionFn,"(#$SingletonCollectionFn TERM) denotes the collection whole sole instance is TERM.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa265).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa265,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa265,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
