x_comment(x_allSubCollectionsAreInstancesOf,"A #$TaxonomicSlotForCollections (q.v.) that can be used to relate a given collection-of-at-least-some-collections to a collection, all of whose specializations are instances of the given collection-of-at-least-some-collections. (#$allSubCollectionsAreInstancesOf COL COL2) means that every specialization of COL is an instance of COL2.  Note that COL2 need not be a specialization of #$Collection, since COL2 may have instances that are not specializations of COL. For example, (#$allSubCollectionsAreInstancesOf #$Situation #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem) means that every collection of situations is a semi-directed path system, but it does not mean that every instance of #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem is a specialization of #$Situation (to make that claim, use the predicate #$typeGenls).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa26c).
