x_comment(x_SituationalObjectType,"A specialization of #$ObjectType (q.v.) whose instances are all and only those collections that are situationally object-like. A collection <code>COL</code> is situationally object-like just in case it generally holds that any proper sub-situation (see #$properSubSituations) of an instance of <code>COL</code> is not itself an instance of <code>COL</code>.  More precisely, a collection <code>COL</code> is an instance of #$SituationalObjectType just in case it satisfies the following: For any distinct <code>OBJ1</code> and <code>OBJ2</code>, if <code>(#$isa OBJ1 COL)</code> and <code>(#$subSituations OBJ1 OBJ2)</code>, then <i>not</i> <code>(#$isa OBJ2 COL)</code>.\n<p>\nFor example, none of the proper sub-situations of a #$Suicide is itself a suicide.  Likewise for #$CrossingAGap.  So #$Suicide and #$CrossingAGap are both instances of #$SituationalObjectType. Conversely, a proper sub-situation of a given #$SportsCompetition might itself be a #$SportsCompetition (e.g. the biathalon during some Olympic games); so #$SportsCompetition is <i>not</i> a situational-object-type.\n<p>\nSee #$SituationalStuffType for the disjoint notion of being situationally stuff-like.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa280).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa280,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa280,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa280,5385).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa280,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa280,[]).
