x_comment(x_IntervalTypeRatingFn,"An instance of #$UnreifiableFunction used in calculating and referring to points along a scale.  (#$IntervalTypeRatingFn SCALE EVALUATION-TYPE REAL) denotes a particular instance INS of #$Quantity that is, for purposes of performing evaluations of type EVALUATION-TYPE, a point on SCALE. The location of INS along SCALE is determined by its position along the real number line between N and M, where N is the assigned value (cf. #$assignedValueOfQuantityForEvaluationType) of one end points (cf. #$scaleEndPoints) on SCALE, and M is the assigned value of the other end point on SCALE. Note that these requirements mean that #$IntervalTypeRatingFn is a partial function (cf. #$PartialFunction).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa28b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa28b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
