xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa28b,[]).
x_comment(x_CoexistenceRelation,"A specialization of #$TemporalExistenceRelation.  This is the collection of relations such that: If EXP is an assertion or a denotational term in which one of these relations, RELN, stands in arg0 of EXP and ARG is a non-zero argument of EXP that is an instance of #$TemporalThing, then, if EXP denotes or is true (depending on whether it is a denotational term or an assertion), then the temporal extent of ARG must subsume the time index of EXP and, if RELN is a function and returns an instance of #$TemporalThing, then applying the function to its arguments results in something whose temporal extent also subsumes the time index of EXP.\n<p>\nMore precisely,\n<p>\nIf RELN is an instance of this collection and a function embedded in an assertion like the following,\n<p>\n(PRED ARG1...ARGN...(RELN R-ARG1 ...R-ARGN))<MT TIME PAR>\n<p>\nthen '(RELN R-ARG1 ...R-ARGN)' denotes a value, VAL, only if, for each argument R-ARG1 - R-ARGN and VAL that is an instance of #$TemporalThing, that argument's (and value's) temporal extent subsumes TIME in MT to PAR.\n<p>\nIf RELN is a predicate in arg0 of an assertion like the following,\n<p>\n(RELN ARG1...ARGN)<MT TIME PAR>\n<p>\nthen '(RELN ARG1...ARGN)' is true in MT at TIME to PAR only if the temporal extent of each argument ARG1 - ARGN that is an instance of #$TemporalThing is such that its temporal extent subsumes TIME in MT to PAR.\n<p>\nFor example, #$TerritoryFn is a function that returns the territory of it's arg1.  Since '(#$TerritoryFn COUNTRY)' only denotes when embedded in an assertion whose time index is such that COUNTRY and that country's territory both subsume that time index, #$TerritoryFn is an instance of #$CoexistenceRelation.  So the following cannot be true:\n<p>\n(#$awareOf BobTheCaveMan (#$TerritoryFn #$France))<PrimitiveMt 30000BC #$TimePoint>\n<p>\nThis follows from the fact that '(#$TerritoryFn #$France)' does not denote anything in 30000BC because France did not exist then.\n<p>\nA sufficient condition for membership in this collection is if the relation is a corresponding function (see #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Generic and its specs) to a predicate that is an instance of #$CoexistencePredicate.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa28c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa28c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa28c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa28c,5409).
