x_comment(x_TaxonomicPredicateForPredicates,"A specialization of both #$TaxonomicPredicate and #$MetaPredicate. Each instance of #$TaxonomicPredicateForPredicates is a predicate used to help define the taxonomy of #$Predicates by specifying relations between various predicates; hence at least two of its argument-places are constrained to instances (see #$argIsa) of #$Predicate or some broad specialization thereof (such as #$BinaryPredicate).  Examples include #$genlPredsWRTArgs and #$genlPredsWRTTypes.  An important specialization of this collection is #$TaxonomicSlotForPredicates (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa290).
