x_comment(x_TaxonomicPredicate,"A subcollection of #$Predicate.  Each instance of #$TaxonomicPredicate is a predicate used to help specify the position of a thing within one of the major taxonomies or hierarchies in the Cyc ontology.  An important specialization of #$TaxonomicPredicate is #$TaxonomicSlot (q.v.).  Whereas instances of #$TaxonomicSlot are binary predicates that specify a specific relation between two terms in a taxonomy, other predicates that are instances of #$TaxonomicPredicate are used to indicate that a relation holds between two terms in a taxonomy in a manner mediated by other terms.  For example, #$genlPredsWRTTypes is an instance of #$TaxonomicPredicate that is not an instance of #$TaxonomicSlot, and (#$genlPredsWRTTypes BINPRED1 BINPRED2 COL1 COL2) means that if (BINPRED1 INS1 INS2) where INS1 is an instance of COL1 and INS2 is an instance of COL2, then (BINPRED2 INS1 INS2).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa291).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa291,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
