x_comment(x_TaxonomicPredicateForAnyThing,"A specialization of both #$TaxonomicPredicate and #$MetaPredicate. Each instance of #$TaxonomicPredicateForAnyThing is a predicate that can in principle be used to help specify the location of anything whatsoever within some taxonomy; hence at least one of its argument-places must be constrained to instances (see #$argIsa) of #$Thing (and to nothing more specific than #$Thing).  For example, #$isaBoth is an instance of this collection. An important specialization of this collection is #$TaxonomicSlotForAnyThing (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa295).
