x_comment(x_agreeInType,"  This predicate provides a means of indicating that two #$DiscourseReferntPegs agree (and overlap) in terms of semantic type, and hence are potentially identical (c.f. #$coReferring).  In particular, (#$agreeInType TERM1 TERM2) means that the known semantic types for TERM1 and TERM2 are compatible (i.e. they're not disjoint) and overlap in some non-trivial way.  In general, it entails that i) some #$nearestIsa for one is a spec of some #$nearestIsa for the other; and ii) no #$nearestIsa for one is #$disjointWith any #$nearestIsa of the other.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa2c1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa2c1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
