x_comment(x_TemporalExistenceRelation,"An instance of #$RelationshipType and a specialization of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation.  Each instance of #$TemporalExistenceRelation is a relation that is \"contemporary\" in one of its arguments places or, if it is a function, in the #$resultIsa.\n<p>\nThat is, if RELN is an instance of this collection, then either\n<p>\nRELN is a predicate and there is at least one i (0 < i <= N), such that if\n<p>\n(RELN ARG-1, ..., ARG-N)<MT TIME PAR>\n<p>\nholds, then the temporal extent of ARG-i must subsume TIME. Or,\n<p>\nRELN is a function such that RELN denotes a value only if\n<p>\n(i) there exists an argument place that is \"contemporary\" in the way described in the condition for predicates  -- RELN will only denote if the temporal extent of the argument in the contemporary spot subsumes the time index of the assertion in which RELN appears as a denotational term.  Or,\n<p>\n(ii) the temporal extent of the assigned value for a given sequence of arguments to RELN subsumes the time index of the assertion in which RELN appears as a denotation term.\n<p>\nFor further information about these conditions see the comments on #$TemporalExistenceRelation and #$CoexistenceRelation.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa2c3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa2c3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa2c3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa2c3,5534).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa2c3,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa2c3,[]).
