x_comment(x_taskHasPrereqWRTPostCond,"An assertion of the form (#$taskHasPrereqWRTPostCond TASK PRE-STATE POST-STATE) is used to relate a type of #$PurposefulAction, TASK, to two instances of #$TaskState, PRE-STATE and POST-STATE. The assertion requires (#$taskPrerequisites TASK PRE-STATE) and (#$taskPostConditions TASK POST-STATE) both be true.  This predicate is intended for complex tasks that are related to multiple prerequisites and multiple post conditions.  If it is the case that a postcondition only depends only a subset of the preconditions, this predicate allows for a representation of that connection. In this way, the abandonning of a post-condition may eliminate the need to meet some of the pre-conditions for TASK.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa2d8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa2d8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa2d8,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
