x_comment('x_RelationalNCRuleFn-InstanceLevel',"(#$RelationalNCRuleFn PRED NUM WORD) denotes a particular form of #$NounCompoundRule which can be derived on the basis of #$denotesArgInReln assertions for which PRED, a #$BinaryPredicate,  is the arg3, NUM is the arg4, and WORD is the arg1.  So, for example, (#$RelationalNCRuleFn #$owns 1 #$Own-TheWord) denotes a rule for interpreting compounds like \"car owner\". In general, the form of the #$ncRuleTemplate for the derived rule will be either (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn COL PRED #$TheNCModifier) or (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromTypeFn COL PRED TheNCModifier) depending on whether NUM has a value of 1 or 2 (respectively).  In either case, the value for COL will correspond to the NUMth argIsa constraint for PRED,   Furthermore, #$ncRuleConstraints for the derived rule will generally be inferred on the basis of the arg constraints of PRED and the #$denotesArgInReln assertion(s) which license the rule.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa30b).
