x_comment(x_discourseReferentPegsDisagreeInType,"  This predicate provides a means of indicating that two #$DiscourseReferentPegs disagree in terms of semantic type, and hence expressions that denote them cannot possibly be co-referential (c.f., #$coReferring).  In particular, (#$discourseReferentPegsDisagreeInType THING1 THING2) entails that THING1 and THING2 are instances of disjoint collections.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa30c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa30c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
