x_comment(x_unclearSentence,"(#$unclearSentence SENTENCE) means that the generation of #$CycLPropositionalSentence SENTENCE (which is usually the subject of a #$suggestedSentence assertion) is not a clearly formed natural-language sentence. Clearly formed, in this case, means that the sentence would be readily understood by anyone with no special training, but with a fluent grasp of the language. For example, \"Cyndy Matuszek is viscidity.\" does not express an obvious concept in English, nor does the sentence \"Abduced term fn cyc problem store fn 4412 agent 279 considers Libya an enemy.\"") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa324).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa324,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
