x_comment(x_EfficaciousSubstanceTypeByComposition,"An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection.  Instances are specializations of #$PartiallyTangible whose instances share a unique physical composition (such as a chemical formula or a genome), and are widely recognized as having the ability to affect observable change on the physical world, particularly in organisms or on other substances.  Though this collection is not a specialization of #$ExistingStuffType, instances are nevertheless \"substances\" in the sense that, in the everyday experience of humans, instances of these collections will typically be observed as \"clumped together\" in stuff-like samples (see #$MobFn and #$ChemicalSubstanceFn for functions that take an instance of #$ExistingObjectType and return the collection of stuff-like samples of that type).  \nExamples include paint thinner, anthrax, and the active ingredient-types in many types of medicines (see #$PharmaceuticalType).  Negative examples include chemicals typically considered inert, such as water, and drug \"cocktails\" the efficacy of which is merely a reflection of the efficacious substance-types they contain.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa34f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa34f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa34f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa34f,5781).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa34f,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa34f,[]).
