x_comment(x_ExposingSomething,"A specialization of #$Action.  Each instance of #$ExposingSomething is an event in which something causes something to be exposed to something.  (The notion of X's being exposed to Y is difficult to define precisely, but very roughly it means that Y has access to, or can reach, X.)  Some examples of #$ExposingSomething: taking off one's hat, stepping out into the sun, turning a page of a book, opening a jar of peanut butter.  An instance of #$ExposingSomething need not be a #$PurposefulAction; consider, e.g. accidentally knocking one's hat off, or a gust of wind blowing one's hat off.  For the relatively static exposure event which follows an instance of #$ExposingSomething, see #$ExposureEvent.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa388).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa388,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
