x_comment(x_sinceEarliestInterval,"(#$sinceEarliestInterval INTERVAL SENTENCE PARAMETER) identifies INTERVAL as the starting interval for the period, ending with the current date (see #$currentDate), throughout which SENTENCE is true, at a granularity specified by PARAMETER.  For example, (#$sinceEarliestInterval (#$DayFn 11 (#$MonthFn #$February (#$YearFn 2003))) (#$outOfOffice #$Lehmann) #$CalendarDay) says that it has been true since February 11, 2003, that Fritz has been out of the office.  To say that Fritz has been out of the office since last Friday, use #$since-NthDate.  To say that he has been out since yesterday, use #$since-Metric.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa390).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa390,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
