x_comment(x_WorkingDraft,"A specialization of #$TextualPCW.  Each instance of #$WorkingDraft is a conceptual work that is a less-than-final version of some (at least prospective) published work (see #$draftOfTextualWork and #$PublishedConceptualWork).\n<p>\nWorking drafts typically undergo numerous changes, or revisions, before a finished work is produced and published.  Thus the boundary between a working draft and the finished product is quite fuzzy.  In some cases it is difficult or impossible to say, even in hindsight, whether a work that existed at some earlier time constitutes (or constituted) a different work than a particular finished work we know today, or was instead simply that latter work itself at a less-than-ultimate stage in its evolution.  To call something CW a #$WorkingDraft at a given time T implies that either (i) there exists at T a distinct, more recently-created published work that CW is/was clearly an earlier draft of or (ii) CW is a still-in-progress work at T that is viewed by its author(s) as a draft of some prospective future published work.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa396).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa396,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa396,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa396,5903).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa396,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa396,[]).
