x_comment(x_LevelOfInformationRichness,"#$LevelOfInformationRichness, a specialization of #$EvaluativeQuantity, is used to describe the degree of richness of a given #$InformationStore.  For example, if a book deals with the topic of thermodynamics, but is only a cursory skeletal outline of the subject, then the book would be considered relatively superficial in regard to the topic of thermodynamics.  Yet another book on thermodynamics, that exhausts the subject in both comprehensiveness and depth, would be considered a relatively rich source of information on thermodynamics.  The degree of \"information richness\" can be applied to any kind of #$InformationStore: e.g., experts, databases, reports, articles, and etc.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa3ba).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa3ba,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
