x_comment(x_sksModuleTypeDirection,"This predicate determines the :direction property of the\n#$SKSIHLModuleTypes created for some structured knowledge source.\n(#$sksModuleTypeDirection SKS HLMODULETYPE DIRECTION) means that all\nHL modules generated for SKS which are of type HLMODULETYPE should\nhave :direction DIRECTION. If not explicitly asserted otherwise, the\ndefault direction for all #$SKSIRemovalModules is\n#$Backward-AssertionDirection.  Similarly, if not explicitly asserted\notherwise, the default direction for all #$SKSIStorageModule is\n#$Forward-AssertionDirection. Also note that this predicate is\ntransitive via #$subKS in its first argument.  So you should make the assertion\nat the highest level SKS term at which you want all of the modules of HLMODULETYPE to have assertion direction DIRECTION.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa3d2).
