x_comment(x_MeasurableQuantity,"A specialization of #$Quantity (q.v.).  This is the collection of quantities that have a numeric component and could actually be used to <i>measure</i> something, as opposed to (say) merely ranking it on a scale.  Arithmetic operations (such as addition and multiplication) can be performed on measurable quantities, as they can on purely numeric scalars (see #$NumericInterval).\n<p>\nSpecializations of #$MeasurableQuantity include #$Distance, #$Temperature, #$Mass, and #$Time-Quantity.  Other, broader specializations are #$OneDimensionalQuantity, #$TwoDimensionalQuantity, and #$ThreeDimensionalQuantity.\n<p>\nAny quantity (that at least in principle could be) returned by a #$UnitOfMeasure (q.v.) function is a measurable quantity.  In CycL, particular measurable quantities are usually represented as the result of applying a unit-of-measure function to a real number or pair of reals.  For example, (#$Meter 5) is the distance 5 meters.\n<p>\nFor predicates that relate things to measurable quantities that characterize them, see #$MeasurableQuantitySlot.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa3dd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa3dd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa3dd,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa3dd,6060).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa3dd,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa3dd,[]).
x_comment(x_ResearchingAndDevelopingFn,"A #$CollectionDenotingFunction and #$UnaryFunction, an expression of the form <code>(#$ResearchingAndDevelopingFn TYPE)</code> represents the sub-collection of #$Research that is dedicated to the learning how to create <code>TYPE</code>, a #$TemporalStuffType.  Thus, (#$ResearchingAndDevelopingFn #$SemiconductorDevice) refers to the collection of events that are dedicated to learning how to create instances of #$SemiconductorDevice.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa3de).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa3de,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa3de,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa3de,6067).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa3de,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa3de,[]).
x_comment(x_typeIsRAndDOfType,"An assertion of the form (#$typeIsRAndDOfType RESEARCH-TYPE THING-TYPE) is used to relate a subcollection of #$Research to an instance of #$TemporalStuffType.  Thus, any instance of RESEARCH-TYPE would be an event that is aimed at learning how to create instance of THING-TYPE.  This is the corresponding predicate for the function #$ResearchingAndDevelopingFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa3df).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa3df,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa3df,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa3df,6068).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa3df,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa3df,[]).
x_comment(x_fieldFostersAdvancedArtifactsOfType,"A binary predicate that relates fields of study to the technologies they advance.  <code>(#$fieldFostersAdvancedArtifactsOfType AREA TECH-TYPE)</code> means that research in the #$FieldOfStudy <code>AREA</code> engenders technological advances in the creation of artifacts of type <code>TECH-TYPE</code>.  For example '(#$fieldFostersAdvancedArtifactsOfType #$ComputerScience #$ComputerProgram-CW)' means computer science fosters advanced computer programs, and <code>(#$fieldFostersAdvancedArtifactsOfType #$NuclearEngineeringField #$NuclearPoweredDevice)</code> means that nuclear science fosters advanced nuclear powered devices.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa3e0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa3e0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa3e0,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
