x_comment(x_TwoDimensionalUnitOfMeasure,"A specialization of #$MultiDimensionalUnitOfMeasure (q.v.).  Each instance of #$TwoDimensionalUnitOfMeasure is a unit-of-measure function that is equal to the \"product\" or \"ratio\" of two #$OneDimensionalUnitOfMeasures.  For example, #$SquareMeter is equal to (#$UnitProductFn #$Meter #$Meter), and #$MilesPerHour is equal to (#$PerFn #$Mile #$HoursDuration).\n<p>\nFor any number or pair of numbers taken as its argument(s), a two-dimensional unit-of-measure returns as value a #$TwoDimensionalQuantity (q.v.), such as an #$Area or a #$Speed.\n<p>\nSpecializations of #$TwoDimensionalUnitOfMeasure include #$UnitOfArea and #$UnitOfSpeed.  See also #$ThreeDimensionalUnitOfMeasure.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa3e9).
