x_comment(x_ThreeDimensionalUnitOfMeasure,"A specialization of #$MultiDimensionalUnitOfMeasure (q.v.).  Each instance of #$ThreeDimensionalUnitOfMeasure is a unit-of-measure function that is equal to the \"product\" or relative \"ratio\" of three #$OneDimensionalUnitOfMeasures (q.v.).  For example, #$CubicMeter is equal to (#$UnitProductFn #$Meter #$Meter #$Meter), and #$MetersPerSecondPerSecond is equal to (#$PerFn (#$PerFn #$Meter #$SecondsDuration) #$SecondsDuration).\n<p>\nFor any number or pair of numbers taken as its argument(s), a three-dimensional unit-of-measure returns as value a #$ThreeDimensionalQuantity (q.v.), such as an #$Volume or an #$Acceleration.\n<p>\nSpecializations of #$ThreeDimensionalUnitOfMeasure include #$UnitOfVolume and #$UnitOfAcceleration.  See also #$TwoDimensionalUnitOfMeasure.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa3eb).
