x_comment(x_MultiDimensionalQuantity,"A specialization of #$MeasurableQuantity (q.v.).  Each instance of #$MultiDimensionalQuantity is a measurable quantity that is defined as the product or ratio of other quantities.  For example, (#$MilesPerHour 65) is a multi-dimensional quantity obtainable by dividing (#$Mile 65) by (#$HoursDuration 1), and (#$CubicMeter 8) is a derived quantity obtainable by multiplying (#$Meter 2) by itself twice.  In contrast, (#$Mile 65), (#$HoursDuration 1), and (#$Meter 2) are all instances of #$OneDimensionalQuantity (cf.).\n<p>\nEach multi-dimensional quantity is in principle equal to the result of applying some (reified or otherwise) #$MultiDimensionalUnitOfMeasure (q.v.) to some number or other #$NumericInterval (or pair of numeric-intervals).\n<p>\nWhen a <i>one-dimensional</i> quantity is multiplied or divided by another one-dimensional quantity, the result is always a multi-dimensional quantity.  But note that this is <i>not</i> true of the results of multiplying and dividing quantities generally.  For example, (#$ProductFn (#$MilesPerHour 65) (#$HoursDuration 1)) is equal to the one-dimensional quantity (#$Mile 65).)\n<p>\nSpecializations of #$MultiDimensionalQuantity include #$TwoDimensionalQuantity and #$ThreeDimensionalQuantity.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa3f1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa3f1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa3f1,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa3f1,6103).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa3f1,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa3f1,[]).
x_comment(x_SimpleSquareQuantity,"A specialization of #$SquareQuantity (q.v.).  Each instance of #$SimpleSquareQuantity <code>SQUARE</code> is equal to the product of some #$OneDimensionalQuantity <code>UNIQUANT</code> and itself.  In other words, the following holds:\n<p>\n    <code>(#$equals SQUARE (#$TimesFn UNIQUANT UNIQUANT))</code> .\n<p>\nFor example, (#$SquareMile 4) is a simple square quantity equal to (#$TimesFn (#$Mile 2) (#$Mile 2)).\n<p>\nSee also #$SimpleCubicQuantity.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa3f2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa3f2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa3f2,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
