x_comment(x_CubicQuantity,"A specialization of #$ThreeDimensionalQuantity (q.v.).  Each instance of #$CubicQuantity <code>CUBIQUANT</code> is equal to the result of multiplying together three instances of #$OneDimensionalQuantity <code>(UNIT L) (UNIT M) (UNIT N)</code> that are themselves measurable by the same #$OneDimensionalUnitOfMeasure <code>UNIT</code>.  In other words, the following holds:\n<p>\n    <code>(#$equals CUBIQUANT (#$TimesFn (UNIT L) (UNIT M) (UNIT N))</code>.\n<p>\nFor example, (#$CubicMeter 24) is a cubic quantity equal to (e.g.) (#$TimesFn (#$Meter 2) (#$Meter 3) (#$Meter 4)).\n<p>\nSpecializations of #$CubicQuantity include #$Volume and  #$SimpleCubicQuantity.  See also #$SquareQuantity.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa3f5).
