x_comment(x_UnitOfRatio,"A specialization of #$MultiDimensionalUnitOfMeasure (q.v.).  Each instance of #$UnitOfRatio is a function that returns an instance of #$RatioQuantity (q.v.) when applied to a number or other #$NumericInterval (or pair of numeric-intervals).  Each unit-of-ratio can (at least in principle) be derived as the result of applying #$PerFn (q.v.) to two units-of-measure.\n<p>\nFor example, #$MilesPerGallon is a unit-of-ratio that is equal to (#$PerFn #$Mile #$Gallon-US).  And (#$MilesPerGallon 40) (e.g.) is equal to the result of dividing  the #$Distance 40-miles by the #$Volume 1-gallon.  Thus:\n<p>\n(#$MilesPerGallon 40) = ((#$PerFn #$Mile #$Gallon-US) 40) = (#$QuotientFn (#$Mile 40) (#$Gallon-US 1)) .\n<p>\nSpecializations of #$UnitOfRatio include #$UnitOfRate and #$UnitOfPressure.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa40b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa40b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa40b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa40b,6193).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa40b,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa40b,[]).
x_comment(x_UnitOfCount,"A specialization of #$UnitOfMeasure (q.v.).  Each instance of #$UnitOfCount is a function that takes one or two numbers (see #$Number-General) as arguments and returns as value a #$CountQuantity (q.v.), such as a particular count of people, cars, or molecules (see the instance #$Mole-ChemicalCountUnit).\n<p>\nUnits-of-count are often represented in CycL using #$UnitOfCountFn (q.v.).  For example, (#$UnitOfCountFn #$Person) is a unit-of-count for counting persons, and ((#$UnitOfCountFn #$Person) 4) is the count-quantity of four persons: the count (e.g.) of all four-person groups (such as the classic lineup of #$TheBeatles-MusicGroup).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa40c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa40c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
