x_comment(x_knownAntecedentRule,"A #$MetaKnowledgePredicate that is used to state a strong pragmatic directive to the #$CycInferenceEngine.  Asserting (#$knownAntecedentRule RULE) tells the inference engine to automatically generate a removal module to implement RULE; i.e. to solve queries unifying with the consequent of RULE by attempting to prove the substituted antecedent of RULE.  When this removal module is used during inference, it attempts to prove the substituted antecedent via removal only (see #$knownSentence).  It does not preclude other uses of RULE in inference.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa42e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa42e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa42e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa42e,6276).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa42e,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa42e,[]).
x_comment(x_agentProhibitsActType,"A binary #$AgentPredicate.  <code>(#$agentProhibitsActType AGENT ACTTYPE)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> prohibits or disallows instances of <code>ACTTYPE</code> from being performed.  This implies that <code>AGENT</code> has some sort of authority or power (be it legal, moral, coercive, or whatever) to make such a prohibition.  It suggests (but does <i>not imply</i>) that <code>AGENT</code> has at least some capability of enforcing the prohibition.  It does not imply that no acts of <code>ACTTYPE</code> are performed, since prohibitions are sometimes violated.\n<p>\nFor example,\n<pre>\n  (#$agentProhibitsActType #$EmilyPost\n    (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn\n      #$Smoking #$eventOccursAt EmilyPostsHouse))</code>\n</pre>\n<p>\nmeans that Emily Post prohibits smoking in her house.\n<p>\nWhen making an #$agentProhibitsActType assertion one should take care to restrict <code>ACTTYPE</code> sufficiently, in light of <code>AGENT</code>'s actual authority and proscriptive intent.  Thus, in the above example, it would be inappropriate to replace the predicate's second argument with\n<pre>\n  (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn\n    #$Smoking\n    #$eventOccursAt\n    #$House-Modern),\n</pre>\nas Post does not have the authority to prohibit smoking in houses generally.\n<p>\nSee also #$lawProscribesActType.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa42f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa42f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa42f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa42f,6277).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa42f,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa42f,[]).
