x_comment(x_workTimeInTimeInterval,"(#$workTimeInTimeInterval TIME-QUANTITY TIME-INTERVAL) means that there is TIME-QUANTITY amount of work time available in\nTIME-INTERVAL. For example, (#$workTimeInTimeInterval (#$HoursDuration 8) (#$DayFn 13 (#$MonthFn #$February (#$YearFn 2004)))) means that February 13, 2004 has 8 hours of work time. This predicate is dependent on the context of use and expresses the 'official' work time within a time interval. This means that although February 13, 2004 has 8 hours of work time associated with it, a given agent may work more or less hours.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa443).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa443,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
