x_comment(x_ZeroDimensionalUnitOfMeasure,"A specialization of #$UnitOfMeasure (q.v.).  Each instance of #$ZeroDimensionalUnitOfMeasure is a unit-of-measure function that, unlike all other types of unit-of-measure, does <i>not</i> return instances of #$MeasurableQuantity (q.v.), but instead returns instances of #$NumericInterval (q.v.).\n<p>\nZero-dimensional units-of-measure are recognized mainly in order to simplify the application of quasi-mathematical operations (e.g. #$PerFn, #$UnitProductFn) to units-of-measure generally.  For example, #$Unity (q.v.) is a zero-dimensional unit-of-measure that returns the #$IntervalOnNumberLine whose least and greatest point-values are given  by its argument(s).  #$Unity is (e.g.) the result of \"multiplying\" (via #$UnitProductFn) #$TimesPerDay by #$DaysDuration.\n<p>\nCf. #$OneDimensionalUnitOfMeasure and #$MultiDimensionalUnitOfMeasure.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa453).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa453,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa453,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa453,6380).
