x_comment(x_ProperIntervalOnNumberLine,"A specialization of both #$IntervalOnNumberLine and #$ScalarProperInterval (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$ProperIntervalOnNumberLine is an proper interval -- i.e. <i>not</i> just a single point (see #$Number-General) -- on the real number line.  For example, the phrase \"numbers greater than zero and less than or equal to 10\" describes such an interval.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa457).
