x_comment(x_allocationPortions,"An assertion of the form (#$allocationPortions WHOLE PART) is used to express a whole-part relation between two instances of #$ResourceAllocationSpecification.  Specifically, the instance of #$ResourceAllocationSpecification WHOLE has the other instance of #$ResourceAllocationSpecification PART as a part.   So, PART represents a portion of the total amount of resources represented by WHOLE.  An alternative relationship between two instances of #$ResourceAllocationSpecification is #$derivedAllocations which represents how one #$ResourceAllocationSpecification makes uses up a portion of an #$ResourceAllocationSpecification.  Let's say that I have two savings accounts the contents of which will go to help me buy a new house.  The money in those two accounts bear the relation #$allocationPortions to the whole #$ResourceAllocationSpecification which is dedicated to that task.  However, I may set aside particular chunks of the whole #$ResourceAllocationSpecification for certain purposes (i.e., paying bank fees), that relationship would be #$derivedAllocations.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa484).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa484,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa484,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa484,6484).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa484,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa484,[]).
x_comment(x_hasTotalAllotment,"An assertion of the form (#$hasTotalAllotment PURPOSE ALLOTMENT) is used to relate an instance of #$NormativeSpecification PURPOSE to the instance of #$Allotment that represents the total of resources that are being dedicated to PURPOSE.  Alternatively, one can think of this as the sum of resources that are specifically and directly alotted for the purpose.  This may be divided into smaller allotments (see #$allocationPortions) for purposes that are subordinate to the main purpose.  Thus, a vacation may have a total budget, and distinct portions of that budget can be devoted to buying tickets, buying meals, etc.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa485).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa485,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa485,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
