x_comment(x_allotmentReservesPercentageOfIndForInterval,"An assertion of the form (#$allotmentReservesPercentageOfIndForInterval ALLOT PERCENT INDIVIDUAL INTERVAL) states that the #$Allotment ALLOT represents a reservation of PERCENT percent of the #$Individual INDIVIDUAL's time during the #$TimeInterval INTERVAL. Every individual assertion using this predicate in a given context is assumed to represent a different reservation.  Therefore, for the same ALLOT and INDIVIDUAL, even if there are two assertions where the #$TimeInterval of one bears the relation #$temporalBoundsContain to the #$TimeInterval of the second assertion, then ALLOT is assumed to have reserved the sum of the two reserved portions. This is a core predicate for describing what an #$Allotment reserves, see also #$allotmentReservesPercentageOfIndForInterval. This predicate assumes that for any set of values for ALLOT, INDIVIDUAL, and INTERVAL, there can be at most one value of PERCENT.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa48a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa48a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
