x_comment(x_nonAssertibleTerm,"A #$MetaPredicate for stating a certain restriction regarding the use of a given term in assertions to the Cyc Knowledge Base.  (#$nonAssertibleTerm TERM) means that a certain class of ground atomic formulas (or \"GAFs\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence) containing this term should not be asserted into the KB.  This condition is hard to precisely define, but the idea is that the term can appear in GAFs that say things about TERM -- that TERM is an instance of certain collections or believed by some cyclist to be someone's favorite term.  But, there is a certain class of assertions in which it should never appear.  For instance #$sentenceTruth is a #$nonAssertibleTerm in that it can't appear in arg0 of GAFs, but, of course, it can appear in arg1 of (#$notAssertible #$sentenceTruth).  #$ELRelation should have no direct instances, so (#$notAssertibleCollection #$ELRelation) holds.  But, of course, that term can appear in other GAFs (#$genls assertions for example).  #$AnytimePSC should not appear as the time dimension in any assertion in the KB.  But, it can appear in asserted GAFs where it does not appear in some argument position of an #$MtSpace NAUT.  This is basically a documentation predicate.  See the two specializations of this predicate, #$notAssertible and #$notAssertibleCollection, which constrain predicates and collections, respectively and which can be given precise definitions.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa499).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa499,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
