x_comment(x_objectExtorted,"A specialization of #$objectOfPossessionTransfer (q.v.) that applies to #$Extortion (q.v.) events in which either money or some other kind of object is extorted.  <code>(#$objectExtorted EXTORTION OBJECT)</code> means that in the course of <code>EXTORTION</code>, the perpetrator coerces the victim to turn over control of <code>OBJECT</code> by threatening him or her with harm.  Typically, <code>OBJECT</code> will be a sum of money or other #$TenderObject, in which case the predicate #$objectTendered also applies.\n<p>\nNote that, while in every instance of #$Extortion <i>something</i> is extorted from the victim, it is possible for an extortion to involve <i>no #$objectExtorted</i>; for what is extorted might instead be an <i>action</i> performed by the victim.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa49c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa49c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
