x_comment(x_RolePredicateAgnosticTowardsPresentTenseTimeIndex,"An instance of #$BinaryRolePredicate is an instance of this collection just in case you cannot infer the time index of its corresponding (not necessarily reified) present tense progressive predicate from the temporal extent of the situation in arg1 of the predicate or the predicate is not the sort that is likely to have a non-davidsonian version.\n<p>\nNote:  One should use the binary tag #$roleWithEventTypeAgnosticWRTTimeIndex\nwhen a role predicate only has this feature relative to a particular class of situations.  Making the predicate an instance of this collection entails that\nit can never be the case we are justified in inferring the time index with respect to any situation that satisfied the argument constraints of the predicate.  For instance,\n<p>\n(#$roleWithEventTypeAgnosticWRTTimeIndex #$assistingAgent #$EntertainmentEvent)\n<p>\nholds because someone can be the assisting agent before or after the entertainment event.  But, the stronger\n<p>\n(#$isa #$assistingAgent #$RolePredicateAgnosticTowardsPresentTenseTimeIndex)\ndoesn't necessarily hold because there could be some specialization of #$Event that is such that agents can only assist in the event during the event.\n<p>\n.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa4af).
