x_comment(x_AbductingSomeone,"A collection of events and a specialization of #$TakingAPersonPrisoner.  In each instance of #$AbductingSomeone, a #$Person is taken captive, moved somewhere, and held by another (or group of others).\n<p>\nAbductions are usually done illegally; see the specialization #$KidnappingSomeone. But note that this need not be the case.  For example, in certain circumstances a government agent might legally abduct a person for questioning; a parent might legally abduct a minor from the grounds of a religious cult; some people claim to have been abducted by aliens.\n<p>\nNote also that, while an abduction is typically done against the victim's will, this might not be the case if s/he is (say) unconscious, extremely ill, mentally disturbed, or very young.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa4c5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa4c5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa4c5,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
