x_comment(x_interestingForArgInReln,"An instance of #$SummaryPredicate.  (#$interestingForArgInReln N PRED) means that for any assertion ASSERTION of the form (RELN . ARGS) such that (#$genlPreds RELN PRED) and (#$assertionSentence ASSERTION SENTENCE), (#$interestingSentence THING SENTENCE) will be true for the Nth argument of SENTENCE.  For example, if (#$interestingForArgInReln 1 #$affiliatedWith) is true, then (#$interestingSentence #$BillClinton (#$headOfStateOf #$BillClinton #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica)) holds, since #$BillClinton is the arg 1 of the (#$headOfStateOf #$BillClinton #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica), that sentence is asserted in the KB, and (#$genlPreds #$headOfStateOf #$affiliatedWith).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa50a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa50a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
