x_comment(x_edibleStuffTypesCommonlyServedTogether,"A #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate.  Where <code>ESTYPE1</code> and <code>ESTYPE2</code> are both specializations of #$EdibleStuff, <code>(#$edibleStuffTypesCommonlyServedTogether ESTYPE1 ESTYPE2)</code> means that instances of <code>ESTYPE1</code> are commonly served with instances of <code>ESTYPE2</code>.  This relation does not hold between edible stuff types when one is an ingredient in the other; for example, it is not the case that (#$edibleStuffTypesCommonlyServedTogether #$SpaghettiMarinara #$SpaghettiNoodle).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa50f).
