x_comment(x_unitDefinition,"A binary predicate that is used to express the relationship between a derived #$UnitOfMeasure (q.v.) and the primitive units from which it is derived.  <code>(#$unitDefinition UNIT DEFN)</code> means that one unit of the #$MultiDimensionalUnitOfMeasure <code>UNIT</code> (i.e. <code>(UNIT 1))</code> is equal to <code>DEFN</code>, where <code>DEFN</code> is represented as a product, quotient, or power built ultimately from #$OneDimensionalUnitOfMeasures applied to the integer 1.  For example,\n<pre>\n  (#$unitDefinition\n    #$MilesPerHour\n    (#$QuotientFn (#$Mile 1) (#$HoursDuration 1)))\n</pre>\n<p>\nmeans that one mile-per-hour is equal to the distance 1-mile divided by the time-quantity 1-hour.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa533).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa533,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
