x_comment('x_Badness-Generic',"A linear-ordered specialization of #$EvaluativeQuantity, and the #$contraryIntervalTypes of #$Goodness-Generic. Instances reflect \"negative\" assessments of the relative worth of a particular thing.  Such assessments are usually made in relation to some (often implicit) standard held by the assessor; this standard might purport to measure a thing's usefulness, or its value, or its moral worth, or its beauty, or something else.  #$Badness-Generic is thus \"generic\" with respect to these various categories of worth.  Particular instances of this collection can be obtained via the various #$GenericValueFunctions.  Note: If a particular dimension of badness is sought you should use one of the specializations of this collection; e.g. #$Badness-Moral, #$Badness-Functional. ") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa540).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa540,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
