x_comment('x_typicalMainConstituent-TypeType',"A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible to a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible.  <code>(#$typicalMainConstituent-TypeType TYPE1 TYPE2)</code> means that an instance of <code>TYPE1</code> will typically have an instance of <code>TYPE2</code> as its #$mainConstituent.  For example, (#$typicalMainConstituent-TypeType #$DrinkingCan #$Aluminum); (#$typicalMainConstituent-TypeType #$T-Shirt #$CottonStuff).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa565).
