xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa58e,[]).
x_comment(x_stageCoversCandidateSubSitType,"An assertion of the form (#$stageCoversCandidateSubSitType TEMP-STAGE SUBSIT-TYPE) is used to relate an instance of #$TemporalStageSpecification TEMP-STAGE to a sub-collection of #$Situation SUBSIT-TYPE.  Instances of #$TemporalStageSpecification are used to give a type-level representation of the temporal features of all the individuals of a particular type of #$Situation, let's call this SIT-TYPE.  In particular, they describe temporal relations that will hold among individual subsituations based on their types and the duration of those subsituations.  This predicate asserts that SUBSIT-TYPE is one of the types of subsituations of instances of SIT-TYPE that TEMP-STAGE is used for representing.  NOTE: such an assertion is agnostic on whether any given instance of SIT-TYPE which actually have an instance of SUBSIT-TYPE as a subsituation.  The more specific predicate #$stageCoversSubSitType asserts such an existential relation.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa58f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa58f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
