x_comment(x_earlierStage,"An assertion of the form (#$earlierStage INTER-SPEC TEMP-STAGE) is used to relate an instance of #$InterStageSpecification to an instance of #$TemporalStageSpecification.  Instances of #$InterStageSpecification are used to provide a type-level representation of a type of #$Situation (let's introduce one and call it SIT-TYPE). In particular, they description the duration of time intervals that subsume or separate the subsituations of instances of SIT-TYPE. Instances of #$InterStageSpecification connect to the situations via this relation to a #$TemporalStageSpecifications.  this predicate picks out the #$TemporalStageSpecification that covers the subsituations that are comparatively earlier in instances of SIT-TYPE. The later #$TemporalStageSpecification is picked out with the predicate #$laterStage.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa591).
