x_comment(x_ProcessFn,"A #$UnaryFunction that takes an #$AccomplishmentType and returns the corresponding #$ProcessType.  <code>(#$ProcessFn ACC-TYPE)</code> denotes the \"process\" version of <code>ACC-TYPE</code>.  For example, whereas each instance of #$ConstructingABuilding is an event in which a complete building is fully constructed, each instance of (#$ProcessFn #$ConstructingABuilding) is an event in which some progress is made toward the construction of a building.  Thus\n<p>\n(#$relationAllExists #$outputsCreated #$ConstructingABuilding #$Building)\n<p>\nholds, but\n<p>\n(#$relationAllExists #$outputsCreated (#$ProcessFn #$ConstructingABuilding) #$Building)\n<p>\ndoes not.\n<p>\nFor any #$AccomplishmentType <code>ACC-TYPE</code>, <code>ACC-TYPE</code> is a specialization of (#$ProcessFn <code>ACC-TYPE)</code>.  Suppose a construction crew spends a day building just the foundation of a house.  This event is an instance of (#$ProcessFn #$ConstructingABuilding), but not an instance of #$ConstructingABuilding.  Now consider the event which comprises the entire construction of the house, from start to finish.  This is an instance of both #$ConstructingABuilding and (#$ProcessFn #$ConstructingABuilding).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa604).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa604,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa604,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
