x_comment(x_geographicalSubRegionsOfState,"A specialization of #$geographicalSubRegions (q.v.) that relates a given #$State-Geopolitical (q.v.) to its subregions.  <code>(#$geographicalSubRegionsOfState STATE SUBSTATE)</code> means that the region <code>SUBSTATE</code> lies wholly within the geopolitical state <code>STATE</code>. \nFor example, this holds: \n<code>(#$geographicalSubRegionsOfState #$Alberta-CanadianProvince (#$CentralRegionFn #$Alberta-CanadianProvince))</code> \nNote that, if either argument to #$geographicalSubRegionsOfState is an instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity, the assertion must be made in #$WorldGeographyDualistMt or a specialization thereof.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa673).
