x_comment(x_frequentEventTypeAtLocationType,"A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a specialization of #$SpatialThing-Localized to a specialization of #$Event-Localized.  <code>(#$frequentEventTypeAtLocationType LOC-TYPE EVENT-TYPE)</code> means that for any given instance <code>LOC</code> of <code>LOC-TYPE</code>, it is reasonable to assume, in the absence of information to the contrary, that instances of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code> occur with medium to very high frequency at <code>LOC</code>.  For example, (#$frequentEventTypeAtLocationType #$RestaurantSpace #$CookingFood) means that for any given instance <code>REST</code> of #$RestaurantSpace, it is reasonable to assume, in the absence of information to the contrary (e.g. the information that the #$Restaurant-Organization occupying <code>REST</code> specializes in serving #$RawFood), that instances of #$CookingFood occur with medium to very high frequency at <code>REST</code>.  See also #$typicalLocationTypeOfEventType.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa6da).
