x_comment(x_mutualAcquaintances,"A specialization of #$acquaintedWith (q.v.) and an instance of #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate. <code>(#$mutualAcquaintances AG1 AG2)</code> means that #$IndividualAgents <code>AG1</code> and <code>AG</code> are acquainted with one another in some fashion.  Either they can visually recognize one another, they have been involved in a conversation with one another, they have personally met one another, or they are in some other manner mutually acquainted.  This predicate differs from #$acquaintedWith only insofar as #$acquaintedWith is not symmetric, whereas #$mutualAcquaintances is symmetric.  An important specialization of #$mutualAcquaintances is #$simpleContactAcquaintances (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa761).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa761,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
