x_comment(x_coIntegralScalars,"A binary #$RuleMacroPredicate that relates #$ScalarIntegralValues (q.v.) that are integral with respect to the same unit of measure (see #$integralWRTUnit).  <code>(#$coIntegralScalars SCALAR1 SCALAR2)</code> means that there is some #$UnitOfMeasure (q.v.) <code>UNIT</code> such that both of these hold:\n<pre>\n  (#$integralWRTUnit SCALAR1 UNIT)\n  (#$integralWRTUnit SCALAR2 UNIT).\n</pre>\nFor example, (#$Meter 5) and (#$Meter 10) are co-integral.\n<p>\nNote that #$coIntegralScalars holds between <i>any</i> two #$Integers, as each integer is integral with respect to #$Unity (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa763).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa763,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
