x_comment(x_EpistemicallyDeterminingTheValueOfASlot,"A specialization of #$Evaluating.  Instances are events in which an agent determines the value of ?X for some open formula FORMULA, where the argument-place in which ?X occurs is functional (see #$functionalInArgs) for the arg0 of FORMULA (see #$operatorFormulas), and the values of all the other arguments in FORMULA are given.  Notable specializations include #$MeasuringSomething and #$DoingAnArithmeticOperation.  Examples include an event in which one measure the height of an object OBJ, and so determines the value of ?X in (#$heightOfObject OBJ ?X).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa77a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa77a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
