x_comment(x_InterArgPredicate,"The collection of #$ArgConstraintPredicates used to put (conditional or unconditional) constraints on polyadic relations in regard to two of their argument-places (or, in a few cases, to put a conditional constraint on relations in regard to two different features of one argument-place).  Each instance of #$InterArgPredicate specifies, with respect to a given #$Relation, either that one of its argument-places (the \"dependent\" one) has a certain feature, contingent upon one (usually a different one) of its argument-place's (the \"independent\" one's) having a certain (possibly different) feature (see #$InterArgConstraintPredicate), or that a particular relation must hold between two arguments of the relation (see #$InterArgRelnPredicate).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa77c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa77c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
