x_comment(x_PoppingOff,"An #$AccomplishmentType and a specialization of #$Separation-Complete (q.v.).  This is the collection of events in which one or more of the #$physicalParts of a tangible object is very quickly detached from it.      Typically, the detached part is projected away from the object.  The detachment might result from forces that are internal or external to the object.\n\nExamples include a button popping off a shirt, a lid popping off a pressurized container, and a hubcap being popped off a wheel with a crowbar.\n\nFor other types of \"popping\" events, see #$PoppingOpenAContainer and #$EjectingAnObject.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa784).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa784,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
