x_comment(x_UnitAtAddressFn,"An expression of the form (#$UnitAtAddressFn  UNIT-STRING LOCATION) takes an instance of #$SubLString UNIT-STRING and an instance of #$PhysicalContactLocation LOCATION and returns another instance of #$PhysicalContactLocation; however, this instance represents a smaller unit of the original instance.  For example, (#$UnitAtAddressFn  '10C' (#$StreetNumberFn 100 (#$StreetNamedFn 'Boylston St.' CityOfBostonMA)) would represent the unit \"10C\" at 100 Boylston St. Boston, MA.  This is an instance of #$PartialFunction since it is possible to form expressions using this function that do not represent actual instances of #$PhysicalContactLocation.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa7c9).
