x_comment(x_TheCurrentSequenceValueFn,"#$TheCurrentSequenceValueFn is an unary, unreifiable\nfunction which returns an #$IndexicalConcept. This term is used to\ndenote the 'current' value for an #$IntegerSequenceGenerator. It is\nintended to be translatable into a DBMS specific function call that\nreturns the current value of the seqence. Cyc obtains the referent\nvalue of the indexical at the time the function is evaluated on the\nDBMS. For instance, using the #$PostgreSQL syntax,\n(#$TheNextSequenceValueFn (#$IntegerSequenceGeneratorFn\n\"my-sequence\")) denotes the result of evaluating the SQL query\n'SELECT currval(\"my-sequence\")'. Compare this function with\n#$TheNextSequenceValueFn, which first increments the sequence before\nreturning its current value.)") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa7dd).
