x_comment(x_situationTopic,"#$situationTopic is a very general binary relation between an instance of #$MentalSituation and an instance of #$Thing.  An assertion of the form (#$situationTopic SIT THING) means that there is some #$IntelligentAgent that is a #$situationConstituents of the #$MentalSituation SIT, that agent participates in SIT, and SIT 'refers to' or 'is about' #$Thing.  This predicate operates at a very coarse granularity for describing #$MentalSituations and so, is inferentially weak.  Its main function is to allow for the introduction of things into a #$MentalSituation even if they are quite peripheral.  Moreover, it does not entail that every #$IntelligentAgent that is a #$situationConstituents in SIT needs have a mental state involving THING.  For instance, in a #$Talking event, someone might miss the part of the conversation where #$Spiderman was introduced.  #$situationTopic could still be used to relate that event to #$Spiderman, even though there is someone involved who has no mental states about that #$Spiderman during that #$Talking event.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa7f9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa7f9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa7f9,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa7f9,7918).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa7f9,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa7f9,[]).
x_comment(x_topicRole,"#$topicRole represents a very general relation between an instance of #$MentalSituation and an instance of #$SomethingExisting.  An assertion of the form (#$topicRole SIT OBJECT) means that OBJECT is an actor in SIT to the extent that a #$MentalState of some #$IntelligentAgent participating in SIT is about OBJECT and that mental state causally influences that agent's behavior during SIT.    The generality of this relation makes it inferentially weak.  Therefore, its more specialized forms are better suited for actual representations.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa7fa).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa7fa,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa7fa,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa7fa,7919).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa7fa,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa7fa,[]).
x_comment(x_evidenceOfPastCrime,"#$evidenceOfPastCrime is a more specialized form of the predicate #$evidence.  It relates an instance of #$CriminalInvesigation to an instance of #$SomethingExisting.  During the course of that particular instance of #$CriminalInvestigation, some agent in the role of #$performedBy is motivated to believe that the #$SomethingExisting is related to some #$ActCommonlyConsideredCriminal that has already occurred.  For instance, a bloody knife discovered during a #$CriminalInvestigation would play the role of #$evidenceOfPastCrime if the relevant performers of the investigation believe the knife to have been used as a weapon.  This predicate provides a coarse representation and buries complex causal and psychological relations. Contrast with #$evidenceOfCriminalIntent.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa7fb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa7fb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa7fb,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
