x_comment(x_initialAdjustmentPeriod,"Many adjustable rate loans (c.f., #$AdjustableRateLoan) have an initial adjustment period (say 6 months or 3 years), after which the interest rate (c.f., #$interestRate) adjusts at regular intervals of a different length than the initial period (typically annually).  (#$initialAdjustmentPeriod LOAN PERIOD) identifies PERIOD as the initial adjustment period for loan.  When the initial adjustment period and the subsequent adjustment period are the same, use #$adjustmentPeriod.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa817).
