x_comment(x_resultSetCardinalityWithConstraints,"This predicate is similar to #$resultSetCardinality in that it is used by the SKSI code to estimate the cost of querying the fields of a physical schema.  More precisely, let SCHEMA denote a physical schema, let PF-1, PF-2, ..., PF-N, denote the physical fields of SCHEMA, and let SELECT_SET and WHERE_SET denote two disjoint subsets of (#$TheSet PF-1 PF-2 ... PF-N) and ..... Then (#$resultSetCardinality SCHEMA SELECT_SET WHERE_SET CONSTRAINTS NUM) means that NUM is the average cardinality of the result set returned from a query in which the fields in SELECT_SET left unbound and the fields of WHERE_SET are bound and the constraints expressed the CycL sentence in CONSTRAINTS are all satisfied.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa8bf).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa8bf,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
