x_comment(x_LocalVariableFn,"An expression of the form (#$LocalVariableFn SENTENCE VARIABLE) picks out an instance of (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLVariable).  Specifically, the expression (#$LocalVariableFn SENTENCE VARIABLE) picks out the #$CycLVariable VARIABLE based on its appearance in the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLSentence) SENTENCE. Although, closely related to the syncategorematic 'function' #$Quote, #$LocalVariableFn is significantly different because of its relativization of VARIABLE to SENTENCE.   The primary utility of this function is for representing assertions about #$CycLSentences in a form that can be easily fed out to alternative representational systems that cannot support second-order representations.  The relativization of VARIABLE to SENTENCE allows us to unambiguously refer to the variables of one  #$CycLSentence, even if syntactically-identical variables appear in multiple #$CycLSentences. NOTE:  The first argument of this function is not quoted so that it is possible to use a term to denote SENTENCE without VARIABLE being symbolically represented within that term.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa8cf).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa8cf,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa8cf,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
