xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa8d2,[]).
x_comment(x_SubSentenceFn,"An expression of the form (#$SubSentenceFn SENTENCE SUB) is used to pick out an instance of  #$CycLAtomicSentence.  Specifically, it is used to denote the #$CycLAtomicSentence SUB with regard to its being a syntactic element of the canonical representation of the #$CycLSentence represented by the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLSentence) SENTENCE.  Although closely related to the syncategorematic 'function' #$Quote, the expression (#$SubSentenceFn SENTENCE SUB) does not denote SUB per se.  Instead, it serves to pick out SUB as a part of the canonical representation of the #$CycLSentence  SENTENCE.  The primary utility of this function is for representing assertions about #$CycL sentences in a form that can be easily fed out to alternative representational systems that cannot support second-order representations.  The contextualization of SUB relative to SENTENCE allows us to unambiguously refer to the elements of one #$CycLSentence, even if syntactically-identical elements appear in multiple #$CycLSentences. NOTE: The first argument of this function is not quoted so that it is possible to use a term to refer to the relevant #$CycLSentence without the actual symbols of SUB appearing within SENT.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa8d3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa8d3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
