x_comment(x_CycLObjectTypeFn,"An expression of the form (#$CycLObjectTypeFn EXPRESSION-TYPE) denotes a sub-collection of #$CycLExpression.  #$CycLExpression and all of its sub-collections have the property #$quotedCollection.  However, there is some utility in having instances #$CycLExpression that refer to other #$CycLExpressions, even though they are syntactically different.  For example, let us assume that term (#$Quote #$Sentence212) was created to refer to the sentence (#$Quote (#$isa #$GeorgeWashington #$HomoSapiens)).  While the latter is an instance of the #$quotedCollection #$CycLClosedSentence, the former is not.  The #$CycLObjectTypeFn function allows us to create new, unquoted collections that allow for #$CycLExpressions to refer to other instances of #$CycLExpression.  For instance,  #$Sentence212 can be an instance of (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLClosedSentence).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa8eb).
