xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa8f7,[]).
x_comment(x_generateWithFormWhenArgInReln,"(#$generateWithFormWhenArgInReln THING FORM ARGNUM RELN) means that any formula whose arg0 is RELN and whose ARGNUMth argument is THING should generate in natural language with a phrase whose head is of the word form FORM.  For example, (#$generateWithFormWhenArgInReln #$Deceased #$regularDegree 2 #$isa) means that a sentence of the form (#$isa FOO #$Deceased) should generate as \"FOO is deceased\" or \"FOO is dead,\" as opposed to something like \"FOO is a dead thing.\"") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa8f8).
