x_comment('x_GeneralizedQuantifier-CoIntersective',"A #$PredicateType ans a specialization of #$GeneralizedQuantifier.  A generalized quantifier <code>QUANT</code> is an instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifier-CoIntersective just in case knowing what things are elements of <code>SOC1</code> but not of <code>SOC2</code> -- that is, knowing the extent of <code>(#$SetOrCollectionDifferenceFn SOC1 SOC2)</code> -- is sufficient to determine the truth value of <code>(QUANT A B)</code>.  The most notable instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifier-Intersective is #$subsetOf.  Other (non-reified) examples include \"all but three\" and \"every ___ but John\".  Non-instances include #$some, #$many, #$few, and #$most.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa98a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa98a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa98a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa98a,8643).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa98a,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa98a,[]).
x_comment('x_GeneralizedQuantifier-Proportional',"A #$PredicateType and a specialization of #$GeneralizedQuantifier. A generalized quantifier QUANT is an instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifier-Proportional just in case it expresses a proportional quantificational relationship between sets or collections.\n<p>\nA <i>binary</i> generalized quantifier BIN-QUANT is a #$GeneralizedQuantifier-Proportional just in case the truth value of (BIN-QUANT SOC1 SOC2) is determined by the proportion of elements of SOC1 that are instances of SOC2. Notable instances of #$GeneralizedQuantifier-Proportional include #$most and #$half.  #$subsetOf, #$no, and #$some are included as limiting cases, since they are equivalent to \"exactly 100%\", \"exactly 0%\", and \"not 0%\", respectively. Other (non-reified) examples include \"fewer than half\" and \"four out of five\". Non-instances include #$aFew, #$many, and #$both.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa98b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa98b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa98b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aa98b,8644).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aa98b,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aa98b,[]).
