x_comment(x_situationTypeStages,"(situationTypeStages SIT-TYPE LIST) means that LIST is an ordered list of specializations of #$Situation, such that each element of LIST is known to be a #$properSubSituationTypes of SIT-TYPE, such that the ordering of LIST corresponds to the temporal ordering of of sub-situation types scripted via #$startsAfterEndOfInSituationType, and such that, for any two successive elements of LIST, MEMBER1 and MEMBER2, it isn't the case that there exists a MEMBER-MID such that (properSubSituationTypes SIT-TYPE MEMBER-MID) and such that (startsAfterEndOfInSituationType SIT-TYPE MEMBER-MID MEMBER1) and (#$startsAfterEndOfInSituationType SIT-TYPE MEMBER2 MEMBER-MID) (i.e., any two successive elements of the list are immediate successors with respect to SIT-TYPE.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aa9b8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aa9b8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aa9b8,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
