x_comment('x_DitransitiveNP-NPObjComplementFrame',"This frame is used for words that take exactly two NP complements, where one NP plays the role of direct object and the other the role of object complement.  Example: 'Fred called Sally a liar'.  One salient way in which this frame is distinguished from #$DitransitiveNP-NPFrame is that the latter undergoes #$DoubleObjectAlternations, while the former does not. Example: 'Fred gave Sally a book' alternates with 'Fred gave a book to Sally' but 'Fred called Sally a liar' does not -- *'Fred called a liar of Sally'.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aaa0b).
