x_comment(x_alternativeActionTypes,"A binary #$FirstOrderCollectionPredicate.  <code>(#$alternativeActionTypes ACTTYPE1 ACTTYPE2)</code> means that performing an  act of <code>ACTTYPE1</code> is commonly considered to be salient and often viable alternative to performing an act of <code>ACTTYPE2</code>, and vice versa.  In some (but not all) cases, <code>ACTTYPE1</code> and <code>ACTTYPE2</code> will be sibling nearest-specializations of some slightly more general type of #$Action.  \n<p>\nFor example, baking-bread-from-scratch and baking-bread-from-a-mix are #$alternativeActionTypes, and both are specializations of #$BakingBread.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aaa1a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aaa1a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aaa1a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
