x_comment('x_stockPrice-High',"A predicate used to state the highest price that a share of a #$PubliclyHeldCorporation's #$StockClass has traded at on the current day.  (#$stockPrice-High STOCKTYPE PRICE DATE EXCHANGE) means that PRICE is the highest price paid for a share of STOCKTYPE so far on the #$CalendarDay that temporally subsumes DATE (i.e. the hightest price paid for such a share between that day's market opening and the end of DATE).  Before the market opens, and on days the market is closed, the high for the last day the market was open remains in effect.  Cf. #$stockPrice-Close.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aaa8d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aaa8d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
