x_comment('x_stockPrice-Last',"A predicate used to state the price that shares of a particular company's stock (of a given \"class\"; e.g. common or preferred) are currently being traded at.  Actually, this price is based on the most recent price-quote for that stock, and quotes are delayed by a set time (e.g. 20-minutes on the London Exchange) from the time of the actual trade.  More precisely, then, (#$stockPrice-Last STOCK PRICE DATE EXCHANGE) means that, as of DATE, the most recent price quoted on EXCHANGE for STOCK is PRICE.  Also see #$stockPrice-Ask and #$stockPrice-Bid.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aaa91).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aaa91,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
