x_comment(x_obligingAgents,"(#$obligingAgents OBLIGATION AGENT) means that the intelligent agent AGENT is owed something (e.g., money) as specified in OBLIGATION, an instance of #$Obligation (a type of #$NormativeSpecification).  See also #$obligatedAgents.  Note that #$obligingAgents and #$obligatedAgents do not stand in the #$negationPreds relation, as OBLIGATION could be broad enough or complicated enough (as in a service contract), where one can play both roles.  However, some obligations, e.g., instances of #$PaymentObligation, are such that no one can stand in both roles simultaneously.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aaadb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aaadb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
