x_comment(x_sksiSourceActivated,"(#$sksiSourceActivated SKS) is true iff SKS has been turned\n'activated' for querying. This is not sufficient alone to guarantee\nthat Cyc can query SKS. In particular, it may the case that SKS has\nbeen activated but the removal module data structures for SKS have not\nbeen registered yet (see #$sksiSourceRegistered). Furthermore, it may\nbe the case that Cyc cannot establish a connection to SKS (see\n#$sksiSourceAccessible). Finally, see also #$sksiSourceQueryable which\nchecks all three conditions.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aaae3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aaae3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aaae3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aaae3,9152).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aaae3,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aaae3,[]).
x_comment(x_sksiSourceAccessible,"(#$sksiSourceAccessible SKS) is true iff it is possible for\nCyc to establish a connection to SKS. That is, i) if SKS is a database\nthen Cyc should be able to open up an SQL connection to it; ii) if SKS\nis a web page then an empty http request to it should succeed (which\nbasically amounts to being able to open a TCP connection to it); iii)\nif SKS is a file hash table then Cyc should be able to open it. See\nalso #$sksiSourceRegistered, #$sksiSourceActivated, and\n#$sksiSourceQueryable.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aaae4).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aaae4,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aaae4,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aaae4,9160).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aaae4,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aaae4,[]).
x_comment(x_sksiSourceRegistered,"(#$sksiSourceRegistered SKS) is true iff the SKSI removal\nmodule data structures for SKS have been 'registered'. Note, however,\nthat source registration is not sufficient to guarantee that it can be\nsuccessfully queried from Cyc. Additionally, it must be true that a\nconnection to the source can be established (See\n#$sksiSourceAccessible) and that the removal modules have been\n'acivated' (see #$sksiSourceActivated). SKS is queryable (see\n#$sksiSourceQueryable) iff all three of these conditions are true.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aaae5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aaae5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aaae5,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
