x_comment(x_arg7Isa,"A binary #$ArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$arg7Isa RELN COL)</code>  means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything given as the seventh argument to <code>RELN</code> must be an instance of <code>COL</code>.  That is,  <code>(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ARG6 ARG7...)</code> is semantically well-formed only if <code>(#$isa ARG7 COL)</code> holds.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see  #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.  See #$argIsa for a similar but more flexible ternary predicate.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aab8c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aab8c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
