xc_kb_names(a65b16517aac2b,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aac2b,[]).
x_comment(x_lawPrescribesActType,"A binary #$IntangibleObjectPredicate.  <code>(#$lawPrescribesActType LAW ACTTYPE)</code> means that <code>LAW</code> requires any agent subject to it (see #$subjectToCOC) to perform at least one (and in some cases more, possibly regularly-recurring) instances of <code>ACTTYPE</code>.  This of course does <i>not</i> imply that such acts are performed, since laws are sometimes violated.\n<p>\nFor example, a law might require everyone within a certain age range to register for the miltary draft.  Or a law might require a given parent to make monthly child-support payments to their child's other parent.\n<p>\nSee also #$lawProscribesActType.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aac2c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aac2c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aac2c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aac2c,9754).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aac2c,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aac2c,[]).
x_comment(x_lawProscribesActType,"A binary #$IntangibleObjertPredicate.  <code>(#$lawProscribesActType LAW ACTTYPE)</code> means that <code>LAW</code> prohibits any agent subject to it (see #$subjectToCOC) from performing instances of <code>ACTTYPE</code>.  This of course does <i>not</i> imply that no such acts are performed, since laws are sometimes violated.\n<p>\nFor example, <code>(#$lawProscribesActType #$StealingIsIllegal #$Stealing)</code> means that the law #$StealingIsIllegal prohibits stealing.\n<p>\nSee also #$lawPrescribesActType and #$agentProhibitsActType.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aac2d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aac2d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aac2d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aac2d,9759).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aac2d,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aac2d,[]).
x_comment('x_ist-Prohibition',"(#$ist-Prohibition MT PROP) means that PROP is prohibited by MT, where MT is a microtheory that corresponds to an instance of #$Obligation via #$contextOfPCW.  This predicate allows the propositional content of prohibitions that apply to actions of agents to be stated in #$CycL.  PROP must be a closed formula.  Statements of the form (#$ist-Prohibition MT PROP) require that PROP mention the variable ?the-agent and/or ?the-action.  If some agent, AGENT, fulfills the role of ?the-agent, and in PROP and AGENT is an #$obligatedAgents for OBLIGATION then (#$agentViolatesObligation AGENT OBLIGATION) is concluded.  If some ACTION can bind to ?the-action in PROP then (#$actionViolatesObligation ACTION OBLIGATION) is concluded.  Once asserted, an #$afterAdding should cause a rule to be added to the system.  This rule will look like (#$implies (#$and PROP (#$obligatedAgents OBLIGATION ?the-agent)) (#$agentViolatesObligation ?the-agent OBLIGATION)).  See also #$ist-Obligation.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aac2e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aac2e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aac2e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aac2e,9764).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aac2e,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aac2e,[]).
x_comment('x_ist-Agreement',"The predicate #$ist-Agreement is used to indicate the propositions which have been agreed upon in a particular agreement.  (#$ist-Agreement AGR-MT PROP) means that the #$Agreement that corresponds to the #$Microtheory AGR-MT (via #$contextOfPCW) pertains to (commits its agreeing parties to) making the proposition (#$CycLSentence-Assertible) PROP true. Since each #$Agreement is represented in Cyc as a #$Microtheory, the way that this is expressed is to say that PROP is considered to <i>be</i> true within the microtheory which represents AGR.  PROP may or may not be true in reality (or, thus, according to #$Microtheorys intended to represent reality).\n<p>\n(#$ist-Agreement AGR-MT PROP) should not be taken to be a simple specialization of (#$ist MT PROP) for cases where MT is an instance of #$Agreement. Whereas #$ist relates any particular microtheory to all assertions that happen to be true in that microtheory, #$ist-Agreement indicates only those assertions in an #$Agreement microtheory which pertain to the agreement itself (and are not just something that happens to be true in it, e.g., that one of the #$agreeingAgents is named \"Joe\").") :- x_cid(a65b16517aac2f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aac2f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aac2f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aac2f,9765).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aac2f,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aac2f,[]).
x_comment(x_obligationOwedTo,"Points from an #$Obligation to the agent to whom the obligation is owed.  Note: this slot is not filled for all obligations.  For example, we probably don't want to commit to a particular agent to whom a mother is obliged in nursing her baby.  However, if Fred accepts Sally's request that he clean the toaster then she is the value on the #$obligationOwedTo for FredsToasterCleaningObligationMt.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aac30).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aac30,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aac30,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
