x_comment(x_suppliedWithTypeAmount,"(#$suppliedWithTypeAmount PT COL AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$Collection COL with which the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT is supplied.  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$suppliedWithTypeAmount is very general.  PT might, for example, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and the range of possible supplies is similarly broad.  If AMOUNT is a #$Rate, AMOUNT indicates the average rate of supply of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE to PT.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aacb0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aacb0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
