x_comment(x_infoGathered,"A ternary predicate that relates a #$MultiDirectionalCommunication (q.v.) and an agent to information received by the latter in the course of the former.  <code>(#$infoGathered COMM AGENT INFO)</code> means that there is a subevent of <code>COMM</code> that is an #$InformationTransferEvent in which <code>AGENT</code> is a #$recipientOfInfo and <code>INFO</code> is an #$infoTransferred.  \n<p>\nWhen it comes to multi-directional communication, #$infoGathered is the \"flip-side\" of #$infoContributed (q.v.).  In successful two-way communication (see #$BiDirectionalCommunication), any information contributed by one party will in turn be gathered by the other party, and vice versa.  In communications among larger groups, however, in which a given party might gather some but not all of the information contributed by the other parties, things can get much more complicated and the foregoing symmetry might not be present.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aacb4).
