x_comment('x_facets-NearStrict',"A #$TaxonomicSlotForCollections and a specialization of #$facets-Generic (q.v.).  (#$facets-NearStrict COL COLTYPE) means that COLTYPE corresponds to one (non-arbitrary) way of dividing (at least some of) COL into disjoint (or \"mostly\" disjoint) subcollections.  The instances of COLTYPE are all \"the same sort\" of subcollection of COL.  For example, #$PersonTypeByOccupation is a near-strict (but not strict) faceting of #$Person: while it is certainly possible for a person to have multiple occupations, it is expected that <i>most</i> people will have no more than one occupation (at a given time).") :- x_cid(a65b16517aace1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aace1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
