x_comment('x_infoTransferred-NLString',"A specialization of #$transferredAIS (q.v.).  <code>(#$infoTransferred-NLString ITE STRING)</code> means that (i) <code>STRING</code> is a character-string transferred as information in the information-transfer event <code>ITE</code>, (ii) <code>STRING</code> is a meaningful expression of some natural language <code>NL</code>, and (iii) the #$Information-Content <code>CONTENT</code> expressed by <code>STRING</code> with respect to <code>NL</code> (in the context of <code>ITE</code>) is itself information transferred (see #$infoTransferred) in <code>ITE</code>.  \n<p>\nFor example, \n\n<pre>\n  (#$infoTransferred-NLString \n    FDRsFirstInauguralAddress\n    \"The only thing we have to fear is fear itself.\")\n</pre>\n<p>\nmeans that in FDR's first Inaugural Address both the English sentence \"The only thing we have to fear is fear itself\" and the proposition that the only thing we have to fear is fear itself were transferred as information.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aacec).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aacec,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aacec,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
