x_comment(x_StuffFn,"(#$StuffFn OBJECT-TYPE) takes an object type as an argument, and returns a \"stuff-like\" version of that object type. (#$StuffFn OBJECT-TYPE) represents a physical portion of a separable, countable object, which is still the same substance, but no longer separable or countable in the same way. For example, a #$Cake is a separable object, but a (#$StuffFn #$Cake) is a non-whole portion of a #$Cake.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aacef).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aacef,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
