x_comment(x_normativeSpecificationDescribesRoleForInd,"The predicate #$normativeSpecificationDescribesRoleForInd is used for partially specifying the satisfaction conditions for an instance of #$NormativeSpecification  Specifically, it associates an instance of #$NormativeSpecification SPEC with a #$BinaryRolePredicate ROLE and an instance of #$SomethingExisting THING, to state the part of satisfying SPEC involves a situation in which THING fills ROLE.  This predicate works in conjunction with #$normativeSpecificationDescribesSituationType.  In short, given assertions of the form (#$normativeSpecificationDescribesSituationType SPEC SIT-TYPE) and (#$normativeSpecificationDescribesRoleForInd SPEC ROLE IND), then the satisfaction of SPEC will involve an instance of SIT-TYPE, SIT, such that the assertion (ROLE SIT IND) is true.  This predicate only provides a partial specification because any number of assertions using it or the predicate #$normativeSpecificationDescribesRoleForType can be used with #$normativeSpecificationDescribesSituationType to represent what needs to be done to satisfy SPEC.  See also #$completeSpecification for more information on constructing rules using these predicates.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aad07).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aad07,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aad07,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aad07,10097).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aad07,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aad07,[]).
x_comment(x_performerInSpec,"(#$performerInSpec SPEC AGT) says that part of satisfying SPEC involves an event in which AGT is an #$IntelligentAgent that plays the role #$performedBy.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aad08).
