x_comment(x_InternalSensoryQuantity,"A specialization of #$SensoryQuantity.  Each instance of #$InternalSensoryQuantity is a state of a sentient being in which it experiences within itself some level of somatic or psycho-somatic feeling, urge, or impulse.  An internal sensory attribute differs from an `external' one in that the sensing being refers the former to itself and the latter to external objects.  #$InternalSensoryQuantity includes states of feeling thirsty, tired, or in pain, as well as various bodily urges such as the urge to sneeze, burp, or urinate.  Sensory attributes that may occur with more or less intensity are represented by indicating a #$LevelOfPain, #$LevelOfPhysicalPleasure, #$LevelOfStress, and so on.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aad11).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aad11,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
