x_comment('x_diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-Necessary',"A specialization of #$properSubSituationTypes (q.v.) that relates #$DiseaseTypes to #$PhysiologicalConditionTypes that constitute their necessary symptoms.  <code>(#$diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-Necessary DISTYPE SYMPTYPE)</code> means that each case of <code>DISTYPE</code> involves (as #$properSubSituations) one or more occurrences of <code>SYMPTYPE</code>.  For example, <code>(#$diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-Necessary #$Asthma #$AsthmaAttack)</code> holds.\n<p>\nOccurrences <code>SYMPTYPE</code> are typically more readily identifiable than the occurrences of <code>DISTYPE</code> that subsume them; hence their usefulfulness in diagnosis and in gauging treatment effectiveness.  But note that this is <i>not</i> part of the definition of the predicate #$diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-Necessary.\n<p>\nSee also the specialization #$diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-NecessaryAndSufficient.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aad4c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aad4c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aad4c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aad4c,10244).
