x_comment(x_temporallyCoexist,"A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate and the most general #$CoexistingObjectsPredicate; a specialization of #$temporallyIntersects (q.v.).  #$temporallyCoexist relates any two temporally-extended things that presently exist or obtain or are occurring. <code>(#$temporallyCoexist TEMP1 TEMP2)</code> means that the temporal extents of <code>TEMP1</code> and <code>TEMP2</code> both subsume the present time.\n<p>\nMore formally: for any #$TimeInterval <code>TIME</code>,\n<pre>\n  (#$temporallyCoexist TEMP1 TEMP2)\n</pre>\nis true at <code>TIME</code> (see #$mtTimeIndex) if and only if both of these:\n<pre>\n  (#$temporallySubsumes TEMP1 TIME)\n\n  (#$temporallySubsumes TEMP2 TIME)\n</pre>\nare atemporally true (i.e. true at #$Always-TimeInterval).\n<p>\nFor example, the sentence <code>(#$temporallyCoexist #$GeorgeWBush #$RonaldReagan)</code> was true at the start of 2004 and false after Reagan's death on June 5 of that year.  On the other hand,  the sentence <code>(#$temporallyCoexist #$GeorgeWBush #$GeorgeWashington)</code> has never been true.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aad69).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aad69,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aad69,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aad69,10306).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aad69,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aad69,[]).
x_comment(x_evaluationResultQuotedIsa,"A binary #$MetaRelation that holds between relations and collections. #$evaluationResultQuotedIsa is primarily used to indicate that any value returned by a given evaluatable function is a quoted instance of a given collection. Where FUNC is a Function-Denotational, (#$evaluationResultQuotedIsa FUNC COL) means that FUNC returns a quoted instance of COL for any sequence of arguments for which FUNC is defined. That is, (#$quotedIsa (FUNC ARG1 ... ARGn) COL) holds for any sequence <ARG1, ..., ARGN> for which FUNC has a value. For example, '(#$evaluationResultQuotedIsa #$SubstringFn #$SubLString)' holds, and it entails (e.g.) '(#$quotedIsa (#$SubstringFn \"ABC\" 1 2) #$SubLString)'.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aad6a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aad6a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aad6a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aad6a,10321).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aad6a,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aad6a,[]).
x_comment(x_focalSubject,"#$focalSubject is a more specialized form of the predicate #$topicRole.  It relates an instance of #$MentalSituation to an instance of #$SomethingExisting.  Like #$topicRole it is intended to relate an entity to an event where that entity is the subject of some mental state of some agent in the role of #$deliberateActors in that event.  This is a slightly richer version in that it states that this entity is focal to the event. For example, an unsuccessful assassination attempt might not physically involve a particular agent, nonetheless we want to refer to the target's role in that event.  Further, a lecture could be about a person who died centuries before the time of that lecture.  This is a weak relationship.  Representations should use more specialized versions of this predicate (i.e., the first example should use #$intendedAttackTargets).  Contrast with #$evidence and #$nonFocalSubjectOfInvestigation.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aad6b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aad6b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aad6b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aad6b,10322).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aad6b,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aad6b,[]).
x_comment(x_candidateStringsForTopic,"This is a very general predicate for relating instances of #$SubLString to the instances of #$Thing with the sense that the instance of #$SubLString might be useful for the purposes of gathering information about #$Thing.  For example, (#$candidateStringsForTopic  GeorgeWBush 'Texas'). This allows us to represent potential relationships (perhaps for machine learning) without committing to an actual connections.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aad6c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aad6c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aad6c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
