x_comment(x_IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn,"A unary function that takes a CycL sentence that can be used in a query (see #$CycLSentence-Askable) and returns the intensional meaning appropriate to the question being asked by such a query.  If the question being asked with <code>SENT</code> is a \"<i>Yes/No</i>\" question, (#$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn <code>SENT</code>) is a #$Proposition, which is true or false with respect to any given context.  If the question being asked with <code>SENT</code> is a \"<i>what things are such that...</i>\" question  -- i.e. a question that asks for bindings for variables -- (#$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn <code>SENT</code>) is an intensional property or \"propositional function\", which has some (possibly empty) extension with respect to any given context.  \n<p>\nMore precisely:  (i) If <code>SENT</code> is a closed sentence, then (#$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn <code>SENT</code>) is the #$Proposition that <code>SENT</code> is true.  (ii) If <code>SENT</code> is an implication of the form <code>(#$implies ANTE CONSEQ)</code> such that any variables occurring free in <code>CONSEQ</code> also occur free in <code>ANTE</code>, then (#$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn <code>SENT</code>) is the #$Proposition that the universal closure of <code>SENT</code> is true.  (iii) If <code>SENT</code> is an implication of the form <code>(#$implies ANTE CONSEQ)</code> such that some variables occurring free in <code>CONSEQ</code> that do <i>not</i> occur free in <code>ANTE</code>, then (#$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn <code>SENT</code>) is the intensional property that holds, in a given context, of exactly those sequences of things that satisfy the open sentence obtained from <code>(#$implies ANTE CONSEQ)</code> by universally quantifying all of the variables occurring free in <code>ANTE</code>.  (iv) Finally, if <code>SENT</code> is an open sentence that is not an implication, then (#$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn <code>SENT</code>) is the intensional property that holds, in a given context, of exactly those sequences of things that satisfy <code>SENT</code>.\n<p>\nThe main purpose of #$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn is to help relate instances of #$KBContentTest-FullySpecified that ask essentially the same question, but do not have exactly the same sentence as their respective #$InferenceSentenceParameter values.  See also #$kbContentTestQuestion-Content.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aad89).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aad89,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aad89,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aad89,10371).
