x_comment(x_PartiallyTangibleTypeByPhysicalFeature,"A #$FacetingCollectionType.  Each instance of #$PartiallyTangibleTypeByPhysicalFeature is a collection of individuals who all share a particular physical property.  For example #$RhNegative is the collection of instances of #$Blood such that each is blood that is of type rh-negative.  This collection represents the property \"being blood type rh-negative\" and something has that property just in case they are an instance of that collection.  Note: these collections represent properties that things have or lack in a relatively absolute sense.  For physical properties that admit of dense degress (e.g. #$Flammability -- although something can be flammable in an absolute sense it is by virtue of having a particular degree of flammability.) see #$PhysicalQuantity. ") :- x_cid(a65b16517aad95).
