x_comment(x_studies,"The expression `(#$studies AGENT THING)' means that the intelligent agent\nAGENT studies THING. The notion of studying here is akin to what is involved in doing research, though it is broader. For example, reading extant material about THING, if there is such, would in most cases be considered part of studying THING, while it would probably count only as preparation for doing\nresearch. It is important that this notion of studying is distinct from the notion of studying for a test. Studying in the present sense may have no connection to any educational event.  Compare also with #$Studying. The notion here definitely\nincludes direct encounters with the THING being studied.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aad98).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aad98,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aad98,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aad98,10408).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aad98,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aad98,[]).
x_comment(x_stateOfAffairsObjectedTo,"A #$BinaryRolePredicate.  <code>(#$stateOfAffairsObjectedTo OBJECTING SENT)</code> means that the #$senderOfInfo in the instance of #$Objecting-CommunicationAct <code>OBJECTING</code> objects to the state of affairs corresponding to the #$CycLSentence-Assertible <code>SENT</code>.  An example of an assertion that could be made using this predicate is\n<p>(#$stateOfAffairsObjectedTo AlicesObjectingToBobsInfidelity <i>P</i>),\n<p>\nwhere <i>P</i> abbreviates a #$CycLSentence-Assertible stating that Bob cheats on his wife Alice.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aad99).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aad99,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aad99,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aad99,10412).
