x_comment(x_relationAllExistsSame,"(#$relationAllExistsSame PRED COLL1 COLL2) holds just in case every instance\nof COLL1 is related by PRED to the same instance of COLL2.  For example, if \nHoustonTexansCollection is the collection of all the group members of the #$HoustonTexans,\nthen (#$relationAllExistsSame #$hasCoach HoustonTexansCollection #$SportsCoach).  This means\nthat every instance of the collection of players on the Houston Texans football team has\nthe same coach.  Another example: \n(#$relationAllExistsSame #$uniformColorOfObject #$Ruby-Gem #$Color) means every ruby\nis the same color.  This predicate is useful if you want to state that a collection of things\nall share some feature, but can't be specific about what feature they share.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aae19).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aae19,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aae19,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aae19,10554).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aae19,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aae19,[]).
x_comment(x_PreparingForSituation,"The collection of #$PurposefulActions in which an agent prepares for a situation (#$Situation). The action can be entirely mental, as in #$MakingAPlan, or can involve #$CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvents, for example, buying food as a preparation for cooking a meal. The action may make the situation prepared for more likely to happen or it may have no causal bearing on that situation. For example, preparing for college may make it more likely that the agent will attend college. However, preparing for a power outage by buying a flashlight doesn't make it more likely that the power outage will occur. See also #$PreparingForUndesirableSituation. To relate #$PreparingForSituations to the #$Situation types that they prepare for, use the function #$PreparingForSitTypeFn. To relate #$PreparingForUndesirableSituations to the #$Situations that they prepare for, use the function #$PreparednessFn. See also #$PreventFromHappening and #$PreventionFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aae1a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aae1a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
