x_comment(x_hasInterAgentStatusWith,"(#$hasInterAgentStatusWith AGENT1 AGENT2 STATUS) means that AGENT2 has STATUS with respect to AGENT1. For example, it is believed that, at least until the US invasion of #$Afghanistan, (#$hasInterAgentStatusWith #$AlQaida #$Afghanistan #$SupportOfSponsorshipOfTerrorism).  This predicate is useful for talking about people and political entities like countries. Countries (and their political leaders) change and obviously so does the status they attribute to people so uses of this predicate should be temporally qualified. ") :- x_cid(a65b16517aae26).
