x_comment(x_corroboratingSourcesForProposition,"<code>(#$corroboratingSourcesForProposition  SOURCE SENTENCE)</code> means that the instance of #$InformationStore <code>SOURCE</code> is a non-trivial source for the proposition expressed by the instance of #$CycLSentence <code>SENTENCE</code>. \n<p>\nThis predicate is meant to take temporal qualification into account.  Thus, if SENTENCE is temporally qualified, a SOURCE corroborates SENTENCE iff an assertion corresponding to SENTENCE (with temporal qualification) is provable  in the context that corresponds to SOURCE.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aae31).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aae31,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
