x_comment('x_Channel-DeeperWaterwayPart',"A specialization of #$Channel-WaterPath.  Each instance of #$Channel-DeeperWaterwayPart is a subregion of a body of water that is intended to allow the passage of boats or ships which would otherwise run aground or encounter hazardous rocks or wrecks.  They are often deeper than their surrounding bodies of water.  Whole channels extend from the surface to the bottom of the body of water and are long and thin.  Unlike a #$Channel-BodyOfWaterLink (cf.), a #$Channel-DeeperWaterwayPart does not have land banks above the water's surface as borders.  Often, #$Channel-DeeperWaterwayParts are created or maintained by human dredging (and are thus #$ConstructionArtifacts).  Less often, they are naturally deep places.  They are usually marked with navigational bouys and appear on nautical charts.\n<p>\nInstances of #$Channel-DeeperWaterwayPart include the channel that allows ships safe passage up the East River off Manhattan, through Hell's Gate and into\nLong Island Sound.  Conversely, the #$EnglishChannel and the #$StraitOfHormuz (e.g.) are <i>not</i> instances of this collection, but are instead instances of #$Channel-BodyOfWaterLink.  But note that an instance of the latter (especially a #$Strait) might have a #$Channel-DeeperWaterwayPart as a subregion.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aae5b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aae5b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aae5b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aae5b,10690).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aae5b,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aae5b,[]).
