x_comment(x_siblings,"(#$siblings ANIMAL-1 ANIMAL-2) means that the #$Animal ANIMAL-1 and the #$Animal ANIMAL-2 are siblings; that is, either they share one or more biological parents (which is always the case if ANIMAL-1 and ANIMAL-2 are #$NonHumanAnimals), or they are siblings by adoption, marriage, or some other social arrangement.  Human siblings are generally (but not always) reasonably close in age (within 15 years or so), and generally (but not always) have grown up together in the same family.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aae86).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aae86,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aae86,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
