x_comment('x_twins-Fraternal',"(#$twins-Fraternal ANIMAL1 ANIMAL2) means that ANIMAL1 and ANIMAL2 are fraternal twins, meaning they are twins that came from different eggs and different sperm.  Fraternal twins always always share the same mother, and probably typically share the same father, but it is possible for fraternal twins to have different fathers.  This happens more often with #$NonHumanAnimals.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aae89).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aae89,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
