x_comment(x_motivesForAction,"(#$motivesForAction ACTION PRED AGENT THING) means one of the motives behind AGENT's performance of ACTION is AGENT's relationship PRED to THING during some period leading up to ACTION.  For example, to express that AGENT's motive for committing a particular roberry is (his or her feelings of) greed, one can write (#$motivesForAction BankRobbery001 AGENT #$feelsEmotion (#$PositiveAmountFn Greed)).  Where THING is an instance of #$CycLSentence-Assertible and PRED is an instance of #$CognitivePredicate, use the more specific #$reasonsForAction.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aaeb3).
