x_comment(x_intentionalMentalSituationRelation,"An intentional mental situation (c.f., #$IntentionalMentalSituation) is a situation in which an agent (c.f., #$Agent-Generic) experiences a mental state that is directed towards, or is \"about\" some object.  This \"aboutness\" is characterized through a relation between the subject and object, such as a belief relation (c.f., #$beliefs) or some other binary relation that defines propositional attitudes.  #$intentionalMentalSituationRelation is a predicate that relates intentional mental situations to the relation (or relations) that hold between the subject and object.  (#$intentionalMentalSituationRelation SITUATION RELATION) means that where AGENT is the subject and OBJECT is the object of SITUATION, SITUATION is such that (RELATION AGENT OBJECT) obtains.  For example, (#$intentionalMentalSituationRelation BobsHopeThatHeWillPassHisExam001 #$hopes) means that in the situation where Bob hopes that he will pass his exam, the #$hopes relation obtains between Bob and the proposition that Bob will pass.  See also #$situationIsSuchThat.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aaf1e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aaf1e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aaf1e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aaf1e,10936).
