x_comment(x_Plateau,"A subcollection of #$Flat-Topographical. Each instance of #$Plateau is an elevated, level or nearly level portion of the earth's surface, larger in area than the #$Summit of a #$Mountain, and bounded on at least one side by steep slopes.  For example, the top surface of a #$Mesa is a plateau.  Plateaus are found both on dry land and on the ocean floor.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aaf27).
