x_comment('x_actorRoles-EPFT',"A simple event-predicate template.  (#$actorRoles-EPFT EVT-TYPE (#$ActorPlaysRoleFn ACTOR1 ROLE1) (#$ActorPlaysRoleFn ACTOR2 ROLE2) ...) means that an instance of EVT-TYPE occurs which is also an instance of (#$ActorPlaysRoleFn ACTOR1 ROLE1), and  (#$ActorPlaysRoleFn ACTOR2 ROLE2), and so on.  In other words, it means an instance of EVT-TYPE occurs in which ACTOR1 is engaged by the relation expressed by ROLE1, and in which ACTOR2 is engaged by the relation expressed by ROLE2, and so on.  For example, (#$actorRoles-EPFT #$ImposingSanctions (#$ActorPlaysRoleFn #$UNSecurityCouncil #$performedBy) (#$ActorPlaysRoleFn #$Iraq #$maleficiary)) is true iff the UN Security Council imposes (is imposing) sanctions on Iraq.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aaf8a).
