x_comment(x_EmptyCollection,"A collection of collections and a specialization of #$EmptySetOrCollection (q.v.).  A collection is an instance of #$EmptyCollection if and only if it has no instances.  \n<p>\nSome collections are by their very nature necessarily empty; e.g. #$Nothing (q.v.).  Conversely, some collections are empty in some contexts and non-empty in others; e.g. #$Unicorn might be empty in the context of the actual world but non-empty in certain mythological contexts.  Similarly, a #$TimeDependentCollection might be empty at certain times and non-empty at certain other times; e.g. the collection of female US presidents is currently empty but will hopefully become non-empty some time in the near future.  This last example demonstrates that #$EmptyCollection is itself a time-dependent collection.\n<p>\nNote that each instance of #$EmptyCollection is #$disjointWith (q.v.) every collection -- including itself.\n<p>\nCf. #$NonEmptyCollection.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aafaa).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aafaa,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
