x_comment(x_NonEmptyCollection,"A collection of collections and a specialization of #$NonEmptySetOrCollection.  A collection is an instance of #$NonEmptyCollection if and only if it has at least one instance.  \n<p>\nSome collections, aguably, are by their very nature necessarily non-empty; e.g. #$Set-Mathematical.  Conversely, some collections are non-empty in some contexts and empty in others; e.g. #$Horse is non-empty in the context of the present-day actual world but empty in certain counterfactual contexts in which horses never existed.  Similarly, a #$TimeDependentCollection might be empty at certain times and non-empty at certain other times; e.g. the collection of female US presidents is currently empty but will hopefully become non-empty some time in the near future.  This last example demonstrates that #$NonEmptyCollection is itself a time-dependent collection.\n<p>\nNote that each instance of #$NonEmptyCollection #$intersectsWith (q.v.) #$Thing.\n<p>\nCf. #$EmptyCollection.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aafab).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aafab,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
