xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aafdb,[]).
x_comment(x_CycLFunctor,"A #$CycLExpressionType and a specialization of #$CycLOperator (q.v.).  Characterized synatactically, this is the collection of all and only those CycL terms that can appear as the main operator (i.e. in the \"arg0\" position) of a #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm. Characterized semantically, this is also the collection of all and only those CycL terms that denote #$Function-Denotationals (q.v.).  Instances of #$CycLFunctor are <i>not</i> themselves functions, but rather are expressions of the CycL language that are used to <i>denote</i> functions.\n<p>\nExamples of #$CycLFunctors include these four expressions:\n<pre>\n  #$PlusFn\n  #$Lambda\n  #$BorderBetweenFn\n  (#$FunctionToArg 2 #$biologicalFather)\n</pre>  \nThese examples reflect the fact that while most CycL functors encountered in practice are #$CycLConstants, a functor might be a #$CycLNonAtomicTerm.\n<p>\nSee also #$CycLPredicator.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aafdc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aafdc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aafdc,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aafdc,11240).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aafdc,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aafdc,[]).
x_comment(x_spatiallyEquidimensional,"An #$EquivalenceRelation that relates #$SpatialThings.  <code>(#$spatiallyEquidimensional OBJ1 OBJ2)</code> means that <code>OBJ1</code> and <code>OBJ2</code> both occupy the same number of spatial dimensions (see #$SpatialThingTypeByNumberOfDimensions).\n<p>\nNote that there are a number of #$SpatialPredicates that are conceived as only relating objects of the same dimensionality; see for example the instances of \n#$RCCBinaryPredicate.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aafdd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aafdd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aafdd,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aafdd,11252).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aafdd,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aafdd,[]).
x_comment(x_CompositeSpaceRegion,"A specialization of #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion (q.v.).  This is the collection of \"composite regions\" in the sense used in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory (q.v.).  A homogeneous extended space region is an instance of #$CompositeSpaceRegion if and only if it has another such region as a proper part (see #$properPartOfSpaceRegion).  \n<p>\nFor example, the space occupied by a full bottle of wine is a composite space region, one of its proper parts being the space occupied by the wine itself.\n<p>\nIs space <i>infinitely divisible</i> into smaller and smaller proper parts?   On this question #$RCCMt is agnostic, #$RCCContinuousSpaceMt assumes the answer is <i>No</i>, and #$RCCWithAtomicRegionsMt assumes the answer is <i>Yes</i>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aafde).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aafde,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aafde,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aafde,11256).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aafde,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aafde,[]).
x_comment(x_AtomicSpaceRegion,"A specialization of #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion (q.v.) and (in #$RCCWithAtomicRegionsVocabularyMt) #$ConvexSpaceRegion.  This is the collection of atomic regions of pure space.  A homogeneous extended space region is an instance of #$AtomicSpaceRegion if and only if it has no proper parts in the sense of #$partOfSpaceRegion.  An atomic region has no parts other than itself.\n<p>\nNote that in #$RCCWithAtomicRegionsVocabularyMt every extended space region is assumed to be decomposable, ultimately, into atomic regions.  Conversely, in #$RCCContinuousSpaceMt #$AtomicSpaceRegion is assumed to be an #$EmptyCollection.\n<p>\nCf. #$CompositeSpaceRegion; and see also #$ScatteredSpaceRegion.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aafdf).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aafdf,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517aafdf,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517aafdf,11261).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517aafdf,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517aafdf,[]).
