x_comment(x_DisconnectedSpaceRegion,"A specialization of #$CompositeSpaceRegion (q.v.).  This is the collection of non-self-connected space regions.  A homogeneous extended space region is an instance of #$DisconnectedSpaceRegion if and only if it is the sum (see #$spaceRegionSum) of two (non necessarily self-connected) parts that are disconnected from each other (see #$disconnectedSpaceRegions). \n<p>\nFor example, the geographical space of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica \nis a disconnected region; the space of #$Alaska-State (e.g.) is a part that is disconnected from the rest of the US-space.  Conversely, the space of #$ContiguousUnitedStates is itself <i>not</i> a disconnected region, but a connected one (cf. #$ConnectedSpaceRegion).\n<p>\nFor regions that are <i>totally disconnected</i>, see the specialization #$ScatteredSpaceRegion.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab01d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab01d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab01d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab01d,11399).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab01d,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab01d,[]).
x_comment('x_diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-NecessaryAndSufficient',"A specialization of #$diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-Necessary (q.v.) that relates #$DiseaseTypes to #$PhysiologicalConditionTypes that constitute their necessary and sufficient symptoms.  <code>(#$diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-NecessaryAndSufficient DISTYPE SYMPTYPE)</code> means that both (i) each case of <code>DISTYPE</code> involves (as #$properSubSituations) one or more occurrences of <code>SYMPTYPE</code> and (ii) no occurrence of <code>SYMPTYPE</code> is a proper sub-situation of a case of any other type of disease than <code>DISTYPE</code>.  For example, <code>(#$diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-NecessaryAndSufficient #$Asthma #$AsthmaAttack)</code> holds.\n<p>\nOccurrences <code>SYMPTYPE</code> are typically more readily identifiable than the occurrences of <code>DISTYPE</code> that subsume them; hence their usefulfulness in diagnosis and in gauging treatment effectiveness.  But note that this is <i>not</i> part of the definition of the predicate #$diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-NecessaryAndSufficient.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab01e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab01e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab01e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab01e,11405).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab01e,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab01e,[]).
