x_comment(x_ConvexSpaceRegion,"A specialization of #$StronglyConnectedSpaceRegion (q.v.).  This is the collection of convex regions as defined in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory (q.v.).  A homogeneous extended space region <code>REGION</code> is an instance of #$ConvexSpaceRegion if and only if any two parts of (see #$partOfSpaceRegion) <code>REGION</code> contain the respective endpoints of a straight line-segment that is itself wholly contained in <code>REGION</code>.\n<p>\nFor example, the space occupied by a rubber ball is a convex region, but that occupied by a fork or a can of soda are not.\n<p>\nBecause the notion of the region delineated by the hull of a space\nregion (see #$ConvexSpaceRegionFn) is a primitive notion in RCC, we axiomatize convex regions as those #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegions that are equal to their own convex region; i.e. (#$convexSpaceRegionOf <code>REGION REGION</code>).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab090).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab090,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
