x_comment(x_UniversalSpaceRegion,"A specialization of #$ConvexSpaceRegion (q.v.).  This is the collection of spatial universes. There is at most one known instance of #$UniversalSpaceRegion with respect to any context in which some #$SpatialThings are known to have locations, either absolutely or relatively (see #$LocationalPredicate and its immediate specializations).   \n<p>\nEach #$UniversalSpaceRegion is extended in some particular number of dimensions (see #$SpatialThingTypeByNumberOfDimensions).  See the specializations #$UniversalSpaceRegion-1D, #$UniversalSpaceRegion-2D, #$UniversalSpaceRegion-3D.\n<p>\nThe spatial universe <code>UNI</code> of a given context #$spatiallySubsumes every known spatial thing of the same or lower dimensionality as <code>UNI</code>, and every known #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion of the same dimensionality as <code>UNI</code> is a #$partOfSpaceRegion <code>UNI</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab093).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab093,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
