x_comment(x_reasonableTrafficableRouteToFor,"<code>(#$reasonableTrafficableRouteToFor PATH OBJ AGT)</code> means that <code>PATH</code> is a reasonable route for <code>AGT</code>, between <code>OBJ</code> and <code>AGT</code>. For example, if one were planning to drive a car from Dallas to Los Angeles for no other purpose than to arrive in L.A., it would not make sense to detour through Panama or Canada: reasonabl;e routes would mainly be on trafficable roads mainly east and south of L.A. and mainly west and north of Dallas (since L.A. is to the west and north of Dallas).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab110).
