x_comment('x_NullSpaceRegion-1D',"A specialization of #$NullSpaceRegion (q.v.) and #$OneDimensionalThing.  #$NullSpaceRegion-1D is the collection of one-dimensional \"null spatial regions\".  There is at most one known instance of #$NullSpaceRegion-1D with respect to any context in which some #$SpaceLines (q.v.) are known to have locations, either absolutely or relatively (see #$LocationalPredicate and its immediate specializations).\n<p>\nBy definition, a 1-D null space region is disconnected from (see #$disconnectedSpaceRegions) every 1-D homogeneous space region (i.e. #$SpaceLine), and is the #$spaceRegionComplement of the 1-D \"spatial universe\" (see #$UniversalSpaceRegion-1D).\n<p>\nThe introduction of 1-D null regions into #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory helps to allow the functions #$SpaceRegionComplementFn, #$SpaceRegionProductFn, and #$SpaceRegionDifferenceFn to be defined as #$TotalFunctions.  For example, #$SpaceRegionComplementFn can then be defined on instances of #$UniversalSpaceRegion-1D (q.v.), and #$SpaceRegionProductFn can be defined for pairs of one-dimensional regions that are #$discreteSpaceRegions.  (Also see the comment on #$NullSpaceRegion.)\n<p>\nSee also #$NullSpaceRegion-2D and #$NullSpaceRegion-3D.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab143).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab143,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab143,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab143,11772).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab143,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab143,[]).
x_comment('x_NullSpaceRegion-3D',"A specialization of #$NullSpaceRegion (q.v.) and #$ThreeDimensionalThing.  #$NullSpaceRegion-3D is the collection of three-dimensional \"null spatial regions\".  There is at most one known instance of #$NullSpaceRegion-3D with respect to any context in which some #$SpaceChunks (q.v.) are known to have locations, either absolutely or relatively (see #$LocationalPredicate and its immediate specializations).\n<p>\nBy definition, a 3-D null space region is disconnected from (see #$disconnectedSpaceRegions) every 3-D homogeneous space region (i.e. #$SpaceChunk), and is the #$spaceRegionComplement of the 3-D \"spatial universe\" (see #$UniversalSpaceRegion-3D).\n<p>\nThe introduction of 3-D null regions into #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory helps to allow the functions #$SpaceRegionComplementFn, #$SpaceRegionProductFn, and #$SpaceRegionDifferenceFn to be defined as #$TotalFunctions.  For example, #$SpaceRegionComplementFn can then be defined on instances of #$UniversalSpaceRegion-3D (q.v.), and #$SpaceRegionProductFn can be defined for pairs of three-dimensional regions that are #$discreteSpaceRegions.  (Also see the comment on #$NullSpaceRegion.)\n<p>\nSee also #$NullSpaceRegion-1D and #$NullSpaceRegion-2D.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab144).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab144,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab144,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab144,11779).
