x_comment(x_SemiProperSpaceRegion,"A specialization of #$CompositeSpaceRegion (q.v.).  A #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion is an instance of #$SemiProperSpaceRegion if and only if it has another homogeneous extended space region as a tangential proper part (#$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion).\n<p>\nCf. #$ProperSpaceRegion.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab156).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab156,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab156,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab156,11803).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab156,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab156,[]).
x_comment(x_StrictlySemiProperSpaceRegion,"A subcollection of #$SemiProperSpaceRegion (q.v.).  A homogeneous extended space region is an instance of #$StrictlySemiProperSpaceRegion if and only if it has a tangential proper part (see #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion) but does <i>not</i> have any <i>non</i>tangential proper parts (see #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion).  This collection is coextensional with the collection-difference of #$SemiProperSpaceRegion and #$ProperSpaceRegion (q.v.).\n<p>\nNote that #$ScatteredSpaceRegion is a specialization of #$StrictlySemiProperSpaceRegion in #$RCCWithAtomicRegionsVocabularyMt.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab157).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab157,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab157,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab157,11806).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab157,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab157,[]).
x_comment(x_skinOfSpaceRegion,"A binary predicate that relates a space region (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion) to its \"skin\" in the sense used in the extension of #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory in which atoms are introduced (see #$RCCWithAtomicRegionsMt).  Intuitively, the skin of a space region can be thought of as its one-atom-thick outermost layer or external surface.\n<p>\nMore precisely, <code>(#$skinOfSpaceRegion SKIN REGION)</code> means that, for any space region <b>ANYREGION</b>, <b>ANYREGION</b> is connected to (see #$connectedSpaceRegions) to <b>SKIN</b> if and only if <b>ANYREGION</b> is connected to an #$AtomicSpaceRegion that is a #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion <b>REGION</b>. \n<p> \nSee also the corresponding function #$SkinOfSpaceRegionFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab158).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab158,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab158,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab158,11809).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab158,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab158,[]).
x_comment(x_identityPreservedUnder,"A binary predicate and specialization of #$closedUnder that relates a given #$SetOrCollection to any unary function that behaves as an identity function on it.  <code>(#$identityPreservedUnder SETORCOL FUNC)</code> means that <code>FUNC</code> takes each element <code>ELEM</code> of <code>SETORCOL</code> to <code>ELEM</code> itself.\n<p>\nFor example, #$RoundDownFn is an identity function on #$Integer but not on #$RationalNumber; #$IdentityFn is an identity function on #$Thing.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab159).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab159,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab159,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab159,11814).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab159,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab159,[]).
x_comment(x_ScatteredSpaceRegion,"A specialization of #$DisconnectedSpaceRegion (q.v.) and (in #$RCCWithAtomicRegionsVocabularyMt) #$StrictlySemiProperSpaceRegion (q.v.).  This is the collection of scattered, or \"totally disconnected\", space regions.  A homogeneous extended space region is an instance of #$ScatteredSpaceRegion if and only if (i) it is a #$DisconnectedSpaceRegion and (ii) is such that each of its parts (see #$partOfSpaceRegion) is itself either a scattered region or an #$AtomicSpaceRegion (q.v.).\n<p>\nWhether a given space region is considered as a #$ScatteredSpaceRegion or merely as a #$DisconnectedSpaceRegion may be a matter of context.  For example, with respect to a map on which the stage-cities of the <i>Tour de France</i> are marked with colored dots, the spatial sum of the cities might be viewed as a scattered region; but the French postal service is more likely to view that sum of cities as a partly disconnected region made up of various #$ProperSpaceRegions.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab15a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab15a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab15a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab15a,11817).
