x_comment('x_partOfSpaceRegion-Inverse',"An #$RCCBinaryPredicate (q.v.) and the inverse of #$partOfSpaceRegion (q.v.).  <code>(#$partOfSpaceRegion-Inverse REGION SUBREGION)</code> means that <code>REGION</code> has <code>SUBREGION</code> as a part, in the sense that every #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion that connects (see #$connectedSpaceRegions) with <code>SUBREGION</code> connects with <code>REGION</code>. \n<p>\n#$partOfSpaceRegion-Inverse is \"partitioned into\" the three specializations: #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse, #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse and\n#$identicalSpaceRegions.  \n<p>\nNote that #$partOfSpaceRegion-Inverse is the relation called <i>P<sup>-1</sup></i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab169).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab169,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
