x_comment(x_cycLIntroduced,"An expression of the form (#$cycLIntroduced  EDIT EXPRESSION) means that the quoted #$CycLExpression EXPRESSION is brought into the instance of #$EditingAnElectronicDocument EDIT at some point after the start of the event.  For instance, during an instance of #$UsingTheQueryLibraryTool, a user might edit the query query (#$isa #$Muffet ?TYPE) to replace the #$CycLVariable ?TYPE with the #$CycLConstant #$Dog.  In that event, #$Dog would play the role of #$cycLIntroduced.  Since instances of #$CycLExpression are abstract and, so, cannot be created or destroyed, this predicate allows us to refer to the expression itself via quotation.  Contrast with #$cycLInputs.  In the example case of editing the query, the #$CycLExpression (#$isa #$Muffet ?TYPE) would play the role of #$cycLInputs since it was an actor from the very beggining of the process. ") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab170).
