x_comment('x_nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse',"An asymmetric transitive #$RCCBinaryPredicate-BaseEight that is a specialization of #$properPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse and the inverse (see #$elInverse) of #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion (q.v.).  <code>(#$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that (i) <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> are space regions (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegions) of the same dimensionality (see #$spatiallyEquidimensional), (ii) <code>REGION1</code> has <code>REGION2</code> as a proper part, and (iii) there is <i>no</i> space region that externally connects with (see #$externallyConnectedSpaceRegions) both <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code>.\n<p>\nFor example, the space occupied by the US has that occupied by Oklahoma as a non-tangential proper part, but has the space occupied by Texas as a <i>tangential</i> proper part (see #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse).\n<p>\nNote that #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse and #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse together make a partition of #$properPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse.\n<p>\nNote also that #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion is the relation called <i>NTPP<sup>-1</sup></i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab19a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab19a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab19a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab19a,11918).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab19a,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab19a,[]).
x_comment('x_tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse',"An asymmetric #$RCCBinaryPredicate-BaseEight that is a specialization of #$properPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse and the inverse (see #$elInverse) of #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion (q.v.).  <code>(#$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that (i) <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> are space regions (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegions) of the same dimensionality (see #$spatiallyEquidimensional), (ii) <code>REGION1</code> has <code>REGION2</code> as a proper part, and (iii) there is some space region that externally connects with (see #$externallyConnectedSpaceRegions) both <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code>.\n<p>\nFor example, the space occupied by the US has that occupied by Texas as a tangential proper part, but has that occupied by Oklahoma as a <i>non-</i>tangential proper part.\n<p>\nNote that #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse and #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse together make a partition of #$properPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse. \n<p>\nNote also that #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion is the relation called <i>TPP<sup>-1</sup></i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab19b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab19b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
