x_comment(x_dateOfDeathEvent,"#$dateOfDeathEvent is a predicate which is intended to be as neutral as possible with respect to various views regarding  life after death and reincarnation.\n<p>\nThere are three main sorts of things, as well as subabstractions of them, which might be said to have a date of death: entities which are Organisms-Whole, entities which are some sort of spiritual thing, and entities which are some kind of composite of the two. In all three cases, the #$dateOfDeathEvent will be the date at which the #$Organism-Whole, or the associated #$Organism-Whole, undergoes a #$Dying event. The #$dateOfDeathEvent of a subabstraction of any of the three would be the #$dateOfDeathEvent of the entity of which it is a subabstraction.\n<p>\nIn #$NaturalismMt only organisms can have a date of death; and every organism\nhas a single such date.\n<p>\nThere are different rules in #$SpiritualistMt.  In the case of resurrection, an organism can have multiple #$dateOfDeathEvents, but only a single birth event.  In the case of life after death, a soul exists past the death of a body in which it is incarnated.  In the case of reincarnation, a spiritual entity can have multiple #$dateOfDeathEvents, at least one for each incarnation.\n<p>\n#$dateOfDeathEvent jibes with common sense talk about death, wherein believers in life after death are willing to assert both that Grandpa is in heaven and that Grandpa died on such and such a date.  Of course, this relates to metonomy between the organism, the body, and the soul.  The assertions mean that Grandpa's soul is in heaven, while his body and the Homo sapiens that used to be identified with Grandpa are both dead.\n<p>\nNote the difference between this predicate and #$dateOfDeath, which ascribes to entities their #$endingDate.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab1e8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab1e8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab1e8,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab1e8,12015).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab1e8,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab1e8,[]).
