x_comment(x_WaterPoweredMill,"Each #$WaterPoweredMill is a building or group of buildings whose main purpose is the production of a more refined/usable product from raw materials, and whose power comes from gravity's action on water.  Such mills will have a waterwheel as a part, and a mechanism for diverting/directing water from a stream or pond to the waterwheel.  The water is caught by compartments on the waterwheel, and the weight of the water causes the wheel to turn, which drives a driveshaft that can be used to grind, squeeze, or operate mechanical devices such as looms or forge bellows.  In modern cultures, water mills have been replaced by first steam, then coal, and now electrically-powered mills that perform these functions and many more, but water power is still used in some parts of the world.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab28c).
