x_comment(x_ComponentCardinalityOfSpaceRegionFn,"A unary function that takes a given space region (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion) to the number of \"maximally connected\" component parts it has.  (#$ComponentCardinalityOfSpaceRegionFn <b>REGION</b>) is the positive integer <b>N</b> such that there are exactly <b>N</b> distinct #$ConnectedSpaceRegions (q.v.) that are component parts of <b>REGION</b> (see #$componentPartOfSpaceRegion).  In particular, <b>N</b>=1 if and only if <b>REGION</b> is an instance of #$ConnectedSpaceRegion, and <b>N</b>>1 if and only if <b>REGION</b> is an instance of #$DisconnectedSpaceRegion (q.v.).\n<p>\nSee the corresponding predicate #$componentCardinalityOfSpaceRegion.  Also see the related function #$AtomicCardinalityOfSpaceRegionFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab2cc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab2cc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab2cc,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab2cc,12263).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab2cc,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab2cc,[]).
x_comment(x_componentCardinalityOfSpaceRegion,"A binary predicate that relates a given space region (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion) to the number of \"maximally connected\" component parts it has.  <code>(#$componentCardinalityOfSpaceRegion REGION N)</code> means that there are exactly <code>N</code> distinct #$ConnectedSpaceRegions (q.v.) that are component parts of <code>REGION</code> (see #$componentPartOfSpaceRegion).  In particular, <code>N</code>=1 if and only if <code>REGION</code> is an instance of #$ConnectedSpaceRegion, and <code>N</code>>1 if and only if <code>REGION</code> is an instance of #$DisconnectedSpaceRegion (q.v.).\n<p>\nCompare this predicate with the related predicate\n#$atomicCardinalityOfSpaceRegion (defined in the #$RCCWithAtomicRegionsMt).  Note that if <code>(#$atomicCardinalityOfSpaceRegion REGION M)</code>, then it is always the case that <code>M</code> is greater than or equal to <code>N</code> (as given above), with <code>M=N</code> if and only if <code>REGION</code> is an instance of #$AtomicSpaceRegion (where <code>M=N=1</code>) or <code>REGION</code> is an instance of #$ScatteredSpaceRegion (where <code>M=N</code>>1).\n<p>\nSee also the corresponding function #$ComponentCardinalityOfSpaceRegionFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab2cd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab2cd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab2cd,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab2cd,12266).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab2cd,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab2cd,[]).
x_comment(x_atomicCardinalityOfSpaceRegion,"A binary predicate that relates a given space region (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion) to the number of \"atoms\" it has as parts.  <code>(#$atomicCardinalityOfSpaceRegion REGION N)</code> means that there are exactly <code>N</code> distinct #$AtomicSpaceRegions (q.v.) that are parts of <code>REGION</code> (see #$partOfSpaceRegion).  In particular, <code>N</code> =1 if and only if <code>REGION</code> is an instance of #$AtomicSpaceRegion, and <code>N</code> >1 if and only if <code>REGION</code> is an instance of #$CompositeSpaceRegion (q.v.).\n<p>\nCompare this predicate with the related predicate\n#$componentCardinalityOfSpaceRegion.  Note that if <code>(#$componentCardinalityOfSpaceRegion REGION M)</code>, then it is always the case that <code>N</code> (as given above) is greater than or equal to <code>M</code>, with <code>M = N</code> if and only if <code>REGION</code> is an instance of #$AtomicSpaceRegion (where <code>M = N = 1</code>) or <code>REGION</code> is an instance of #$ScatteredSpaceRegion (where <code>M = N</code> > 1).\n<p>\nSee also the corresponding function #$AtomicCardinalityOfSpaceRegionFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab2ce).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab2ce,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab2ce,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab2ce,12272).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab2ce,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab2ce,[]).
x_comment(x_AtomicCardinalityOfSpaceRegionFn,"A unary function that takes a given space region (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion) to the number of \"atoms\" it has as parts.  (#$AtomicCardinalityOfSpaceRegionFn <b>REGION</b>) is the positive integer <b>N</b> such that there are exactly <b>N</b> distinct #$AtomicSpaceRegions (q.v.) that are parts of <b>REGION</b> (see #$partOfSpaceRegion).  In particular, <b>N</b> =1 if and only if <b>REGION</b> is an instance of #$AtomicSpaceRegion, and <b>N</b> >1 if and only if <b>REGION</b> is an instance of #$CompositeSpaceRegion (q.v.).\n<p>\nSee this function's corresponding predicate #$atomicCardinalityOfSpaceRegion.  And compare this function to the related function #$ComponentCardinalityOfSpaceRegionFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab2cf).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab2cf,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab2cf,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
