x_comment(x_directSpaceRegionSum,"A ternary predicate that relates a pair of mutually discrete space regions to their mereological sum or union in the sense of #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.  <code>(#$directSpaceRegionSum SUM REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that (i) <code>SUM</code> is the sum (see #$spaceRegionSum)\nof <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> and (ii) <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> are discrete from each other (see #$discreteSpaceRegions).\n<p>\nNote that this predicate is an #$ELRelation (q.v.) whose #$expansion is given in terms of #$spaceRegionSum and #$discreteSpaceRegions.  See also the\ncorresponding function #$DirectSpaceRegionSumFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab2f3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab2f3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab2f3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
