x_comment(x_typedGenlPredsWRTQuotedArgs,"An instance of #$TaxonomicPredicateForPredicates that is a specialization of #$genlPredsWRTQuotedArgs, bearing a relationship to that predicate that is analogous to the relationship between #$typedGenlPreds and #$genlPreds.  #$typedGenlPredsWRTQuotedArgs is used to express a #$typedGenlPreds -like relationship between a predicate SPEC-PRED that has at least one quoted argument place (see #$quotedArgument) and a predicate GENL-PRED of the same arity that<br><br> 1) has argIsa/argGenl constraints that are at least as general as those of SPEC-PRED,<br><br> 2) is <i>not</i> quoted in at least one of the argument places in which SPEC-PRED is, and<br><br>  3) is <i>only</i> quoted in argument places in which SPEC-PRED is also quoted.  <p>As such, GENL-PRED need not have any quoted argument places.  <p>In (#$typedGenlPredsWRTQuotedArgs SPEC-PRED GENL-PRED SET), SET is the set of integers that correspond to quoted argument places in SPEC-PRED that are <i>not</i> quoted in GENL-PRED, thereby indicating a recipe for deriving a sentence SPEC-SENT whose arg0 is SPEC-PRED from a sentence GENL-SENT whose arg0 is GENL-PRED:  First, each argument ARG in GENL-SENT occuring in the Nth argument place, where N is neither 0 nor a member of LIST, will occur in the Nth argument place in SPEC-SENT if and only if ARG meets the Nth argument constraints of SPEC-PRED.  All other non-0 arguments OTHER-ARGS in GENL-SENT, which by definition occur in the Mth argument place, where M is an element of SET, will appear as explicitly quoted arguments in SPEC-SENT, in those same argument places, just in case OTHER-ARGS meets the quoted argument constraints of the Mth argument place in SPEC-PRED.  For example,\n<pre>\n   (#$typedGenlPredsWRTQuotedArgs #$cycLActors #$situationConstituents (#$TheSet 2))\n</pre>\nentails that whenever\n<pre>\n   (#$situationConstituents WritingACommentForHashDollarDog\n       (#$Quote #$Dog))\n</pre>\nholds,\n<pre>\n   (#$cycLActors WritingACommentForHashDollarDog #$Dog)\n</pre>\nfollows.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab364).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab364,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab364,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab364,12449).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab364,[]).
