x_comment('x_intervalOfTypeLiesBetween-Inclusive',"<code>(#$intervalOfTypeLiesBetween-Inclusive INTERVAL TYPE EARLY LATE)</code> means that the instance of #$TimeInterval <code>INTERVAL</code> is an interval of type <code>TYPE</code> that is subsumed by (c.f., #$temporallySubsumes) the interval started by (c.f., #$temporallyStartedBy) the earliest interval of <code>TYPE</code> that temporally intersects (c.f., #$temporallyIntersects) the instance of #$TemporalThing <code>EARLY</code>, and finished by (see #$temporallyFinishedBy) the latest interval of <code>TYPE</code> that temporally intersects the instance of #$TemporalThing <code>LATE</code>.  For example,\n<pre>   (#$intervalOfTypeLiesBetween-Inclusive\n           (#$MonthFn #$June (#$YearFn 1990)) #$CalendarMonth\n           (#$DayFn 4 (#$MonthFn #$January (#$YearFn 1968))) #$Now)\n</pre>\nmeans that the June 1990 is one of the instances of #$CalendarMonth that occurs during the interval formed from the first month that intersects (#$DayFn 4 (#$MonthFn #$January (#$YearFn 1968))) -- namely January 1968 -- and the last month that, as you read this, intersects the referent of the indexical #$Now.  <p>Note that though in the above example, <code>EARLY</code> and <code>LATE</code> are both instances of #$TimeInterval, <code>EARLY</code> and <code>LATE</code> can be any instance of #$TemporalThing for which a temporally intersecting interval of TYPE can be found: \n<pre>   (#$intervalOfTypeLiesBetween-Inclusive\n           (#$YearFn 1945) #$CalendarYear\n           (#$EndFn #$WorldWarII)\n           (#$OrganizationFoundingFn #$LebaneseHizballah))\n</pre>means that the year 1945 is an instance of #$CalendarYear subsumed by the interval started by the year 1945 (the year in which WWII ended) and finished by the year 1982 (the year in which Hizballah was founded).  Similarly, \n<pre>   (#$intervalOfTypeLiesBetween-Inclusive\n           (#$YearFn 1945) #$CalendarYear #$WorldWarII\n           (#$OrganizationFoundingFn #$LebaneseHizballah))\n</pre>means that 1945 is a year that lies between the years 1939 and 1983.  See also #$intervalOfTypeLiesBetween-Exclusive.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab3e9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab3e9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab3e9,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab3e9,12652).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab3e9,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab3e9,[]).
x_comment(x_SomeUseRights,"A specialization of #$Situation. Each instance of this collection is a situation that consists of someone having some use rights to an object. See the comments on #$ExclusiveUserRights and #$SituationTypeByUserRights for a fuller explanation of how this is cashed out. #$SomeUseRights is a very general instance of #$SituationTypeByUserRights that means that a user has some, as opposed to no, right to use of an object or facility. In most cases, a more specific #$SituationTypeByUserRights (q.v.) can be used.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab3ea).
