x_comment('x_geometricallyInsideSpaceRegion-Open',"A binary predicate and specialization of #$geometricallyInsideSpaceRegion (q.v.) that relates two space regions (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion) when the first is geometrically-inside the second and there is an open channel from the first to the outside of the second.  \n<p>\nMore precisely, <code>(#$geometricallyInsideSpaceRegion-Open INSIDE REGION)</code> holds if and only if (i) <code>(#$geometricallyInsideSpaceRegion INSIDE REGION)</code> holds) and (ii) the mereological sum of the inside of and the outside of <code>REGION</code> is strongly-connected, i.e. this holds:\n<pre>\n  (#$isa \n    (#$SpaceRegionSumFn \n      (#$InsideOfSpaceRegionFn <code>REGION</code>) \n      (#$OutsideOfSpaceRegionFn <code>REGION</code>))\n    #$StronglyConnectedSpaceRegion) .\n</pre>\nFor example, if a ball is resting inside a baseball glove, the space region occupied by the ball is #$geometricallyInsideSpaceRegion-Open the space region occupied by the glove.\n<p>\nCf. #$geometricallyInsideSpaceRegion-Closed.\n<p>\nNote that #$geometricallyInsideSpaceRegion-Open is the relation called <i>GEO-INSIDE-OPEN</i> in #$ASpatialLogicBasedOnRegionsAndConnection-Article.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab3ec).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab3ec,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab3ec,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab3ec,12669).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab3ec,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab3ec,[]).
