x_comment(x_NullSpaceRegion,"A specialization of #$HomogeneousSpaceRegion and #$PositiveDimensionalThing (qq.v.).  #$NullSpaceRegion is the collection of \"null spatial regions\".  There is at most one known instance of #$NullSpaceRegion with respect to any context in which some #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegions (q.v.) are known to have locations, either absolutely or relatively (see #$LocationalPredicate and its immediate specializations).\n<p>\nEach #$NullSpaceRegion is of some particular positive number of dimensions (see #$SpatialThingTypeByNumberOfDimensions).  See the specializations #$NullSpaceRegion-1D, #$NullSpaceRegion-2D, and #$NullSpaceRegion-3D.  By definition, a null space region of a given dimensionality is disconnected from (see #$disconnectedSpaceRegions) every homogeneous space region of that same dimensionality (see #$spatiallyEquidimensional).\n<p>\nThe introduction of null regions into #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory allows the functions #$SpaceRegionComplementFn, #$SpaceRegionProductFn, and #$SpaceRegionDifferenceFn to be defined as #$TotalFunctions.  For example, #$SpaceRegionComplementFn can then be defined on #$UniversalSpaceRegions (q.v.), and #$SpaceRegionProductFn can be defined for pairs of regions that are #$discreteSpaceRegions (q.v.).  (For more details, see the rules on the above functions.)") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab3fd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab3fd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab3fd,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab3fd,12725).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab3fd,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab3fd,[]).
x_comment(x_PolyDimensionalThing,"A #$SpatialThingTypeByDimensionality and a specialization of #$PositiveDimensionalThing.  Each instance of #$PolyDimensionalThing is a spatial thing that has a dimensionality of two or higher, and thus is either a two- or three- (or higher-) dimensional spatial object.  \n<p>\nExamples of #$PolyDimensionalThings include tangible or intangible spatially-localized polydimensional objects, such as the flat surface of a tabletop and the table itself, as well as abstract geometrical objects that are at least two-dimensional, such as a Platonic cube.  Specializations of this collection include #$PartiallyTangible, #$BilateralObject, and #$TwoDimensionalGeometricThing.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab3fe).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab3fe,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab3fe,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab3fe,12730).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab3fe,[]).
