x_comment(x_SpaceRegionProductFn,"A binary function that takes a pair of space regions (see #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegion) of the same dimensionality (see #$spatiallyEquidimensional)to their mereological product or intersection in the sense of #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.  (#$SpaceRegionProductFn <b>REG1 REG2</b>) is the unique #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegion <b>PROD</b> such that any region connects with (see #$connectedSpaceRegions) <b>PROD</b> if and only if it connects with some region <b>REGION</b> such that <b>REGION</b> is a part of (see #$partOfSpaceRegion) both <b>REG1</b> and <b>REG2</b>. \n<p>\nSee the corresponding predicate #$spaceRegionProduct.  Also see #$SpaceRegionSumFn and #$SpaceRegionDifferenceFn.\n<p>\nNote that #$SpaceRegionProductFn is the function called <i>prod</i> in #$ASpatialLogicBasedOnRegionsAndConnection-Article.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab406).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab406,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
