x_comment(x_spaceRegionProduct,"A ternary predicate that relates a pair of space regions (see #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegion) of the same dimensionality (see #$spatiallyEquidimensional) to their mereological product or intersection in the sense of #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.  <code>(#$spaceRegionProduct PROD REG1 REG2)</code> means that <code>PROD</code> is the unique space region such that any region connects with (see #$connectedSpaceRegions) <code>PROD</code> if and only if it connects with some region <code>REGION</code> such that <code>REGION</code> is a part of (see #$partOfSpaceRegion) both <code>REG1</code> and <code>REG2</code>. \n<p>\nSee the corresponding function #$SpaceRegionProductFn.  Also see #$spaceRegionSum and #$spaceRegionDifference.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab40b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab40b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
