x_comment(x_symmetricSpaceRegionDifference,"A ternary predicate that relates a pair of space regions (see #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegion) of the same dimensionality (see #$spatiallyEquidimensional) to their \"symmetric difference\".  <code>(#$symmetricSpaceRegionDifference SYMDIFF REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that <code>SYMDIFF</code> is the mereological difference (see #$spaceRegionDifference)\nbetween the sum (see #$spaceRegionSum) of <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> and the product (see #$spaceRegionProduct) of <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code>.\n<p>\nCurrently, this predicate is an #$ELRelation whose #$expansion given in terms of\n#$spaceRegionDifference, #$spaceRegionProduct, and #$spaceRegionSum.\n<p>\nSee also the corresponding function #$SymmetricSpaceRegionDifferenceFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab414).
