x_comment(x_identicalSpaceRegions,"An equivalence relation and a #$RCCBinaryPredicate-BaseEight (q.v.) that is a specialization of both #$cospatial and #$equals.  <code>(#$identicalSpaceRegions REGION1 REGION2)</code> holds if and only if <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> are space regions (see #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegions) such that (i) <code>REGION1</code> is a part of (see #$partOfSpaceRegion) <code>REGION2</code> and (ii) <code>REGION2</code> is a part of <code>REGION1</code>.  Thus, #$identicalSpaceRegions is the #$equals relation restricted to space regions.\n<p>\nNote that #$identicalSpaceRegions is the relation called \"=\" in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab415).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab415,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab415,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab415,12816).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab415,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab415,[]).
x_comment('x_properPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse',"An asymmetric transitive #$RCCBinaryPredicate (q.v.) that is a specialization of #$partOfSpaceRegion-Inverse and the <i>inverse</i> of #$properPartOfSpaceRegion (q.v.).  <code>(#$properPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse REGION SUBREGION)</code> means that <code>SUBREGION</code> and <code>REGION</code> are space regions (see #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegions) of the same dimensionalty (see #$spatiallyEquidimensional) such that <code>REGION</code> has <code>SUBREGION</code> as a part, but <code>SUBREGION</code> does <i>not</i> have <code>REGION</code> as a part.  It follows that <code>REGION</code> and <code>SUBREGION</code> are not identical (see #$identicalSpaceRegions). \n<p>\nFor example, the space region occupied by the US has that occupied by Texas as a proper part, but does <i>not</i> have itself as a proper part.\n<p>\n#$properPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse is \"partitioned into\" the two specializations #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse and #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse.\n<p>\nNote that #$properPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse is the relation called <i>PP<sup>-1</sup></i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab416).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab416,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab416,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab416,12819).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab416,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab416,[]).
x_comment(x_properPartOfSpaceRegion,"An asymmetric transitive #$RCCBinaryPredicate (q.v.) that is a specialization of #$partOfSpaceRegion (q.v.).  <code>(#$properPartOfSpaceRegion SUBREGION REGION)</code> means that <code>SUBREGION</code> and <code>REGION</code> are space regions (see #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegions) of the same dimensionalty (see #$spatiallyEquidimensional) such that <code>SUBREGION</code> is a part of <code>REGION</code>, but <code>REGION</code> is <i>not</i> a part of <code>SUBREGION</code>.  It follows that <code>SUBREGION</code> and <code>REGION</code> are not identical (see #$identicalSpaceRegions). \n<p>\nFor example, the space occupied by Texas is a proper part of that occupied by the US, but is <i>not</i> a proper part of itself.\n<p>\n#$properPartOfSpaceRegion is \"partitioned into\" the two specializations #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion and #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion.  See also #$properPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse.\n<p>\nNote that #$properPartOfSpaceRegion is the relation called <i>PP</i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab417).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab417,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab417,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab417,12826).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab417,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab417,[]).
x_comment(x_overlappingSpaceRegions,"A reflexive and symmetric #$RCCBinaryPredicate that is a specialization of both #$connectedSpaceRegions and #$spatiallyIntersects.  <code>(#$overlappingSpaceRegions REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> are space regions (see #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegions) of the same dimensionalty (see #$spatiallyEquidimensional) that have a common part (see #$partOfSpaceRegion).  \n<p>\n#$overlappingSpaceRegions is \"partitioned into\" three of its immediate specializations: #$partiallyOverlappingSpaceRegions, #$partOfSpaceRegion, and #$partOfSpaceRegion-Inverse.\n<p>\nFor example, the space regions respectively occupied by #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica and the Sonoron desert (which straddles the US and Mexico)\nare overlapping, while those of the US and #$Mexico are not.\n<p>\nThe contrary predicate (see #$negationPreds) of #$overlappingSpaceRegions is #$discreteSpaceRegions.\n<p>\nNote that #$overlappingSpaceRegions is the relation called <i>O</i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab418).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab418,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab418,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab418,12833).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab418,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab418,[]).
x_comment(x_rcc8RelationHoldsBetween,"A ternary predicate that relates an #$RCCBinaryPredicate-BaseEight (q.v.) predicate to two #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegions (q.v.).  <code>(#$rcc8RelationHoldsBetween RCC8PRED REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that <code>RCC8PRED</code> holds between <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code>.\n<p>\nNote that there is <i>exactly one</i> instance of #$RCCBinaryPredicate-BaseEight that holds between any two instances of #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegion in the\n#$UniversalSpaceRegion (q.v.) of a given context.  Hence, this predicate could be useful for writing rules for a theory of topological state changes.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab419).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab419,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab419,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab419,12843).
