x_comment(x_connectedSpaceRegions,"A reflexive and symmetric #$RCCBinaryPredicate that is a specialization of both #$touches-Directly and #$spatiallyEquidimensional, (qq.v.).  #$connectedSpaceRegions is the primitive relation of connection in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.  Intuitively, <code>(#$connectedSpaceRegions REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> are space regions (see #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegions) of the same dimensionality that either touch or overlap.  \n<p>\nAll fifteen #$RCCBinaryPredicates are defined, ultimately, in terms of  #$connectedSpaceRegions.  Of these fifteen, the eight mutually-exclusive and jointly-exhaustive <i>basic</i> relations defined in the RCC8 theory (see #$RCCBinaryPredicate-BaseEight) describe <i>degrees of connectedness</i> between regions.  (Seven of the eight base relations are specializations of #$connectedSpaceRegions; the remaining relation, #$disconnectedSpaceRegions, is defined as the relative complement or #$negationPreds of #$connectedSpaceRegions.)  \n\n  \n<p>\n#$connectedSpaceRegions is denoted by \"C\" in #$ASpatialLogicBasedOnRegionsAndConnection-Article.\n<p>\nSee also the specializations #$externallyConnectedSpaceRegions and #$overlappingSpaceRegions.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab41a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab41a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab41a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab41a,12847).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab41a,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab41a,[]).
x_comment(x_disconnectedSpaceRegions,"An irreflexive and symmetric #$RCCBinaryPredicate-BaseEight (q.v.) that is a specialization of both #$discreteSpaceRegions and #$spatiallySeparated.  #$disconnectedSpaceRegions holds between certain #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegions that are #$spatiallyEquidimensional (qq.v.).  <code>(#$disconnectedSpaceRegions REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> are not connected (cf. #$connectedSpaceRegions).  Thus, they neither intersect (cf. #$overlappingSpaceRegions) nor touch (cf. #$externallyConnectedSpaceRegions).\n<p>\nFor example, the space regions respectively occupied by #$Canada and #$Mexico are mutually disconnected, while those occupied by #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica and #$Mexico are not.\n<p>\nNote that #$disconnectedSpaceRegions is the relation called <i>DC</i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab41b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab41b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab41b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab41b,12856).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab41b,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab41b,[]).
x_comment(x_discreteSpaceRegions,"An irreflexive and symmetric #$RCCBinaryPredicate that is a specialization of both #$spatiallyDisjoint and #$spatiallyEquidimensional.  <code>(#$discreteSpaceRegions REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> are space regions (see #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegions) of the same dimensionality that do not spatially overlap (cf. #$overlappingSpaceRegions).  Thus, they are either spatially separated (see #$disconnectedSpaceRegions) or touching (see #$externallyConnectedSpaceRegions).\n<p>\nFor example, the space regions respectively occupied by #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica and #$Mexico are discrete, while those of the US and Sonoron desert (which straddles the US and Mexico) are not.\n<p>\nNote that #$discreteSpaceRegions is the relation called <i>DR</i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab41c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab41c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab41c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab41c,12861).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab41c,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab41c,[]).
x_comment(x_SkinOfSpaceRegionFn,"A unary function that takes a space region (see #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegion) to its \"skin\" in the sense used in the extension of #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory in which atoms are introduced (see #$RCCWithAtomicRegionsMt).  Intuitively, the skin of a space region can be thought of as its one-atom-thick outermost layer or external surface.\n<p>\nMore precisely, (#$SkinOfSpaceRegionFn <b>REGION</b>) is the space region <b>SKIN</b> such that, for any space region <b>ANYREGION</b>, <b>ANYREGION</b> is connected to (see #$connectedSpaceRegions) to <b>SKIN</b> if and only if <b>ANYREGION</b> is connected to an #$AtomicSpaceRegion that is a #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion <b>REGION</b>. \n<p>\nNote that #$SkinOfSpaceRegionFn is #$undefined (q.v.) for atomic space regions and #$NullSpaceRegions. \n<p> \n#$SkinOfSpaceRegionFn is the function called <i>skin</i> in #$ASpatialLogicBasedOnRegionsAndConnection-Article.\n<p>\nSee also the corresponding predicate #$skinOfSpaceRegion.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab41d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab41d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab41d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab41d,12866).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab41d,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab41d,[]).
x_comment(x_convexSpaceRegionOf,"A binary predicate and a specialization of #$convexSpaceRegionSubsuming-Minimal (q.v.) that relates a given #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegion (q.v.) to the minimal #$ConvexSpaceRegion that subsumes it.  <code>(#$convexSpaceRegionOf CONVEX REGION)</code> means that <code>CONVEX</code> is the space region delimited by the \"convex-hull\" or convex-cover of a <code>REGION</code>.\n<p>\nSee also the corresponding function #$ConvexSpaceRegionFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab41e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab41e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab41e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
