x_comment(x_outsideSpaceRegion,"A binary predicate that relates a given space region (see #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegion) to any space region that is \"outside\" it in the sense used in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.\n<p>\nMore precisely, <code>(#$outsideSpaceRegion OUTSIDE REGION)</code> means that <code>OUTSIDE</code> is discrete from (see #$discreteSpaceRegions) the minimal convex space region subsuming <code>REGION</code> (see #$convexSpaceRegionOf). \n<p>\nFor example, the space occupied by the intact shell of a chicken egg at a given  time is #$outsideSpaceRegion the space occupied by the yolk of the egg.\n<p>\nNote that #$outsideSpaceRegion is the relation called <i>OUTSIDE</i>\nin #$ASpatialLogicBasedOnRegionsAndConnection-Article.\n<p>\nSee also #$outsideSpaceRegion-Inverse, #$outsideOfSpaceRegion-Maximal and #$insideSpaceRegion.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab421).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab421,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab421,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
