x_comment(x_Container,"The collection of tangible objects whose primary function (see #$primaryFunction) is to contain something (see #$ContainingSomething).  Note that just about anything can serve as a container without actually being a container.  For example the palm of your hand when cupped may contain some marbles.  But because your palm is not always configured as and does not function primarily as a container, it would not be represented as a #$Container but would rather stand in a particular <i>relation</i> to the marbles via some containment predicate.  To relate contents to the thing containing them (whether or not that thing is a #$Container) use one or more specific predicates indicating the type of containment present (#$in-ContOpen, #$in-ContClosed, #$in-ContFullOf, #$in-Held, #$packagedIn, #$physicallyContains, #$protectiveContains, ...).  If the type of containment is not known use the general predicate #$in-ContGeneric.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab430).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab430,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
