x_comment(x_partiallyInsideSpaceRegion,"A binary #$SpaceRegionPredicate that relates a given space region (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion) to another space region that it is partially (and not completely) \"inside\".  \n<p>\n<code>(#$partiallyInsideSpaceRegion REGION1 REGION2)</code> holds if and only if (i) <code>REGION1</code> is discrete from <code>REGION2</code> (see #$discreteSpaceRegions) and (ii) <code>REGION1</code> partially overlaps (see #$partiallyOverlappingSpaceRegions) with the region delineated by the convex cover of <code>REGION2</code> (see #$convexSpaceRegionOf).  \n<p>\nFor example, the space occupied by the popsicle stick is partially inside the space occupied by the frozen, edible part of the popsicle.\n<p>\nNote that #$partiallyInsideSpaceRegion is the relation called <i>P-INSIDE</i> in #$ASpatialLogicBasedOnRegionsAndConnection-Article.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab437).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab437,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab437,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab437,12959).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab437,[]).
