x_comment('x_partiallyInsideSpaceRegion-Inverse',"A binary #$SpaceRegionPredicate that relates a given space region (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion) to another space region that is partially (and not completely) \"inside\" it.  \nThis predicate is the inverse of #$partiallyInsideSpaceRegion.\n<p>\n<code>(#$partiallyInsideSpaceRegion-Inverse REGION1 REGION2)</code> holds if and only if (i) <code>REGION2</code> is discrete from <code>REGION1</code> (see #$discreteSpaceRegions) and (ii) <code>REGION2</code> partially overlaps (see #$partiallyOverlappingSpaceRegions) with the region delineated by the convex cover of <code>REGION1</code> (see #$convexSpaceRegionOf).  \n<p>\nFor example, the space occupied by the edible part of a popsicle has the space occupied by the popsicle stick partially inside it.\n<p>\nNote that #$partiallyInsideSpaceRegion-Inverse is the relation called <i>P-INSIDE<sup>-1</sup></i> in #$ASpatialLogicBasedOnRegionsAndConnection-Article.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab438).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab438,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
