x_comment('x_LinearObject-Straight',"A specialization of #$LinearObject (q.v.). #$LinearObject-Straight is the collection of all linearly-shaped objects that are more-or-less straight (i.e. not curved), whether tangible or intangible.  \n<p>\nNote that the criterion for being \"straight\" in the present sense varies from context to context.  For example, the standard of straightness for limning a football field is less precise than that for pure geometry.  \n<p>\nImportant geometrical specializations of #$LinearObject-Straight are #$Line-Straight, #$Ray-Geometrical, and #$LineSegment.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab43d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab43d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
