x_comment(x_SpaceRegionComplementFn,"An #$InvertibleFunction (q.v.) that takes a space region to its mereological complement in the sense of #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.  \n<p>\n(#$SpaceRegionComplementFn <b>REGION</b>) is the #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegion <b>COMPLEMENT</b> such that for any such space region <b>SPACE</b> (i) <b>SPACE</b> connects with <b>COMPLEMENT</b> (see #$connectedSpaceRegions) if and only if <b>SPACE</b> is <i>not</i> a nontangential proper part of<b> REGION</b> (see #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion) and (ii) <b>SPACE</b> overlaps <b>COMPLEMENT</b> (see #$overlappingSpaceRegions) if and only if <b>SPACE</b> is not a part of <b>REGION</b> (see #$partOfSpaceRegion).\n<p>\nThe complement of a given #$UniversalSpaceRegion (q.v.) is the #$NullSpaceRegion (q.v.) of the same dimensionality, and vice versa.  The introduction of null space regions allows #$SpaceRegionComplementFn to be defined as a #$TotalFunction.\n<p>\nNote that #$SpaceRegionComplementFn is the function called <i>compl</i> in #$ASpatialLogicBasedOnRegionsAndConnection-Article.  See also the corresponding predicate #$spaceRegionComplement; and cf. #$SpaceRegionComplementOfInFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab44a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab44a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab44a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab44a,13024).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab44a,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab44a,[]).
x_comment(x_spaceRegionComplement,"A symmetric predicate that relates a space region to its mereological complement in the sense of #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.  \n<p>\n<code>(#$spaceRegionComplement COMPLEMENT REGION)</code> holds if and only if, for  any #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegion <code>SPACE</code>, (i) <code>SPACE</code> connects with <code>COMPLEMENT</code> (see #$connectedSpaceRegions) if and only if <code>SPACE</code> is <i>not</i> a nontangential proper part of <code>REGION</code> (see #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion) and (ii) <code>SPACE</code> overlaps <code>COMPLEMENT</code> (see #$overlappingSpaceRegions) if and only if <code>SPACE</code> is not a part of <code>REGION</code> (see #$partOfSpaceRegion).\n<p>\nThe complement of a given #$UniversalSpaceRegion (q.v.) is the #$NullSpaceRegion (q.v.) of the same dimensionality, and vice versa.  The introduction of null space regions allows this predicate's corresponding function, #$SpaceRegionComplementFn, to be defined as a #$TotalFunction.\n<p>\nSee also #$spaceRegionComplementOfIn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab44b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab44b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab44b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
