x_comment('x_LinearObject-Finite',"A specialization of #$LinearObject (q.v.). #$LinearObject-Finite is the collection of all and only linearly-shaped objects that are finite in length.  They might be straight or curved, tangible or intangible.  A finite linear object might have two end points (e.g. a straight line segment), no end points (e.g. a closed curve or simple loop), or one end point (e.g. a loop with a \"tail\").\n<p>\nAn important specialization of #$LinearObject-Finite is #$LineSegment, whose instances are strictly one-dimensional.\n<p>\nCf. #$LinearObject-Infinite.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab57f).
