x_comment(x_StronglyConnectedSpaceRegion,"A specialization of #$ConnectedSpaceRegion (q.v.).  This is the collection of \"strongly connected\" regions in the sense of #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory (q.v.).  A homogeneous extended space region <code>REGION</code> is an instance of #$StronglyConnectedSpaceRegion if and only if (i) <code>REGION</code> is a connected region and (ii) any two homogeneous extended space regions <code>SUB1</code> and <code>SUB2</code> whose sum is <code>REGION</code> are strongly connected to each other (see #$stronglyConnectedSpaceRegions).  That is, there exists a part of <code>SUB1</code> (call it <code>P1</code>) and a part of <code>SUB2</code> (call it <code>P2</code>) such that the #$convexSpaceRegionOf (q.v.) the sum of <code>P1</code> and <code>P2</code> is also a part of <code>REGION</code>.   Intuitively, this means that a strongly-connected region is not the sum of two regions that are point- or edge-connected; there is a \"channel\" between them. \n<p>\nNote that a strongly connected region may be hollow.  For example, a cup occupies a strongly-connected region.  A negative example is the sum of the spaces occupied by two tangentially connected balls, which is connected but not strongly- connected.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab588).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab588,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab588,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
