x_comment(x_ConvexThing,"A specialization of #$SpatiallyContinuousThing (q.v.).  This is the collection of convex spatial things, tangible and intangible.  Each instance <code>CONVEX</code> of #$ConvexThing is such that, for any two points subumed by (see #$spatiallySubsumes) <code>CONVEX</code>, the straight line-segment between those points is itself subsumed by <code>CONVEX</code>.  \n<p>\nFor example, a billiard ball is a convex thing but a boomerang is not; neither is a football (as it's hollow) or a sponge (as it has holes).\n<p>\nSpecializations of #$ConvexThing include #$ConvexSpaceRegion and #$ConvexTangibleObject.  See also the generalization #$StarConvexThing.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab598).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab598,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
