x_comment(x_spatioTemporallyIntersectingEntryFormatInArgs,"An instance of #$SpecificEntryFormatPredicate (q.v.) that is used only with argument-places that are constrained to instances (see #$argIsa) of #$SpatialThing and #$TemporallyExistingThing (q.v.). (#$spatioTemporallyIntersectingEntryFormatInArgs PRED N) means that, for any particular way of fixing the other arguments to PRED besides the Nth, for any two spatio-temporal things such that if either one is taken as the Nth argument to PRED, those spatio-temporal things must be such that they spatially intersect with one another (see #$spatiallyIntersects) and they temporally intersect with one another (see #$temporallyIntersects). That is, if the sequences <... ARGN ...> and <... ARGN-PRIME ...> differ at most in their Nth items and both (PRED ... ARGN ...) and (PRED ... ARGN-PRIME ...) hold, then if (#$argIsa PRED N #$SpatialThing) and (#$argIsa PRED N #$TemporallyExistingThing) then (#$spatiallyIntersects ARGN ARGN-PRIME) holds (i.e. (#$not (#$spatiallyDisjoint ARGN ARGN-PRIME)) holds) and (#$temporallyIntersects ARGN ARGN-PRIME) holds (i.e. (#$not (#$temporallyDisjoint ARGN ARGN-PRIME)) holds).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab5e7).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab5e7,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
