x_comment(x_CotemporalPredicate,"A specialization of #$TemporalExistencePredicate (q.v.).  This is the collection of predicates that are used to make statements that imply the current temporal existence of any of their arguments that happen to be temporal things.  \n<p>\nMore precisely, a predicate <code>PRED</code> is an instance of #$CotemporalPredicate if and only if the following two conditions hold.  (i) If a sentence of the form <code>(PRED ARG<sub>1</sub> ... ARG<sub>N</sub>)</code> is true at a given time <code>T</code>, then any <code>ARG<sub>i</sub></code> (<code>1<=i<=N</code>) that is a #$TemporalThing temporally-subsumes <code>T</code> (see #$temporallySubsumes).  (ii) <code>PRED</code> holds of at least one sequence of arguments that includes at least one instance of #$TemporalThing.\n<p>\n(Condition (ii) above prevents predicates that never hold of temporal things from trivially qualifying as #$CotemporalPredicates. Its practical import is that at least one of <code>PRED</code>'s argument-places must not be type-constrained (see #$argIsa) to any collection that is #$disjointWith #$TemporalThing.)\n<p>\nFor example, #$owns is a #$CotemporalPredicate.  So the sentence <code>(#$owns Nick Spot)</code> with time-index (see #$mtTimeIndex) <code>(#$YearFn 1992)</code> implies (given that Nick and Spot are temporal things) that Nick and Spot were alive throughout 1992.  In contrast, the predicate #$awareOf is <i>not</i> a #$CotemporalPredicate.  The sentence <code>(#$awareOf Fred #$GeorgeWashington)</code>, with the same time-index as above, does <i>not</i> imply <code>(#$temporallySubsumes #$GeorgeWashington (#$YearFn 1992))</code>.\n<p>\nSee also the specialization #$CoexistingObjectsPredicate, the collection of cotemporal predicates <i>all</i> of whose argument-places are constrained (at least) to #$TemporalThing.  And see the predicate #$contemporaryInArg.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab66d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab66d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab66d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab66d,13710).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab66d,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab66d,[]).
