x_comment('x_SurfaceRegion-SemiBounded',"A specialization of #$SurfaceRegion (q.v.).  This is the collection of surfaces that have an infintely long edge and no closed boundaries (such as a perimeter or hole).  More precisely, a surface is an instance of #$SurfaceRegion-SemiBounded if and only if (i) it has a boundary; (ii) its (total) boundary is -- or has a part that is -- spatially-continuous, infinite, and unbounded; and (iii) it is <i>not</i> an instance of #$SurfaceRegion-Bounded (cf.)  A semi-bounded surface might be intangible or (at least in principle) tangible.\n<p>\nFor example, a #$HalfPlane is a semi-bounded surface whose boundary is a #$Line-Straight.  Also, cf. #$SurfaceRegion-Unbounded.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab681).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab681,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
