xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab68a,[]).
x_comment('x_Surface-Empirical',"A specialization of #$Surface and #$SpaceRegion-Empirical (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$Surface-Empirical is a two-dimensional, continuous portion of #$TheSpatialUniverse-Empirical (q.v.).  \n<p>\nNote that a physical object, being three-dimensional, can only be partially located at a #$Surface-Empirical.  An empirical space surface might <i>intersect</i> the space occupied by a physical object, but is never #$cospatial with it.  (Cf. #$SpaceChunk-Empirical.)  The only objects properly localizable at instances of #$Surface-Empirical are intangible objects of two or less dimensions.  For example, the intangible surface that delimits (a) the space occupied by a table and (b) the space above the top surface of the table is an empirical space-surface.\n<p>\nSee also #$LineSegment-Empirical and #$Point-Empirical.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab68b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab68b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab68b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
