x_comment('x_relationExplicitlyInvokesTypeDerivatively-ArgIsa',"<code>(#$relationExplicitlyInvokesTypeDerivatively-ArgIsa RELATION COLL)</code>  means that RELATION has an explicit #$argIsa constraint to a specialization SPEC of COLL.  For example, since <code>(#$arg2Isa #$actionMotives #$Motive)</code>, <code>(#$relationExplicitlyInvokesTypeDerivatively-ArgIsa #$actionMotives #$Motive)</code> holds, since #$actionMotives has an explicit #$argIsa constraint of #$Motive, and <code>(#$genls #$Motive #$Motive)</code>.  Similarly, <code>(#$relationExplicitlyInvokesTypeDerivatively-ArgIsa #$actionMotives #$IntentionalMentalSituation)</code> given the #$argIsa constraint of #$Motive, and the fact that <code>(#$genls #$Motive #$IntentionalMentalSituation)</code> holds.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab6ed).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab6ed,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab6ed,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
