x_comment(x_EllipticalRegion,"A specialization of both #$PlaneFigure and #$RoundObject (qq.v.).  This is the collection of all two-dimensional space regions whose boundaries are #$Ellipses (q.v.).  Geometrically, an elliptical region is an two-dimensional region bounded by a closed curve that is the path of a point that moves so that the sum of its distances from two fixed points (called \"foci\") is constant.  \n<p>\nAn important specialization of #$EllipticalRegion is #$CircularRegion, the collection of elliptical regions such that the distance between their boundaries' two foci is zero. \n<p>\nCf. #$Ellipsoid.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab6fc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab6fc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
