x_comment(x_RegularPolygonTypeFn,"A unary function that takes a collection of all polygons having a given number of sides to the subcollection containing just the <i>regular</i> (i.e. equilateral and equiangular) polygons with that number of sides.  \n<p>\nWhere <b>N-GON</b> is a #$PolygonTypeByNumberOfSides (q.v.), (#$RegularPolygonTypeFn <b>N-GON</b>) is <b>REG-N-GON</b>: the specialization of <b>N-GON</b> whose instances are all and only the <b>N</b>-sided regular polygonal regions.  <b>REG-N-GON</b> is thus the \"intersection\" of <b>N-GON</b> and #$RegularPolygon (q.v.).  For example, (#$RegularPolygonTypeFn #$Quadrilateral) is #$Square.  \n<p>\nSee also #$EquilateralPolygon and #$EquiangularPolygon.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab70a).
