x_comment(x_fieldValue,"Let INDEXICAL denote a #$PhysicalFieldIndexical, and VALUE denote a #$KSID.  Then (#$fieldValue INDEXICAL VALUE) is true precisely if the value of the physical field referred to by INDEXICAL is VALUE in some row of some knowledge source in which the physical field is defined.  INDEXICAL is associated with a particular physical field using the predicate #$indexicalForPhysicalField, this physical field is associated with a physical schema using the predicate #$physicalFields, and the physical schema is associated with a structured knowledge source using the predicate #$physicalSchemaSourceMap.  See also #$rowInSourceClaims, which expresses in CycL (via a conjunction of one or more #$fieldValue literals) one or more specific field values appearing in a row of a structured knowledge source.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab71d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab71d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
