x_comment('x_locatedAtPoint-SurfaceGeographical',"(#$locatedAtPoint-SurfaceGeographical OBJECT GEO-POINT) means that\nOBJECT, an instance of #$SpatialThing-Localized, is geographically located\nat GEO-POINT on the geographical surface of reference. This relation expresses the fact that the geographical location of an extended #$SpatialThing includes some precise point. For non zero\ndimensional objects, if GEO-SPACE is the region of two-dimensional\ngeographical space occupied by OBJECT\n(see #$exactlyLocatedAt-SurfaceGeographical), GEO-POINT is incident in\n(see #$incidentInSpaceRegion) in GEO-SPACE. To locate precisely a point itself, use\n#$exactlyLocatedAt-SurfaceGeographical") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab744).
