x_comment('x_SQLOperatorSyntax-Postfix',"A #$CSQLToSQLTranslationSyntaxDirective which directs the\nCSQL to SQL translator to use operator postfix syntax. This term\nshould appear only within a #$csqlOperatorToSQLOperator assertion. For\nexample, the sentence\n<pre>\n(#$csqlOperatorToSQLOperator #$CSQLFactorialFn \"!\" #$PostgreSQL #$SQLOperatorSyntax-Postfix)\n</pre>\ntells the translator that when translating a literal such as\n(#$CSQLFactorialFn 4) into SQL which is to be evaulated by a\n#$PostgreSQL DBMS, it postfix the operator after its argument(s), so\nthat the resultant SQL literal would be \"4!\".") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab75d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab75d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
