x_comment(x_SQLFunctionSyntax,"A #$CSQLToSQLTranslationSyntaxDirective which directs the\nCSQL to SQL translator to use function syntax. This term should appear\nonly within a #$csqlOperatorToSQLOperator assertion. For example, the\nsentence\n<pre>\n(#$csqlOperatorToSQLOperator #$CSQLSineFn \"sin\" #$PostgreSQL #$SQLFunctionSyntax)\n</pre>\ntells the translator that when translating a literal such as\n(#$CSQLSineFn 1.7323) into SQL which is to be evaulated by a\n#$PostgreSQL DBMS, it should apply function syntax, so that the\nresultant SQL literal would be \"sin(1.7323)\".") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab75e).
