x_comment(x_partiallyOverlappingSpaceRegions,"An irreflexive and symmetric #$RCCBinaryPredicate-BaseEight that is a specialization of #$overlappingSpaceRegions and #$partiallySpatiallyIntersects (qq.v.).  <code>(#$partiallyOverlappingSpaceRegions REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> are space regions (see #$HomogeneousPositiveDimensionalSpaceRegions) of the same dimensionalty (see #$spatiallyEquidimensional) that overlap, but are such that neither is part of the other.  Thus, #$partiallyOverlappingSpaceRegions is logically contrary to (i.e. a #$negationPreds of) both #$partOfSpaceRegion and #$partOfSpaceRegion-Inverse.\n<p>\nFor example, the space region occupied by the Sonoran desert (which straddles the US and Mexico) partially overlaps with that occupied by the US.\n<p>\nNote that #$partiallyOverlappingSpaceRegions is the relation called <i>PO</i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab775).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab775,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab775,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
