x_comment(x_partiallySpatiallyIntersects,"A symmetric, irreflexive #$RelativeLocationalPredicate that is a specialization of #$spatiallyIntersects (q.v.) and a <i>contrary</i> (see #$negationPreds) of #$spatiallySubsumes (q.v.).  <code>(#$partiallySpatiallyIntersects OBJECT1 OBJECT2)</code> means that the spatial extents of <code>OBJECT1</code> and <code>OBJECT2</code> overlap, but only partially, so that neither is completely included in the other.  Thus, there is some part of <code>OBJECT1</code> that is disjoint with <code>OBJECT2</code>, and vice versa.\n<p>\nFor example, the sonoran desert, which straddles the US and Mexico, partially intersects both of those countries.  And the circular regions in a standard Venn diagram partially intersect one another.\n<p>\nSee also the specialization #$partiallyOverlappingSpaceRegions.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab77d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab77d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
