x_comment(x_HomogeneousSpaceRegion,"A specialization of #$SpaceRegion (q.v.).  A space region <code>REGION</code> is an instance of #$HomogeneousSpaceRegion if and only if it is of uniform dimensionality.  That is, for some <code>N</code> >= 0: (i) <code>REGION</code> is <code>N</code>-dimensional, (ii) <code>REGION</code> does not include any protrusion or separated piece that is of a lower dimensionality than <code>N</code>, and (iii) there is no hole in <code>REGION</code> that is of a lower dimensionality than <code>N</code>.  Thus, a two-dimensional space region is homogeneous provided it has no protruding or separated or \"missing\" line(-segment) or point.  \n<p>\nNote that a homogeneous space region might or might not be self-connected (see #$ConnectedSpaceRegion); thus it might consist of two or more mutually-disconnected pieces, as long as each piece is of the same uniform dimensionality.\n<p>\nSpecializations of #$HomogeneousSpaceRegion include #$SpaceChunk, #$Surface, #$Line, and #$Point.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab78c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab78c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab78c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab78c,14403).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab78c,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab78c,[]).
x_comment(x_HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion,"The intersection of #$ExtendedSpaceRegion and #$HomogeneousSpaceRegion (qq.v.); this is the collection of homogeneous extended regions of space.  Each instance <code>REGION</code> of #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion is a portion of a pure space (i.e. a #$SpaceRegion) that (i) has positive spatial extent and (ii) is partwise homogeneous. \n<p>\nCondition (i) above means that <code>REGION</code> is <code>N</code>-dimensional for some <code>N</code> >= 1 (see #$SpatialThingTypeByDimensionality; but cf. #$Point and #$NullSpaceRegion). Condition (ii) means that there is a sense of \"part\" (viz. #$partOfSpaceRegion) such that <code>REGION</code> is constituted wholly of parts that are of the same dimensionality (<code>N</code>) as <code>REGION</code> itself.\n<p>\nNote that in a given context we make the assumption that this collection is coextensional with the collection of all spatial things that connect with (see #$connectedSpaceRegions) the unique #$UniversalSpaceRegion (q.v.) recognized in that context. \n<p>\nSpecializations of #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion include #$ConnectedSpaceRegion, #$CompositeSpaceRegion, and #$GeometricFigure.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab78d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab78d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab78d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab78d,14408).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab78d,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab78d,[]).
