x_comment(x_Cone,"A specialization of both #$ThreeDimensionalGeometricThing and #$RoundObject.  Each instance of #$Cone is a three-dimensional geometric object with a circular base; the rest of the surface of the object is formed by lines joining each point of the periphery of the base to a common vertex.  Examples include both tangible objects (e.g. a solid traffic cone) and intangible space regions (e.g. the space swept out by rotating a particular right triangle about one of its sides).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab79f).
