x_comment(x_EquidimensionalSpatialPredicate,"The collection of polyadic #$SpatialPredicates that are used to relate only spatial things that occupy the same number of dimensions (see #$SpatialThingTypeByNumberOfDimensions).\n<p>\nThe most general <i>binary</i> #$EquidimensionalSpatialPredicate is #$spatiallyEquidimensional.  A notable specialization of this predicate-type is #$RCCBinaryPredicate.\n<p>\nNote that most of the equidimensional spatial predicates currently refied in the Cyc Knowledge Base admit arguments (see #$admittedArgument) of different dimensions, but only <i>hold</i> between arguments that are of the same dimensionality (see e.g. #$connectedSpaceRegions).    Some equidimensional predicates, however, only admit arguments of one particular dimensionality (see e.g. #$parallelLines).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab7b6).
