x_comment(x_normativeSpecificationDescribesSituationType,"The predicate #$normativeSpecificationDescribesSituationType is used to associate instances of #$NormativeSpecification with the sub-collections of #$Situation that are their focal content.  <code>(#$normativeSpecificationDescribesSituationType SPEC TYPE)</code> means that the content of #$NormativeSpecification <code>SPEC</code> is directed at the occurence of an instance of <code>TYPE</code>.  This specification is vague because the attitude which an agent will have toward an instance of <code>TYPE</code> depends on the specialization of #$NormativeSpecification to which <code>SPEC</code> belongs.  For example, if <code>SPEC</code> is an instance of #$NormativeSpecification-Avoidance, then the relevant agents are trying to prevent an instance of TYPE from occurring.  The specification of <code>SPEC</code> can be completed using the predicates #$normativeSpecificationDescribesRoleForInd and #$normativeSpecificationDescribesRoleForType (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab7ba).
