x_comment(x_maximumExtensionParameterOfObject,"This predicate relates an object to the distance that is is largest extent.  For instance (#$maximumExtensionParameterOfObject OBJ DIST)\nmeans that length, height and width and diameter (where applicable)\nare all less than or equal to DIST and one or more of the extensions is equal to\nDIST.  More straightforwardly, we might define this as the length of the longest line segment that passes through the object and whose end points are on the outer surface of the object.  Note that this will often be the length of the object but there are some situations in which the length won't be the greatest extension.  Also note that this predicate does not relate all spatial things to a distance.  For instance, spatially disconnected things would not have a greatest extension.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab7cc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab7cc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
