x_comment(x_predicateLicensesSenseExtensionFromPOSInArgToPOSInArg,"<code>(#$predicateLicensesSenseExtensionFromPOSInArgToPOSInArg PREDICATE POS-1 N POS-2 M)</code> means that PREDICATE, an instance of #$SenseExtendingPredicate, licenses the extension of the sense of some word that denotes arguments appearing in its Nth place to arguments appearing in its Mth place.  For example, \n<pre>\n(#$predicateLicensesSenseExtensionFromArgToArg #$woodTypeOfPlantType #$CountNoun 1 #$MassNoun 2)</pre>\nmeans that for <code>WOOD-TYPE</code> and <code>PLANT-TYPE</code> such that\n<pre>\n(#$woodTypeOfPlantType PLANT-TYPE WOOD-TYPE),</pre>\nthere is likely to be some word(s) that, as a count noun, denotes PLANT-TYPE whose sense can be extended to also denote WOOD-TYPE with a mass noun.  For example, there is a count-noun sense of the word \"redwood\" (see #$Redwood-TheWord) that denotes the tree (c.f., #$RedwoodTree); that the collection of such trees bears the #$woodTypeOfPlantType relation to the collection of samples of wood from such trees, licenses a mass-noun sense extension of \"redwood\" to denote that second collection.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab7d7).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab7d7,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
