x_comment('x_Slope-Vertical',"An instance of #$SlopeTypeByGradientLevel (q.v.) and a specialization of #$Slope-Topographical.  Each instance of #$Slope-Vertical is a region with a slope so great as to be nearly (or absolutely) vertical.  Examples include the faces of #$Cliffs.\n<p>\nNote the the slope (see #$slopeOfRegion) of a absolutely vertical region is actually infinite.  Thus, such regions are better described in terms of the angles (see #$AngularDistance) they make with the horizontal plane.  We stipulate that a \n#$Slope-Vertical makes a 75- to 90-degree angle with the horizontal.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab7e8).
