x_comment(x_productTypeOriginatesIn,"(#$productTypeOriginatesIn PROD-TYPE REGION) relates product types with the regions where the agents who are responsible for designing, financing, and planning the construction of that product type are found.  That is (#$productTypeOriginatesIn PROD-TYPE REGION) significant executive/creative/engineering/financial aspects of production of PROD-TYPE occur in REGION. Thus one would not assert (#$productTypeOriginatesIn #$JapaneseCar #$Texas-State) because mere fabrication of the cars occurs there; the funding and creative aspect happens in Japan.  One would assert  properly (#$productTypeOriginatesIn #$ToyotaCar #$Japan) and and describe their assembly with (#$productTypeManufacturedIn #$ToyotaCar #$Texas-State)") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab7f2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab7f2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab7f2,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab7f2,14655).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab7f2,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab7f2,[]).
x_comment(x_productTypeManufacturedIn,"(#$productTypeManufacturedIn PROD-TYPE REGION) relates product types with the regions where instances of the collection are actually created.  So, REGION is one place where instances of PROD-TYPE actually come into being.  So, a product can be planned and designed in one place, but actually assembled in another.  The predicate #$productTypeManufacturedIn refers to this latter region.  The former relation between a product type and a region is covered by the predicate #$productTypeOriginatesIn. NOTE: there is no direct entailment relationship between these two predicates.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab7f3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab7f3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab7f3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
