x_comment(x_FreeSpaceRegion,"A specialization of #$SpaceChunk-Empirical and #$ConnectedSpaceRegion (qq.v.).  Each instance of  #$FreeSpaceRegion is a connected, three-dimensional region of free (i.e. virtually empty) space located in the empirical universe (see #$TheSpatialUniverse-Empirical).  \n<p>\nNote that the precise meaning of \"free\" or \"empty\" here depends on the context.  In the context of subatomic physics, where \"empty\" is defined as containing no particles, a free space region would be a complete #$Vacuum.  In certain other contexts (e.g. #$AmbientConditionsMt) a free space region would be one occupied by nothing but air (see #$Atmosphere).  An undersea context might treat space regions filled with seawater as free.  \n<p>\nNote also that a #$FreeSpaceRegion is intangible, and not to be confused with the material (if any) that occupies it (cf. #$FreeSpaceContent).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab7f7).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab7f7,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab7f7,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab7f7,14660).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab7f7,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab7f7,[]).
x_comment(x_contentOfFreeSpace,"A specialization of #$exactlyLocatedAt-Spatial (q.v.) that relates a given #$FreeSpaceRegion to the content (if any) that fills it (see #$FreeSpaceContent).  <code>(#$contentOfFreeSpace CONTENT FREESPACE)</code> means that <code>CONTENT</code> is the piece of tangible fluid occupying the <code>FREESPACE</code>.  For example, this predicate relates the #$Air in your livingroom to the free space region subsumed by the interior of the room.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab7f8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab7f8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab7f8,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab7f8,14665).
