x_comment(x_specPredOfPredicateLicensesSenseExtensionFromPOSInArgToPOSInArg,"<code>(#$specPredOfPredicateLicensesSenseExtensionFromPOSInArgToPOSInArg PREDICATE POS-1 N POS-2 M)</code> means that there exists an instance SPECPRED of #$Predicate such that:<br>\n<br>\n<code>(#$genlPreds SPECPRED PREDICATE)</code>, and\n<br><br><code>(#$predicateLicensesSenseExtensionFromPOSInArgToPOSInArg SPECPRED POS-1 N POS-2 M)</code>.<br><br>\nAs such, <code>SPECPRED</code> is an instance of #$SenseExtendingPredicate.  Since the complete extent of #$Predicate is not known, <code>SPECPRED</code> might not be reified in Cyc; #$specPredOfPredicateLicensesSenseExtensionFromPOSInArgToPOSInArg thus allows us to use lexical and commonsense data to hypothesize the existence of a #$SenseExtendingPredicate.  For example, #$conceptuallyRelated is often used to relate two concepts denoted by the same word (e.g., #$Dancing and #$Dance-Party, both of which are denoted by #$Dance-TheWord (with different parts-of-speech).  However, #$conceptuallyRelated serves often as a promissory note, indicating the existence of a more specific relation that hasn't be represented in the KB yet.  If <code>(#$conceptuallyRelated VERB-DENOTATION COUNT-NOUN-DENOTATION)</code> can be proved for enough pairs of values for <code>VERB-DENOTATION</code> and <code>COUNT-NOUN-DENOTATION</code>, this could license concluding\n<pre>\n(#$specPredOfPredicateLicensesSenseExtensionFromPOSInArgToPOSInArg #$conceptuallyRelated #$Verb 1 #$CountNoun 2),</pre> effectively launching a sense-extension hypothesis (c.f., #$SenseExtensionHypothesisMicrotheory) in which there exists a spec-pred of #$conceptuallyRelated that does license this sort of sense-extension.  For more information, see #$predicateLicensesSenseExtensionFromPOSInArgToPOSInArg.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab7fe).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab7fe,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab7fe,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab7fe,14676).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab7fe,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab7fe,[]).
