x_comment(x_between,"An instance of #$RelativeLocationalPredicate.  <code>(#$between THIS THAT MID)</code> means that <code>MID</code> is in the space separating <code>THIS</code> and <code>THAT</code>, and is directly between them.  Depending on the context, \"directly between\" might imply that <code>MID</code> lies on a straight line between <code>THIS</code> and <code>THAT</code>, or that it lies on a great circle between them.\n<p>\nFor the notion of \"betweenness\" along a particular physical path (e.g. Austin is between Dallas and San Antonio on Highway I-35), or on some trajectory, see #$betweenOnPath.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab804).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab804,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
