x_comment(x_wordSenseExtensionBrokeredByPred,"<code>(#$wordSenseExtensionBrokeredByPred WORD SPEECH-PART-1 DENOTATION SPEECH-PART-2 EXTENSION BINARY-PREDICATE)</code> means that the fact that <pre>\n   (#$wordSenseExtension WORD SPEECH-PART-1 DENOTATION SPEECH-PART-2 EXTENSION)</pre> is explained <i>in part</i> by the fact that <pre>\n   (BINARY-PREDICATE ARG1 ARG2)</pre> for some <code>ARG1</code> and <code>ARG2</code> such that \n<pre>\n   (#$denotation WORD ARG1 SPEECH-PART-1 N)</pre> for some N. <p>The reason why this sense extension is only <i>partly</i> explained by the above considerations reflects the fact that due to Cyc's incomplete knowledge, there will be many cases where BINARY-PREDICATE is not an instance of #$SenseExtendingPredicate, and so cannot <i>reliably</i> broker sense extensions from SPEECH-PART-1 to SPEECH-PART-2 for any word denoting one of its arg1s.  Rather, there is a possibly unreified specialization SPEC-PRED of BINARY-PRED (see #$genlPreds) that is an instance of #$SenseExtendingPredicate, and the fact that (SPEC-PRED ARG1 ARG2) fully explains the sense extension in question.  ") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab806).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab806,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab806,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab806,14692).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab806,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab806,[]).
x_comment('x_wordSenseExtensionBrokeredByPred-Inverse',"<code>(#$wordSenseExtensionBrokeredByPred-Inverse WORD SPEECH-PART-1 DENOTATION SPEECH-PART-2 EXTENSION BINARY-PREDICATE)</code> means that the fact that <pre>\n   (#$wordSenseExtension WORD SPEECH-PART-1 DENOTATION SPEECH-PART-2 EXTENSION)</pre> is explained <i>in part</i> by the fact that <pre>\n   (BINARY-PREDICATE ARG1 ARG2)</pre> for some <code>ARG1</code> and <code>ARG2</code> such that \n<pre>\n   (#$denotation WORD ARG2 SPEECH-PART-1 N)</pre> for some N. <p>The reason why this sense extension is only <i>partly</i> explained by the above considerations reflects the fact that due to Cyc's incomplete knowledge, there will be many cases where BINARY-PREDICATE is not an instance of #$SenseExtendingPredicate, and so cannot <i>reliably</i> broker sense extensions from SPEECH-PART-1 to SPEECH-PART-2 for any word denoting one of its arg1s.  Rather, there is a possibly unreified specialization SPEC-PRED of BINARY-PRED (see #$genlPreds) that is an instance of #$SenseExtendingPredicate, and the fact that (SPEC-PRED ARG1 ARG2) fully explains the sense extension in question.  ") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab807).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab807,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab807,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab807,14697).
