x_comment(x_UnicodeDenotingASCIIString,"#$UnicodeDenotingASCIIString is the collection of #$ASCIIString-Standard strings (hence 7-bit clean) that may include valid Cyc Unicode escapes, and hence may denote any string of Unicode characters (see #$UnicodeStringFn).  \n<p>\nCyc's Unicode escapes are of the form &uhhhhhh; where the h's are 2 to 6 hexadecimal digits (0-9, A-F, a-f).  For example,  \"&uA3;\" denotes the \"fancy L\" currency symbol for #$Pound-GreatBritain.\n<p>\nSee http://www.unicode.org/charts/ for the definitive encodings for all Unicode characters.  http://www.htmlhelp.com/reference/html40/entities/ is easier to use, but gives only the more common characters.  Note that the HTML encoding syntax differs slightly from Cyc's, but the hexadecimal values used are identical.  Only hexadecimal format is supported; named entities (e.g. &pound;) are not.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab831).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab831,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
