x_comment(x_governmentOfGeoEntityMembers,"A specialization of #$hasMembers with properties that facilitate efficient reasoning about membership in an instance of #$RegionalGovernment.  #$governmentOfGeoEntityMembers relates an instance of #$Person <code>PERSON</code> in its arg2 to an instance <code>GOVERNMENT</code> of #$RegionalGovernment of which <code>PERSON</code> is a member in one of two ways: Either directly, through an assertion of the form <code>(#$governmentOfGeoEntityMembers GOVERNMENT PERSON)</code>, or else indirectly, through <code>(#$governmentOfGeoEntityMembers ENTITY PERSON)</code>, where <code>(#$government ENTITY GOVERNMENT)</code> is the case.  As such, #$governmentOfGeoEntityMembers is essentially disjunctive in meaning, and is essentially a rule macro (c.f., #$RuleMacroPredicate) such that\n<pre>\n   (#$governmentOfGeoEntityMembers X Y)</pre>\niff\n<pre>\n   (#$or\n      (#$and\n         (#$isa X #$RegionalGovernment)\n         (#$hasMembers X Y))\n      (#$thereExists ?GOVERNMENT\n         (#$and\n            (#$isa X #$GeopoliticalEntity)\n            (#$hasMembers ?GOVERNMENT Y)\n            (#$government X ?GOVERNMENT)))).</pre>  This meaning is enforced via\n<pre>\n   (#$conservativeViaArg #$governmentOfGeoEntityMembers #$government 1)\n   (#$conservativeViaArgInverse #$governmentOfGeoEntityMembers #$government 1)</pre> which means that the arg2 will be <i>guaranteed</i> to bear the #$governmentOfGeoEntityMembers relation, and thus the #$hasMembers relation, to the relevant government and country, regardless of which is specified.<p>This relation replaces the need for explicit rules to explicitly conclude membership in a government or a country from known membership in one.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab844).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab844,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab844,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab844,14870).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab844,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab844,[]).
