x_comment(x_Cylinder,"A specialization of #$ThreeDimensionalThing.  Each instance of #$Cylinder is a three-dimensional object that has a straight or curved #$Tube (q.v.) as its \"side\" surface; any cross-section taken with respect to its side is (at least roughly) circular, and any two such cross-sections have (at least roughly) the same diameter.  A cylinder of finite length will also have a circular base and a circular top as parts of its boundary; an infinite cylinder has no top, and might have no base either.\n<p>\nExamples of cylinders include tangible objects (such as a roll of nickels) as well as intangible cylindrical space regions.\n<p>\nFor cylinders with straight sides, see the specialization #$RightCylinder.  See also #$CylindricalSurface and #$HollowCylindricalObject.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab849).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab849,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
