x_comment(x_RightCylinder,"A specialization of #$Cylinder and #$ThreeDimensionalGeometricThing (qq.v).  Each instance of #$RightCylinder is a cylinder that has a <i>straight</i> #$Tube (q.v.) as its \"side\" surface.  In other words, its radial axis is a straight line(-segment) (see #$LinearObject-Straight).\n<p>\nExamples of right cylinders include tangible objects (such as a roll of nickels) as well as intangible right cylindrical space regions.\n<p>\nSee also #$CylindricalSurface and #$HollowCylindricalObject.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab84c).
