x_comment(x_CommonShapeFn,"A unary #$GenlsPreservingFunction (q.v.) that takes a given type of tangible object to the collection of all objects that are shaped like objects of that type.  More precisely, (#$CommonShapeFn <b>OBJTYPE</b>) is the (most inclusive) specialization of #$ShapedObject all of whose instances have the same (most specific) shape shared by all non-pathological instances of <b>OBJTYPE</b>.  \n<p>\nFor example, (#$CommonShapeFn #$DomesticCat) is the collection of all cat-shaped objects, which includes not just cats themselves, but also cat-shaped toys, cookie-cutters, cushions, space-regions, etc.\n<p>\nThe fact that this function returns the <i>most inclusive</i> collection of <b>OBJTYPE</b>-shaped things ensures that (#$CommonShapeFn #$DomesticCat) includes <i>all</i> (not just some) cat-shaped objects.  The fact that the function returns the collection all of whose instances have the <i>most specific</i> shape common to (non-pathological) <b>OBJTYPE</b>s ensures that (#$CommonShapeFn #$DomesticCat) does <i>not</i> include, say, all animal-shaped objects.\n<p>\nSee also the corresponding \"instance-level\" predicate #$objectShapeType.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab858).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab858,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab858,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
