x_comment(x_grosslyIncompleteWithArgNotFullyBound,"A binary #$InferenceCompletenessPredicate that can apply to a\npredicate and a specified\nargument-place. (#$grosslyIncompleteWithArgNotFullyBound PRED N) means\nthat for any sequence SEQ such that PRED holds of SEQ, the Cyc\ninference engine can provide through removal tactics , at best, a minimal range of the values\n(VALUE-1, VALUE-2, ..., VALUE-K) such that these values are the\nNth elements of SEQ. \n<p>\n(#$grosslyIncompleteWithArgNotFullyBound PRED N) also means that the Cyc\ninference engine will treat as \"grossly incomplete\" any removal tactic for a\nproblem with PRED in the arg0 position and with the Nth argument position not fully bound.\n<p>\nCf. #$grosslyIncompleteWithAllArgsNotFullyBound and\n#$grosslyIncompleteWithAnyArgsNotFullyBound.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab883).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab883,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
