xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab88e,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab88e,[]).
x_comment(x_MuslimBrotherhoodOrganization,"#$MuslimBrotherhoodOrganization is intended to group together several organizations that are all typically referred to by the name 'Muslim Brotherhood,' but which have not been identified as a single group or sub-groups of one larger umbrella organization.  In the context of world affairs in 2005, #$MuslimBrotherhood-Egypt appears to be the most likely referent for the name because of its long history in Middle Eastern politics and its continuing political influence in Egypt ") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab88f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab88f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab88f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab88f,15037).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab88f,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab88f,[]).
x_comment(x_GeometricShapeTypeBySizeFunction,"A specialization of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  Each instance of #$GeometricShapeTypeBySizeFunction takes as arguments one or more #$Distances, and returns a specialization of a particular #$GeometricShapeTypeBySize whose instances all have those distances as their relevant size dimensions (see #$extensionParametersOfObject).\n<p>\nFor example, #$RightCylinderTypeFn is a shape-type function that takes two distances as arguments, and returns the specialization of #$RightCylinder whose instances have the first distance as their height and the second distance as their diameter.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab890).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab890,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab890,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab890,15038).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab890,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab890,[]).
x_comment(x_RightCylinderTypeFn,"A #$GeometricShapeTypeBySizeFunction that takes a pair of positive distances (see #$Distance-Absolute) to the collection of all straight cylinders that have the corresponding size dimensions.  More precisely, (#$RightCylinderTypeFn <b>HEIGHT DIAM</b>) is the collection of all and only those #$RightCylinders (q.v.) whose #$heightOfObject is <b>HEIGHT</b> and whose #$diameterOfObject is <b>DIAM</b>.\n<p>\nFor example, a roll of nickels is an instance of (roughly) (#$RightCylinderTypeFn (#$Inch 3.5) (#$Inch 0.875)).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab891).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab891,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab891,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab891,15041).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab891,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab891,[]).
x_comment(x_GeometricShapeTypeBySize,"A #$SecondOrderCollection and a specialization of #$SpatialThingTypeByGeometricShape (q.v.).  Each instance of #$GeometricShapeTypeBySize is a specialization of #$GeometricallyDescribableThing (q.v.) that groups things according to their size (i.e. the #$Distance(s) that they are extended along one or more spatial dimensions).  \n<p>\nInstances of #$GeometricShapeTypeBySize include (#$RectangularSolidTypeFn  (#$Inch 12) (#$Inch 12) (#$Inch 12)), the collection of all 12'' x 12'' x 12'' cubes.\n<p>\nNote that the above-used function #$RectangularSolidTypeFn is an instance of #$GeometricShapeTypeBySizeFunction (q.v.), all of whose instances are functions that take #$Distances as arguments and return instances of #$GeometricShapeTypeBySize.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab892).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab892,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab892,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab892,15044).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ab892,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ab892,[]).
x_comment(x_DocumentationPredicate,"A #$PredicateType whose instances are #$Predicates specifically designed for in-KB documentation purposes, such as  facilitating #$Cyclists in their understanding of the Cyc system, tracking knowledge representation work being done in the Cyc Knowledge Base, or noting cleanup work to be done.  \n<p>\nNote that documentation predicates are usually not involved in inference.  They may be excluded from knowledge bases in which available memory is a premium without affecting the performance of applications. #$DocumentationPredicate is used in code to determine which documentation to show to the user when they request to see documentation for a first-order reified term (or \"FORT\").") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab893).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab893,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab893,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ab893,15049).
