x_comment(x_IrregularMilitaryForce,"A specialization of #$MilitaryOrganization.  Each instance of #$IrregularMilitaryForce is a military organization that is not regularly established, but rather, exists in connection with (and usually only for the duration of) a specific conflict or situation.  A group member of an irregular military force might be a regular (instance of) #$MilitaryPerson who is assigned a special military task very different from his usual ones, or might be someone who is not regularly a #$MilitaryPerson at all but is nevertheless assigned a military task.  \n<p>\nFor example, suppose a Central American army officer organized a group of villagers to help defend against an impending invasion.  The group would for a time constitute a part of the country's irregular army force -- which force would itself be an instance of (#$IrregularForcesFn #$Army-BranchOfService).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab8d1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab8d1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab8d1,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
