x_comment(x_subWorkPriorToSubWorkInWork,"An instance of #$TernaryOrderingPredicate. <code>(#$subWorkPriorToSubWorkInWork EARLY-SUBWORK LATER-SUBWORK WORK)</code> means that the instance <code>WORK</code> of #$ConceptualWork is structured in such a way that the sub-work (see #$subWorks) <code>EARLY-SUBWORK</code> comes before  the sub-work <code>LATER-SUBWORK</code> (or in a performance of <code>WORK</code>, a performance of <code>EARLY-SUBWORK</code> is typically presented to the audience before a performance of <code>LATER-SUBWORK</code>).  For example, <code>(#$subWorkPriorToSubWorkInWork TaxMan-TheSong TomorrowNeverKnows-TheSong Revolver-TheAlbum)</code> means that the song \"Tax Man\" comes before the song \"Tomorrow Never Knows\" on the Beatles album, <i>Revolver</i>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab8f1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab8f1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
