x_comment('x_Section-MilitaryOrganization',"A specialization of #$ModernMilitaryOrganization.  Each instance of #$Section-MilitaryOrganization is a tactial military unit of a size that puts it in-between two standard echelons (see #$MilitaryUnitTypeByEchelon).  Different branches of military service consider different sorts of units to be \"sections\".   For example, in the #$UnitedStatesArmy and #$UnitedStatesMarineCorps, a section is a unit that is smaller than (and is a #$subOrganizations of) a #$Platoon-MilitaryEchelon and larger than a (and has as a sub-oganization at least one) #$Squad-MilitaryEchelon.  In the #$UnitedStatesNavy, a section of ships is one-half of a #$Division-MilitaryEchelon, and a section of aircraft consists of two aircraft.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab92a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab92a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
