x_comment(x_MilitaryUnitTypeByEchelon,"A #$SecondOrderCollection.  Each instance of #$MilitaryUnitTypeByEchelon is a collection of #$ModernMilitaryOrganizations that are of the same standard echelon (though not necesarily part of the same #$BranchOfMilitaryService, or even sub-organizations of the same country).  Examples include #$Platoon-MilitaryEchelon and #$Division-MilitaryEchelon.\n<p>\nSpecializations of #$MilitaryUnitTypeByEchelon include the partially-overlapping collections #$USMarineCorpsEchelon, #$USArmyEchelon, and #$IranianArmyEchelon.\n<p>\nTo state that a military unit is of a particular echelon, use \n#$echelonOfUnit.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab938).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab938,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
