x_comment(x_TotallyOrderedCollection,"A collection of collections and a specialization of #$CollectionWithAnEventLikeOrder (q.v.).  Each instance of #$TotallyOrderedCollection is a collection whose instances are conventionally regarded as being ordered by some relation <code>RELN</code>, where <code>RELN</code> totally orders <code>COL</code>.  A relation <code>RELN</code> <i><b>totally orders</b></i> a collection <code>COL</code> just in case <code>RELN</code> is <i>reflexive</i>, <i>antisymmetric</i>, and <i>transitive</i> on <code>COL</code>, and <code>COL</code> is <i>connected</i> with respect to <code>RELN</code> (i.e. for any instances <code>INST1</code> and <code>INST2</code> of <code>COL</code>, either <code>(RELN INST1 INST2)</code> or <code>(RELN INST2 INST1)</code> holds).\n<p>\nFor example, the integers are conventionally regarded as being ordered by #$greaterThanOrEqualTo, which totally orders #$Integer. Thus #$Integer is an instance of #$TotallyOrderedCollection, and (since all integers are scalars) of its specialization #$TotallyOrderedScalarIntervalType (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab978).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab978,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ab978,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
