x_comment(x_supplyThroughAmountDuring,"(#$supplyThroughAmountDuring PT1 COL PT2 THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$Collection COL with which the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1 is supplied through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2 (on their way from their origin) during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$supplyThroughAmountDuring is very general.  In various assertions PT1 might, for instance, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and PT2 might, for example, be a #$Hose, a #$Railway, a #$GeographicalRegion, or a #$BloodVessel.  The range of possible supplies is similarly broad.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  If AMOUNT is a #$Rate, AMOUNT indicates the average rate of supply of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE to PT1 through PT2 during the temporal extent of THING.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab9c0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab9c0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
