x_comment(x_grosslyIncompleteWithAllArgsNotFullyBound,"A unary #$InferenceCompletenessPredicate that can apply to a\npredicate. (#$grosslyIncompleteWithAllArgsNotFullyBound PRED) means\nthat the Cyc inference engine will treat as \"grossly incomplete\" any\nremoval (but not transformation) tactic for a problem with PRED in the\narg0 position and with all other argument positions not fully bound.\n<p> A good example of a predicate that is\n#$grosslyIncompleteWithAllArgsNotFullyBound is #$spatiallySubsumes-TypeType.\nGenerally, for no two shapes will it ever be asserted that one fits in\nthe other.  <p> Cf. the specialization of this predicate,\n#$grosslyIncompleteWithAnyArgsNotFullyBound, as well as\n#$grosslyIncompleteWithArgNotFullyBound.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab9f7).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab9f7,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
