x_comment(x_radialDistancePredicate,"A specialization of #$coordinateValuePredicateOfSystem (q.v.).  <code>(#$radialDistancePredicate RAD-PRED SYS)</code> means that <code>RAD-PRED</code> is the binary predicate used to express the radial distance coordinates of #$SpatialThings in the #$PolarCoordinateSystem (q.v.) <code>SYS</code>.  <code>RAD-PRED</code>'s two argument-places will be restricted (via #$argIsa) to instances of #$SpatialThing (or some specialization thereof) and #$Distance, respectively.\n<p>\nThus, for example <code>(RAD-PRED POINT (#$Meter 5))</code> would mean that, in <code>SYS</code>, the distance from <code>POINT</code> to the pole is 5 meters.\n<p>\nSee also #$azimuthAnglePredicate and #$altitudeAnglePredicate.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ab9fe).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ab9fe,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
