x_comment(x_topicForInstancesOfTypeInSuperTopic,"<code>(#$topicForInstancesOfTypeInSuperTopic SUB-TOPIC SUPER-TOPIC COLLECTION)</code> means that <code>SUB-TOPIC</code> is a topic that contains all and only the instances of the #$Collection <code>COLLECTON</code>, which is in turn contained in <code>SUPER-TOPIC</code> (a super topic of <code>SUB-TOPIC</code>).  For example:\n<p>\n<pre>\n(#$topicForInstancesOfTypeInSuperTopic \n#$GeopoliticalEntities-Individuals-Geography-Topic\n#$GeopoliticalEntities-Geography-Topic\n#$GeopoliticalEntity)\n</pre>\n<p>\nmeans that #$GeopoliticalEntities-Geography-Topic is a supertopic of #$GeopoliticalEntities-Individuals-Geography-Topic, and that #$GeopoliticalEntity is in the topic #$GeopoliticalEntities-Geography-Topic, and that  #$GeopoliticalEntities-Individuals-Geography-Topic contains all and only the instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity.") :- x_cid(a65b16517aba17).
