x_comment('x_Posture-Configuration',"A subcollection of #$Configuration.  Each instance of\n#$Posture-Configuration is a #$Situation that consists of the body of\nan #$Animal being in a certain configuration or orientation\n(e.g., crouching or lying prone).  Note that bodily postures are also\nrepresented in #$Cyc as subcollections of #$Animal (see #$AnimalTypeByPosture) -- that is, as collections of animals who possess the relevant posture.  To relate collections in these two different schemes, use\n#$configurationForPostureType and its corresponding function,\n#$Posture-ConfigurationFn .") :- x_cid(a65b16517aba4d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517aba4d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
