x_comment(x_FunctionDenotingFunction,"A specialization of #$IndividualDenotingFunction (q.v.) and the collection of functions that always return functions.  A function <b>FUNC</b> is an instance of #$FunctionDenotingFunction if and only if, for any (sequence of) argument(s) <b>ARGS</b> for which <b>FUNC</b> is defined, the value it yields -- i.e. <b>(FUNC . ARGS)</b> -- is an instance of #$Function-Denotational.\n<p>\nInstances of #$FunctionDenotingFunction include #$Lambda, #$FunctionToArg, and #$FunctionCompositionFn.  Thus (e.g.) (#$FunctionCompositionFn #$SuccessorFn #$SquaredFn) is the function that takes any integer and returns the square of its successor.\n<p>\nSpecializations of #$FunctionDenotingFunction include #$MetricUnitPrefix.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abaff).
