x_comment(x_relationOnlyInstance,"A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate (q.v.) that can be used to state that a binary predicate relates to a given thing only instances of a certain collection.  <code>(#$relationOnlyInstance PRED COL GIVENTHING)</code> means that, for any thing <code>THING</code>, <code>(PRED THING GIVENTHING)</code> holds only if <code>THING</code> is an instance of <code>COL</code>.  This is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:\n<pre>\n  (#$implies\n    (PRED ?X GIVENTHING)\n    (#$isa ?X COL)) .\n</pre>\nNote the the above does <i>not</i> entail that that there <i>is</i> some instance <code>THING</code> of <code>COL</code> such that <code>(PRED THING GIVENTHING)</code> holds.\n<p>\nCompare with #$relationAllInstance and #$relationExistsInstance. See also the shared  #$NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abb41).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abb41,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abb41,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abb41,16804).
