x_comment(x_interpretationMtCorrespondsToHypothesis,"<code>(#$interpretationMtCorrespondsToHypothesis INTERP-MT HYP-MT)</code> means that for some instance <code>PEG</code> of #$LinguisticExpressionPeg-CompleteUtterance, <code>INTERP-MT</code> is an interpretation context that contains a possible CycL representation of <code>PEG</code>, while <code>HYP-MT</code> is an instance of #$SemanticInterpretationHypothesisMicrotheory that contains the hypothesis that the interpretation contained in <code>INTERP-MT</code> is the correct interpretation.\n<p>More formally, for <code>PEG</code>, <code>(#$pegInterpretationMts PEG INTERP-MT)</code> and <code>(#$semanticInterpretationHypothesisMtForPeg HYP-MT PEG)</code> where there is an interpretation <code>CYCL</code> such that <code>(#$interpretationMtContent-CycL INTERP-MT CYCL)</code> and <code>(#$mtFocalContent HYP-MT (#$pegInterpretation-CycL PEG CYCL))</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abb52).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abb52,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abb52,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abb52,16837).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abb52,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abb52,[]).
x_comment(x_quantityMeasured,"<code>(#$quantityMeasured MEASURING SLOT)</code> means that in <code>MEASURING</code>, an instance of #$DeterminingTheValueOfASlot, the (arg2) value of <code>SLOT</code> was determined for some #$evaluee-Direct.  For example, <code>(#$quantityMeasured MeasuringTheHeightOfTheEiffelTower-001 #$heightOfObject)</code> means that this particular event of measuring the height of the Eiffel Tower resulted in learning the value for <code>HEIGHT</code> in the sentence <code>(#$heightOfObject #$EiffelTower HEIGHT)</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abb53).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abb53,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abb53,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
