x_comment(x_SocialGatheringAtResidence,"A subcollection of #$HostedSocialGathering, each instance\n#$SocialGatheringAtResidence takes place at someone's residence, be it\na house, apartment, dorm room, etc.  It is common in many cultures to\nhost certain types of social gatherings at one's residence.  Examples\ninclude both certain types of #$Party-Celebration (e.g.,\n#$DinnerParty, #$BirthdayParty), and more informal get-togethers for\nconversation, #$PlayingACardGame, etc.  In many cultures there are\nspecific social expectations regarding behavior of hosts and guests at\nsuch occasions.  The #$hostOfEvent for such a gathering usually,\nthough not always, lives at the residence.  By contrast, a resident\nwill rarely if ever be a guest at such a gathering (see\n#$guestAtSocialGathering).") :- x_cid(a65b16517abb77).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abb77,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abb77,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abb77,16917).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abb77,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abb77,[]).
x_comment(x_guestAtSocialGathering,"(#$guestAtSocialGathering GATHERING INDIV) means that INDIV\nis a guest at GATHERING.  Guests are #$attendees (typically, invited)\nto whom some form of hospitality or entertainment is being offered,\nand who have little or no responsibility for administering\nGATHERING.  (#$guestAtSocialGathering GATHERING INDIV) thus entails\nthat INDIV is neither the #$hostOfEvent, nor there primarily to\nprovide help -- e.g., hired entertainers or\ncooks. (#$guestAtSocialGathering GATHERING INDIV) entails that\nGATHERING has a (distinct) #$hostOfEvent.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abb78).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abb78,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abb78,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abb78,16929).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abb78,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abb78,[]).
x_comment(x_DeterminingAnArithmeticMean,"A specialization of #$DeterminingACentralTendencyAmongASetOfValues.  One determines a mean by adding up N values and dividing the sum by N.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abb79).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abb79,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
