x_comment(x_DeterminingACentralTendencyAmongASetOfValues,"A specialization of #$SolvingAProblem, #$DeterminingACentralTendencyAmongASetOfValues is the collection of all activities that, using some method or other (e.g, determining a median) that allows one to determine a central tendency for some group of values, frequently, though imprecisely described as determining an \"average.\"  Notable specializations of this collection are instances of #$TechniqueType, such as #$DeterminingAnArithmeticMean, #$DeterminingAMode, and #$DeterminingAMedian.  These specializations are disjoint with one another, not because one cannot arrive at the same answer using each method (i.e., one could accidently \"determine\" the mean by determining the mode -- where the values in question are 5, 5, 4, 6, the mode, mean and median are identical), but because these collections are defined procedurally.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abb7c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abb7c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abb7c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
