x_comment('x_Replying-Noncommittal',"A specialization of #$Replying.  In each instance of\n#$Replying-Noncommittal, the #$senderOfInfo replies to some prior\ncommunication (PRIOR-COMM), but does not express a firm commitment\nconcerning its content.  The type of commitment that is withheld\ndepends on the\n#$IllocutionaryForce of PRIOR-COMM.  For example, when PRIOR-COMM is an\ninstance of #$Requesting-CommunicationAct, replies which are\ninstances of #$Replying-Noncommittal neither agree to nor\n reject the request.  If PRIOR-COMM is an instance of\n#$Offering-CommunicationAct, a #$Replying-Noncommittal response neither expressly\naccepts nor declines the offer (cf., #$Accepting-CommunicationAct,\n#$Declining-CommunicationAct).") :- x_cid(a65b16517abb84).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abb84,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abb84,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abb84,16949).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abb84,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abb84,[]).
x_comment(x_EndingOfTemporalThing,"A #$TemporalObjectType and specialization of #$Event.  Each instance of #$EndingOfTemporalThing is an event in which some #$TemporallyExistingThing comes to a (permanent) end, i.e. ceases to temporally subsume the present moment (and does not temporally subsume any future moment).  (We use the vague \"moment\" instead of the precise #$TimePoint, as we do not want to rule out the possibility that a #$TemporallyExistingThing may <i>gradually</i> come to an end.)\n<p>\nInstances of #$EndingOfTemporalThing include the ending of #$WorldWarII, the death of #$Socrates, and #$TheTwentiethCenturyCE's coming to an end. \n<p>\nSpecializations of this collection can be specified compositionally using #$EndingFn.  A notable specialization, in which the thing coming to an end is an instance of #$SomethingExisting, is #$DestructionEvent.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abb85).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abb85,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
