x_comment(x_nodeCoveredByPeg,"<code>(#$nodeCoveredByPeg NODE EXPRESSION-PEG)</code> means that the instance of #$LinguisticExpressionPeg <code>EXPRESSION-PEG</code> has is an occurrence of an instance <code>AIS</code> of #$GraphicalAIS (typically an instance of #$TextString) that corresponds to a syntactic node <code>NODE</code> in a parse tree for a structure of which <code>AIS</code> is a (possibly non-proper) part.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abbaf).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abbaf,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abbaf,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abbaf,17091).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abbaf,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abbaf,[]).
x_comment(x_candidateConditionOnReferentExpression,"A predicate to characterize salient features of a referential expression used in a discourse context. (#$candidateConditionOnReferentExpression EXPRESSION-PEG EXPRESSION-TYPE) is true iff EXPRESSION-TYPE is a feature of EXPRESSION-PEG in the local context. \n\nNote that 'candidate conditions' in the sense of this predicate can be incompatible syntactic attributes. That is why #$candidateConditionOnDiscourseReferent is not a specialization of #$localConditionOnReferentExpression (q.v.). For a similar predicate applicable to #$DiscourseReferentPegs, see #$candidateConditionOnDiscourseReferent.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abbb0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abbb0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abbb0,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abbb0,17092).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abbb0,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abbb0,[]).
x_comment(x_localConditionOnReferentExpression,"A predicate to characterize the features (cf. #$LinguisticExpressionType) of the referential expressions in a discourse. (#$localConditionOnReferentExpression EXPRESSION-PEG EXPRESSION-TYPE) means that (#$isa EXPRESSION-PEG EXPRESSION-TYPE) is a provisional constraint on the referential expression EXPRESSION-PEG that we can extract from the current discourse state. Properties constraining a discourse-referent expression can be either agreement features expressed as #$LinguisticExpressionTypes. The properties of the <i>referents</i> themselves, i.e., the collections of which they are instances, can be expressed with #$localConditionOnDiscourseReferent (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16517abbb1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abbb1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abbb1,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abbb1,17095).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abbb1,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abbb1,[]).
x_comment(x_PresupposedDiscourseReferentFn,"This function denotes the implicit discourse entity presupposed\nby a definite NP discourse referent. (#$PresupposedDiscourseReferentFn PEG\nUDS) is the entity presupposed by PEG, and UDS is the discourse structure\nto which it is assigned (i.e., in which it is created). Example: bridging\nanaphora") :- x_cid(a65b16517abbb2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abbb2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abbb2,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abbb2,17096).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abbb2,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abbb2,[]).
x_comment(x_viableBridgingCriterionForReferents,"(#$viableBridgingCriterionForReferents PEG ANAPHOR PRED) means\nthat the conditions of familiarity and uniqueness presuppositions required\nfor picking the coreferent of ANAPHOR are satisfied by PEG with respect to\n(some specialization of) the relation PRED. For example\n(viableBridgingCriterionForReferents PEG1 \nPEG2 #$parts) when it is known in the discourse that (isa PEG1 Automobile)\nand (isa PEG2 SteeringWheel).") :- x_cid(a65b16517abbb3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abbb3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abbb3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
