xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abbb7,[]).
x_comment(x_candidateConditionOnDiscourseReferent,"A predicate to capture those properties of a discourse entity that can be evinced directly from the local discourse context in which it is first introduced. (#$candidateConditionOnDiscourseReferent PEG COND) is true iff (#$isa PEG COND) is a constraint on PEG entailed by at least one of the #$proposedMeaning of PEG. \n\nBecause they depend on #$proposedMeaning, 'candidate conditions' in the sense of this predicate can be inconsistent (e.g., disjoint collections, incompatible attributes, etc.). That is why #$candidateConditionOnDiscourseReferent is not a specialization of #$localConditionOnDiscourseReferent (q.v.). For a similar predicate applicable to #$LinguisticExpressionPegs, see #$candidateConditionOnReferentExpression.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abbb8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abbb8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abbb8,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abbb8,17118).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abbb8,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abbb8,[]).
x_comment(x_localConditionOnDiscourseReferent,"A predicate to characterize those properties of a discourse entity that can be evinced directly from the local discourse context. (#$localConditionOnDiscourseReferent PEG COND) means that (#$isa PEG COND) is a provisional constraint on PEG that we can extract from the current discourse state. Properties constraining a discourse referent can be  either the collection (which are the semantic values of nouns, in general) or  agreement features of the discourse expression itself, represented as #$LinguisticExpressionTypes (for which, however, see #$localConditionOnReferentExpression). Such properties can be used to determine appropriate coreferent targets even when the full semantics of a node is not yet available.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abbb9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abbb9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abbb9,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abbb9,17121).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abbb9,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abbb9,[]).
x_comment(x_excludedCoreferentInUDS,"(#$excludedCoreferentInUDS UDS PEG1 PEG2) is true if PEG1\n\nis an anaphoric discourse entity in UDS and PEG2 has been ruled out as a\n\ncoreference candidate for PEG2. This could mean that PEG2 is not accessible\n\nfrom UDS, or that it violates applicable syntactic or semantic\n\nconstraints.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abbba).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abbba,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abbba,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
