x_comment(x_evaluationProcedureEvalueeType,"<code>(#$evaluationProcedureEvalueeType EVALUATION-TYPE TYPE)</code> means that <code>EVALUATION-TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$Evaluating is, by design, an procedure for evaluating instances of <code>TYPE</code>, a collection.  For any given instance of <code>EVALUATION-TYPE</code>, there could be things other than an instance of <code>TYPE</code> that get evaluated, but that is incidental: To be an instance of <code>EVALUATION-TYPE</code> it must be the intention of the performer that an instance of <code>TYPE</code> be evaluated.  See also #$evaluee-Direct and #$evaluationTypeDirectEvalueeType.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abbfa).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abbfa,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
