x_comment(x_evaluationProcedureEvaluationDimension,"<code>(#$evaluationProcedureEvaluationDimension EVALUATION-TYPE PREDICATE)</code> means that <code>EVALUATION-TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$Evaluating is, by design, a procedure for evaluating instances of <code>TYPE</code>, for some instance of #$Collection <code>TYPE</code>, along the dimension <code>PREDICATE</code>, an instance of #$ScalarIntervalSlot.  In particular, for every instance <code>EVALUATION</code> of <code>EVALUATION-TYPE</code> where <code>THING</code> is evaluated (see #$evaluee-Direct), the intended outcome of <code>EVALUATION</code> is the determination of <code>VALUE</code> such that <code>(PREDICATE THING VALUE)</code>.  Or, to be more formal, it is the intention of the performer of <code>EVALUATION</code> that for some <code>VALUE</code> <code>(#$evaluationOutputSentences EVALUATION (PREDICATE THING VALUE))</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abbfd).
