x_comment('x_BodyOfWater-Intermittent',"Each instance of #$BodyOfWater-Intermittent is a #$TopographicalFeature characterized by the frequent presence of a relatively large volume of water, but which is usually dry part of the time (cf. #$BodyOfWater-Intermittent-DryPhase and #$BodyOfWater-Intermittent-WetPhase).  Often the presence of water is seasonal, accumulating during the wet part of the year and drying at other times.  For some intermittent bodies of water, the cycle is longer or erratic, but on some humanly-perceivable time scale.  Bodies of water that disappear over a very long time scale or because of particular geologic events (e.g., a spring that stops flowing due to an earthquake) are not considered intermittent in this sense.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abc0c).
