x_comment(x_NullBoundary,"A specialization of #$NullSpaceRegion (q.v.).  Each instance of #$NullBoundary is a null space region that is the (empty) boundary of a #$SpatiallyUnboundedThing (q.v.), according to a convention adopted in certain geometrical contexts.  This convention is a simplifying assumption that allows a \"boundary function\" (the function from things in space to their boundaries; see #$boundaryOfSpatialThing) to be defined as a #$TotalFunction on the collection #$SpatialThing.  At most one null boundary is recognized with respect to any given context.  \n<p>\nNote that the dimensionality (see #$dimensionOfSpatialThing) of any null boundary is set by fiat to -1.  This conforms with the #$OpenGISSimpleFeaturesSpecificationForSQL standard.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abc11).
