x_comment(x_anatomicallyExteriorTo,"(#$anatomicallyExteriorTo EXTERIOR-OBJ INTERIOR-OBJ) means that EXTERIOR-OBJ lies in the #$ExteriorDirection of INTERIOR-OBJ, when viewed in the frame of reference of the object with #$AnimalBodyShapeType (often, a #$HomoSapiens) that they are both located in.  Note that INTERIOR-OBJ is therefore interior to EXTERIOR-OBJ; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `interior to'.  EXTERIOR-OBJ and INTERIOR-OBJ are often, but not always, #$AnimalBodyRegions.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abc5f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abc5f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
