x_comment(x_SiltySoilRegion,"A specialization of #$FineGrainedSoilRegion. #$SiltySoilRegion is the collection of #$GeographicalRegions where the soil is composed of silt. Silty soil is designated by the primary letter of (M) in the #$UnifiedSoilClassificationSystem. When dry, silty soil provides excellent trafficability, although it is very dusty. However, it absorbs water quickly and turns to a deep, soft mud (a quick condition), which is definite obstacle to movement.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abc87).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abc87,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
