x_comment(x_SandySoilRegion,"A specialization of both #$CoarseGrainedSoilRegion and #$SoftTerrain. #$SandySoilRegion is the collection of #$GeographicalRegions where the soil consists of sand: rock grains 0.6cm in diameter and smaller. Sandy soil is designated by the primary letter of (G) in the #$UnifiedSoilClassificationSystem. Sand is classified as coarse, medium, or fine, and is angular or rounded. When wet enough to become compacted or when mixed with clay, sand provides excellent trafficability. Very dry, loose sand is an obstacle to vehicles, particularly on slopes. Under wet conditions, remoldable sands react to traffic in a manner similar to fine-grained soils.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abc8b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abc8b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
