xc_kb_names(a65b16517abca1,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abca1,[]).
x_comment(x_SomewhatPoorlyDrainedRegion,"A specialization #$GeographicalRegion. Instances of #$SomewhatPoorlyDrainedRegion are regions where the soil is wet at shallow depths for significant periods during the growing season. Internal free-water is commonly shallow to moderately deep and transitory to permanent. Unless the soil is artificially drained, the growth of most mesophytic plants is markedly restricted. The soil commonly has (i) a low to very low saturated hydraulic conductivity, (ii) a high water table, (iii) receives water from a lateral flow, (iv) experiences persistent rainfall, or a combination of these factors. (<i>Field Book for Describing and Sampling Soils, U.S. Department of Agriculture</i>)") :- x_cid(a65b16517abca2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abca2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abca2,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abca2,17620).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abca2,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abca2,[]).
x_comment(x_WellDrainedRegion,"A specialization #$GeographicalRegion. Instances of #$WellDrainedRegion are regions where water moves through the soil readily, but not rapidly. Internal free-water commonly is deep or very deep available to plants in humid regions during much of the growing season. Wetness does not inhibit growth of roots for significant periods during most growing seasons. The soil is deep to, or lacks redoximorphic features. (<i>Field Book for Describing and Sampling Soils, U.S. Department of Agriculture</i>)") :- x_cid(a65b16517abca3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abca3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abca3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abca3,17621).
