x_comment(x_DryTropicalForest,"A specialization of #$ScrubbyVegetationRegion. Instances of #$DryTropicalForest are areas of semi-deciduous forest\ngrowing in semi-arid areas of South America and the Indian\nsubcontinent. Rainfall in these areas usually averages less than 250mm\nper annum. Thorny scrub and low- to medium-sized trees with thick bark\nand deep roots characterize the vegetation. Source: <i>The Times Atlas of\nthe World (1995)</i>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abcae).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abcae,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
