x_comment('x_forbidden-SitRelationToSitType',"(#$forbidden-SitRelationToSitType <b>SIT</b> <b>PRED</b>\n<b>FORBIDDEN-TYPE</b>) means that there should be no instance\n<b>FORBIDDEN-INS</b> of <b>FORBIDDEN-TYPE</b> such that\n(<b>PRED</b> <b>SIT</b> <b>FORBIDDEN-INS</b>).  Assertions involving\nthis predicate -- which specify what <i>should</i> not be the case --\nshould be made in a normative context, e.g., one that reflects the\ncontents of a particular $#CodeOfConduct.  Usually, <b>SIT</b> will be\nsubject to such a prohibition in virtue of satisfying some general\ndescription, e.g., one stated in the antecedent of a\n#$CycLRuleAssertion. ") :- x_cid(a65b16517abcbd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abcbd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abcbd,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
