x_comment('x_oughtToBe-SubSitTypeRelationToSubSitType',"(#$oughtToBe-SubSitTypeRelationToSubSitType <b>SIT</b>\n<b>SUB-TYPE1</b> <b>PRED</b> <b>SUB-TYPE2</b>) means that, for\nany instance <b>SUB-INS1</b> of <b>SUB-TYPE1</b> that occurs as a\n#$subSituations of <b>SIT</b>, there should be an instance\n<b>SUB-INS2</b> of <b>SUB-TYPE2</b> such that (<b>PRED</b>\n<b>SUB-INS1</b> <b>SUB-INS2</b>).  Assertions involving this predicate\n-- which specify what <i>should</i> be the case -- should be made in a\nnormative context, e.g., one that reflects the contents of a\nparticular #$CodeOfConduct.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abcc1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abcc1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
