x_comment(x_SpatialDifferenceFn,"A binary function that takes a pair of tangible objects, space regions, or spatially-localized events to their mereological difference.  (#$SpatialDifferenceFn <b>DIFFERENCE THING1 THING2</b>) is the unique #$SpatialThing (of the same basic type as <b>THING1</b> and <b>THING2</b>) <b>DIFFERENCE</b> such that a spatial thing intersects (see #$spatiallyIntersects) <b>DIFFERENCE</b> if and only if it intersects with <b>THING1</b> and is disjoint with (see #$spatiallyDisjoint) <b>THING2</b>.  \n<p>\nNote that \"<i>of the same basic type</i>\" in the above means that the three relata are either all #$PartiallyTangibles, all #$SpaceRegions, or all #$Event-Localizeds.  This restriction is needed in order to ensure the uniqueness of <b>DIFFERENCE</b>, since a tangible object, a space region, and an event can have the same spatial extent (see #$cospatial), despite their being distinct things.\n<p>\nSee the corresponding predicate #$spatialDifference.  Also see #$SpatialSumFn and #$SpatialProductFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abcd5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abcd5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abcd5,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
