x_comment(x_BroadleafForest,"A specialization of #$Forest. Each #$BroadleafForest is a forest region where deciduous trees predominate, found mainly in the #$NorthernHemisphere-Region. In Western Europe and North America before 1600, a wide variety of tree species occupied these regions, e.g., oak, ash, beech, elm, maple, hickory, alder, and birch, but due to exploitation little of the original forest regions remain. The #$USArmyFieldManual5-33VegetationMapCode assigns #$BroadleafForests a Vegetation Map Code of (<code>D</code>).") :- x_cid(a65b16517abcfa).
