x_comment('x_sihmsMutuallySupportive-ConceptReferredToInDistinctWays',"An instance of #$IrreflexiveBinaryPredicate and #$TransitiveBinaryPredicate.  <code>(#$sihmsWithCommonSuperExpressionMutuallySupportive SIHM-1 SIHM-2)</code> means that the instances <code>SIHM-1</code> and <code>SIHM-2</code> of #$SemanticInterpretationHypothesisMicrotheory are mutually supportive, in a very specific way:  Given three instances of #$LinguisticExpressionPeg <code>PEG</code>, <code>SUB-PEG-1</code> and <code>SUB-PEG-2</code> such that <code>(#$properSubExpressions PEG SUB-PEG-1)</code> and <code>(#$properSubExpressions PEG SUB-PEG-2)</code> where <code>SUB-PEG-1</code> and <code>SUB-PEG-2</code> are not sub-expressions of each other, and <code>SIHM-1</code> and <code>SIHM-2</code> contain hypothesized semantic interpretations of <code>SUB-PEG-1</code> and <code>SUB-PEG-2</code>,  <code>(#$sihmsWithCommonSuperExpressionMutuallySupportive SIHM-1 SIHM-2)</code> holds just in case <code>SIHM-1</code> and <code>SIHM-2</code> distinguish themselves from other pairs of interpretations of parts of <code>PEG</code> by virtue of a semantic closeness between them that could help form a sense of what <code>PEG</code> is about.  <p>For example, if <code>PEG</code> is an occurrence of the sentence, \"Oil and other natural resources will increase in value as the earth's population continues to grow,\" and among the various interpretation hypotheses for the sub-expressons of <code>PEG</code> are <code>SIHM-1</code>, that \"oil\" in this context maps to #$Petroleum-CrudeOil; <code>SIHM-2</code>, that \"oil\" maps to #$ArtistsOilPaint, and <code>SIHM-3</code>, that \"natural resources\" maps to #$NaturalResourceType,  then because <code>(#$isa #$Petroleum-CrudeOil #$NaturalResourceType)</code>, <code>SIHM-1</code> and <code>SIHM-2</code> count as mutually supportive, whereas <code>SIHM-2</code> and <code>SIHM-3</code> do not.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abd65).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abd65,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abd65,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abd65,18013).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abd65,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abd65,[]).
x_comment('x_sihmsMutuallySupportive-ConceptReferredToInDistinctWays',"An instance of #$IrreflexiveBinaryPredicate and #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate.  <code>(#$sihmsMutuallySupportive-ConceptReferredToInDistinctWays SIHM-1 SIHM-2)</code> means that the instances <code>SIHM-1</code> and <code>SIHM-2</code> of #$SemanticInterpretationHypothesisMicrotheory are mutually supportive in a very specific way:  Given three instances of #$LinguisticExpressionPeg <code>PEG</code>, <code>SUB-PEG-1</code> and <code>SUB-PEG-2</code> such that <code>(#$properSubExpressions PEG SUB-PEG-1)</code> and <code>(#$properSubExpressions PEG SUB-PEG-2)</code> where <code>SUB-PEG-1</code> and <code>SUB-PEG-2</code> are not sub-expressions of each other, <code>SIHM-1</code> and <code>SIHM-2</code> contain hypothesized semantic interpretations <code>I1</code> of <code>SUB-PEG-1</code> and <code>I2</code> of <code>SUB-PEG-2</code>, and these pegs are occurrences of distinct strings,  <code>(#$sihmsMutuallySupportive-ConceptReferredToInDistinctWays SIHM-1 SIHM-2)</code> holds just in case <code>I1</code> is identical to <code>I2</code>.  <p>For example, if <code>PEG</code> is an occurrence of the sentence, \"Oil is a natural resource whose value will continue to grow, as the demand for crude will rise as the economies and populations of developing countries continue to grow,\" and among the various interpretation hypotheses for the sub-expressons of <code>PEG</code> are <code>SIHM-1</code>, that \"oil\" in this context maps to #$Petroleum-CrudeOil and <code>SIHM-2</code>, that \"crude\" maps to #$Petroleum-CrudeOil, then <code>SIHM-1</code> and <code>SIHM-2</code> count as mutually supportive.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abd66).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abd66,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abd66,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abd66,18014).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abd66,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abd66,[]).
