x_comment('x_classificationSystemOf-Focally',"<code>(#$classificationSystemOf-Focally ONTOLOGY TYPE)</code> means that <code>SYSTEM</code>, an instance of #$ClassificationSystem, is, focally, an system that classifies elements of the set or collection (#$SetOrCollection) <code>TYPE</code>.  That a classification system is <i>focally</i> a system of classifying some type <code>TYPE</code> does not mean that every concept in the system is an instance of <code>TYPE</code>.  For example, an ontology (#$Ontology) will also contain relations and operators that enable it to represent facts and rules, where those facts and rules will serve primarily to define the instances of <code>TYPE</code> that occur in the ontology, and, to a lesser extent, to define the concepts that are needed to define those instances of <code>TYPE</code>.  For example, an ontology of biological species might also contain concepts, such as height, weight, and anatomical concepts that, though not the focus of the ontology per se, must have some representation in the ontology to be of use in representing biological species.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abd7f).
