x_comment(x_TemporallyContinuousThing,"A specialization of #$TemporalThing.  Each instance of #$TemporallyContinuousThing <code>CONT</code> is a thing that occupies (see #$temporalExtent) or is one continuous chunk of time.  More precisely: <code>CONT</code> #$temporallySubsumes (q.v.) every time-interval between its #$startingPoint and #$endingPoint.   Thus, there is no time-interval between the start and end of <code>CONT</code> during which <code>CONT</code> does not exist (if a #$SomethingExisting) or occur (if an #$Event) or obtain (if a #$StaticSituation) or which <code>CONT</code> does not have as one of its #$timeSlices (if a #$TimeInterval).\n<p>\nFor example, all #$Dates are temporally-continuous (see the specialization #$ContinuousTimeInterval), and most or all ordinary physical objects are temporally-continuous.\n<p>\nSee also #$SpatiallyContinuousThing.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abd91).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abd91,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abd91,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abd91,18095).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abd91,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abd91,[]).
x_comment(x_interrupts,"A specialization of #$temporallyDisjoint that holds between two events such that the occurring of one interrupts the occuring of the other.  <code>(#$interrupts INTERRUPTOR INTERRUPTEE)</code> means that <code>INTERRUPTOR</code> at least temporarily puts a stop to <code>INTERRUPTEE</code>.  \n<p>\nNote that if <code>INTERRUPTOR</code> is a continuous event (see #$TemporallyContinuousThing) then it must start after <code>INTERRUPTEE</code> starts.  If <code>INTERRUPTEE</code> resumes after the interruption, it does so only after <code>INTERRUPTOR</code> (permanently or temporarily) stops occurring.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abd92).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abd92,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
