x_comment(x_temporalExtent,"A binary #$TemporalPredicate and specialization of #$cotemporal (q.v.) that relates each #$TemporalThing to the #$TimeInterval that it occupies.  <code>(#$temporalExtent TEMP TIME)</code> means that <code>TIME</code> is the time-interval of longest #$duration (q.v.) during which <code>TEMP</code> exists (if <code>TEMP</code> is a #$SomethingExisting) or occurs (if an #$Event) or obtains (if a #$StaticSituation).  If <code>TEMP</code> is itself a time-interval, the above #$temporalExtent sentence holds if and only if <code>TIME</code> is identical to <code>TEMP</code>.\n<p>\nNote that if <code>(#$temporalExtent TEMP TIME)</code> holds, <code>TIME</code> is a #$ContinuousTimeInterval (q.v.) if and only if <code>TEMP</code> is an instance of #$TemporallyContinuousThing (q.v.).\n<p>\nNote also that it is <i>not</i> the case that anything having a #$temporalExtent is a #$TemporallyExtendedThing (cf.), as that collection excludes all #$SomethingExistings. \n<p>\nSee also the corresponding function #$TemporalExtentFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abdbb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abdbb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abdbb,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
