x_comment(x_queryVariable,"<code>(#$queryVariable QUERY-SPEC SET)</code> means that in response to the query specification <code>QUERY-SPEC</code> (which is a query with exactly one free variable), the #$CycInferenceEngine currently generates an assignment <code>SET</code> of bindings.\n<p>\nFor example, the following is currently true:\n<p>\n<pre>\n (#$queryVariable\n   (#$QueryFn  \n     (#$ist #$SimpleAstronomyDataVocabularyMt\n     (#$isa ?PLANET #$Planet))\n   (#$TheSet\n       #$PlanetMars    #$PlanetEarth   #$PlanetTauBooB  #$PlanetMercury     \n       #$PlanetVenus   #$PlanetSaturn  #$PlanetNeptune  #$PlanetJupiter\n       #$PlanetUranus  #$PlanetPluto))\n</pre>\n<p>\nSee also #$queryAnswers and #$queryBindings.\n") :- x_cid(a65b16517abdc5).
