x_comment(x_parallel,"An #$EquivalenceRelation and a very general quasi-spatial predicate that is used to state that two lines, aligned objects, or vectors are parallel or point in parallel directions.  <code>(#$parallel INDIV1 INDIV2)</code> means that <code>INDIV1</code> and <code>INDIV2</code> are parallel.  One or both of <code>INDIV1</code> and <code>INDIV2</code> might be a (tangible or intangible) line or line-segment (see #$LinearObject), a physical object with a well-defined lengthwise axis, or a vector (see #$VectorInterval).  \n<p>\nWhen appropriate, consider using one a more specialized predicate, such as #$parallelLines, #$parallelVectors, #$aligned, or #$parallelPaths.  And cf. #$perpendicular.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abdd4).
