x_comment(x_perpendicular,"A very general quasi-spatial predicate that is used to state that two lines, surfaces, aligned objects, or vectors are perpendicular or oriented in perpendicular directions.  <code>(#$perpendicular INDIV1 INDIV2)</code> means that <code>INDIV1</code> and <code>INDIV2</code> are perpendicular.  One or both of <code>INDIV1</code> and <code>INDIV2</code> might be a (tangible or intangible) line or line-segment (see #$LinearObject), a surface (see #$SurfaceRegion), physical object with a well-defined lengthwise axis, or a vector (see #$VectorInterval).  \n<p>\nSee also the specializations #$perpendicularObjects and #$perpendicularVectors.  And cf. #$parallel.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abdd5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abdd5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
