x_comment(x_CycLPredicator,"A #$CycLExpressionType and a specialization of #$CycLOperator (q.v.). Characterized synatactically, this is the collection of all and only those CycL terms that can appear as the main operator (i.e. in the \"arg0\" position) of a #$CycLClosedSentence. Characterized semantically, this is also the collection of all and only those CycL terms that denote #$Predicate relations. Examples of #$CycLPredicators include these three CycL expressions:\n<pre>\n  #$genls \n  #$loves\n  (#$TypeCapableFn #$behaviorCapable)\n</pre>\nThese examples reflect the fact that while most #$CycLPredicators encountered in practice are #$CycLConstants, a predicator might be a #$CycLNonAtomicTerm.\n<p>\nSee also #$CycLFunctor.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abdf5).
