x_comment('x_EvaluatableFunction-Contextualized',"A #$FunctionType and a sub-collection of #$EvaluatableFunction.  As a\nsub-collection of #$EvaluatableFunction, each instance of this collection is\nassociated with a piece of procedural code (see #$evaluationDefn); however, the\nbehavior of that code and, as a consequence, the value returned by this\nfunction, can vary in even minutely different contexts.   Moreover, the factors that govern this behavior are complex or diffuse such that they cannot be provided as arguments to the function.  This collection has an important relationship to forward inference because, during truth maintenance, the verification of the value returned by such a function cannot be accomplished simply by calling the function again (unlike, say #$PlusFn).  Thus, there is special handling for the evaluations of these functions in order to provide stability to forward inference. For example, the function #$RandomIntegerFn is intended to return a random integer. Since that function should not return the same digit every time it is called,  a forward inference based on an earlier value that was returned should not be undone because a new value was returned on a subsequent call.  #$EvaluatableFunction-Contextualized and #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation are 'orthogonal.' So, a #$Function-Denotational could be instances of both; however,  #$EvaluatableFunction-Contextualized is not a sub-collection of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation because a function like #$RandomIntegerFn could have two simultaneous calls on different processes and return different results.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abe45).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abe45,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abe45,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abe45,18463).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abe45,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abe45,[]).
x_comment('x_EvaluatableRelation-Contextualized',"A sub-collection of #$EvaluatableRelation.  As a sub-collection of #$EvaluatableRelation, each instance of this collection is associated with a piece of procedural code (see #$evaluationDefn); however, the behavior of that code and, as a consequence, the behavior of these relations can vary in even minutely different contexts.  Moreover, the factors that govern this behavior are complex or diffuse such that they cannot be provided as additional arguments . #$EvaluatableRelation-Contextualized and #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation are 'orthogonal.' So, a relation could be an instance of both; however, #$EvaluatableRelation-Contextualized is not a sub-collection of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation because simultaneous evaluations could produce different results.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abe46).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abe46,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abe46,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abe46,18468).
