x_comment(x_cotemporal,"A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate and an #$EquivalenceRelation that is a specialization of both #$temporalBoundsIdentical and #$temporallySubsumes (qq.v.).  <code>(#$cotemporal TEMP1 TEMP2)</code> means that <code>TEMP1</code> and <code>TEMP2</code> have precisely the same temporal extent (see #$temporalExtent).\n<p>\nNote that if both <code>TEMP1</code> and <code>TEMP2</code> are instances of #$TemporallyContinuousThing (q.v.), the above is equivalent to <code>(#$temporalBoundsIdentical TEMP1 TEMP2)</code>.  But if at least one of them is not continuous, they might have identical temporal bounds (i.e. start and end points) and yet not be cotemporal.\n<p>\nSpecializations of #$cotemporal include #$cotemporalSubEvents (which applies to #$Events) and #$simultaneousWith (which applies to #$TimePoints).") :- x_cid(a65b16517abe63).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abe63,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
