x_comment(x_groupMemberType,"The predicate #$groupMemberType is used to characterize the membership of a particular group.  <code>(#$groupMemberType GROUP TYPE)</code> means that all of <code>GROUP</code>'s members are instances of the collection <code>TYPE</code>.  \n<p>\nFor example, to state that the #$groupMembers of the Austin City Council are humans, one would write (#$groupMemberType AustinCityCouncil #$Person).  The members of a particular group might be characterized in more than one way; e.g., a Hispanic Business Council may have both the #$groupMemberType #$EthnicGroupOfHispanics and the #$groupMemberType #$BusinessPerson (provided that all of its members are Hispanic business people).  For 'typical' or 'expected' characteristics of members, see also #$memberTypes and #$orgTypeTypicallyHasMemberTypes.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abe79).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abe79,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
