x_comment(x_defined,"A unary predicate, whose argument-place is \"quoted\" (see #$quotedArgument), that is used to state that a given CycL non-atomic term does denote something.  Where <code>NAT</code> has the form <code>(FUNC . ARGS)</code>, <code>(#$defined NAT)</code> means that <code>NAT</code> has a denotatum because <code>FUNC</code> (the function denoted by the main functor in <code>NAT</code>) returns a value for the argument sequence <code>ARGS</code>.  In other words,  <code>FUNC</code> is defined on the sequence <code>ARGS</code>.\n<p>\nCf. #$undefined.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abe94).
