x_comment(x_SubFunctionTypePreservingRelnInArgFn,"A ternary #$SubcollectionFunction that takes a #$FunctionType to the specialization of it comprising those instances that preserve a specified binary relation with respect to a specified argment-place.  (#$SubFunctionTypePreservingRelnInArgFn <b>FUNCTYPE PRED N</b>) is the collection <b>SUBFUNCTYPE</b> consisting of all and only those instances of <b>FUNCTYPE</b> that preserve the relation <b>PRED</b> with respect to their <b>N</b>th argument-place (see #$preservesRelnInArg).  That is, if <b>FUNC</b> is an instance of <b>SUBFUNCTYPE</b>, then whenever two members of <b>FUNC</b>'s domain stand in the relation <b>PRED</b>, their respective images in <b>FUNC</b>'s range stand in <b>PRED</b> also.\n<p>\nFor example, (#$SubFunctionTypePreservingRelnInArgFn #$SurfaceProjection #$partOfSpaceRegion 1) is the collection of #$SurfaceProjections (q.v.) that preserve the part-whole relation between space-regions.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abeae).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abeae,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
