x_comment(x_TextTopicStructureFn,"A #$UnaryFunction and #$EvaluatableFunction-Contextualized. Evaluating an expression of the form (#$TextTopicStructureFn TEXT) will return a list of lists of lists of length three.  The function presumes  that it is receiving a natural language expression containing at least one sentence.  The elements of the overall list will represent the individual sentences contained in TEXT.  Those elements are ordered based on the sequence of their appearance in TEXT. Each of those 'middle' lists represents a sentence.  Its elements represent #$Cyc's understanding of the words in the sentence.  Each element is a list of length 3 and they are ordered relative to the words appearance in the individual sentences.  The first element is a #$CharacterString that represents a particular word in the sentence.  The second element is a #$SpeechPart. The third element is a #$Set-Mathematical containing the possible denotations of the first element of the list based on the part of speech that is the second element.  The possible denotations receive some filtering to remove overly abstract or 'ke irrelevant' concepts.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abec2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abec2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abec2,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abec2,18666).
