x_comment(x_resultIsaForType,"A #$SetOrCollectionPredicate that is used to state that a particular #$resultIsa (q.v.) condition holds of all functions of a given type.  <code>(#$resultIsaForType FUNCTYPE COL)</code> means that <code>(#$resultIsa FUNC COL)</code> holds for any instance <code>FUNC</code> of <code>FUNCTYPE</code>.  \n<p>\nNote that the above does <i>not</i> preclude <code>(#$argIsa FUNC SUBCOL)</code> holding for some specialization <code>SUBCOL</code> of <code>COL</code>; e.g. there might in some cases be an asserted condition on <code>FUNC</code>'s result that is stricter than that given by <code>COL</code>.  For example, <code>(#$resultIsaForType #$RelationDenotingFunction #$Relation)</code> holds even though some relation-valued functions have #$Predicate as their asserted #$resultIsa condition.  \n<p>\nSee also #$argIsaForType.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abede).
