x_comment(x_physicallyCapableOf,"<code>(#$physicallyCapableOf OBJ SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> can physically play <code>ROLE</code> in a situation of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>.  This does not imply that <code>OBJ</code> is capable of doing so in the sense of know-how (see  #$skillCapableOf), nor does it mean that <code>OBJ</code> has the resources to do so (see #$resourceCapableOf).  For instance, (#$anatomicallyCapableOf  #$MarthaThePassengerPigeon #$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy), but if Martha were caged, then (#$not (#$physicallyCapableOf #$MarthaThePassengerPigeon  #$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy)).  Similarly, if Martha's feet were stuck in lime, she would also not be physically capable of flying.  It is this sense of  capability that this predicate is meant to express.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abef8).
