x_comment(x_CylindricalSurface,"A specialization of #$TwoDimensionalGeometricThing (q.v.).  Each instance of #$CylindricalSurface is the two-dimensional, non-planar, surface of a #$Cylinder (q.v.).  A cylindrical surface might be the entire surface (see #$boundaryOfSpatialThing) of a finite cylinder (see #$CylindricalSurface-WithTopAndBottom), or it might be just the tubular \"side\" surface of a finite or infinite cylinder (see #$CylindricalSurface-WithoutTopAndBottom).  Note that, in the case of an infinitely long cylinder with no top or bottom, the side surface <i>is</i> the entire surface.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abf15).
