x_comment(x_parallelOfSpheroid,"A specialization of the binary predicate #$spheroidalSection (q.v.) that relates any #$Spheroid that is not a perfect #$Sphere to each of its <i>parallels</i>, or lines of latitude.  <code>(#$parallelOfSpheroid PARALLEL SPHEROID)</code> means that <code>PARALLEL</code> is a #$Circle that is a section of <code>SPHEROID</code> centered at a point on <code>SPHEROID</code>'s #$axisOfSurfaceOfRevolution (q.v.) and #$perpendicular to that axis.  Thus any two parallels of a given spheroid are indeed #$parallel to each other.  The parallel centered at the spheroid's center is its <i>equator</i> (see #$equatorOfSpheroid).") :- x_cid(a65b16517abf65).
