x_comment('x_Field-Mathematical',"A #$Field-Mathematical is a unary function which assigns a scalar or vector (#$ScalarOrVectorInterval) to each #$Point in a region of space. Fields are often used in physics to model quantities that vary throughout space. For example, the speed and direction of a moving fluid; the strength and direction of some force, such as the magnetic or gravitational force; the distribution of temperature throughout a region; the distribution of pressure in a gaseous region. The first two examples are types of #$VectorFields, while the latter two examples are types of #$ScalarFields.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abf73).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abf73,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
