x_comment('x_atLeastN-GenQuant',"(#$num-GenQuant COL1 COL2 N) means that there are exactly N elements of COL1 which are also elements of COL2.  This predicate is a sort of macro-predicate which can be used to represent the meaning of arbitrarily many English numeric determiners like \"two\", \"three\", etc.  More specialiuzed predicates for specific numbers can be defined in terms of #$num-GenQuant.  Thus, for instance, #$two-GenQuant can be defined as (#$num-GenQuant COL1 COL2 2).") :- x_cid(a65b16517abf85).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abf85,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
