x_comment('x_Culture-Specification',"A subcollection of #$Specification.  Each instance of #$Culture-Specification is a broad -- often\nextremely broad and heterogenous -- set of norms and\ndescriptive claims that is pervasively, and somewhat unconsciously,\nfollowed within some broad social grouping.\n\nMany social groups follow a distinctive #$Culture-Specification,\nincluding many nationalities\n(#$PersonTypeByNationality), ethnicities\n(#$PersonTypeByEthnicity), and professions\n(#$PersonTypeByOccupation).  \n\n<p>Typically, the elements of a #$Culture-Specification include\nnorms for social behavior and assignments of social\nsignificance to actions (see, for example, #$EtiquetteOfCultureFn).\nBut cultures may also specify actions or beliefs related to various other subjects, including\nreligious practice, artistic style and activity, and sociological\nphenomena.</p><p>\n\nThe process of learning of #$Culture-Specification usually begins at a\nyoung age, and results in its elements becoming largely internalized.\nSome elements of a #$Culture-Specification -- e.g., aspects of the\n#$NaturalLanguage spoken -- may not be directly accesssible to\nconsciousness even in principle.</p>\n\nA #$Culture-Specification emerges from and is sustained by the activity of agents, and\nmay go out of existence (see #$TemporallyExistingThing).  Component specifications may be added, subtracted, or modified over time.  Associated with each #$Culture-Specification is a corresponding\n#$Culture-Practice, which is the complex event composed of the many\n'followings' of the specification, as well shifts in it, by culture\nmembers over time.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abf92).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abf92,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abf92,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abf92,19029).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abf92,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abf92,[]).
