x_comment(x_GeopoliticalBorder,"The collection of all boundaries, borders, and lines of demarcation that are used to separate one geopolitical region from another.  This includes such things as national borders, the boundaries of #$TimeZones, the boundaries of free trade zones, and maritime and airspace limits.  Borderline cases might be boundaries at the state level--eg, state lines and municipal boundaries.  Note also that instances of #$GeopoliticalBorder are cases of #$GeographicalThing-Intangible.  Although the geographical regions which they serve to demarcate are #$PartiallyTangible enough, the borders that serve to do the demarcating are not.  They are abstractions:  you can't see them or touch them physically.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abf96).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abf96,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abf96,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
