x_comment('x_CulturalConvention-Specification',"A subcollection of #$Specification.    Each instance of\n#$CulturalConvention-Specification is the specification of an activity\nor practice that is a regular part of certain\ncultures, but not of others (though see below).  Practices\nspecified by #$CulturalConvention-Specifications are learned, and\ntypically involve a particular form of activity that is not fully\nnecessitated by biological need or physical environment (e.g., eating\nis not a convention, but eating with certain utensils may be.)\n  To be an\ninstance of #$CulturalConvention-Specification, a specification must\nbe widely followed within a culture by persons in applicable\ncircumstances.  Note that a #$CulturalConvention-Specification is an\nabstract standard for behavior (mentally encoded by culture members),\nrather than the collection of actions conforming to this standard.\n Each is thus a #$subWorks of certain instances of\n#$Culture-Specification. (If there are universals in learned human\nbehavior, they can be considered parts of a general human\nculture).\n Also note that\n#$CulturalConvention-Specification includes both norms of behavior --\nsee #$EtiquetteOfCultureFn -- and customary forms of activity\ndeviations from which would not be considered offensive.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abf99).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abf99,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abf99,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abf99,19066).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abf99,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abf99,[]).
