x_comment(x_setOrCollectionUnion,"A #$TaxonomicSlot for #$SetOrCollections.  <code>(#$setOrCollectionUnion UNION SET-OF-CLASSES)</code> means that <code>UNION</code> is the set-or-collection that is the union of all of the set-or-collections in <code>SET-OF-CLASSES</code>.  More precisely, any thing <code>THING</code> is an #$elementOf <code>UNION</code> if and only if <code>THING</code> is an element of at least one element of <code>SET-OF-CLASSES</code>.  Furthermore, we stipulate that (i) if each element of <code>SET-OF-CLASSES</code> is a set (see #$Set-Mathematical) then <code>UNION</code> is a set and (ii) if each element of <code>SET-OF-CLASSES</code> is a #$Collection then <code>UNION</code> is a collection.  If the elements of <code>SET-OF-CLASSES</code> include both a set and a collection then <code>UNION</code> will either be a set or a collection, though in many cases we might not be able to determine which, and can only conclude that <code>UNION</code> is a #$SetOrCollection.\n<p>\nSee the corresponding function #$SetOrCollectionUnionFn.  Also see #$setOrCollectionUnion2 and #$setOrCollectionIntersection.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abfa3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abfa3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abfa3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
