x_comment(x_interiorOfSetInTopologicalSpace,"If <code>SPACE</code> is a #$TopologicalSpace with base set <code>BASE</code> and <code>SET</code> is a subset of <code>BASE</code>, then the <i>interior</i> of <code>SET</code> is the set of elements of <code>SET</code> for which <code>SET</code> is a neighborhood. (See #$neighborhoodOfThingInTopologicalSpace) In CycL, this relation is expressed as <code>(#$interiorOfSetInTopologicalSpace INTERIOR SET SPACE)</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abfb0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abfb0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
