x_comment(x_separationOfSetInTopologicalSpace,"If <code>SPACE</code> is a #$TopologicalSpace with base set <code>BASE</code> and <code>SET</code> is a subset of <code>BASE</code>, then the sets <code>A</code> and <code>B</code> form a <i>separation of</i> <code>SET</code> if and only if the following conditions are met:\n<p>\n(S<sub>I</sub>) <code>A</code> and <code>B</code> are both non-empty, i.e. #$different from #$TheEmptySet.\n<p>\n(S<sub>II</sub>) <code>SET</code> is the union of <code>A</code> and <code>B</code>.\n<p>\n(S<sub>IIIa</sub>) The intersection of the closure of <code>A</code> and <code>B</code> is empty.\n<p>\n(S<sub>IIIb</sub>) The intersection of the closure of <code>B</code> and <code>A</code> is empty.\n<p>\nIn #$CycL, this relation is expressed as <code>(#$separationOfSetInTopologicalSpace A B SET SPACE)</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abfb4).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abfb4,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
