x_comment(x_primeMeridianForCoordinateSystem,"<code>(#$primeMeridianForCoordinateSystem MERIDIAN SYSTEM)</code> means that <code>MERIDIAN</code> is the #$LongitudeLine from which the azimuth angle for <code>SYSTEM</code> (see #$azimuthAnglePredicate) measures angles. That is, if <code>AZIMUTH-PRED</code> is the azimuth angle predicate for <code>SYSTEM</code>, then <code>(AZIMUTH-PRED MERIDIAN (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure 0))</code> and the value of <code>AZIMUTH-PRED</code> is positive for locations to the east of <code>MERIDIAN</code> and negative for locations west of <code>MERIDIAN</code>. Often, <code>MERIDIAN</code> is the #$PrimeMeridian-Greenwich, however there are some coordinate systems that use other meridians.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abfc5).
