x_comment(x_duration,"A #$TemporalPredicate and #$MeasurableQuantitySlot (qq.v.) that relates a temporal thing to the length of time (see #$Time-Quantity) during which it existed, happened, or obtained.  <code>(#$duration TEMPTHING TIME)</code> means that <code>TIME</code> is the amount of time during which <code>TEMPTHING</code> existed (if a #$SomethingExisting) or happened (if an #$Event) or obtained (if a #$StaticSituation).\n<p>\nNote that if <code>TEMPTHING</code> is an instance of #$TemporallyContinuousThing (q.v.), its #$duration is the same as its #$timeSpan (q.v.): the total elapsed time from its start to its end.  But if <code>TEMPTHING</code> is discontinuous, its duration is strictly less than its time-span.  For example, the playing of the 2004 Super Bowl game has a duration of one hour, but a time-span of several hours.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abfd4).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abfd4,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517abfd4,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517abfd4,19201).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517abfd4,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abfd4,[]).
x_comment(x_occursWhile,"#$occursWhile is a binary predicate relating an event to an instance of #$TemporallyExtendedThing.  <code>(#$occursWhile EVENT TET)</code> means that the event <code>EVENT</code> occurs entirely within the temporal extent of <code>TET</code>.  Thus, <code>(#$occursDuring EVENT TET)</code> implies that <code>(#$temporallySubsumes TET EVENT)</code>. For example, if <code>ASSN</code> is the assassination of Martin Luther King, Jr., then <code>(#$occursWhile ASSN (#$YearFn 1968))</code>.  This is a generalization  of #$occursDuring.  The latter requires an instance of #$TimeInterval while this predicate allows the use of instances of #$TemporallyExtendedThing.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abfd5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abfd5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
