xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517abfea,[]).
x_comment(x_MercatorProjection,"A type of map projection and a specialization of both #$CylindricalProjection and #$EquatorialProjection (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$MercatorProjection involves projecting a #$Spheroid onto a cylinder (see #$CylindricalSurface-WithoutTopAndBottom) that is tangent with the spheroid along the equator (see #$equatorOfSpheroid).  The projection is such that rhumb lines appear as straight lines, and their directions can be measured directly in the map.  Both meridians and parallels are expanded at a ratio equal to the secant of the latitude (with a minor correction made for the oblate-spheroidal shape of the Earth's surface); since the secant of 90 degrees is infinity, the poles cannot be shown.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abfeb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517abfeb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
