x_comment(x_TransverseMercatorProjection,"A type of map projection and a specialization of #$CylindricalProjection (q.v.).  Each instance of #$TransverseMercatorProjection involves projecting a spheroid to a cylinder that is tangent with the spheroid along a meridian (see #$meridianForAxisOfSurfaceOfRevolution).  Also known as \"transverse (or inverse) orthomorphic projections\", they are useful for maps covering a wide band of latitude and a relatively short distance on either side of the tangent meridian. \n<p>\nTransverse Mercator projections use a ficticious graticule, with a ficticious equator at the tangent meridian; and ficticious poles, meridians, parallels, and so forth are defined accordingly.  The <i>Universal Transverse Mercator (UTM) grid </i> is a military grid superimposed upon a transverse Mercator graticule.") :- x_cid(a65b16517abfed).
