x_comment(x_StereographicProjection,"A specialization of #$AzimuthalProjection and #$PerspectiveProjection (qq.v.).  These are also known as <i>azimuthal orthomorphic</i> projections.  In a #$StereographicProjection, the origin of the projecting rays (see #$projectionPointOfOrigin) is the point on the spheroid directly opposite the point of tangency with the target surface.  The scale of a stereographic projection increases (and thus, distortion increases) with distance from the point of tangency, but the increase is gradual enough that an entire hemisphere can be shown without excessive distortion.\n<p>\nStereographic projections are commonly used for maps of polar regions.  A <i>Universal Polar Stereographic</i> (UPS) grid, mathematically adjusted to the graticule, is used as a reference system.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac005).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac005,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac005,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
