x_comment(x_AzimuthalEquidistantProjection,"A specialization of #$AzimuthalProjection that is disjoint with #$PerspectiveProjection.  In a #$AzimuthalEquidistantProjection, the scale of distances is constant along any radial line from the point of tangency.  If the point of tangency is at a pole (see #$PolarAzimuthalEquidistantProjection), then meridians appear as straight lines eminating from the pole, and parallel appear as equally-spaced concentric circles cenered at the pole.  An azimuthal equidistant projection can be used to show the entire spheroid, but the distortion becomes great as the distance from the point of tangency increases.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac00a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac00a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
