x_comment(x_FrictionProcess,"A specialization of #$ForceAffectingAnObjectsMovement.  Each instance of #$FrictionProcess is an event in which at least one of the acting forces (see #$actingForces) isa a #$FrictionVector.  When a #$FrictionProcess occurs it inhibits the relative motion between objects which are in physical contact (see #$touches).  If motion is already happening, the force acts in a direction opposite to motion.  If the motion has not started, as in the case of static friction, the frictional force acts in a direction opposite that of the net applied forces.  Examples include air friction, rolling friction, and mechanical friction.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac019).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac019,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac019,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
