x_comment('x_LinearObject-Bounded',"A specialization of #$LinearObject (q.v.). #$LinearObject-Bounded is the collection of all and only linearly-shaped objects that have two boundaries or end-points.  They might be straight or curved, tangible or intangible.  All bounded linear objects are finite in length (see #$LinearObject-Finite), as infinite linear objects can have at most one end-point. \n<p>\nSpecializations of #$LinearObject-Bounded include #$LineSegment-Straight and #$EllipticalCurve, both of whose instances are strictly one-dimensional.\n<p>\nCf. #$LinearObject-Unbounded and #$LinearObject-SemiBounded.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac038).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac038,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
