x_comment(x_MinutesDuration,"A #$UnitOfTime (q.v.) function that takes one or two real numbers as arguments and returns, as its value, a comparable #$Time-Quantity  (q.v.) measured in minutes.  Thus an expression of the form <code>(#$MinutesDuration NUM)</code> denotes the (\"point-value\") time-quantity of being exactly <code>NUM</code> minutes in duration, and an expression of the form <code>(#$MinutesDuration MIN MAX)</code> denotes the (properly interval-like) time-quantity of being at least <code>MIN</code> minutes and at most <code>MAX</code> minutes in duration.\n<p>\nSee also #$SecondsDuration and #$HoursDuration.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac06c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac06c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
