x_comment('x_Pound-UnitOfMass',"A #$UnitOfMass and an #$FPSUnitOfMeasure (qq.v.).  #$Pound-UnitOfMass is the basic unit of mass in the British (FPS) system.  \n(#$Pound-UnitOfMass 1) is the amount of mass possessed by an object weighing one pound (cf. #$Pound-UnitOfForce) at sea-level on the Earth's surface.  One pound is equal to sixteen #$Ounces (q.v.).\n<p>\nStrictly speaking, the FPS <i>pound</i> is the unit of force, analogous to the #$Newton in the MKS system.  #$Pound-UnitOfMass is introduced here primarily to facilitate interconversions between pounds and kilograms in the terrestrial frame of reference.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac06e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac06e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac06e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
