x_comment(x_AzimuthalProjection,"A specialization of #$DirectMapProjection (q.v.).   Each instance of #$AzimuthalProjection is a map projection whereby points on the source spheroid are mapped directly to a flat target surface tangent to the spheroid, rather than by way of an intermediate #$DevelopableSurface.  They are also known as <i>zenithal</i> projections.  Typically, the target surface wil be tangent to the spheroid at one of its poles (see #$PolarProjection; but cf. #$ObliqueGnomonicProjection).  An azimuthal projection correctly represents the bearing of any point from the point of tangency.  \"Great circles\" through the point of tangency (e.g. the meridians, if the projection is polar) appear as straight lines.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac080).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac080,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac080,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac080,19525).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac080,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac080,[]).
x_comment(x_setOrCollectionUnion2,"A binary predicate that relates a pair of #$SetOrCollections to their union.  <code>(#$setOrCollectionUnion2 UNION CLASS1 CLASS2)</code> entails that, for any thing <code>THING</code>, <code>THING</code> is an #$elementOf <code>UNION</code> if and only if <code>THING</code> is an element of <code>CLASS1</code> or an element of <code>CLASS2</code>.  Furthermore, we stipulate that (i) if both <code>CLASS1</code> and <code>CLASS2</code> are sets (see #$Set-Mathematical) then <code>UNION</code> is a set and (ii) if both <code>CLASS1</code> and <code>CLASS2</code> are #$Collections then <code>UNION</code> is a collection.  If one of them is a set and the other a collection then <code>UNION</code> will either be a set or a collection, though in many cases we might not be able to determine which, and can only conclude that <code>UNION</code> is a #$SetOrCollection.\n<p>\nAlso see #$setOrCollectionUnion and #$setOrCollectionIntersection2.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac081).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac081,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac081,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac081,19526).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac081,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac081,[]).
x_comment(x_neighborhoodOfSetInTopologicalSpace,"If <code>SPACE</code> is a topological space with base set <code>BASE</code> (see #$baseSetOfTopologicalSpace), <code>NEIGHBORHOOD</code> is a subset of <code>BASE</code>, and <code>SET</code> is a subset of <code>NEIGHBORHOOD</code>, then <code>NEIGHBORHOOD</code> is a <i>neighborhood</i> of <code>SET</code> if and only if there exists an open set <code>OPENSET</code> of <code>SPACE</code> which is a subset of <code>NEIGHBORHOOD</code> and contains <code>SET</code> as a subset. In #$CycL, this relation is expressed as <code>(#$neighborhoodOfSetInTopologicalSpace SET NEIGHBORHOOD SPACE)</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac082).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac082,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac082,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac082,19529).
