x_comment(x_creationTemplateAssertions,"(#$creationTemplateAssertions TEMPLATE ASSERTION) means that ASSERTION is one of the assertions that forms the instance of #$CycCreationTemplate, TEMPLATE. This means that the code-level function associated with TEMPLATE (see #$creationTemplateForSubLFunction) is responsible for adding an analogous assertion to the KB.  The assertion is analgous in the following way:  Let ASSERTION = (ARG-0 ARG-1 ... ARG-N).  For any arg ARG in ARG-0 - ARG-N that is known to be an exemplar FORT for TEMPLATE (see #$creationTemplateFORTs), an analogous assertion will be one just like ASSERTION, but with ARG replaced by an appropriately analogous FORT reified during the call to that code-level function.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac097).
