x_comment(x_UnaryPolynomialOfDegreeWithCoefficientsFn,"An expression of the form (#$UnaryPolynomialOfDegreeWithCoefficientsFn DEGREE LIST) denotes a #$UnaryPolynomialFunction of degree DEGREE (that is the highest power to which the variable is raised), where the Nth element of list is the coefficient of the term in function that is raised to the power N-1.  For instance, an expression of the form (#$UnaryPolynomialOfDegreeWithCoefficientsFn 2 (TheList 3 4 1) could be written out as f(x) = x^2 + 4x + 3.  This function abstracts away from the actual choice of variables in the formula.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac09c).
