x_comment(x_TopologicalSpaceTypeBySeparationProperty,"#$TopologicalSpaceTypeBySeparationProperty is a specialization of #$TopologicalSpaceType which identifies #$TopologicalSpaces according to their separation properties. More precisely, each instance of #$TopologicalSpaceTypeBySeparationProperty is a specialization of #$TopologicalSpace determined by how tightly a closed subset can be contained within an open set. The measure of tightness is the extent to which this envelope can separate the subset from other subsets. Following the standard mathematical convention, the names of these collections are all prefixed by the letter 'T' followed by a numeral between 0 and 4. The incresasing sequence of numerals refers to the increasing degree of separation.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac100).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac100,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac100,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
