x_comment(x_organizationKeyMembers,"This predicate is used to identify an important member of a particular organization, i.e., one who plays a crucial role in its successful operation.  (#$organizationKeyMembers ORG PER) means that the #$Person PER holds a key position in the #$Organization ORG.  A key position in an organization is one whose vacancy would severely and negatively impact the functioning of the organization.  Common key roles are: a leader (e.g., President, C.E.O., Admiral), a senior executive, a board member, a cabinet member, a junta member, a major owner, or other important decision-makers.  Because #$organizationKeyMembers is closely tied to the functioning of an organization, the role and characteristics of a key member may be highly specialized; for example, #$organizationKeyMembers of a professional sports team, or #$organizationKeyMembers of a surgical practice.  A key member is, or often gives input to, the organization's leader and thus may substantially influence the decisions of the organization.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac10d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac10d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac10d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
