x_comment(x_compoundStringSenseExtension,"<code>(#$wordSenseExtension WORD SPEECH-PART-1 DENOTATION SPEECH-PART-2 EXTENSION LIST)</code> means that the use of the word <code>WORD</code> with speech part <code>SPEECH-PART-2</code> followed by the string picked out by <code>LIST</code>  to mean <code>EXTENSION</code> is an extension of the sense of the #$compoundString associated with <code>LIST</code> and <code>WORD</code> -- in particular the sense with speech part </code>SPEECH-PART-1</code> and denotation <code>DENOTATION</code>.  For example, \n<pre>\n(#$compoundStringSenseExtension #$Bird-TheWord #$CountNoun #$BirdOfPrey #$MassNoun (MeatFn BirdOfPrey))</pre>\nmeans that the use of \"bird of prey\" as a mass noun to refer to meat from birds of prey is an extension of the count noun sense of \"bird of prey\" meaning the #$BirdOfPrey.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac134).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac134,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac134,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac134,19788).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac134,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac134,[]).
x_comment(x_multiWordStringSenseExtension,"(#$multiWordStringSenseExtensionBrokeredByPred WORD SPEECH-PART-1 DENOTATION SPEECH-PART-2 EXTENSION BINARY-PREDICATE LIST) means that the fact that\n\n   (#$multiWordStringSenseExtension WORD SPEECH-PART-1 DENOTATION SPEECH-PART-2 EXTENSION LIST)\n\nis explained in part by the fact that\n\n   (BINARY-PREDICATE ARG1 ARG2)\n\nfor some ARG1 and ARG2 such that\n\n   (#$multiWordString WORD SPEECH-PART-1 ARG1)\n\nfor some N.\n\nThe reason why this sense extension is only partly explained by the above considerations reflects the fact that due to Cyc's incomplete knowledge, there will be many cases where BINARY-PREDICATE is not an instance of #$SenseExtendingPredicate, and so cannot reliably broker sense extensions from SPEECH-PART-1 to SPEECH-PART-2 for any word denoting one of its arg1s. Rather, there is a possibly unreified specialization SPEC-PRED of BINARY-PRED (see genlPreds) that is an instance of SenseExtendingPredicate, and the fact that (SPEC-PRED ARG1 ARG2) fully explains the sense extension in question. ") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac135).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac135,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac135,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac135,19792).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac135,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac135,[]).
x_comment('x_multiWordStringSenseExtensionBrokeredByPred-Inverse',"<code>(#$multiWordStringSenseExtensionBrokeredByPred-Inverse WORD SPEECH-PART-1 DENOTATION SPEECH-PART-2 EXTENSION BINARY-PREDICATE LIST)</code> means that the fact that <pre>\n   (#$multiWordStringSenseExtension WORD SPEECH-PART-1 DENOTATION SPEECH-PART-2 EXTENSION LIST)</pre> is explained <i>in part</i> by the fact that <pre>\n   (BINARY-PREDICATE ARG1 ARG2)</pre> for some <code>ARG1</code> and <code>ARG2</code> such that \n<pre>\n   (#$multiWordString LIST WORD SPEECH-PART-1 ARG2)</pre> for some N. <p>The reason why this sense extension is only <i>partly</i> explained by the above considerations reflects the fact that due to Cyc's incomplete knowledge, there will be many cases where BINARY-PREDICATE is not an instance of #$SenseExtendingPredicate, and so cannot <i>reliably</i> broker sense extensions from SPEECH-PART-1 to SPEECH-PART-2 for any word denoting one of its arg1s.  Rather, there is a possibly unreified specialization SPEC-PRED of BINARY-PRED (see #$genlPreds) that is an instance of #$SenseExtendingPredicate, and the fact that (SPEC-PRED ARG1 ARG2) fully explains the sense extension in question.  ") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac136).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac136,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac136,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac136,19807).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac136,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac136,[]).
x_comment(x_multiWordStringSenseExtensionBrokeredByPred,"<code>(#$multiWordStringSenseExtensionBrokeredByPred WORD SPEECH-PART-1 DENOTATION SPEECH-PART-2 EXTENSION BINARY-PREDICATE LIST)</code> means that the fact that <pre>\n   (#$multiWordStringSenseExtension WORD SPEECH-PART-1 DENOTATION SPEECH-PART-2 EXTENSION LIST)</pre> is explained <i>in part</i> by the fact that <pre>\n   (BINARY-PREDICATE ARG1 ARG2)</pre> for some <code>ARG1</code> and <code>ARG2</code> such that \n<pre>\n   (#$multiWordString LIST WORD SPEECH-PART-1 ARG1)</pre>. <p>The reason why this sense extension is only <i>partly</i> explained by the above considerations reflects the fact that due to Cyc's incomplete knowledge, there will be many cases where BINARY-PREDICATE is not an instance of #$SenseExtendingPredicate, and so cannot <i>reliably</i> broker sense extensions from SPEECH-PART-1 to SPEECH-PART-2 for any word denoting one of its arg1s.  Rather, there is a possibly unreified specialization SPEC-PRED of BINARY-PRED (see #$genlPreds) that is an instance of #$SenseExtendingPredicate, and the fact that (SPEC-PRED ARG1 ARG2) fully explains the sense extension in question.  ") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac137).
