xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac149,[]).
x_comment(x_BilateralObject,"A specialization of #$SpatialThing-Localized.  Each instance of #$BilateralObject is an object that has a well-defined pair of opposing sides (see #$objectSides) -- such as front and back, bottom and top, or left and right.  \"Well-defined\" here just means either naturally-determined (e.g. the front-back of a mammal and the top-bottom of a hill) or conventionally-determined (e.g. the left-right of a car and the top-bottom of a soda can).  \n<p>\nExamples of non-bilateral objects are ball bearings and sugar cubes.\n<p>\nSee also the specializations #$FrontAndBackSidedObject, #$LeftAndRightSidedObject, and #$TopAndBottomSidedObject.  An object that is an instance of all three of these collections is a #$HexalateralObject.\n<p>\nAlso see #$bilateralAxes and #$NoteAboutSidedObjects.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac14a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac14a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac14a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
