x_comment(x_BinaryQuantityPredicate,"A specialization of #$BinaryPredicate and #$IntangibleObjectPredicate whose instances relate things to quantities.  A binary predicate is an instance of #$BinaryQuantityPredicate if and only if its #$arg1Isa or its #$arg2Isa (or both) is a specialization of #$Quantity.  Examples include #$sizeParameterOfObject, #$followingValue, #$lifeExpectancy, and many others.  \n<p>\nNote that if a binary quantity predicate is such that (i) its #$arg2Format is #$intervalEntryFormatInArgs and (ii) its #$arg1Isa is <i>not</i> a specialization of #$Quantity, it is an instance of the more specialized collection #$QuantitySlot.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac16e).
