x_comment('x_ensures-AgentProp',"A binary #$PropositionPredicate that is used to state that an agent makes sure that something is the case.  <code>(#$ensures-AgentProp AGENT SENT)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> ensures that <code>SENT</code> is true: <code>AGENT</code> determines whether <code>SENT</code> is true and, if it's not, intentionally performs an action that causes <code>SENT</code> to become true.  This implies that <code>SENT</code> expresses a contingent truth: although <code>SENT</code> is (at least upon being ensured) in fact true, it might not have been true (and perhaps wasn't true before being ensured).  Typically, immediately before ensuring <code>SENT</code>, <code>AGENT</code> wants <code>SENT</code> to be true (and might even believe it's likely to be true already), but is not certain that it's true.  \n<p>\nFor example, I sometimes ensure that the back door is locked when I'm about to leave my house.  First, I go and check the door.  If I find it's locked, I'm done.  Or, if it's unlocked, I lock it, and then I'm done.  \n<p>\nSee also #$ensures-SitProp.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac176).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac176,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac176,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac176,19960).
