x_comment(x_mealServed,"(#$mealServed <code>HAVING-A-MEAL</code> <code>MEAL</code>)\nmeans that <code>MEAL</code> is the instance of #$Meal that is acted\non during <code>HAVING-A-MEAL</code>.  That is, <code>MEAL</code> is\nthe #$Meal that is served or otherwise provided for consumption during\n<code>HAVING-A-MEAL</code>, and which is subsequently consumed during\nthat event.  Note that <code>MEAL</code> need not be <i>completely</i>\nconsumed during <code>HAVING-A-MEAL</code> -- portions may remain to\nbe finished later or discarded.  Thus, #$mealServed is not a\nspecialization of #$consumedObject.  Also, <code>MEAL</code> need not\nbe served to the participants in <code>HAVING-A-MEAL</code> in the\nformal sense of #$ServingFoodOrDrink, since participants may fetch\ntheir own portion of <code>MEAL</code> themselves.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac187).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac187,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
