x_comment(x_nounLearnerConjecturedTypeFromNounUsages,"<code>(#$nounLearnerConjecturedTypeFromNounUsages USAGES COLLECTION)</code> means that where <code>USAGES</code> represents all observed usages of an unknown noun in the subject or direct object relation to verbs, the Noun Learner (see #$CycNounLearnerTool) conjectures that the noun denotes an instance or specialization of <code>COLLECTION</code>.  The Noun Learner's conjecture is based on statistical analysis of verb-argument cooccurrences in some text corpus (like, perhaps, the New York Times from 2001).  <code>USAGES</code> must take the form of an extensional list <code>(#$TheList SUBJECT-USAGES OBJECT-USAGES)</code> where <code>SUBJECT-USAGES</code> is the list of infinitive verb-strings of which the noun occurred as the subject and <code>OBJECT-USAGES</code> is the list of infinitive verb-strings of which the noun occurred as the direct object.  A given verb can appear more than once in a list to reflect multiple occurrences with the noun.<p>For example, <code>(#$nounLearnerConjecturedTypeFromNounUsages (#$TheList (#$TheList \"explode\") (#$TheList \"fire\" \"fire\" \"load\")) #$Weapon)</code> means that, given that a noun occurred once as the subject of the verb \"explode\", twice as the direct object of \"fire\", and once as the direct object of \"load\", the Noun Learner conjectures that it denotes an instance or specialization of #$Weapon.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac19d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac19d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac19d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac19d,20024).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac19d,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac19d,[]).
x_comment(x_nounLearnerConjecturedTypeForNounFromCorpus,"<code>(#$nounLearnerConjecturedTypeForNounFromCorpus NOUN-STRING COLLECTION CORPUS)</code> means that, based on statistical analysis of its usages in the text corpus <code>CORPUS</code>, the Noun Learner conjectures that the noun <code>NOUN-STRING</code> denotes an instance or specialization of <code>COLLECTION</code>.  For example, <code>(#$nounLearnerConjecturedTypeForNounFromCorpus \"rutabaga\" #$EdibleStuff #$NewYorkTimes2001TextCorpus)</code> means that \"rutabaga\" is conjectured to denote an instance or specialization of #$EdibleStuff.  Be sure to use non-plural forms of nouns in queries.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac19e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac19e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac19e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
