x_comment(x_SimilarityMetricFn,"An instance of #$EvaluatableFunction, <code>(#$SimilarityMetricFn THING-1 THING-2)</code> evaluates to an instance of #$Real0-1 that indicates a measure of similarity between <code>THING-1</code> and <code>THING-2</code>. Higher values indicate a larger degree of similarity; by definition <code>(#$SimilarityMetricFn THING THING)</code> evaluates to 1.  <p>Similarity here is based on the ontology, and is computed as the intersection of the number of generalizations of <code>THING-1</code> and <code>THING-2</code> over the union of their generalizations, where a \"generalization\" of a thing <code>THING</code> includes every collection <code>COLL</code> such that <code>THING</code> is either an instance or specialization of <code>COLL</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac1a1).
