x_comment('x_SQLOperatorSyntax-InverseInfix',"A #$CSQLToSQLTranslationSyntaxDirective which directs the CSQL to SQL translator to invert the argument order and then use operator infix syntax. This term should appear only within a #$csqlOperatorToSQLOperator assertion. For example, the sentence\n<pre>                                                                                              \n(#$csqlOperatorToSQLOperator #$CSQLRegexStringMatch \"~\" #$PostgreSQL #$SQLOperatorSyntax-InverseInfix)\n</pre>\ntells SKSI's CycL to SQL translator that to translate a literal such as\n<pre>\n(#$CSQLRegexStringMatch \"[DL]og\" \"Dog\")\n</pre>\ninto an SQL expression to be evaulated by a #$PostgreSQL DBMS, it should invert the argument order and then infix the operator between its arguments, so that the resultant SQL literal would be\n<pre>\n'Dog' ~ '[DL]og'.\n</pre>") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac1b5).
