x_comment(x_SurfaceProjection,"A collection of unary functions that map subregions of one two-dimensional surface (the #$projectionSource) to subregions of another (the #$projectionTarget).  Each instance <code>PROJ</code> of #$SurfaceProjection (with source <code>SOURCE</code> and target <code>TARGET</code>) is a function that (i) is defined only on space regions subsumed by <code>SOURCE</code>, (ii) is defined on every <i>part</i> (see #$partOfSpaceRegion) of <code>SOURCE</code>, and (iii) takes anything it's defined on to some space region subsumed by <code>TARGET</code>.  \n<p>\nNote that, clause (ii) above notwithstanding, <code>PROJ</code> might <i>not</i> be defined on every region <i>subsumed by</i> (see #$spatiallySubsumes) <code>SOURCE</code>.  For example, a given #$ConicProjection might be defined on every subregion of a hemisphere except the pole.\n<p>\nOf particular interest are those surface projections whose source is all or part of a #$Spheroid (such as an idealization of the Earth's surface) and whose target is a #$FlatSurfaceRegion (such as might serve as the \"spatial universe\" of a two-dimensional #$Map).  See #$MapProjection.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac1f0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac1f0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac1f0,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac1f0,20126).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac1f0,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac1f0,[]).
x_comment(x_IdempotentBinaryFunction,"A specialization of #$BinaryFunction.  A binary function <code>FUNC</code> is an instance of #$IdempotentBinaryFunction if and only if it has the following property: for any thing <code>THING</code> that is an #$admittedArgument to both of <code>FUNC</code>'s argument-places, <code>(FUNC THING THING) = THING</code>.  \n<p>\nExamples of idempotent binary functions include #$CollectionIntersection2Fn, #$SpatialSumFn, and the binary version of #$Unity, viz. (#$Lambda (?X ?Y) (#$Unity ?X ?Y)).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac1f1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac1f1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac1f1,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac1f1,20131).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac1f1,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac1f1,[]).
x_comment(x_EarthsGeoidSurface,"The shape of the #$PlanetEarth's gravitational equipotential surface. That is, the #$EarthsGeoidSurface is the unique surface which satisfies the following conditions:\n<p>\n1. Given any #$Point, <code>POINT</code>, on the surface, the normal line at <code>POINT</code> (see #$normalLineAtPointOnSurface) is parallel to the #$GravitationalForceVector at <code>POINT</code>;\n<p>\n2. The magnitude of the #$GravitationalForceVector at <code>POINT</code> is constant for all <code>POINT</code>s on the surface.\n<p>\nA consequence of this definition is that the #$EarthsGeoidSurface is the surface to which the oceans would conform over the entire planet, if they were free to adjust to the combined effect of the Earth's mass attraction and the centrifugal force of the Earth's rotation.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac1f2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac1f2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac1f2,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac1f2,20134).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac1f2,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac1f2,[]).
x_comment(x_normalLineAtPointOnSurface,"A line is <i>normal</i> to a surface if and only if it is perpendicular to the tangent plane of the surface at the point at which the line intersects the surface. <code>(#$normalLineAtPointOnSurface POINT LINE SURFACE)</code> means that <code>LINE</code> is the #$Line-Straight which passes through the #$Point, <code>POINT</code>, and is perpendicular to (see #$perpendicularObjects) the tangent plane of the #$Surface, <code>SURFACE</code>, at <code>POINT</code> (see #$tangentPlaneAtPointOnSurface).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac1f3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac1f3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac1f3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
