x_comment(x_ResultStandsInRelationFn,"<code>(#$ResultStandsInRelationFn BINARY-PREDICATE)</code> denotes the instance <code>PRED</code> of #$MetaFunction and #$BinaryPredicate such that <code>(#$metaFunctionBasis PRED BINARY-PREDICATE)</code>.  For example,  <code>(#$ResultStandsInRelationFn #$isa)</code> denotes the same thing as #$resultIsa -- namely, a meta-function that relates a function to a collection such that any defined result of applying that function will be an instance of that collection.  Similarly, <code>(#$ResultStandsInRelationFn #$genls)</code> denotes the same thing as #$resultGenl -- a meta function that relates a function to a collection such that any defined result of applying it will be a specialization of that collection.  #$ResultStandsInRelationFn allows one to construct such meta functions on the fly, and avoids the need for separate forward rules for each such meta function.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac1fc).
