x_comment(x_nounStringOccursAsObjectForVerbStringsInCorpus,"<code>(#$nounStringOccursAsObjectForVerbStringsInCorpus STRING USAGES SOURCE)</code> means that <code>USAGES</code> represents all observed usages of the noun with nonplural string <code>STRING</code> as an object in the instance of #$InformationStore <code>SOURCE</code>.  <code>USAGES</code> must take the form of an extensional list (see #$List-Extensional) of infinitive verb-strings.  A given verb can appear more than once in a list to reflect multiple occurrences with the noun.<p>For example, <code>(#$nounStringOccursAsObjectForVerbStringsInCorpus \"apple\" (#$TheList \"eat\" \"eat\" \"slice\" \"toss\") #$NewYorkTimes2001TextCorpus)</code> means that in the New York Times 2001 corpus, the noun 'apple' occurred twice as the object of the verb 'to eat,' once as the object of the verb 'to slice,' and once as the object of the verb 'to toss.'<p> See also #$nounStringOccursAsSubjectForVerbStringsInCorpus.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac20b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac20b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
