x_comment(x_liftTo,"This predicate, used primarily for rules, allows one to override a particular microtheory dimension.  For example, '(#$liftTo (#$MtTimeDimFn (#$YearFn 1997)) (#$objectFoundInLocation OBJ LOC))' says that '(#$objectFoundInLocation OBJ LOC)' is true in the microtheory that would result from replacing the time index (see #$mtTimeIndex) of the current context (the result of querying '(#$indexicalReferent #$QueryMt ?X)') with '(#$MtTimeDimFn (#$YearFn 1997))'.  ") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac210).
