x_comment(x_PackedCyclifierLexiconSpecification,"A specialization of #$CyclifierLexiconSpecification.  Instances of #$PackedCyclifierLexiconSpecification will return semTrans semantics that will pack as much ambiguity as possible into a single lexical entry.  For example, if the word \"blork\" has two denotations, #$Blork and #$Blonk, that fit in the same syntactic contexts, the lexical entry returned by a #$PackedCyclifierLexiconSpecification will be of the form (#$isa :NOUN (#$TheIntendedOneOfFn \"blork\" #$Blork #$Blonk)).  This contrasts with a #$CyclifierLexiconSpecification, which would return two separate entries: (#$isa :NOUN #$Blork) and (#$isa :NOUN #$Blonk).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac22e).
