x_comment(x_occupiedActors,"This predicate relates an agent to an event that s/he is occupied with participating in, in the sense of being busy  with or absorbed in the event.  <code>(#$occupiedActors EVENT AGENT)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is occupied with participating in <code>EVENT</code>.  \n<p>\nNote  that #$occupiedActors is a specialization of #$deliberateActors,  and thus the foregoing is not to be confused with <code>AGENT</code>'s being  occupied with <code>EVENT</code> in the sense that s/he merely #$thinksAbout <code>EVENT</code> in a focused way, as (say) a contemporary historian might be  \"occupied\" with the reign of King Louis XIV.  For this latter sense of 'occupied', see #$occupiedWith.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac239).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac239,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
