x_comment('x_SpatialThing-Localized',"A specialization of both #$SpatialThing and #$TemporalThing.  This is the collection of all spatial things, tangible or intangible, that can meaningfully be said to have location or position in the empirical universe.   \n<p>\nExamples of spatially-localized things include all #$PartiallyTangible things, such as trees and ships, as well as certain #$Intangible spatial things, like the #$EarthsEquator.  Also included are those events that can be pinned-down to specific places (see #$Event-Localized), and thus all #$PhysicalEvents.  Excluded from this collection are any #$SpatialThings that are <i>not</i> localized, such as -- arguably -- purely abstract geometrical figures (e.g. a Platonic sphere). \n<p>\nNote that a fictional or imaginary object (such as Frodo, Captain Queeg, or #$HAL9000-TheComputer) is typically localized with respect to the universe of the fictional/imagnary context in which it is found, and so is an instance of #$SpatialThing-Localized with respect to that context.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac267).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac267,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac267,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac267,20355).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac267,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac267,[]).
x_comment(x_GeneralizedSpatialSumFn,"A unary function that takes a set of spatial things (see #$SpatialThingSet) of the same basic type (i.e. #$PartiallyTangible, #$SpaceRegion, or #$Event-Localized) to their mereological sum or union.  Where <b>SET</b> is a set of tangible objects (space regions, spatially-localized events), (#$GeneralizedSpatialSumFn <b>SET</b>) is the tangible object (space region, spatially-localized event) that is the spatial sum of all the elements of <b>SET</b>.  \n<p>\nThis function is a generalization of the function #$GeneralizedSpaceRegionSumFn, which takes equidimensional sets of homogeneous space regions (see #$EquidimensionalSpaceRegionSet) to their mereological sum.\n<p>\nSee the corresponding predicate #$generalizedSpatialSum.  Also see #$GeneralizedSpatialProductFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac268).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac268,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac268,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac268,20360).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac268,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac268,[]).
x_comment(x_generalizedSpatialSum,"A binary predicate that relates a set of spatial things (see #$SpatialThingSet) of the same basic type (i.e. #$PartiallyTangible, #$SpaceRegion, or #$Event-Localized) to their mereological sum or union.  <code>(#$generalizedSpatialSum SUM SET)</code> means that <code>SUM</code> is the spatial sum of all the elements of <code>SET</code>.  \n<code>SUM</code> is itself of the same basic type as the elements of <code>SET</code>; e.g. if <code>SET</code> is a set of tangible objects, then <code>SUM</code> is a tangible object.\n<p>\nThis predicate is a generalization of the predicate #$generalizedSpaceRegionSum, which relates a set of equidimensional, homogeneous space regions (see #$EquidimensionalSpaceRegionSet) to their sum.\n<p>\nSee the corresponding function #$GeneralizedSpatialSumFn.  Also see #$generalizedSpatialProduct.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac269).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac269,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac269,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac269,20365).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac269,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac269,[]).
x_comment(x_GeneralizedSpatialProductFn,"A unary function that takes a set of spatial things (see #$SpatialThingSet) of the same basic type (i.e. #$PartiallyTangible, #$SpaceRegion, or #$Event-Localized) to their mereological product or intersection.  Where <b>SET</b> is a set of tangible objects (space regions, spatially-localized events), (#$GeneralizedSpatialProductFn <b>SET</b>) is the tangible object (space region, spatially-localized event) that is the spatial product of all the elements of <b>SET</b>.  \n<p>\nThis function is a generalization of the function #$GeneralizedSpaceRegionProductFn, which takes equidimensional sets of homogeneous space regions (see #$EquidimensionalSpaceRegionSet) to their mereological sum.\n<p>\n#$GeneralizedSpatialProductFn is #$undefined (or, in certain cases, returns a #$NullSpaceRegion) for any set of spatial things such that some of its elements are #$spatiallyDisjoint from others.  It is not defined on any set whose members are not all of the same basic spatial type.\n<p>\nSee the corresponding predicate #$generalizedSpatialProduct.  Also see #$GeneralizedSpatialSumFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac26a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac26a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac26a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac26a,20371).
