x_comment(x_ActionAttributeLevelQuantity,"A specialization of #$Quantity.  Each instance of #$ActionAttributeLevelQuantity is a particular <i>level</i> or amount of a certain type of quantity that an #$Action, or the performance of it, can exhibit.  \n<p>\nFor example, (#$HighAmountFn #$Dangerousness) is an #$ActionAttributeLevelQuantity\npossessed by actions that are highly dangerous.  (#$MediumAmountFn #$Gracefulness)  is an action-attribute-level quantity exhibited by any moderately graceful performance of an action.  The latter example is also an instance of the more specialized collection #$PerformanceLevelQuantity (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac27b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac27b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac27b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac27b,20406).
