x_comment(x_earliestDateOfFactOfCalendarCoveringType,"(#$earliestDateOfFactOfCalendarCoveringType ASSERT CAL-TYPE DATE) means that either DATE is itself an instance of CAL-TYPE and (#$earliestDateOfFact ASSERT DATE), or that there is a date, SOME-DATE, such that (#$earliestDateOfFact ASSERT SOME-DATE), such that DATE is a 'component'of SOME-DATE (i.e., (#$termFormulas DATE SOME-DATE)), DATE is an instance of CAL-TYPE, and there is no other component of SOME-DATE that is an instance of CAL-TYPE that is any earlier than DATE.  Intuitively, (#$latestDateOfFactOfCalendarCoveringType ASSERT CAL-TYPE DATE) means that DATE is the earliest date of type CAL-TYPE at which the content expressed by ASSERT is known to be true in the KB.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac282).
