x_comment('x_WNAllHypernymDenotsForWordPOSFn-Default',"A #$BinaryFunction and #$EvaluatableFunction that returns a #$Set-Mathematical of (quoted) instances of #$CycLExpression.   An evaluation of an expression of the form (#$WNAllHypernymDenotsForWordPOSFn-Default LEXICAL-WORD POS)  function consults the #$WordNetKnowledgeBase #$WordNet-Version2_0 to find direct hypernyms for the #$LexicalWord LEXICAL-WORD based on the #$SpeechPart POS.   A direct hypernym of the #$WordNetSynset BASE-SS is a more general #$WordNetSynset where there is an asserted, rather than implied,  #$wnHypernym relation.    Based on the #$LexicalWords that it finds, it will return all known #$denotations for those hypernym words for POS.  As its arguments indicate, this function operates to relate a #$LexicalWord to (possibly many) instances of #$CycLExpression.  It does not associate instances of #$WordNetSynset and  #$CycLExpression, therefore, its results will reflect the ambiguity in mapping from words to concepts.  The 'default' aspect of the name indicates that this functions employs the simplest method for going from lexical words to concepts.  Other functions could incorporate different available methods.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac28d).
