x_comment(x_authorizedToControl,"(#$authorizedToControl CONTROLLER THING) means that\nCONTROLLER is authorized (in some fashion, see below) to control the\nactivities or disposition of THING.  #$authorizedToControl is\nessentially a <i>de jure</i> version of #$controls -- it expresses the\n<i>authority</i> to control, rather than actual control.  These two\nrelationships often go together, of course.  But it is also possible\nto have such authority but not use it (or be unable to), and possible\nto exert control without relevant authorization.  For example, if\nPERSON1 #$owns THING and PERSON2 #$steals it, then PERSON1 retains the\n(legal) authority to control THING, but actual control passes to\nPERSON2.  The 'authority' expressed by this predicate often has a\nlegal basis, as in the case of ownership.  But certain other sources\nmay also confer authority.  For example, such authority might attach\nto a certain position within an organization (i.e., be recognized\nwithin the organization), even if that authority is not legally\nenforceable (in fact, even if the organization is illegal, e.g., a\ncriminal organization).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac2ad).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac2ad,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac2ad,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac2ad,20491).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac2ad,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac2ad,[]).
x_comment(x_occursDuring,"#$occursDuring is a binary predicate relating an event to a time interval in which it occurs.  <code>(#$occursDuring EVENT TIMEINTERVAL)</code> means that the event <code>EVENT</code> occurs entirely within the time interval <code>TIMEINTERVAL</code>.  Thus, <code>(#$occursDuring EVENT TIMEINTERVAL)</code> implies that <code>(#$temporallySubsumes TIMEINTERVAL EVENT)</code>. For example, if <code>ASSN</code> is the assassination of Martin Luther King, Jr., then <code>(#$occursDuring ASSN (#$YearFn 1968))</code>.  See also #$dateOfEvent.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac2ae).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac2ae,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
