x_comment(x_magneticInclinationAtPointOnEarth,"The <i>magnetic inclination</i> at any geographical point, <code>POINT</code>, on #$PlanetEarth is the angle between the gravitational vector at <code>POINT</code> and the vertical component of the Earth's magnetic field at <code>POINT</code>. In #$CycL, this relation is denoted by <code>(#$magneticInclinationAtPointOnEarth POINT INCLINATION)</code>. The #$MagneticNorthPoleOfEarth is by definition the point on #$PlanetEarth where the inclination is (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure 0), and the #$MagneticSouthPoleOfEarth is the point on #$PlanetEarth where the inclination is (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure 180).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac2ce).
