x_comment(x_IntervalEndedByLastSubintervalOfTypeFn,"A binary evaluatable function which takes a #$TimeInterval and a #$TimeParameter and returns a #$TimeInterval.  <code>(#$IntervalEndedByLastSubintervalOfTypeFn INTERVAL TYPE)</code> denotes the time interval ended by the last subinterval of <code>INTERVAL</code> of type <code>TYPE</code>.  Note that this is only defined if <code>INTERVAL</code> subsumes an instance of <code>TYPE</code>.  So, for example, (#$IntervalEndedByLastSubintervalOfTypeFn (#$YearFn 2004) #$CalendarMonth) denotes (#$IntervalEndedByFn (#$MonthFn #$December (#$YearFn 2004))).  On the other hand, (#$IntervalEndedByLastSubintervalOfTypeFn (#$YearFn 2004) #$CalendarDecade) is undefined.  See also #$ELIntervalEndedByLastSubintervalOfTypeFn and #$IntervalStartedByFirstSubintervalOfTypeFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac2f9).
