x_comment(x_SimpleHarmonicOscillation,"A simple harmonic oscillation is a harmonic oscillation which is neither damped nor driven. That is, the primary object moving in the oscillation is not acted upon by either a frictional force or a driving force. A simple harmonic oscillation is a special case of a conservative physical event for which, by definition, the sum of the potential and kinetic energy of the primary object moving is constant.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac30e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac30e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
