x_comment(x_HarmonicOscillation,"A harmonic oscillation is a periodic movement in which the motion of the primary object moving satisfies the following properties.\n<p>\n1. The motion is symmetric about an equilibrium position at which point no net force acts on the system.\n<br>\n2. The restoring force is proportional to and oppositely directed to the displacement at any point along the oscillating object's trajectory. \n<br>\n3. The motion is periodic.\n<p>\nHarmonic oscillations are further characterized by the additional forces which may act upon the system. If the object's velocity is attenuated by a fricitonal force, the oscillation is <i>damped</i>. (See #$DampedHarmonicOscillation.) If the object's acceleration is acted on by an external, periodic force, the oscillation is <i>driven</i>. (See #$DrivenHarmonicOscillation) If the oscillation is neither damped nor driven, it is <i>simple</i>. (See #$SimpleHarmonicOscillation). See also #$DrivenAndDampedHarmonicOscillation.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac311).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac311,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac311,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac311,20691).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac311,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac311,[]).
x_comment('x_ChemicalReaction-Intentional',"A specialization of #$PurposefulAction-ResourceDriven.  Every instance of #$ChemicalReaction-Intentional is an act of intentionally causing a #$ChemicalReaction.  That is, either the #$ChemicalReaction itself or the #$chemicalProducts-Macroscopic which result from the #$ChemicalReaction is the goal of some agent.  The script involves four subscenes.  First, there is an instance of #$GainingControl. In this first scene, the #$ChemicalSubstanceTypes that are the #$precursors-Chemical of the reaction's products are acquired. Second there is a #$FollowingInstructions scene.  This scene involves executing the standardized methodology for transforming the precursors into the product.  This second scene overlaps the third scene, an instance of #$Incorporation-Physical in which the precursors are brought together.  Next, there is a #$ChemicalReaction which produces an instance of the intended #$ChemicalSubstanceType. Finally, there is a scene of type (#$GainingControlOfFn #$ChemicalSubstanceType), in which the agent performing the script gains control of the products of the chemical reaction.  Specifications of this script can be picked out, based on the produced #$ChemicalSubstanceType, using #$ChemicalReaction-IntentionalFn .") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac312).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac312,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac312,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac312,20700).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac312,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac312,[]).
