x_comment('x_candidateFallsBetweenArgsWRTOrderingByPred-Exclusive',"(#$candidateFallsBetweenArgsWRTOrderingByPred-Exclusive PRED THING LOWER-BOUND UPPER-BOUND) means that as a result of some user interaction it has been determined that it is likely that THING falls between LOWER-BOUND and UPPER-BOUND, exclusive, in the (partial) ordering determined by PRED.  PRED is a predicate that induces at least a partial ordering of the members of its domain.  For instance, #$heightOfObject induces a partial ordering of the members of its domain by virtue of the fact that all objects in the domain of that predicate can be partially ordered by height.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac33e).
