x_comment(x_completeByConvention,"An instance of #$CompletenessGroundsPredicate (q.v.) that is used to state, about a collection or predicate whose extent is inferentially complete (see #$InferenceCompletenessPredicate), that the completeness derives mainly from a conventional stipulation, rather than from the nature of the items in the extent themselves. \n<p>\nFor example, <code>(#$completelyAssertedCollection #$DayOfWeekType)</code> holds, and so does <code>(#$completeByConvention #$DayOfWeekType)</code>.  In contrast, #$completeByConvention does <i>not</i> hold of the completely-decidable collection #$Integer. Cf. #$completeByNature.  \n<p>\nSee also the specializations #$completeByExternalConvention and #$completeByCycConvention.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac36d).
