x_comment('x_accelerationOfObject-Direction',"This predicate relates an object to the direction in which it is accelerating. <code>(#$accelerationOfObject-Direction OBJECT DIRECTION)</code> means that the acceleration of <code>OBJECT</code> has the vector direction <code>DIRECTION</code>. Note that physically, acceleration is a vector valued quantity, possessing both a direction and a magnitude. This predicate is intended to relate only the direction of acceleration to the object, irrespective of the magnitude component of acceleration.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac38d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac38d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
