x_comment(x_subCollectionTypes,"A #$TaxonomicSlot (q.v.) that relates pairs of  #$CollectionTypes (q.v.).  <code>(#$subCollectionTypes COLTYPE SUBCOLTYPE)</code> means that every instance of <code>SUBCOLTYPE</code> is a specialization (see #$genls) of some instance of <code>COLTYPE</code>.\n<p>\nFor example, <code>(#$subCollectionTypes #$ObjectTypeByGender #$PersonTypeByGender)</code> holds because each (most-inclusive) collection of <i>persons</i> grouped by gender (e.g. #$FemininePerson) is a specialization of some (most-inclusive) collection of <i>objects</i> grouped by gender (viz. #$FeminineObject).\n<p>\nNote that the instances of <code>SUBCOLTYPE</code> and <code>COLTYPE</code> mentioned in the above definition might or might not actually be reified in \nthe Cyc Knowledge Base.  Thus, the above example would still be true even if the collection #$FeminineObject were not represented in the KB.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac3a5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac3a5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac3a5,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
