x_comment(x_quantityChangeFraction,"#$quantityChangeFraction\nrelates an instance of #$QuantityChangeEvent to a fractional measure\nof the change in quantity that constitutes that event.\n(#$quantityChangeFraction <code>QUANTITY-CHANGE</code>\n<code>FRACTION</code>) means, given (#$quantityChangeAmount <code>QUANTITY-CHANGE</code> <code>AMOUNT</code>), that\n<code>AMOUNT</code> is an increase or decrease in the\n#$startingQuantity (q.v.) of <code>FRACTION</code> (e.g., a\n#$Percent).  <code>FRACTION</code> may be positive or negative.  See\nalso #$changesQuantityByFraction, a #$QuaternaryPredicate which allows\nus to relate changes in #$QuantitySlot values to broader events and\ntime intervals, as well as to #$QuantityChangeEvents.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac425).
