x_comment(x_ContemporaryInResultFunction,"A specialization of #$TemporallyQualifiableFunction and #$TemporalExistenceRelation.  Each instance of this collection is a function that is \"contemporary\" in the value it returns.  That is, if FUNC is an instance of this collection and '(FUNC ARG-1 ARG-N)' appears as a denotational term in an assertion ASSERT<MT TIME PAR>, then FUNC has a value for the given series of args ARG-1 through ARG-N only if that value's temporal extent subsumes TIME.  For instance,\n<p>\n(#$isa (#$TerritoryFn #$France) #$GeographicalRegion)<MT 3,000B.C. TimePoint>\n<p>\nis false because #$TerritoryFn is an instance of #$ContemporaryInResultFunction and hence '(#$TerritoryFn #$France)' does not return a value for the time index 3,000B.C..\n<p>\nA sufficient condition for membership in this collection for any function, FUNC, is that there exists a PRED, that is #$contemporaryInArg in arg N and\n<p>\n(#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical FUNC PRED N).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac455).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac455,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac455,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac455,21291).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac455,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac455,[]).
x_comment(x_TimeDependentRelation,"A specialization of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation (q.v.).  #$TimeDependentRelation is the collection of all (not eternally-empty) predicates and functions that are such that nothing remains in their extensions eternally.  \n<p>\nA predicate <code>PRED</code> is an instance of #$TimeDependentRelation if and only if both (i) for any sequence of things <code>SEQ</code> and time <code>T</code>, if <code>PRED</code> holds of <code>SEQ</code> at <code>T</code>, then there is some different time <code>T'</code> such that <code>PRED</code> does <i>not</i> hold of <code>SEQ</code> at <code>T'</code> and (ii) there is some sequence and some time such that <code>PRED</code> holds of that sequence at that time.  (Condition (ii) is needed to exclude relations with necessarily empty extensions, such as <i>is neither identical to nor distinct from</i>.)   For example, #$likesAsFriend is time-dependent. <code>(#$likesAsFriend Amy Bob)</code> can be true today but false tomorrow (and will certainly not be true after Amy and Bob are dead).  On the other hand, #$isa is not time-dependent but merely temporally-qualifiable; although it holds of some things temporarily, it holds of some other things eternally.\n<p>\nA function <code>FUNC</code> is an instance of #$TimeDependentRelation if its value for any given sequence of arguments in its (non-empty) domain, and/or the fact that is <i>has</i> a value for that sequence, changes over time.  #$TerritoryFn is an example of a time-dependent function.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac456).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac456,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac456,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac456,21300).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac456,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac456,[]).
