xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac463,[]).
x_comment(x_TimeIndependentRelation,"The collection of all #$Relations whose extentions (see #$relationExtension) do not change over time.  A relation <code>RELN</code> is an instance of #$TimeIndependentRelation if and only if there is <i>no</i> sequence <code>SEQ</code> and times <code>T1</code> and <code>T2</code> such that <code>RELN</code> holds among <code>SEQ</code> at <code>T1</code> but not at <code>T2</code>.  Thus, if <code>RELN</code> holds of a given sequence at any time, it holds of it at all times.\n<p>\nExamples of time-independent relations include #$greaterThan, which relates numbers and other #$ScalarIntervals eternally, and #$simultaneousWith, which relates #$TimePoints eternally.\n<p>\nNote that a relation whose extension is necessarily empty, such as <i>is neither identical to nor distinct from</i>, trivially qualifies as time-independent.\n<p>\nCf. #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac464).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac464,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
