x_comment(x_UnderspecifiedIntervalFunctionFn,"<code>(#$UnderspecifiedIntervalFunctionFn INTERVAL-TYPE)</code> is a\nfunction-denoting function which returns temporally qualifiable functions.\n<code>((#$UnderspecifiedIntervalFunctionFn INTERVAL-TYPE) THING)</code> is\nthe quantity of <code>INTERVAL-TYPE</code> that <code>THING</code> has, wheter or not that quantity is measured or even measurable.  For example,\n((#$UnderspecifiedIntervalFunctionFn #$Mass) #$EiffelTower) denotes a mass: namely, the mass of the Eiffel Tower.  Functions denoted by\n#$UnderspecifiedIntervalFunctionFn are typically used in conjunction with #$valueOf\n(q.v.). For example, (#$valueOf ((#$UnderspecifiedIntervalFunctionFn #$Mass)\n#$EiffelTower) (#$MetricTon 10100)) is true.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac4a4).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac4a4,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac4a4,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
