x_comment(x_VectorQuantity,"A specialization of #$VectorInterval and #$Quantity (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$VectorQuantity is a vector composed of a direction and a quantity (where the quantity ios the vector's magnitude).\n<p>\nFor example, the vector with the direction #$Up-Generally and the magnitude (#$Meter 5) is a #$VectorQuantity, whereas the  vector with the direction #$Up-Generally and the magnitude 5 is a #$VectorInterval that is not a vector quantity.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac4aa).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac4aa,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
