x_comment(x_StrategyScoreForHypothesesFn,"An #$EvaluatableFunction. An expression of the form (#$StrategyScoreForHypothesesFn MT HYP1 HYP2) will return a #$RealNumber that is the score that is received by the two instances of #$HypotheticalContext HYP1 and HYP2 relative to the #$Microtheory MT which stores the representation of the parameter values that describe an instance of some sub-collection of #$ScoringSoftwareStrategy. (see #$optimizedStrategyForm, the relation that ties the #$ScoringSoftwareStrategy type to MT). The function acts as an interface to a set of underlying (but unreferenced) reasoning modules. The first parameter, MT represents the particular strategy that is being invoked, possibly with additional settings for the strategy. The second and third arguments represent the two hypotheses that are the subject of scroing strategy.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac4d5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac4d5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac4d5,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
