x_comment('x_candidatePegInterpretations-Partial-CycL',"<code>(#$candidatePegInterpretations-Partial-CycL PEG CYCL)</code> means that the CycL expression <code>CYCL</code> is a CycL interpretation of some part of the content of <code>PEG</code>, an instance of #$LinguisticExpressionPeg.  Note that #$candidatePegInterpretations-Partial-CycL is not the #$negationPreds of #$candidatePegInterpretations-NonPartial-CycL, as it is possible that an interpretation of part of a peg (e.g., #$JohnLennon as an interpretation of \"Lennon\" in \"John Lennon\") can also be an interpretation for the whole peg (e.g., \"John Lennon\").") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac4fd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac4fd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
