x_comment(x_Policy,"A specialization of #$NormativeSpecification (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Policy is a specification which contains the terms of some policy of a particular agent or agents.  #$Policy is thus stronger than #$NormativeSpecification, since some normative specifications may describe the way the world should be without describing what agents should do.\n<p>\nInstances of #$Policy would include U.S. Federal government hiring policies (see #$OrganizationPolicy), an individual's policy to refrain from violating rules of grammar when writing, to go to the gym three times a week, or to be honest (it is widely noted that honesty is the best policy).\n<p>\nNote that most policies with more than one committed agent are instances of #$Agreement (q.v.), a specialization of #$Policy.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac507).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac507,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac507,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
