x_comment('x_interArgEqualsIsa1-2',"A ternary instance of #$InterArgEqualsIsaPredicate (q.v.). (#$interArgEqualsIsa1-2 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when INDEPENDENT-ARG appears as the first argument to RELN, a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the second argument must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, (RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG ARG2 ...) is semantically well-formed only if ARG2 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL. For example, (#$interArgEqualsIsa1-2 #$softwareParameterValueInSpecification #$InferenceSentenceParameter #$CycLSentence-Assertible) means that (#$softwareParameterValueInSpecification #$InferenceSentenceParameter VALUE SPEC) is semantically well-formed only if VALUE is an instance of #$CycLSentence-Assertible.\n<p>\nFor an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.  See #$interArgEqualsIsa for a similar but more general predicate that is quintary, allowing the user to specify the positions of the independent and dependent arguments.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac524).
