x_comment(x_extractedRelationBasedOnPrepositionInStructure,"Nouns and prepositional complements pose special problem to compositional approaches to the semantic interpretation of natural language sentences.  Consider the sentence \"Chirac was president of France.\"  One cannot successfully construct the right semantic interpretation by building a CycL sentence that <i>merely</i> combines the semantics of the \"president\" (e.g., #$PresidentOfOrganization) with those of \"of\" (say #$possessiveRelation), as there are lots of ways in which Chirac might be an instance of #$PresidentOfOrganization (e.g., he's president of his local book club) and be \"of\" France (e.g., he was born there). The correct semantics involves recognizing that the noun \"president\" and its complement form a unit (\"president of\") that can be mapped more or less directly to a relation (#$president) that can relate the respective denotations of \"Chirac\" and \"France.\"\n<p>In many cases where a noun is known to Cyc, we have ways of handling this correctly (see, e.g., #$denotesArgInReln and #$RelationalNounSlot).  But where a noun is unknown, (e.g., \"exclave\" in \"Cabinda is an exclave of Angola\"), the relation is frequently missing, and so must, along with the denotation for the new noun, be first represented in Cyc in order to form a semantic interpretation of the sentence. \n  <code>(#$extractedRelationBasedOnPrepositionInStructure RELN PREP STRUCTURE)</code> means the relation <code>RELN</code> has been reified by Cyc in order to fill just this sort of ontological gap, made evident by the occurrence of a preposition-string (see #$prepositionStrings) associated with the preoposition <code>PREP</code> in the abstract structure <code>STRUCTURE</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac532).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac532,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac532,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac532,21859).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac532,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac532,[]).
x_comment(x_candidateForRelationExtractionBasis,"<code>(#$candidateForRelationExtractionBasis STRUCTURE COLLECTION WORD)</code> means that the instance <code>STRUCTURE</code> of #$AbstractStructure is a candidate for the reification of a new relation due to its relationship to the collection <code>COLLECTION</code> and the word <code>WORD</code>.  In particular, <code>COLLECTION</code> is a concept that has been extracted from (see #$conceptExtractedViaReferenceInStructure) a structure <code>PRIOR</code> such that a larger structure <code>WHOLE</code> spans <code>PRIOR</code> and <code>STRUCTURE</code> in the right way (e.g., in the way that \"president of\" spans \"president\" and \"of\") and where <code>WORD</code> (e.g., #$Of-TheWord) is related to <code>STRUCTURE</code> by virtue of sharing a common string.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac533).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac533,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
