x_comment(x_pcwIdentifiesRolePlayer,"(#$pcwIdentifiesRolePlayer\n<code>PCW</code> <code>SIT</code> <code>ROLE</code>) means that\n<code>PCW</code> identifies some item as playing <code>ROLE</code> in\n<code>SIT</code>.  That is, <code>PCW</code> contains an identifying\nreference to <code>ITEM</code> (in the sense of the predicate\n#$pcwIdentifies, qv.), and also asserts the #$Proposition that\n(<code>ROLE</code> <code>SIT</code> <code>ITEM</code>).  Note that\n(#$pcwIdentifiesRolePlayer <code>PCW</code> <code>SIT</code>\n<code>ROLE</code>) does not entail (<code>ROLE</code> <code>SIT</code>\n<code>ITEM</code>), i.e., the identification could be mistaken.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac583).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac583,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
