x_comment(x_incidentInSpaceRegion,"A binary #$SpaceRegionPredicate and an (inverse) specialization of #$spatiallySubsumes and #$parts that relates space points to the space regions they are in.  <code>(#$incidentInSpaceRegion POINT REGION)</code> means that<code> POINT</code> is incident in <code>REGION</code>.  \n<p>\n#$incidentInSpaceRegion is introduced as a new primitive relation in an extension of #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory (where it is called <i>IN</i>), and is used there to help define #$connectedSpaceRegions and #$partOfSpaceRegion in terms of #$Point and #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion.  Thus, two regions connect to one another if and only if there is a point that is incident in both; and one region is part of another if and only if all points incident in the first are incident in the second.\n<p>\nSee also the specializations #$incidentInInteriorOfSpaceRegion and #$incidentInBoundaryOfSpaceRegion.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac5b8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac5b8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
