x_comment(x_pathTraversableFromToBy,"An instance of #$QuaternaryPredicate. <code>(#$pathTraversableFromToBy PATH FROM TO TYPE)</code> implies that (i)the #$Path-Simple <code>PATH</code> connects <code>FROM</code> and <code>TO</code> (so that <code>(#$pathBetween PATH FROM TO)</code>) holds), and (ii) <code>PATH</code> is capable of serving as a pathway for instances of TYPE between <code>FROM</code> and <code>TO</code>. \n<p>\nNote that this predicate is _not_ commutative in its second and third arguments, since a type of movement from one location to another might not be reversible. For example, one can get to the top of a stairway from the bottom, but not to the bottom from the top, by ascending that stairway (see the collection #$AscendingStairs).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac5bc).
