x_comment(x_slotInverseValueRangeWRTCollection,"A ternary predicate that relates a #$BinaryPredicate to a #$Collection to a #$Set-Mathematical.  <code>(#$slotInverseValueRangeWRTCollection PRED COL SET)</code> means that <code>SET</code> is the set of all (and only those) things that are related to some instance of <code>COL</code> by <code>PRED</code>.  That is, a thing <code>OBJ</code> is an element of <code>SET</code> if and only if there is at least one instance <code>INST</code> of <code>COL</code> such that <code>(PRED OBJ INST)</code> holds.  For example, the inverse value-range of #$cityInState for #$State-UnitedStates is the set of US cities.\n<p>\nSee also #$slotValueRangeWRTCollection.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac5c3).
