x_comment(x_properTimeSlices,"A #$TemporalPartPredicate and a specialization of both #$timeSlices and #$properParts (qq.v.) that relates a temporal thing to any of its \"pure\" proper temporal parts.  <code>(#$properTimeSlices TEMP SLICE)</code> means that <code>SLICE</code> is a proper part of <code>TEMP</code> that is distinguished from <code>TEMP</code> purely in terms of its #$temporalExtent, which is properly subsumed by the temporal extent of <code>TEMP</code> itself.  In other words, <code>SLICE</code> is \"everything there is to\" <code>TEMP</code> during the particular #$TimeInterval that <code>SLICE</code> occupies.  For example, today's noon hour has the interval from 12:00 noon to 12:30 p.m. today as one of its proper time-slices; the first act of a particular performance of \"Hamlet\" is a proper time-slice of that performance of the whole play.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac5cb).
