x_comment(x_actTypeRoleEffectiveForActTypeRole,"A quintary (5-place) #$RuleMacroPredicate.  <code>(#$actTypeRoleEffectiveForActTypeRole ACT-TYPE-1 ROLE-1 ACT-TYPE-2 ROLE-2 THING)</code> is shorthand for the following rule: \n<pre>\n(#$implies\n  (#$and\n    (#$subcollectionOfWithRelationTo ACT-TYPE-1 ROLE-1 THING ?SUBCOL-1)\n    (#$subcollectionOfWithRelationTo ACT-TYPE-2 ROLE-2 THING ?SUBCOL-2))\n  (#$effectiveActTypeForActType ?SUBCOL-1 ?SUBCOL-2))\n</pre>\nThus, for example,\n<pre>\n(#$actTypeRoleEffectiveForActTypeRole #$PushingSomeone #$objectActedOn #$FallingDown #$primaryObjectMoving #$Bob)\n</pre>\nsays, basically, that pushing Bob is a good way to make him fall down.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac5ed).
