x_comment('x_Device-RemoteControlled',"A collection. The instances of #$Device-RemoteControlled are those devices which can be controlled remotely when they are being used. For every instance of this collection there is an instance of #$RemoteControlDevice with which to do the controlling. Examples are some instances of #$TelevisionSet of which the channels, volume, etc. can be controlled remotely. Also many instances of #$TransportationDevice-Unmanned can be guided by remote control. This control need not happen throughout the event of using the device. An example of this are the laser-guided missiles that are only guided at the end by pointing with the laser to the intended target.\n<p>\nNote that a #$Device-RemoteControlled may also be a #$Device-ProximatelyControlled.  For devices that can only be controlled remotely, see #$Device-RemoteControlledOnly.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac607).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac607,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
