x_comment('x_ILPMode-Orthogonal-SpecializationStrategyMt',"#$ILPMode-Orthogonal-SpecializationStrategyMt is a microtheory containing rules that implement a specific strategy for getting the mode and type information for ILP. The strategy implemented in this microtheory is the leaf strategy (see #$ILPMode-LeafStrategyMt) along with a way of introducing a collection that links together argument positions that are constrained by orthogonal collections. This linkage is needed for ILP systems like ALEPH so that it understands that the same value can show up in both argument positions that Cyc constrains to orthogonal collections.\n<p>\nThe specialization strategy introduces the #$CollectionIntersectionFn of the orthogonal collection argument constraints.\n<p>\nFor instance, the first argument of #$rulerInDynasty is #$Monarch-HeadOfState and the second argument of #$father is #$MaleAnimal. This strategy introduces (#$CollectionIntersectionFn (#$TheSet #$MaleAnimal #$Monarch-HeadOfState)) as the collection which would link the two argument positions.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac66e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac66e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac66e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
