x_comment(x_DecimalRealNumberOfMaximumPrecisionFn,"(#$DecimalRealNumberOfMaximumPrecisionFn PRECISION SCALE) denotes an instance of #$ComputerDatatypeType which is also a #$RealNumberDatatype, in that the values stored in variables or fields having this type are #$RealNumbers.  However, not every #$RealNumber can be stored in a variable or field of this type. PRECISION states the total maximum number of significant digits allowed in a value, and SCALE give the maximum number of digits to the right of the decimal point.  The amount of storage allocated to a variable or field of this type varies according to the PRECISION given.  A datatype denoted by (#$DecimalRealNumberOfMaximumPrecisionFn PRECISION SCALE) can store only real numbers which are precisely representable as decimal numbers within the PRECISION and SCALE limits provided.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac6ca).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac6ca,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
