x_comment(x_ncRuleReificationRelationGeneralityCutoffs,"<code>(#$ncRuleReificationRelationGeneralityCutoffs PREDICATE)</code> identifies <code>PREDICATE</code> as a generality limit on when a new NC rule should be constructed such that that rule has a #$semanticRelationForNCR constraint.  For example, <code>(#$ncRuleReificationRelationGeneralityCutoffs #$actors)</code> means that Cyc should not reify a new NC rule <code>RULE</code> such that <code>#$semanticRelationForNCR RULE PRED)</code> where <code>(#$genlPreds #$actors PRED)</code>.  As such, #$ncRuleReificationRelationGeneralityCutoffs is transitive via #$genlPreds in its argument.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac6db).
