x_comment(x_GeometryCoordinateTransformFn,"This function is used to transform the coordinate system\nwith respect to which a given geometry is represented.\n<code>(#$GeometryCoordinateTransformFn GEOMETRY SYSTEM)</code> denotes\n<code>GEOMETRY</code> but with coordinates in the #$CoordinateSystem\n<code>SYSTEM</code>. In practice, this function is just a wrapper\naround #$PostGISCoordinateTransformFn, which is actually used by SKSI\nto perform coordiante transformations on geometries stored in a\nPostGIS enabled spatial database. Here, however, we reference the\ntarget coordinate system directly, instead of its spatial reference id\n(see #$sridForCoordinateSystem).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac6e0).
