x_comment(x_UnlimitedSizeComputerDatatypeType,"The collection of all computer data types such that program variables or database fields which are typed by a particular instance of this collection have a variable amount of storage, with no limit specified by the user, allocated to store their data.  The actual amount of storage used by an instance of such a type depends on the data stored there.  For example, the #$PostgreSQL TEXT datatype is a variable-size datatype of unlimited length. A field of this type may store character strings of length ten or ten thousand or more. Note that \"Unlimited\" in this context means \"not limited at field creation time;\" i.e., there is no parameter given to specify a maximum size for a TEXT field. In practice, though, a field typed by an instance of  #$UnlimitedSizeComputerDatatypeType will have SOME limit imposed by available disk, memory, or the DBMS implementation.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac6e3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac6e3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac6e3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac6e3,22597).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ac6e3,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ac6e3,[]).
x_comment(x_VariableLimitedSizeDatatypeType,"The collection of all computer data types such that program variables or database fields which are typed by a particular instance of this collection have a variable amount of storage allocated to store their values, depending on the particular datum stored there.  Furthermore, at the time of field creation or variable definition, the user specifies the maximum amount of storage that can be used.   For example, fields typed by the SQL type VARCHAR(8), aka (#$StringOfMaximumLengthFn 8), will allow strings as long as eight characters to be stored, but no longer strings, and if a shorter string is stored in that field, the amount of storage used will be only what is required to hold the characters of the string.  The DBMS implementation will not allow strings longer than 8 characters to be stored in a VARCHAR(8) field.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac6e4).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac6e4,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
