x_comment(x_maxSubsetConsistentWithElement,"<code>(#$maxSubsetConsistentWithElement SET-OF-COLLS COLL SUBSET-OF-COLLS)</code> means that every element of <code>SET-OF-COLLS</code> that is not disjoint with <code>COLL</code> is an element of <code>SUBSET-OF-COLLS</code>, and that <code>SUBSET-OF-COLLS</code> is a subset of <code>SET-OF-COLLS</code>.\n<p>\nFor example, \n<p>\n<pre>\n<code>(#$maxSubsetConsistentWithElement (#$TheSet #$Monarch-HeadOfState #$FemaleAnimal #$War) #$FemaleAnimal (#$TheSet #$FemaleAnimal #$Monarch-HeadOfState))</code>\n</pre>\n<p>\nmeans that:<br>\n1. (#$TheSet #$FemaleAnimal #$Monarch-HeadOfState) is a subset of (#$TheSet #$Monarch-HeadOfState #$FemaleAnimal #$War), and <br>\n2. every element of (#$TheSet #$Monarch-HeadOfState #$FemaleAnimal) is is not disjoint with #$FemaleAnimal.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac702).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac702,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
