x_comment(x_foreignKeyConstraintWithActionType,"<code>(#$foreignKeyConstraintWithActionType REFERENCED-SCHEMA REFERENCED-KEY REFERENCING-SCHEMA REFERENCING-FIELD-LIST MODIFY-TYPE RESTRICTION-TYPE)</code> means that: <p>\n1. A foreign key reference (see #$foreignKeyMap) holds between <code>REFERENCED-SCHEMA</code>, <code>REFERENCED-KEY</code>, <code>REFERENCING-SCHEMA</code>, and <code>REFERENCING-FIELD-LIST</code>;<p>\n2. Whenever an agent attempts to perform a database modification of type <code>MODIFY-TYPE</code> on a record in the table corresponding to <code>REFERENCED-SCHEMA</code> that will modify one or more of the values of the <code>REFERENCED-KEY</code> fields, then the database management system will enforce an integrity constraint of type <code>RESTRICTION-TYPE</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac727).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac727,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
