x_comment(x_BorderBetweenPolitiesFn,"(#$BorderBetweenPolitiesFn GEO-1 GEO-2) applied to two #$GeopoliticalEntitys returns the entire intangible Border (if any) that separates their territories.  The border returned by #$BorderBetweenPolitiesFn may be discontinuous (such as the border between France and Spain, interrupted by Andorra), or circular (such as the border between Italy and San Marino), or in abnormal cases it may even have multiple disconnected and nested cyclic fragments (the border between Belgium and Netherlands, due to the Baarle-Nassau and Baarle-Hartog enclaves), or move back and forth periodically (such as at the Isle des Faisans).  In any case, (#$BorderBetweenPolitiesFn GEO-1 GEO-2) must denote exactly one object (if it denotes at all) since #$BorderBetweenPolitiesFn is a function.  #$BorderBetweenPolitiesFn is undefined for pairs of  #$GeopoliticalEntitys whose territories do not actually share a border, such as #$Albania and #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.  See also #$politiesBorderEachOther, assertions using that predicate express a necessary and sufficient condition on the entities involved returning a value with this function and #$BorderBetweenFn which defines the border between two #$GeographicalRegions.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac729).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac729,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ac729,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ac729,22720).
