x_comment(x_normalWholeTypeForPartType,"<code>(#$normalWholeTypeForPartType PART-TYPE WHOLE-TYPE)</code> means that\ninstances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> are normally parts of instances of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>. Usually, an instance of <code>PART-TYPE</code> will be incapable of serving its\nnormal function if it is not part of some instance of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>.\n<p>\nFor example, (#$normalWholeTypeForPartType #$DoorKnob #$DoorInABuilding)\nis true because door knobs are normally parts of doors, and are incapable of serving their intended function when they are not parts of doors.\n<p>\nSimilarly, (#$normalWholeTypeForPartType  #$AchillesTendon #$LowerLeg) is true because achilles tendons are normally parts of lower legs, and any achilles tendon is  incapable of performing its normal function if it is not part of a lower leg.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac73d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ac73d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
