x_comment(x_CostumeFn,"<code>(#$CostumeFn INDIVIDUAL)</code> denotes the collection of costumes (see #$Costume) that are intended to visually evoke images of <code>INDIVIDUAL</code>, an instance of #$Individual.  For example, <code>(#$CostumeFn #$Spock)</code> denotes the collection of Mr. Spock costumes,  <code>(#$CostumeFn #$EiffelTower)</code> denotes the collection of Eiffel Tower costumes, and so forth.  To talk about costumes for <i>types</i> rather than <i>individuals</i> (e.g., \"pirate costumes\"), use #$CostumeOfTypeFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac830).
