x_comment(x_RoundClosestToNthDecimalFn,"A macro-function that takes a real number or a scalar quantity to the nearest amount expressible in up to some specified number of decimal places.  For example, (#$RoundClosestToNthDecimalFn (#$Meter 2.416) 2) is (#$Meter 2.42) and (#$RoundClosestToNthDecimalFn 3.14159 0) is 3.\n<p>\nSee also #$RoundClosestFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ac839).
