x_comment(x_OrderingPredicate,"A specialization of #$AntiSymmetricBinaryPredicate, #$TransitiveBinaryPredicate, and #$ObjectPredicate (q.v.).  Each instance of #$OrderingPredicate is an antisymmetric, transitive, binary predicate that can be used for ordering a #$Series (q.v.) in such a way that the predicate relates each member of the series to each subsequent member.  An ordering predicate can also be used for similarly ordering the instances of a #$CollectionWithAnEventLikeOrder (q.v.).\n<p>\nFor spatial predicates that can be used to order #$PhysicalSeries, see the specialization #$SpatialOrderingPredicate.") :- x_cid(a65b16517acb86).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517acb86,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
