x_comment(x_TerrorismOWLExportBinaryPredicate,"Instances of this collection are binary predicates whose extent we want to export in any OWL export of terrorism data.  Typically the export will be constrained as follows:\n<pre>\n        (1) There will be some query to retrieve the individuals we want to export information about -- generally a query that pulls back terrorist agents and acts.\n        (2)  Any instances of #$Collection involved in assertions with the individuals that satisfy the query mentioned in (1) using the predicates from this collection or the predicates that are instances of #$OwlExportableRelation should have their top level OWL definitions included in the export and the assertion should be exported. (use specializations of this collection for less than a full terrorism data export.</pre>\n\nConsider the following examples.  Example 1: Assume that #$affiliatedWith is an instance of TerrorismOWLExportBinaryPredicate.  Further assume that PERSON1 and PERSON2 are both bindings for the query in (1).  If (#$affiliatedWith PERSON1 PERSON2) is asserted, then export that assertion.  Example 2: #$relationInstanceExists is an instance of #$OwlExportableRelation, #$organismKilled is an instance of #$TerrorismOWLExportBinaryPredicate and ATTACK1 is an instance of the query in (1).  If (#$relationInstanceExists #$organismKilled ATTACK1 MilitaryPerson) is asserted, then export that assertions and provide the top level definition of MilitaryPerson.") :- x_cid(a65b16517acbba).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517acbba,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
