x_comment(x_conflateToInSystem,"A predicate used to construct specialized lexicons for a classification system, such as an ontology (see #$Ontology) or taxonomy (see #$Taxonomy).  <code>(#$conflateToInSystem THING-1 THING-2 SYSTEM)</code> means that for purposes of mapping natural language to nodes in the system <code>SYSTEM</code>, natural language references to <code>THING-1</code> should be interpreted as references to <code>THING-2</code>.  For example, <code>(#$conflateToInSystem #$CalendarQuarter #$FiscalQuarter #$InvestmentRelatedThingTaxonomy)</code> means that references to #$CalendarQuarter (e.g., \"quarter\") should be understood as referring to #$FiscalQuarter.  Such assertions result in additions to the lexicon for the system in question, which also makes it possible for the system and lexicon to be separated from the Cyc KB as a bundle, preserving the mappings in question.") :- x_cid(a65b16517acc01).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517acc01,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517acc01,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517acc01,24443).
