x_comment(x_schemaIntegrationInputReifiedMappingTypeSet,"If <code>INTEGRATION</code> is an #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources and <code>INPUT-SET</code> is the set of input sources to be integrated (see #$schemaIntegrationInputSKSSet), then <code>(#$schemaIntegrationInputReifiedMappingTypeSet INTEGRATION TYPE-SET)</code> means that <code>TYPE-SET</code> is the set of types such that a field associated with some element of INPUT-SET has that type and has values that are specified by a #$ReifiedMapping.\n\nTypically, the elements of <code>INPUT-SET</code> are related to some element of <code>TYPE-SET</code> as follows: For each <code>TOP-KS</code> element of <code>INPUT-SET</code> find its 'parts' via #$subKS. For each of these parts, find the element of <code>TYPE-SET</code> by looking up on #$sourceCMLSFieldType.") :- x_cid(a65b16517acc30).
