x_comment(x_AstronomicalObject,"A specialization of #$InanimateObject-Natural.  The collection of all things of the types studied by astronomers.  Each instance of #$AstronomicalObject is a (usually quite large) natural, inanimate object that is located in the physical universe and is not on the surface of the Earth.  (But note that #$PlanetEarth itself <i>is</i> an instance of this collection.)  An \n#$AstronomicalObject might be either an individual heavenly body (see \n#$AstronomicalBody) or a group or system made up of such bodies (see e.g. \n#$Galaxy and #$PlanetarySystem).  See also the specialization \n#$CelestialObject, instances of which are visible from the Earth.") :- x_cid(a65b16517acc4d).
