x_comment(x_SeizingAndHoldingHostage,"A specialization of #$ActsCommonlyConsideredCriminal.  In\neach instance of #$SeizingAndHoldingHostage, an agent seizes and\nsubsequently holds as hostage(s) one or more #$Persons.  Instances\nof this collection thus have instances of both #$HostileSeizure and #$HoldingHostages as sub-events.  Note that the seizure may occur as part\nof a #$KidnappingSomeone -- where the person seized is subsequently\ntransported to an unknown or inaccessible location -- or may simply\nconsist of gaining control over the person by threat of force (e.g.,\nholding someone at gunpoint while issuing demands).  Typically, the\npurpose of the #$perpetrator is to coerce other agents --\nwho have a #$positiveVestedInterest in the #$hostages -- to accede to some\ndemand.  See, for example, the specialization #$SeizingAndHoldingHostageForRansom.") :- x_cid(a65b16517acd10).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517acd10,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
