x_comment('x_Entertainer-PerformanceContributor',"An instance of #$PersonTypeByActivity.  Each instance of #$Entertainer-PerformanceContributor is a person who contributes to the performance aspect of an entertainment event.  Thus #$Entertainer-PerformanceContributor is a generalization of #$Entertainer (the collection of entertainers), but is not identical to it.  A canonical example of a person who is an instance of this collection but not #$Entertainer would be  a professional athlete.  Such a person works in the entertainment industry (see #$EntertainmentIndustry), not as an entertainer (in the sense of #$Entertainer) <i>per se</i>, but as someone who practices his or her craft with a focal goal of contributing to an individual or team victory, and, in doing so, contributes to the execution (performance) of an entertainment event.  The entertainment of the audience is a by-product the athlete's actions, and is not his or her focal concern.") :- x_cid(a65b16517acd13).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517acd13,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517acd13,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517acd13,24841).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517acd13,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517acd13,[]).
x_comment(x_structureInUrbanArea,"This predicate relates a structure to the urban area in which it is located.  (#$structureInUrbanArea STRUCT AREA) means that STRUCT is located in AREA.  For instance, (#$structureInUrbanArea #$ArcDeTriomphe (#$TerritoryFn #$CityOfParisFrance))  means that the Arc de Triomphe is located in the geographical extent of Paris, France, which  is (in the context of the assertion) an urban area.") :- x_cid(a65b16517acd14).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517acd14,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
