x_comment(x_relationAllOnly,"A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can be used to state that a given binary predicate stands in a certain relation to two collections.  <code>(#$relationAllOnly BINPRED COL1 COL2)</code> means that for any instance <code>INST1</code> of <code>COL1</code>, only instances of  <code>COL2</code>, say <code>INST2</code>, are such that <code>(BINPRED INST1 INST2)</code> holds.  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:\n<pre>\n(#$implies\n  (#$and\n    (#$isa ?INST1 COL1)\n    (BINPRED ?INST1 ?INST2))\n  (#$isa ?INST2 COL2)) .\n</pre>\nSo #$relationAllOnly (and its defining axiom; see #$expansion) enables this common type of rule to be stated more tersely.\n<p>\nFor example, '(#$relationAllOnly #$eatsWillingly-Instance #$Herbivore #$PlantBLO)' means that every herbivore willingly eats only plants or parts thereof.  See also #$relationOnlyAll and #$NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.") :- x_cid(a65b16517acd37).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517acd37,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517acd37,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517acd37,24877).
