x_comment(x_Helix,"A #$GeometricShapeType and a specialization of #$Spiral (q.v.).  This is the collection of all helices, tangible or abstract.  Each instance of #$Helix is a spiral (i.e. a curved #$LinearObject that makes one or more turns about an axis) such that each turn about the axis is the same size, and the successive turns \"proceed\" linearly in the general direction parallel to the axis.  Thus, a helix can fit on the surface of a cylinder having that same axis.  \n<p>\nExamples of helices include some wire springs and the frieze on #$TrajansColumn.\n<p>\nCf. #$DoubleHelix.") :- x_cid(a65b16517acd73).
