x_comment(x_derivedFrom,"<code>(#$derivedFrom PRODUCT MATERIAL)</code> means that <code>PRODUCT</code> has been made from <code>MATERIAL</code> by an irreversible process; e.g., an element of #$Table-PieceOfFurniture may have been #$derivedFrom an instance of #$MapleTree.  \n<p>\nNote that #$derivedFrom is <i>not</i> transitive: A particular Door121 may be derived from OakTree53, SandMob442, and several other things.  Subsequently, someone may break down the door and make Mallet0234 out of some of the  wood and a WindowPane120825 out of some (or all) of the glass. Both Mallet0234  and WindowPane120825 are #$derivedFrom Door121, but Mallet0234 is not  #$derivedFrom SandMob442, nor is WindowPane120825 #$derivedFrom OakTree53.") :- x_cid(a65b16517acd7f).
