x_comment(x_pairwisePropertyOfCollection,"(#$pairwisePropertyOfCollection MODIFIER COLLECTION THING) states that THING is the property described by MODIFIER.  This is a very general predicates and its meaning in a given context is determined by what stands in its arg1.  For example, \n\n    <pre>\n        (#$pairwisePropertyOfCollection #$Longest-Between COLLECTION DURATION)</pre>\n\nmeans that DURATION is the longest empty duration between members of COLLECTION.  That is, it looks at the instances of COLLECTION and for each sequential pair it calculates the duration between them and returns the longest duration as the value for DURATION.  Note that COLLECTION must be a collection of temporal things for which the start and end dates are known.\n.") :- x_cid(a65b16517acde4).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517acde4,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517acde4,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517acde4,25121).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517acde4,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517acde4,[]).
x_comment('x_pairwisePropertyOfCollection-IncludeReferenceEntities',"A quaternary #$QueryMacroPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$pairwisePropertyOfCollection-IncludeReferenceEntities MODIFIER COLLECTION THING SET)</code> states that <code>THING</code> is the property described by <code>MODIFIER</code> and <code>SET</code> is a set of instances of <code>COLLECTION</code> that jointly satisfy the final comparision in terms of <code>MODIFIER</code>.  This is a very general predicate and its meaning in a given context is determined by what stands in its arg1.  For example, \n<pre>\n  (#specifiedPropertyOfCollection-IncludeReferenceEntities #$Longest-Between COLLECTION DURATION SET)\n</pre>\nmeans that <code>DURATION</code> is the longest duration between (the respective ending and starting points of) sequential intances of <code>COLLECTION</code>, and <code>SET</code> is a set of sequential instances that have <code>DURATION</code> between them.  (Note that, in this case, <code>COLLECTION</code> must be a collection of temporal things for which the start and end dates are known.)") :- x_cid(a65b16517acde5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517acde5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517acde5,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517acde5,25128).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517acde5,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517acde5,[]).
