x_comment(x_suggestionsForPredRelativeToIsaInArg,"<pre>(#$suggestionsForPredRelativeToIsaInArg PRED COLL-1 N COLL-2 M)</pre> holds just in case COLL-1 is the collection of terms that are suitable suggestions for substitution into arg N of PRED when an instance of COLL-2 stands in arg M.\n\n<br><br>\nFor example,   \n<br><br>\n(#$suggestionsForPredRelativeToIsaInArg #$relationInstanceExists #$CasualtyPredReplacement 1 #$AgentCasualtyPredicate 1)\n<br><br>\n means that instances of #$CasualtyPredReplacement should be offered up as suggested replacements in arg1 of #$relationInstanceExists literals when an instance of #$AgentCasualtyPredicate appears in arg1 of the literal.\n\nNote that if you just want to specify the suggested replacements regardless of the terms appearing in other argument positions you can assert:\n\n<pre>(#$suggestionsForPredRelativeToIsaInArg PRED COLL-OF-REPLACEMENTS N #$Predicate 0)</pre>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ace01).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ace01,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
