x_comment(x_CoEquivalenceBinaryPredicate,"A specialization of  #$IrreflexiveBinaryPredicate, #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate, and  #$QuasiTransitiveBinaryPredicate (qq.v.).  A binary predicate <code>PRED</code> is a #$CoEquivalenceBinaryPredicate if and only if <code>PRED</code> is irreflexive, symmetric, and <b><i>quasi-transitive</i></b>.  This collection consists of exactly all of the instances of #$QuasiTransitiveBinaryPredicate that are also symmetric and irreflexive.\n<p>\nNote that a necessary condition on <code>PRED</code>'s being a co-equivalence predicate is that its two argument-places must be co-satisfiable; see #$cosatisfiableInArgs and #$NoteOnArgumentCosatisfiabilityRequirement.\n<p>\nInstances of #$CoEquivalenceBinaryPredicate include #$cohabitants, #$connectedTerminals, and #$twins.\n<p>\nCf. #$EquivalenceRelation.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ace36).
