x_comment(x_genericCycLMappingToSourceString,"The most general predicate for representing mappings of terms from data sources into Cyc. <code>(#$genericCycLMappingToSourceString THING SOURCE STRING)</code> means that there is some mapping of a denotation of <code>STRING</code> as it occurs in <code>SOURCE</code> to a concept, represented in Cyc, that is closely related to THING.  This mapping might be one in which <code>STRING</code> denotes <code>THING</code> (a \"true\" mapping -- see #$synonymousExternalConcept), or one in which <code>STRING</code> maps to a concept not reified in Cyc, but to a concept that can be characterized in terms of operations on <code>THING</code> (see, e.g., #$synonymousExternalPred-Inverse, #$synonymousExternalPredWRTTypes, and #$synonymousExternalPredWRTTypes-Inverse).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ace73).
