x_comment(x_textualPCWSubSections,"<code>(#$textualPCWSubSections LARGER-WORK SUB-WORK)</code> relates <code>LARGER-WORK</code>, an instance of #$TextualPCW, to <code>SUB-WORK</code>, a distinct instance of #$TextualPCW that is a sub-work (see #$subWorks) of <code>LARGER-WORK</code> that is recognizably so due to stylistic or structural features that, usually by design, are intended to set it apart as a somewhat self-contained work.  Examples include chapters in books, articles in magazines or journals, and the sections and sub-sections of an article that are typically demarcated with titles or some sort of numbering scheme.<br><br>#$textualPCWSubSections is to be distinguished from its specialization, #$textualPCWSections, which is used relates an instance of #$TextualPCW to a #$textualPCWSubSections that is explicitly identified as a \"section\" (as opposed to some other category, such as a chapter).") :- x_cid(a65b16517acf1c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517acf1c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
