x_comment(x_NthActOfCongressFn,"A partial function from integers to an instance of #$TemporalThing. <code>(#$NthActOfCongressFn CONGRESS-NUM ACT-NUM)</code> denotes the temporal thing <code>ACT</code> such that from its starting date onward, it has the following properties: It is an instance of #$ActOfCongress, it was the creation of the <code>CONGRESS-NUM</code>th United States Congress (see #$NthUSCongressFn), and it was the <code>ACT-NUM</code>th act of that congress.  This function is useful for on-the-fly reification of Congressional acts, as they are enumerated by congressional session number and ordinal -- e.g., \"Pub. Law 104 17\" refers to the 17th law act of the 104th congress, representable with this function-term as <code>(#$NthActOfCongressFn 17 104)</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517acf45).
