x_comment(x_specificationBenefitsAgent,"<code>(#$specificationBenefitsAgent SPEC AGENT)</code> identifies <code>AGENT</code> as an instance of #$Agent-Generic who benefits/would benefit from the terms set forth in the instance <code>SPEC</code> of #$NormativeSpecification. <code>SPEC</code> will typically be an instance of #$GoalOrientedSpecification, such as a plan or proposal, or an instance of #$Agreement; in either case, situation-types are described in <code>SPEC</code> that, were they instantiated, some benefit befalls <code>AGENT</code> as a consequence of the terms of <code>SPEC</code>.  <code>AGENT</code> need not be explicitly mentioned in or even aware of <code>SPEC</code> in order to benefit (as that benefit might occur as an unintended consequence).  However, typically, when agents craft specifications such as plans or agreements, they attempt to ensure that #$specificationBenefitsAgent holds of the specification and themselves.") :- x_cid(a65b16517acf8c).
