x_comment(x_logicalResultSetCardinality,"This predicate is used by the SKSI code to estimate the cost of querying the fields of a logical schema.  More precisely, let SCHEMA denote a logical schema, let LF-1, LF-2, ..., LF-N, denote the logical fields of SCHEMA, and let SELECT_SET and WHERE_SET denote two disjoint subsets of (#$TheSet LF-1 LF-2 ... LF-N). Then (#$logicalResultSetCardinality SCHEMA SELECT_SET WHERE_SET NUM) means that NUM is the average cardinality of the result set returned from a query in which the fields in SELECT_SET left unbound and the fields of WHERE_SET are bound.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad003).
