x_comment('x_above-Generally',"<code>(#$above-Generally OVER-OBJ UNDER-OBJ)</code> means that the #$SpatialThing-Localized <code>OVER-OBJ</code> is more or less above the #$SpatialThing-Localized <code>UNDER-OBJ</code>. To be more precise: if <code>OVER-OBJ</code> is within a cone-shaped set of vectors within about 45 degrees of #$Up-Directly pointing up from <code>UNDER-OBJ</code> (see #$Up-Generally), then <code>(#$above-Generally OVER-OBJ UNDER-OBJ)</code> holds. This is a more general predicate than #$above-Directly (q.v.), but it is a more specialized predicate than #$above-Higher (q.v.). It probably most closely conforms to the English word \"above.\"") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad232).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad232,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
