x_comment(x_properPhysicalPartTypes,"A #$RuleMacroPredicate and a specialization of #$physicalPartTypes.  Where <code>TYPE1</code> and <code>TYPE2</code> are both specializations of #$PartiallyTangible, <code>(#$properPhysicalPartTypes TYPE1 TYPE2)</code> means that every instance of <code>TYPE1</code> has an instance of <code>TYPE2</code> as a proper physical part.  For example, (#$properPhysicalPartTypes #$RoseBouquet #$RoseFlower).\n<p>\nMost assertions with #$properPhysicalPartTypes are default true, because it is generally possible for some instances of a collection to lack parts of a type that most instances of that collection always have.  For example, (#$properPhysicalPartTypes #$Finger #$Fingernail) is default true, even though a some fingers might lack fingernails as parts.\n<p>\nCf. #$normalWholeTypeForPartType, which is used to relate typical part types to the whole types of which they are ordinarily parts.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad288).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad288,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
