x_comment(x_MilitarySpaceLaunchOperation,"A specialization of #$MilitaryOperation. Each instance of #$MilitarySpaceLaunchOperation is a complex event during which a military organization prepares a rocket (see #$RocketPropelledTransportationDevice) and rocket-supporting systems (e.g. a #$RocketRange) for transportation in outer space (see #$SpaceTransportationEvent).  Each instance involves preparation events, and, in those cases where the prepartation events are successful, a rocket launch (see #$LaunchingARocket).  Each instance that involves a rocket launch also involves additional post-launch events, during which the rocket travels toward outer space and is tracked by facilities at the stations on the launch site's rocket range.  Completely succesful instances of this collection terminate when the launch vehicle no longer needs to be tracked by the launching agent, for example when the launch vehicle for the spaceflight has been expended or has safely landed at its destination.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad28d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad28d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ad28d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ad28d,26483).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ad28d,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ad28d,[]).
x_comment(x_companyQuarterlyEarnings,"An instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation, <code>(#$companyQuarterlyEarnings COMPANY AMOUNT)</code><T> means that at the calendar quarter T (but not necessarily at any proper sub-interval of T), the earnings of the company <code>COMPANY</code> are <code>AMOUNT</code>, an instance of #$MonetaryValue.  The earnings of a company are arrived at by subtracting certain expenses and taxes from revenues.  As such, #$companyQuarterlyEarnings is #$netIncome as applied to instances of #$Business.  This sense of \"earnings\" can be contrasted to the related notion of \"earnings\" as applied to individual people, which refers to the money (typically, the gross) earned through employment or investments.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad28e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad28e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ad28e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ad28e,26484).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ad28e,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ad28e,[]).
x_comment(x_contextOfPCWInterpretation,"A #$FunctionalPredicate that relates conceptual works, agents that interpret them, and a time to the propositions that are in the interpretations. <tt>(#$contextOfPCWInterpretation PCW CONTEXT AGENT TIME)</tt> means that CONTEXT is the context that contains all the propositions endorsed by AGENT on the record (and their closure) at TIME as part of the inteprpretation of PCW.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad28f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad28f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ad28f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ad28f,26485).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ad28f,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ad28f,[]).
x_comment(x_ContextOfPCWInterpretationFn,"A ternary function that returns an instance of #$Microtheory when given a #$PropositionalConceptualWork, an #$IntelligentAgent, and a time interval as arguments. (#$ContextOfPCWInterpretationFn PCW AGENT TIME) denotes the microtheory containing the propositions (and their upward closure) that AGENT goes on the record at TIME as claiming that PCW contains.  Essentially, it is the the interpretation by AGENT of PCW at TIME, or at least the portion of the interpretation that AGENT is willing claim.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad290).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad290,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ad290,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
