x_comment(x_uniquelyBehaviorCapable,"<code>(#$uniquelyBehaviorCapable OBJ SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> is the unique object that would be capable (in the sense of #$behaviorCapable (q.v.)) of playing <code>ROLE</code> in any instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>. <code>(#$uniquelyBehaviorCapable OBJ SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> does not imply that <code>OBJ</code> actually can play <code>ROLE</code> in <i>every</i> instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> -- it means only that if anything can play such a role, only <code>OBJ</code> can do so.  However, specific circumstances during some instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> may prevent even <code>OBJ</code>  from playing the role  <code>ROLE</code>.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad2a9).
