x_comment('x_behaviorIncapable-CapabilityCompromised',"<code>(#$behaviorIncapable-CapabilityCompromised OBJ SITTYPE ROLE)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> is incapable of playing <code>ROLE</code> in any instance of <code>SITTYPE</code>, as a consequence of malfunctioning or being a defective instance of its type. Thus, <code>(#$behaviorIncapable-CapabilityCompromised EddieTheAdultEagle #$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy)</code> means that <code>EddieTheAdultEagle</code> is incapable of flying, though this must be due to some particular thing being wrong with Eddie, since it is generally true that <code>((#$TypeCapableFn #$behaviorCapable) #$Eagle #$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy)</code> . Cf. #$behaviorIncapable and #$functionalityCompromised.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad2bf).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad2bf,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
