x_comment(x_PrimaryLexicalMapping,"Interpretations of words or phrases which are considered to be primary mappings. A mapping is a primary mapping the phrase would be expected to evoke the concept out of context.  Some words and phrases can have more than one primary mapping (e.g. 'bat' means either baseball bat or the flying mammal), but most words have only one primary mapping.  If a meaning is only evoked with the help of contextual clues, it should not be a #$PrimaryLexicalMapping, but is instead one of the other instances of #$LexicalMappingStrength.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad2e5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad2e5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
