x_comment(x_internalPowerSource,"This relation is intended to capture the comparatively vague concept of the 'power source' of a #$SelfPoweredDevice.  More specifically (#$internalPowerSource DEVICE SOURCE) means that when DEVICE exhibits some motion that is part of its intended behavior, a causal explanation of this motion can be given that treats SOURCE as one of the principle physical causes and origins of this motion.  The scope of the predicate is thus extremely broad. E.g., a car's battery can be considered to be an #$internalPowerSource, but so can the car's engine.  The only provisos are that the 'source' so identified must be a #$properPhysicalParts of the device it helps power, and that the device in question must, accordingly, be a #$SelfPoweredDevice.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad30f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad30f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ad30f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
