x_comment(x_bridgingPredicateForPredicate,"(#$bridgingPredicateForPredicate PRED-BASE PRED-BRIDGE (#$TheSet ARG1, ... , ARGN))  means that PRED-BRIDGE is the consequent of a transformation rule that, essentially, transforms into PRED-BASE in order to generate bindings.  The third argument will be a set of lists that determine the correspondence between the argument positions in PRED-BASE and PRED-BRIDGE.  The first item in the list corresponds to the argument position of PRED-BASE and the second item in the list corresponds to the argument position of the PRED-BRIDGE.  For example, (#$bridgingPredicateForPredicate #$rdf-type #$isa (#$TheSet (#$TheList 1 1) (#$TheList 2 2))) means that, in certain contexts #$isa literals are solved by transforming into #$rdf-type and the arg1 of #$rdf-type corresponds to arg1 is #$isa and arg2 of #$rdf-type corresponds to arg2 of #$isa. ") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad32b).
