x_comment('x_generateSupplementalFormulasForElements-TermGenls',"(#$generateFormulasForElements-TermGenls TERM SET) means that if a specialization of TERM is a valid term in the search query results, then elements of SET ( a set or collection), INS, should have the appropriate formulas generated for them.  This predicate is used in the CAE query search.  The appropriate formula, at this point is determined by whether INS is a collection or a predicate.  If INS is a collection, then (#$isa ?X INS) is the appropriate formula.  If INS is a predicate with arity N, then (INS ?VAR1, ..., VARN)is the appropriate formula.  At that point, any formulas resulting from the instantiation of terms from the valid terms set should be placed in the \"supplemental fragments\" folder.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad3b6).
