x_comment(x_baseForm,"(baseForm WORD STRING) means that STRING is one of the base forms for WORD.  Most words have only one base form, but multiple base forms are necessary in some cases.  For example, some prefixes are just as valid with or without a hyphen.  In these cases, there will be two valid #$baseForm values.  For example, 're-implant' and 'reimplant' are both good base forms for (#$WordWithPrefixFn #$Re-ThePrefix #$Implant-TheWord).  In general, #$baseForm should only be asserted for less-preferred base forms, while the preferred base form should be asserted with #$preferredBaseForm.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad3f3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad3f3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
