x_comment(x_cyclicalProcessTypeFocus,"(#$cyclicalProcessTypeFocus CYCLE-CLASS FOCUS-CLASS) means that, in any instance of CYCLE-CLASS, there is an instance of FOCUS-CLASS that is in some way physically integrated into every output and every input of each stage within the cycle.  For example, consider the (#$NitrogenCycleFn #$ContinentOfNorthAmerica).  This is an instance of #$NitrogenCycle, and features instances of the characteristic stages associated with #$NitrogenCycles: #$NitrogenFixation, #$Nitrification, #$NitrogenAssimilation, etc..  Although free #$Nitrogen is emphatically not an input or output of every stage instantiation, #$Nitrogen or a chemical compound containing #$Nitrogen is involved in every stage of the process, and #$Nitrogen itself can be regarded as the principle role player in the narrative thread of the cycle's description.  Thus, #$Nitrogen is regarded as the #$cyclicalProcessTypeFocus of the #$NitrogenCycle.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad40a).
