x_comment(x_MarketSupplyFn,"A function which returns the quantity of instances of a given #$ExistingObjectType and specialization of #$Product that suppliers in a #$Market are willing to provide for a specific #$MonetaryValue.  More specifically, (#$MarketSupplyFn MARKET PRODUCT-TYPE PRICE) denotes the total quantity of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE that suppliers in MARKET are willing to supply for PRICE. Thus, e.g. (#$MarketSupplyFn (#$MarketFn #$Automobile (#$YearFn 2008) #$Italy) #$LamborghiniP400Car (#$USDollar 60000)) denotes how many Lamborghini P400s will be supplied in the 2008 Italian automobile market for a price of $60,000 per car.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad41c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad41c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
