x_comment(x_MarketDemandFn,"A function which returns the quantity of instances of a given #$ExistingObjectType and specialization of #$Product that consumers in a #$Market are willing to buy for a specific #$MonetaryValue. More specifically, (#$MarketDemandFn MARKET PRODUCT-TYPE PRICE) denotes the total quantity of instances of PRODUC-TYPE that consumers in MARKET are willing to buy for PRICE.  Thus, e.g. (#$MarketDemandFn (#$MarketFn #$Automobile (#$YearFn 2008) #$LosAngeles) #$LamborghiniP400Car (#$USDollar 60000)) denotes how many Lamborghinis will/would be purchased by consumers in the 2008 L.A. auto market for a price of $60,000 per car.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad41d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad41d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
