x_comment(x_MarketSupplyInUnitsFn,"A funtion which returns the quantity of instances of a given #$ExistingStuffType, as measured by a specified #$UnitOfMeasure, that suppliers in a given #$Market will supply for a given monetary value.  More specifically, (#$MarketSupplyInUnitsFn MARKET STUFF-TYPE UNIT PRICE) denotes the number of UNITs of STUFF-TYPE that suppliers in MARKET will supply for PRICE.  Thus, e.g., (#$MarketSupplyInUnitsFn (#$MarketFn #$Oil (#$YearFn 2008) #$SaudiArabia) #$Petroleum-CrudeOil #$Barrel-UnitOfVolume (#$Dollar 110)) denotes the number of barrels of crude oil that the 2008 Saudi oil market will supply for a price of $110.00.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad41e).
