x_comment(x_RatifyingSomething,"A specialization of #$PoliticalEvent and #$AdoptingANorm (qq.v.).  This is the collection of all acts of ratifying an #$Agreement or #$CodeOfConduct (qq.v.).   Each instance of #$RatifyingSomething is an political action in which an #$Organization formally sanctions or approves some proposed agreement or code.  In many cases, the ratifying organization is the #$governingBody of some larger subsuming group, and the agreement/code concerns the members of the larger group.\n<p>\nIn some cases, ratification by the relevant organization is a necessary and sufficient condition for the agreement/code's taking effect at all.  For example, a city council might ratify a proposed municipal law (or not), and an electorate might ratify a certain ballot measure (or not).  In other cases (such as instances of #$RatifyingAnInternationalAgreement), a particular organization's ratifying the agreement/code is just a necessary and sufficient condition for <i>that organization's</i> being bound (see #$normativelyBoundAgents) by the agreement/code, which other groups may independently decide to ratify.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad445).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad445,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ad445,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
