x_comment('x_firstPublicationDate-CW',"<code>(#$firstPublicationDate-CW WORK DATE)</code> means that the #$ConceptualWork <code>WORK</code> was first published on #$Date <code>DATE</code>.  Publication here means the distribution of more than one copy of a work to the public or an identifiable subset of the public consisting of more than a few members.  Note that publication here does not imply that a particular #$ConceptualWork has been printed or physically distributed (a work may be electronically distributed).  To have a publication date implies that a #$ConceptualWork has been made available to, or accessible by, the public or a portion of the public.  Publication date is not the same as creation date (see #$workCreationDate).  A #$ConceptualWork that has been created, but not made available to anyone except the creator of the work, has not been published and has no #$firstPublicationDate-CW.  The #$firstPublicationDate-CW of a #$ConceptualWork is necessarily the same as the #$publicationDate-IBO of the first instantiation of that #$ConceptualWork that is published. ") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad448).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad448,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ad448,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
