x_comment(x_inReactionTo,"This is the weakest and most general of all the predicates dealing with \"reaction\" or \"response\" that incorporates an intentional component.  <code>(#$inReactionTo ACT SITUATION)</code> means that some <code>AGENT</code> has a goal such that <code>AGENT</code> believes <code>SITUATION</code> changes the likelihood of the goal, and that one of the outcomes of this belief is <code>ACT</code>, which is performed by (see #$performedBy) <code>AGENT</code> (i.e., <code>ACT</code> is done deliberately).  This predicate does not cover cases of involuntary or instinctive reaction, for which a weaker sense of causation is appropriate.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad4a0).
