x_comment(x_LawOfDiminishingMarginalUtility,"An instance of #$EconomicLaw that claims that, over a given period, as instances of some good are accumulated (or consumed) by an agent, the utility or desirability of those instances to that agent decrease.  For example, if an individual has a taste for apples and is hungry, he or she might be willing to purchase one or two apples at some set price, but will value additional apples less and less (and will be willing to pay less and less) as he or she consumes more.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad4ac).
