x_comment(x_jurisdictionScopeOfCourt,"This predicate captures the important concept of the scope or kind of case that a #$Court-Judicial in a given judicial system is permitted to hear.  In particular, U.S. legal tradition distinguishes between 'original jurisdiction' and 'appellate jurisdiction'.  A given #$Court-Judicial, COURT, has original jurisdiction iff (#$jurisdictionScopeOfCourt COURT #$CourtCase-Original) and appellate jurisdiction iff (#$jurisdictionScopeOfCourt COURT #$CourtCase-Appellate).") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad4d4).
