xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ad557,[]).
x_comment(x_netDecreasingFunctionOnArg,"(A function characterizing predicate used to describe the behavior of a #$FixedArityFunction.  (#$netDecreasingFunctionOnArg FN N) is true iff the following conditional holds.  Let L-TERM be the result returned by the #$FixedArityFunction FN on a tuple of arguments where H-ARG is the Nth argument.  Let H-TERM be the result returned by FN on the same set of arguments save that the Nth argument is replaced with L-ARG, and suppose (#$greaterThan H-ARG L-ARG):  then (#$greaterThan H-TERM L-TERM).  In the vernacular, (#$netIncreasingFunctionOnAf FN N) means that the value returned by FN decreases as the value of the Nth argument supplied to FN increases, the other argument values remaining constant.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad558).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad558,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
