x_comment('x_BrandenburgVTheStateOfOhio-CourtCase',"An important case concerning #$USCitizensRightToFreedomOfSpeech.  The particulars were that #$ClarenceBrandenburg, a member of the Ku Klux Klan, was taped at an Ohio Klan rally making numerous racist remarks, burning a cross, and accusing the (#$GovernmentFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica) of suppressing Caucasians.  He was convicted under Ohio's Criminal Syndicalism statute for advocating violence, and his appeal to state appellate court was dismissed.  The #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt struck down the law under which Brandenburg was convicted on the grounds that only speech which threatened to induce 'imminent lawless action' could be proscribed, given first amendment protections (the #$ImminentLawlessActionPrinciple).  This ruling placed considerable strictures on the #$ClearAndPresentDangerPrinciple enunciated by #$OliverWendellHolmesJr some 50 years before.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad58a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad58a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ad58a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ad58a,27349).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ad58a,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ad58a,[]).
x_comment(x_overturnsPrecedent,"(#$overturnsPrecedent NORM-LATER NORM-EARLIER) means that NORM-LATER is adopted at some later date than NORM-EARLIER, and effectively overrules the convention established by NORM-EARLIER, either through specialization or outright contradiction.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad58b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad58b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ad58b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ad58b,27350).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ad58b,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ad58b,[]).
x_comment(x_ImminentLawlessActionPrinciple,"The principle enunciated in #$BrandenburgVTheStateOfOhio-CourtCase.  This considerably tightened the latitude of the #$ClearAndPresentDangerPrinciple set forth by the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt six decades earlier:  specifically, the court stated that only speech which could be reasonably construed as provoking or inciting imminent violation of the law was unprotected by the #$FirstAmendment-USConstitution.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad58c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad58c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ad58c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ad58c,27351).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ad58c,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ad58c,[]).
x_comment('x_NewYorkTimesVTheUnitedStates-CourtCase',"When Daniel Ellsburg leaked a top secret 2.5 million word classified report on the history of U.S. involvement in the #$VietnamWar to the #$NewYorkTimesCompany in early 1971, the paper began publishing it in installments in June of that year.  The administration of #$RichardNixon sought to have a federal district court immediately issue an injunction to cease and desist from publication, arguing that the exercise would cause irreparable harm to U.S. Defense Interests. After numerous inconclusive attempts to enlist Federal courts on one side and the other, both the administration and the paper appealed to the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt.  The court, in a 6-3 opinion, ruled that the administration had not shown sufficient justification for prior restraint, and that the paper was therefore free to continue publication.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad58d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad58d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ad58d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ad58d,27352).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ad58d,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ad58d,[]).
x_comment(x_marketDemandIsPriceUnitElasticWRTChange,"<code>(#$marketDemandIsPriceUnitElasticWRTChange MARKET PRODUCT OLD-PRICE NEW-PRICE)</code> means that percentage of change in <code>MARKET</code>'s price of <code>PRODUCT</code> from <code>OLD-PRICE</code> to <code>NEW-PRICE</code> is identical to the percentage of change in demand for that product at those prices.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad58e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad58e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ad58e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ad58e,27353).
xc_kb_names(a65b16517ad58e,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16517ad58e,[]).
x_comment(x_marketDemandIsPerfectlyPriceInelasticWRTChange,"<code>(#$marketDemandIsPerfectlyPriceInelasticWRTChange MARKET PRODUCT OLD-PRICE NEW-PRICE)</code> means that given a change in <code>MARKET</code>'s price of <code>PRODUCT</code> from <code>OLD-PRICE</code> to <code>NEW-PRICE</code>, there will be no change in demand; precisely speaking, theabsolute value of the elasticity of demand in response to this change is 0.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad58f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad58f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16517ad58f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part06.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16517ad58f,27354).
