x_comment(x_substituteProductTypes,"<code>(#$substituteProductTypes TYPE-1 TYPE-2)</code> means that <code>TYPE-1</code> and <code>TYPE-2</code> are substitute product types, meaning that shifts in price in <code>TYPE-1</code> and shifts in the demand for <code>TYPE-2</code> tend to move in the same direction.  This relation is highly context-sensitive; product-type complementarity holds between two product types in specific markets under specific conditions.  As such <code>(#$substituteProductTypes TYPE-1 TYPE-2)</code> will be true only in contexts (microtheories) where such markets are identified and where such conditions obtain.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad5ae).
xc_microtheory(a65b16517ad5ae,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
