x_comment(x_CaseAppealedToTheSupremeCourt,"The collection of all instances of #$CourtCaseWithOneOrMoreAppeals that are appealed to the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt.  The procedure is for the #$plaintiffs or #$defendants in the case to engage in a #$PetitioningForAWritOfCertiori, that is, a request that the court issue a #$WritOfCertiori-LegalDocument to hear the case.  The court periodically meets in private conference (#$ConferenceOfTheUnitedStatesSupremeCourt) to consider a filtered subset of these petitions (#$PetitionForAWritOfCertiori-LegalDocument.  The court votes on each petition:  if four or more justices agree that the case rises to the level of a constitutuional issue, the court proceeds with an #$IssuingAWritOfCertiori.  Otherwise, the court executes a #$DenyingAPetitionOfCertiori.  The criteria used in deciding whether or not a cert petition merits the court's attention include resolving a conflict in the interpretation of a federal law or a constitutional provision, correcting an egregious departure from accepted jurisprudence, resolving an important question of federal law, and reviewing a decision of a lower court that conflicts with a previous decision of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt.") :- x_cid(a65b16517ad5c6).
